window.SH_INDEX=[{"p":"Advancements","h":"","u":"advancements.html","t":"Static Hollow has its own advancements tab, added in 1.34.0. Its root reads Static Hollow: Something has been watching you. There are 69 advancements under it in 1.63.3, from the end of chapter four to the Dead Water, plus one for every chapter's gear. Spoilers, obviously. Each one shows its frame as the game draws it: a task (square), a goal (rounded) or a challenge (spiked; drawn doubled here). 9 are hidden until you earn them. The icons are the mod's own textures where the advancement uses one of its items."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The tab","u":"advancements.html#the-tab","t":"Static Hollow Something has been watching you. The root's own icon in game is the Rosemont Device."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter four","u":"advancements.html#chapter-four","t":"Advancement In game How Not Collected challenge hidden Put the Rosemont Device into the Great Bloom. It's still beating. Launch the Device from the ledge. See the launch . The Bell Tolls goal Kill a Bellwether. The rest of them won't know where to go. Kill a Bellwether, at the head of a horde or on its own. The Last Light challenge hidden End the changed Bloom Kill the changed Bloom. The Omni Ray challenge hidden Call SENTINEL down on the changed Bloom Fire the Omni at it from 50 blocks or more off its mouth. Zero Responsibility goal hidden Have the Omni taken back - for the future Carry the Omni off the blight. Always Persistent task hidden Try to make the Ray Gun again Put the Ray Gun together in a crafting grid after the Watcher took the Omni. Ten Days Later goal hidden The Watcher comes back - with a warning about the parasites Wait ten days (world clock) after the Omni Ray."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter five","u":"advancements.html#chapter-five","t":""},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The static","u":"advancements.html#the-static","t":"Advancement In game How Something Inside task Let a Parasite hold on long enough to get into you Don't crouch. Four seconds. Cut It Out task Cut a parasite's brood out with a Surgical Kit Surgical Kit on yourself, someone else or an animal. Burn It Out task Burn the brood out of yourself before it's too big Stand in fire before it's three quarters grown. It Came Out of Me challenge hidden Live through a brood bursting out of your back Let it grow all the way, and survive 7 hearts. Head of the Pack goal Kill a Static Hound Pack Leader, and watch the pack break Kill the one with the brood sac on its back. Not One of Them task See a villager turn into one of the Hollowed Be alone with it at night, or hurt it."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The outbreak","u":"advancements.html#the-outbreak","t":"Advancement In game How It Isn't Itself goal Be there when something the parasite took over turns Be within 24 blocks when a creature carrying the parasite reaches the end and turns: five seconds of seizing, arching and screaming, then it tears open. See the turned ."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The relay","u":"advancements.html#the-relay","t":"Advancement In game How Dead Air task Find the relay the parasites talk through Reach Relay 6 . Cut the Cord challenge Cut the last of the tethers off the relay's mast while what's at its foot still lives Climb the mast and break all three tethers before killing the Amalgam. Off the Air goal Kill the Amalgam and silence the relay Kill the Amalgam . Tuned In task Listen in on them with the Relay Core Hold the Relay Core to your ear."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The Null","u":"advancements.html#the-null","t":"Advancement In game How The Null task Come to the drive-in where the last of their static runs down Reach the Starlite Drive-In . Signal Lost task Put an Afterimage all the way here long enough to kill it Kill an Afterimage while Tuned In, while it reaches for you, or during the reel. The Last Reel goal Run the last reel through to its end, and see where they come from Four frames in the projector, the Relay Core on you, and hold the booth."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The Null Static Zone","u":"advancements.html#the-null-static-zone","t":"Advancement In game How The Null Static Zone task Go through the tear at the drive-in, to where all of the static ran down Hold the Last Reel over the tear, and step in. Cut Loose goal Cut the last of the Carrier's threads Climb the four spires and break the knots. Signing Off challenge Kill the Carrier, and see the Watcher take what's left of it Kill the Carrier . The Hush task Step over the line into one of the old pale houses, where the static can't follow Enter a Hush . Unmade goal See a hound come apart in a Hush's door Lead a Static Hound to a Hush. Put Your Ear to It task Listen at one of the ears cut into the old stones Use a Listening Stone ."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The Hive","u":"advancements.html#the-hive","t":"Advancement In game How It Speaks task Hear the Chorus speak through its own A night after the Hive has grown, be out under the open sky: five of the pure forms come up out of the ground round you and it speaks through them. The Hive task Come to where the parasite is growing itself a mind Reach the Hive . The needle the Watcher gives you after It Speaks points to it. Senseless goal Tear open all four of the Chorus's nerve nodes Break all four nerve nodes on the stalks round the pit (climb the steps round the stalks). It Ran challenge Drive the Chorus down out of its pit Bring the Chorus down to a quarter of its health. It won't die: it runs, down into the ground."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The Deep","u":"advancements.html#the-deep","t":"Advancement In game How Warmer task Follow the Chorus Fragment's whispers to where it went down Follow the Chorus Fragment to the Sinkhole at Halloway's Low Field, and come up to its rim. Down Where It Is Warm goal Stand on the Throat at the bottom of the burrow, and let it take you into the Deep Go down the Burrow's six turns and stand on the Throat in the chamber at the bottom. It Came Up challenge Kill the Reach: the hand the Chorus tore up out of the ground at your home Every few nights, at your home, one of the Chorus's hands tears up out of the ground (its own bar, its own music). Kill it before it sinks back down after four minutes. Everyone within 96 blocks gets it. Not a Sound task Make boots out of a Listener's ears Craft Hushed Boots: leather boots, two Listener's Ears and string. Stand Still challenge Kill the Deaf King in his hall Kill the Deaf King on his dais at the end of the Old Halls. Follow the way-stones from the Gullet. The Last Voice challenge Kill the Chorus, whole, in the Warm Heart Kill the Chorus, whole, in the Warm Heart. Follow the fragment there."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter six: the Door at the End of the World","u":"advancements.html#chapter-six","t":"The End is shut once you've signed off. All of these start with carrying the Last Voice into it. See chapter six ."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Part one: the Audience","u":"advancements.html#part-one-the-audience","t":"Advancement In game How The Door at the End of the World goal Carry the Last Voice into the End, and break his seal Carry the Last Voice into the End. Something cracks across the sky, and the Door goes down east of the obsidian you arrive on. Take Your Seat task Go through the Door into the Stalls Walk the causeway to the island and into the static in the Door: the Stalls . Quiet, Please challenge Keep perfectly still through the Crowd's Hush From two thirds of the Crowd's health down it puts a Hush on the house. Don't move or strike for the whole four seconds. Standing Ovation challenge Bring the Crowd down Step onto the front aisle under the screen and kill the Crowd . Front Row goal See who was sitting in the front row Be there for the cutscene after the Crowd dies: one seat in the front row is still taken."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Part two: the Watcher's Vault","u":"advancements.html#part-two-the-watchers-vault","t":"Advancement In game How Admit One goal Hold the Last Ticket up to the seam in the screen Hold the Last Ticket up to the seam in the Great Screen. Behind the Picture task Go through the seam, into the Watcher's Vault Go through the open seam into the Watcher's Vault . What He Kept goal Take all three things out of his keeps Open the three round steel doors off the nave and take the Omni's Heart, What's Left of the Carrier and His First Reel. The Final Reel challenge Burn the Projectionist through Bring all three to the Watch and kill the Projectionist . What He Kept Out goal See his first reel Be there when he runs his first reel, after the Projectionist."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Part three: What He Kept Out","u":"advancements.html#part-three-what-he-kept-out","t":"Advancement In game How The Other Side goal Go through the Door at the End of the World, its static gone black Walk into the Door once its static has gone black: the Other Side . Every Colour at Once task See the Omni's heart put into his last projector's lamp Fight the Viewer to two thirds, when he loads the Omni's Heart into his last projector. Out of Sight challenge Get through the first third of the Viewer without it ever seeing you right through Get through the Viewer's first third without ever being Seen right through. Keep a painted flat between you and its eye. It Gets Up goal Be there when what he kept out stands up At a third left he runs the Carrier through the projector, and the Viewer stands up. Thank You for Watching challenge See the last show See the last show through to the credits. You're sent home with the record of the same name."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter seven: the First Signal","u":"advancements.html#chapter-seven","t":"See chapter seven . Advancement In game How The Hub goal Be taken into the realm he made, after the credits After the last show's credits, his hand comes up through them: you're taken into the Hub . ENOUGH challenge hidden Hear the First Signal - and jump See his speech through to the First Signal coming through, and go off the edge with him. The First Signal goal hidden Come down from the Hub, and hear what it is Come down out of the Hub. Since 1.62.0 that's onto the rig in the Dead Water. Channel Changer task Be given the Remote He gives it to you as you come down. (In the Dead Water it breaks in your hand a moment later: you still get this.) Previously On... task Go back to a chapter through one of the Hub's portals Walk into one of the six replay portals in the Hub's gallery."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Chapter eight: the Dead Water","u":"advancements.html#chapter-eight","t":"See chapter eight . Advancement In game How Dead Water task Come down through his portal onto the rig Come down through his portal onto the rig in the Dead Water . Back On Air goal Mend the Remote with what a Static Leviathan sings with Craft the Broken Remote, a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ and a copper ingot together, while you're stranded there. See the leviathans ."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"Gear for every chapter","u":"advancements.html#gear-for-every-chapter","t":"Since 1.60.0 each chapter has its own armour set, weapons and tools: see gear for every chapter . These count what you've had in your inventory, so you don't need everything at once. Advancement In game How Keep Watch task Put on all of the Vigil: the iron hood, its candles, the coat. Have each of the four Vigil pieces (chapter one). Out Standing in the Field task Put on all of the Scarecrow's clothes. Have each of the four Scarecrow pieces (chapter two). Rooted task Put on all of the Bloomwoven. Have each of the four Bloomwoven pieces (chapter three). Specimen task Put on all of the Specimen gear, jar and all. Have each of the four Specimen pieces (chapter four). Off the Air task Put on all of Dead Air. Have each of the four Dead Air pieces (chapter five). Not the same as the relay's Off the Air. Front of House task Put on all of the Usher's uniform. Have each of the four pieces of the Usher's Uniform (chapter six). Live task Put on all of the On Air gear. Have each of the four On Air pieces (chapter seven). Something for Every Chapter challenge Hold a weapon from every chapter. Have one of the two weapons from each of the seven chapters: the Censer or Bell Clapper, the Pitchfork or Omen Staff, the Thorn Whip or Spore Mace, the Bone Saw or Reactor Rod, the Tuning Fork or Relay Staff, the Splicer or Fly Hook, the Antenna Glaive or On Air Mace. Rerun task Beat a replay again and keep what it leaves: a Rerun Reel. Beat a replay from the Hub again and pick up one of the Rerun Reels it leaves. Chapter seven's gear is made with them."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"The world","u":"advancements.html#the-world","t":"Advancement In game How Fallout task Break open a Fallen Star Mine a Fallen Star and get Star Static. Small ones come down near you at night. See falling stars ."},{"p":"Advancements","h":"All of them, as toasts","u":"advancements.html#at-a-glance","t":"Not Collected hidden Put the Rosemont Device into the Great Bloom. It's still beating. The Bell Tolls Kill a Bellwether. The rest of them won't know where to go. The Last Light hidden End the changed Bloom The Omni Ray hidden Call SENTINEL down on the changed Bloom Zero Responsibility hidden Have the Omni taken back - for the future Always Persistent hidden Try to make the Ray Gun again Ten Days Later hidden The Watcher comes back - with a warning about the parasites Something Inside Let a Parasite hold on long enough to get into you Cut It Out Cut a parasite's brood out with a Surgical Kit Burn It Out Burn the brood out of yourself before it's too big It Came Out of Me hidden Live through a brood bursting out of your back Head of the Pack Kill a Static Hound Pack Leader, and watch the pack break Not One of Them See a villager turn into one of the Hollowed It Isn't Itself Be there when something the parasite took over turns Dead Air Find the relay the parasites talk through Cut the Cord Cut the last of the tethers off the relay's mast while what's at its foot still lives Off the Air Kill the Amalgam and silence the relay Tuned In Listen in on them with the Relay Core The Null Come to the drive-in where the last of their static runs down Signal Lost Put an Afterimage all the way here long enough to kill it The Last Reel Run the last reel through to its end, and see where they come from The Null Static Zone Go through the tear at the drive-in, to where all of the static ran down Cut Loose Cut the last of the Carrier's threads Signing Off Kill the Carrier, and see the Watcher take what's left of it The Hush Step over the line into one of the old pale houses, where the static can't follow Unmade See a hound come apart in a Hush's door Put Your Ear to It Listen at one of the ears cut into the old stones It Speaks Hear the Chorus speak through its own The Hive Come to where the parasite is growing itself a mind Senseless Tear open all four of the Chorus's nerve nodes It Ran Drive the Chorus down out of its pit Warmer Follow the Chorus Fragment's whispers to where it went down Down Where It Is Warm Stand on the Throat at the bottom of the burrow, and let it take you into the Deep It Came Up Kill the Reach: the hand the Chorus tore up out of the ground at your home Not a Sound Make boots out of a Listener's ears Stand Still Kill the Deaf King in his hall The Last Vo"},{"p":"Credits","h":"Static Hollow","u":"credits.html#static-hollow","t":"Made by Death Licence All Rights Reserved Version on this site 1.63.3 Music The mod's own 63 pieces on the soundtrack, and more for chapter eight: see the soundtrack"},{"p":"Credits","h":"Built into the mod","u":"credits.html#built-into-the-mod","t":"Orbital Railgun by Mishkis, from Rayness's Renewed port (the NeoForge port it was taken from), both under the MIT licence (see LICENSE-orbital-railgun.txt in the mod). The Ray Gun and the Omni are built on it: its gun model, its texture, its sounds and its strike. Static Hollow's own gun pack for Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero (the Mended SMG, Shotgun and Marksman Rifle), built into the Fabric mod."},{"p":"Credits","h":"In the modpacks","u":"credits.html#in-the-modpack","t":"Mod or pack By Licence and how it's used What it's for Fabric Loader and Fabric API FabricMC The Fabric version runs on them Sodium CaffeineMC Rendering speed (Fabric) Iris Shaders IrisShaders Shader packs on Fabric Lithium CaffeineMC Faster game logic (Fabric) Entity Culling tr7zw Skips drawing creatures hidden behind walls (Fabric) First-person Model and Not Enough Animations tr7zw Your own body in first person (Fabric) Sound Physics Remastered henkelmax Installed but switched off since 1.61.1 Reverb, echo and muffling, if you switch it back on Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero [Unofficial] Refabricated The TaCZ team The Mended guns (Fabric) Forge Config API Port Fuzs Needed by TaCZ Biomes O' Plenty the Glitchfiend team Unmodified Biomes; Static Hollow's structures, music and fog are made to fit them TerraBlender and GlitchCore Glitchfiend Unmodified GlitchCore is needed by Biomes O' Plenty and Serene Seasons, TerraBlender by Biomes O' Plenty; the Hollow's own biomes come into the world through TerraBlender Serene Seasons the Glitchfiend team Unmodified, with Static Hollow's settings The seasons Puddles & Floods PigCart MIT. Unmodified on Fabric; on Forge a port of 1.1.6 made for the pack ( LICENSE-puddles-floods.txt , source and notes in companions/puddles-floods-forge ) Puddles in the rain, rivers that flood Water Erosion 13rac1 GNU GPL v3. Ported to 26.3 for the pack and shipped with its source ( companions/water-erosion ) Running water that wears the land away Streams: Reflowing NiceJohn Unmodified Streams that follow the land (Fabric) Cinematic Interactions Southware MIT. A build made for the pack, with Static Hollow's sounds and look ( companions/cinematic-interactions ) Workstations as first-person scenes \"Just a Hammer\" RDiamonds CC BY 4.0 Cinematic Interactions' hammer model Photon SixthSurge Downloaded unmodified The default shader pack Hysteria and Insanity ElocinDev Downloaded unmodified Shader packs the mod also makes its own copies of The shader packs are downloaded unmodified; the \"-StaticHollow\" copies are made on each player's own computer and never shipped. What the newer mods do in the game is on cold, thirst and the world ."},{"p":"Credits","h":"Ideas the README credits","u":"credits.html#ideas","t":"These gave the mod an idea. In each case the README says nothing of theirs is used. Tectonic (MIT): lava glowing at the very bottom of the deep oceans. The deep is the game's own terrain, stretched. Olaf's Relatively Placed Blocks : small blocks sharing one space. Tough As Nails : the cold and the thirst. Subnautica (1, 2 and Below Zero), Alex's Caves and Thalassophobia : the Dead Water's seas. Every creature, model, texture and sound there is Static Hollow's own."},{"p":"Credits","h":"Tools","u":"credits.html#tools","t":"Blockbench for the creatures' models. The project files come separately as StaticHollow-Blockbench.zip . Real-ESRGAN , an AI upscaler, for the optional HD packs (and since 1.61.0 the chapter gear in them)."},{"p":"Credits","h":"This website","u":"credits.html#this-wiki","t":"Every story detail, item description, note and line of dialogue comes from the mod's own files (its README, language file, data and source), version 1.63.3. The screenshots are the mod's own CurseForge screenshots, and the soundtrack cover and the Dead Channel logo are the mod's. The home page's scene is rebuilt from the mod's own main-menu layers, and the item and advancement icons are the mod's own textures. The cover art is the mod's CurseForge image. Fonts, all under the SIL Open Font License and included with the site: Big Shoulders Display (Patric King), Spectral (Production Type) and Courier Prime (Alan Dague-Greene)."},{"p":"Credits","h":"Legal","u":"credits.html#legal","t":"Static Hollow is an independent mod for Minecraft. It and this website are not official Minecraft products and are not approved by or associated with Mojang or Microsoft. Minecraft is a trademark of Mojang. Creepypasta and folklore characters belong to the stories and places they come from."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html","t":"The ring of thorned roots round the risen Great Bloom Boss, twice Appears when You bring the Rosemont Device within 32 blocks of the risen Great Bloom Health 600 (Reborn). Reborn Again: 900 Size Ten feet tall; four blocks in his last phase Weak to Fire (takes half again). Sixty damage in three seconds puts him on one knee Drops The Bloomshears, three Bloom Heartwood and the Gardener's Seed, both times"},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"The release","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#the-release","t":"Carry the Rosemont Device toward the risen Great Bloom. Within 32 blocks, the Bloom goes still and turns every petal on the Device. Then it gags, heaves, and spits the Gardener back up in a gush of nectar, his body knitting itself together with vines. It folds its petals shut over its mouth, and a ring of thorned roots six blocks high comes up round the arena (48 blocks out from the Bloom since 1.38). Nothing gets through the ring, and it tears at whatever pushes against it. If you end up outside it alone, after ten seconds the roots part to let you back in. here he comes. it's giving him back. it doesn't want that thing anywhere near its mouth. ??? as the Bloom gives him back"},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Description","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#description","t":"He's rebuilt on the first Gardener's own body: ten feet tall, the long canvas coat (rotted now, stained with the Bloom, torn where its petals came through), the wide hat, the cage of root ribs, the long thin arms and root feet. Everything the Bloom did to him is still there: grey bark split along every seam with the Bloom's petals breathing in the splits, the ribs pried open round a small copy of the Bloom's mouth in his chest, the Bloom's red petals round the hollow of his face with two green lights deep in it and a jaw of teeth under them. His left arm is a tentacle ending in a hook. In his right hand are the Bloomshears : two of the Bloom's teeth hinged by a tendril."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"How he fights","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#how-he-fights","t":""},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Phase 1","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#phase-1","t":"Shear Snap: the shears opened wide, then snapped shut in front of him. Hedge Sweep: he crouches and twists, sweeping 270 degrees round him. Root Lattice: shears into the ground, and three fanned lines of root spikes run out toward you. Pollen Breath: head back, then a golden cone: weakness, slowness, and the Bloom's infection. At 65% he screams and tears the shears apart at the hinge, taking one blade in his hook. The ring cracks open in three places and the Flesh pours in. It goes for him as hard as for you."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Phase 2","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#phase-2","t":"Twin Cut: blades crossed overhead, three cuts and a slam. Petal Storm: he spins up on his tentacle in a spiral of razor petals. Get in close or behind them. Graft Leap: he lands where you were, and the Bloom grafts itself onto the ground there. It heals him while he stands in it, burns, and withers in half a minute. Feed: he reaches through for one of the Flesh's infected and eats it (+30 health). Tendril Call: the ground cracks under you. At 30% the Bloom pours itself into him. He grows to four blocks, petals burst out of his back, and his chest mouth opens. The music turns into The Choir ."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Phase 3","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#phase-3","t":"Whip-Shears: the blades on root chains, whirled overhead and swept across twelve blocks in front of him. Chest Choir: the chest mouth's shockwave, which also brings down whatever you built in front of him. The Bloom Eclipse (once, at 20%): the Bloom closes its dome, the dark comes down, and four spore pods fall into the arena. Each one you don't break within fifteen seconds heals him 50 and lets two tendrils up. The Wilting Embrace (once, below 10%): his tentacle takes you and he walks you toward the Bloom's mouth. Hit him six times to break free."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"How to survive him","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#how-to-survive-him","t":"Bring fire. He takes half again from it. Burst damage works: sixty damage inside three seconds puts him on one knee. When the ring cracks at 65%, the Flesh's infected come in. Let them fight him, but kill the ones he reaches for, because each one he eats heals him 30. Break all four spore pods during the eclipse. Keep the Device close. The Watcher: \"keep the device close. i'll come for you when it's time.\""},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Reborn Again","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#reborn-again","t":"Since 1.40, killing him isn't the end. The Bloom grows him back once more: the Gardener, Reborn Again , faster and harder. The tracker reads \"The Bloom is growing him back. Stay near it.\" it isn't letting him go. it's growing him back. stay close. kill him again, and i'll open it. ??? as the Bloom grows him back Kill him the second time, and the Watcher rips the portal into the Bloom open for the launch . Reborn Again has half as much health again (900), hits harder (13 to the Reborn's 10), is quicker on his feet and a quarter quicker between moves, and never quite stops bleeding the Bloom's light out of every split in him. His bar turns red and reads \"The Gardener, Reborn Again\". He drops the same things."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"His end","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#his-end","t":"When he dies the shears wilt, he kneels, his petals fall, and he's left as a heap of leaves round a seed. The ring withers back into the ground and the Bloom shuts itself up tight. The Bloomshears (Graft): full swings snip twice, and the Bloom in them hates the Flesh, so they hit infected half again as hard. Use them to drive three lines of thorned roots toward what you face. Bloom Heartwood (three): close-grained, pale, still warm, green light running in it like sap. The Gardener's Seed : a hard black seed the size of a fist, split along one seam. Something in it breathes. Bloom Heartwood goes into Chapter Three's gear: the Heartwood tools, the Thorn Whip, the Spore Mace and two pieces of the Bloomwoven (see Gear for every chapter )."},{"p":"The Gardener, Reborn (and Reborn Again)","h":"Turned","u":"entities/gardener-reborn.html#turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take him. Turned, he's the Reborn, Consumed . The Hub's replay portal for The Bloom brings him back for another go."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html","t":"Shown in game as \"Tentacle of the Great Bloom\" Grabs How many Eight round the Great Bloom's mouth Size Thick as trees at first; since 1.27.2, towers as wide as a hill at the root Sounds A tentacle lashes, grabs, drags; bones creak in its grip Death message \"[you] was eaten by the Great Bloom\""},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"Description","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#description","t":"Round the Great Bloom's mouth rise eight tentacles, feeling about, curling over at their tips. Down in its realm they come up out of the green round the islands like towers, each as wide as a hill at the root, curling over far above you. Every light in the Bloom beats with its heart, the veins in the tentacles too."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"When you fall","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#when-you-fall","t":"Fall off an island in the Bloom and a tentacle whips up out of the green after you. Since 1.27.2 it comes straight up out of the Bloom's throat under you, twenty blocks thick. It coils round you and drags you back through the air and down into its mouth. Anything else that falls goes the same way. Caught, your sight closes in red and shakes, you hear your bones creak in its grip and your breath forced out of you, slime and blood trail off you, and over its mouth its teeth close in over your sight from all round, ring by ring, until there is nothing. Since 1.38 you go down its throat alive, into its stomach. Chat: \"Something huge is reaching up out of the green for you...\" then \"It has you.\""},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"When the Binding breaks","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#when-the-binding-breaks","t":"Touch the Binding twice and the Great Bloom goes mad. Its tentacles come up out of the green round the Binding's island (out of its throat, since 1.27.2), over the edge, and take hold. You have ten seconds. Then they pull the whole island down its throat, rift and all, and take anyone left out there one by one."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"Round the risen Bloom","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#round-the-risen-bloom","t":"The Bloom that rises through the glasshouse reaches for anything within about 26 blocks, players first. The changed Bloom reaches for anything within ninety, and when it's hungry it comes up out of the ground under anyone out on its petals: cracks first, then its tentacles, one where you'll be if you keep going. When you carry the Rosemont Device toward it, its roots come up after you: green cracks open under your feet, and two seconds later a tendril bursts out that whips, holds and infects whatever it catches (\"Something in the ground has you.\")."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"Over the ledge","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#over-the-ledge","t":"During the launch, the colossal Bloom's tentacles rise up round the ledge and hang over it, trembling, held back. The Watcher is holding them. don't look at them. i've got them. i can't hold them long. ??? on the ledge After the Device goes off, the tentacles wither black. After the Omni Ray, they're gone, vaporized with its mouth and throat."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"The great flower's tendril","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#the-great-flowers-tendril","t":"The great flower under the dome, before any of this, has a single tendril of its own. It fastens on, slows you to a crawl and drags you in, drinking, and holds you at its throat and bites, again and again; after the third bite it spits you out. Three good hits tear the tendril and free you (\"It has you! Hit it to tear yourself free!\")."},{"p":"The giant tentacles","h":"How to survive them","u":"entities/giant-tentacles.html#how-to-survive-them","t":"Don't fall. In the Bloom, the bridges and edges are the danger, not the creatures. A tentacle that takes you drags you into the Bloom's mouth, and since 1.38 down into its stomach. Bring a weapon to cut your way out. When the Binding breaks, don't stop to watch. Ten seconds."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html","t":"The cathedral's sanctuary Boss Summoned at The Hollow Reliquary, with one head of each of the nine creepypastas Size Five blocks tall Health 500 Phases Two: its first form, and its dark form from half health Drops The Saint's Heart, 4 to 5 Saint's Shrouds, and by chance gold ingots (60%), a totem of undying (25%) or an enchanted golden apple (5%). It has no head to drop. The Hollow Saint Nine eyes in the iron grid, all of them on you."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Summoning it","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#summoning","t":"In the cathedral's sanctuary, put one head from each of the nine different creepypastas on the nine pedestals round the Hollow Reliquary, then right-click the reliquary with an empty hand. The summoning takes about ten seconds and it can't be hurt until it has fully risen. The floor goes dark and a circle of runes burns open; a beam of light streams out of every head into an orb over the reliquary; souls and embers pour in and lightning crawls over it; the floor cracks and red light comes up through it. Then the Saint rises up out of the ground into the light, slowly, and roars with many dead voices at once: a flash, rings of light, a pillar into the sky, and everything nearby thrown back into darkness."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Description","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#description","t":"It stands five blocks tall in a deep cowl. Its iron mask is a grid bolted over raw flesh, with nine real eyes bulging out of their square sockets that roll on their own and all turn to fix on you when you look at it. Under the mask a jaw drops open on long teeth. Its robe, in a blood red trimmed with tarnished gold, is torn open over its ribs and the heart beating behind them. Vertebrae break out of its back. It wears an antler crown and a halo of rusted spikes, and it has four arms. Sewn into the robe are the faces of the nine, each one straining out of the cloth, twitching, its mouth falling open. In the dark its eyes, its mouth, its heart and the faces' eyes burn. Its heartbeat booms across the cathedral while it lives."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#first-form","t":"Calls the nine. A red-black portal tears open in the ground for each creepypasta it calls, and it claws its way up out of it to fight beside the Saint. Screams static that blinds you and throws you back. From half health it starts teleporting behind you and calling lightning down on everyone. Bleeding III makes it reel for a moment: it staggers and doubles over, and blood pours out of the wound in its gut."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"At half health, it changes","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#it-changes","t":"It freezes and rises off the ground, arms flung wide, every face on it screaming. The Watcher hanging from the ceiling turns to it, a black sun swelling between its hands, and pours a crackling river of shadow down into the Saint's heart. A rune circle burns into the ground under it and spins faster and faster, the faces tear loose from its robe one by one and rise, screaming, and the air goes violet-black. Nothing you do can hurt it now. Then it bursts: a flash, a pillar of light, shockwaves along the ground, its ribs blown out in shards, and the whole world kicks."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Its dark form","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#dark-form","t":"It drops back down charred black and cracked with burning light, every eye red, its ribs wrenched open, and its heart pushed out of its chest, turned black and veined with violet light. The boss bar turns purple. From here it is faster, teleports behind you in a burst of shadow, calls lightning down, and uses its dark magic: Abyssal Rupture It raises all four arms and a violet circle burns open under every player near it, spinning faster and crackling for a second and a half. Then a pillar of black-violet power erupts out of each one: 12 damage, flung into the air, and darkness. Get out of the circle."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Bring the chapter's gear. The Static Mail's full set makes creepypastas within 32 blocks glow through walls, which helps against the ones it calls up. The Saint's Requiem is made from its own heart, so it can't help you here, but the Sinew Cleaver's Rend stacks Bleeding, and Bleeding III makes the Saint reel. Watch the floor in its dark form: a violet circle under your feet means move now. It teleports behind you from half health. Keep turning."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Its end","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#its-end","t":"When it dies, the Watcher won't let it stay. Its beam turns red and burns the ground open under the Saint: a portal to hell, ringed with burning runes. The Saint tries to claw its way up into the air, every arm reaching, and a huge burning hand rises out of the portal and closes round it. Twice it shoves the fingers apart and drags itself half out; twice the hand clenches and yanks it back. Then it is dragged down through the hole, screaming, and the portal slams shut in a blast of fire. The chat reads The Hollow Saint has fallen. It leaves the Saint's Heart , a real heart still beating in your hand, on the ground and in an item frame. Since 1.40, its tomb in the cathedral's undercroft stands empty, the gate forced from the inside and its chains broken. do you understand what you've done? they were keeping it in. it was the only thing in this world bigger than me. ??? after the Saint falls"},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Field notes","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#field-notes","t":"The priest's journal in the undercroft says the Saint lay sealed in its tomb \"under nine chains and nine candles, one for each of the heads they took to make it\", and that he kept the candles burning forty years. Read his journal and the bell-ringer's tally ."},{"p":"The Hollow Saint","h":"Turned","u":"entities/hollow-saint.html#turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take it. Turned, it's the Saint Unmade : dragging itself on tentacles, its chest a mouth the height of it. The Projectionist's reruns bring back its shadow beam, and the Hub's replay portal for The Hollow raises it out of the floor again."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"","u":"entities/index.html","t":"Every creature in Static Hollow, in the order you meet them, across all eight chapters. Bosses and the creatures with the most to them have their own case files; everything else is here. Each chapter's creatures are marked in that chapter's colour. Almost everything has its own 3D model, sounds, attacks and death, its own drop, and a spawn egg in the Static Hollow creative tab. Since 1.48.0 nearly all of them can also be taken over by the parasite and turned into something else: see the Turned . The twenty creatures of chapters one to three that have heads (the nine creepypastas, the nine killers and cryptids, the Gardener and the Rootlings) drop theirs the first time you kill each, then at 10% plus 5% a level of Looting. The Hollow Saint has no head to drop."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter one: the Nine","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-one","t":"They hunt everyone once the Forsaken Altar is awake, mostly in the dark. All nine are dragged back down when the Breach Altar wakes."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"??? (the Watcher)","u":"entities/index.html#the-watcher-entry","t":"Never attacks Stares, waves, points, peeks, and sometimes stands right behind you. It speaks at every turning point in the story."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hollow Saint","u":"entities/index.html#hollow-saint-entry","t":"Boss of chapter one What the nine were all pieces of. Raised at the cathedral's reliquary with one head from each."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Hollow Neighbor","u":"entities/index.html#hollow-neighbor","t":"Hostile to players only Stalks you, vanishes and reappears behind you, knocks on doors and whispers. Every few minutes it sends you a chat message pretending to be a friend, and if you're indoors near a window it rises up behind the glass, taps on it and says it to your face. Its pinprick pupils follow you, even on its placed head. Attacks: The Long Neck (its neck stretches across the gap and its mouth drags you in) and Turn Around (it's gone in a puff of smoke and its hands are on your shoulders from behind)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Stitchjaw","u":"entities/index.html#stitchjaw","t":"Hostile to everything Crawls flat like a lizard and climbs walls. Every bite that lands opens the wound further: Bleeding I, II, III. Attacks: Death Roll (jaws locked on you, rolling like a crocodile) and Seam Burst (every stitch tears at once in a ring of thread, bone and blood)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Weeping Shepherd","u":"entities/index.html#weeping-shepherd","t":"Neutral, fights back Weeps, and stares if you stare. Hunts the undead. A rusted bell tolls as it walks. Attacks: The Toll (three rings of pale light along the ground that burn the undead) and The Crook (a crack of pale fire torn along the ground)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Lullaby Mother","u":"entities/index.html#lullaby-mother","t":"Neutral by day, hostile at night Steals villagers and whispers a broken lullaby. Her hits can drag you into the Hollow, a sealed black room under the world, for 15 seconds. When she dies she draws a kitchen knife and drives it into her own eye. Attacks: Hush Now (she rocks you like a baby while the life runs out of you; hurt her to make her drop you) and The Knife (five stabs, fast)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Broadcast","u":"entities/index.html#broadcast","t":"Hostile to players A man with an old CRT television for a head, its screen crawling with live static. It skips toward you like a dropped video frame. Don't look at it : staring at the screen burns you every second. Don't touch it : it shocks. Its antenna tips glow green once it has seen you, burn red while you look at it, and flash red when it strikes. Attacks: Dead Air (a flickering line pins where it's aiming, then a beam of raw static) and Frame Skip (it drops three frames and is beside you, behind you, in front of you)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Little Lamb","u":"entities/index.html#little-lamb","t":"Neutral until you hit it A crying child that follows you. Hit it and it shows its real face and gets fast. Hunts livestock. Attacks: The Shriek (a cone of scream) and Pounce and Gnaw (it clings to you, chewing)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hymnal","u":"entities/index.html#the-hymnal","t":"Hostile to players and iron golems Floats. Its song slows and weakens you and heals the other creepypastas. At Bleeding III blood wells up along the stitches over its eyes, but it never stops singing. Attacks: The Page Storm (pages with edges like razors) and The Rapture (a chord from a choir that isn't there lifts you off your feet)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Underneath","u":"entities/index.html#the-underneath","t":"Waits Buried with only its hands showing; stand near it too long and it claws its way out. It breathes under your bed and comes up for you when you lie down. Get out of bed within about four seconds. Never in Creative or on Peaceful. Attacks: Hands From Below and Burrow (a ridge of earth tears toward you and it bursts up under your feet)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Antlerkin","u":"entities/index.html#antlerkin","t":"Hunts everything Imitates cows, pigs and sheep to lure prey. Faster in the dark, and fastest at night, when it calls and runs its prey down until dawn with its eyes burning ember to amber in its skull. Attacks: The Charge (let it hit a wall and it stands there dazed) and The Toss . The Antlerkin, close."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Mourners","u":"entities/index.html#mourner","t":"In the cathedral's pews Praying, their heads turning after you. Hurt one, or play the organ, and they all stand up. At nightfall the dead are back in their pews. At the Soul Well they kneel round the altar as its keepers."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Interred","u":"entities/index.html#interred","t":"In the undercroft's tombs Open a sarcophagus and what was buried in it might be the Interred, who sits up and climbs out. The sealed ones open by themselves when you come close. The Lullaby Mother, the Broadcast, the Underneath, the Hollow Neighbor, the Watcher and the Antlerkin have no blood left to lose and never bleed."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter two: the killers and the things from the woods","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-two","t":"Five killers and four cryptids come up once the Breach Altar is awake. They stalk first and only come for you once they've watched long enough, or you hit them."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Mended","u":"entities/index.html#the-mended-entry","t":"Boss of chapter two, 750 health All nine sewn into one thing by the Watcher at the Mending Altar."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Bunnyman","u":"entities/index.html#the-bunnyman","t":"Killer, in the dark, near water A tall man in a filthy rabbit suit with a fire axe. Catch him watching and he stops dead, tilts his head and waves. When he comes, it's a crouch and a spring with the axe coming down as he lands. Chops through wooden doors on Normal and Hard. Throws a hatchet, and goes into a frenzy of chops when badly hurt."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hookman","u":"entities/index.html#the-hookman","t":"Killer A starved giant in a torn straitjacket, gauze round his head, a rusted meat hook for a hand. He flings the hook on a chain, catches you and reels you in, and pulls riders off horses, boats and carts. Every cut bleeds. He also sweeps the hook low and impales you on it."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hogshead","u":"entities/index.html#the-hogshead","t":"Killer, 90 health, armoured A butcher the size of a doorway in a rotting pig's head. He squeals, lowers his head and charges; if he reaches you he takes you by the throat. Sidestep and he slams into the wall, stunned: hit him then. Also slams the ground and gores."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Porcelain Man","u":"entities/index.html#the-porcelain-man","t":"Killer, indoors A life-size porcelain doll in a tailcoat. While anyone is looking at him he doesn't move, only his glass eyes; look away and he's closer, in a different pose. He opens doors. He can only be hurt from behind. His music box slows and blinds whoever isn't looking at him."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Harvestman","u":"entities/index.html#the-harvestman","t":"Killer, plains and savannas at night A scarecrow on a post in a field, a crow on its shoulder. Walk close and it climbs down at you. Look away for long and the post is empty. Its scythe sweeps wide: get out of the arc. It calls its crows down and tears roots up out of the ground. Killed, it falls apart into straw and the crow flies off. The Harvestman, down off its post."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Mothman","u":"entities/index.html#mothman","t":"Cryptid, under the night sky Red eyes in the night sky. It circles high and hangs still when you look up at it. Then it screeches (darkness at the edge of your sight, legs heavy), dives claws-first, and sometimes takes you up and lets go. Most of all by rivers and on boats. Bring a bow. Mothman, hanging still in the fog."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Jersey Devil","u":"entities/index.html#the-jersey-devil","t":"Cryptid, pine forests at night Goat legs, bat wings, a horse's skull on a long neck. It screams when it starts hunting (weakness, nausea), springs into the air and glides down onto you; up close it rears and kicks. Breathes fire and sweeps you with its tail."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Dogman","u":"entities/index.html#dogman","t":"Cryptid, forests and taiga at night A wolf that walks like a man. It runs on all fours, faster than you, stands up to howl (it roots you to the spot), pounces and mauls: claw, claw, then a bite that bleeds. It drags you down by the leg and flings you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Flatwoods Monster","u":"entities/index.html#the-flatwoods-monster","t":"Cryptid, hills and woods in the dark A tall shape in a spade-shaped hood with a glowing red face. It glides, never hurrying, leaving a burning mist. Stare into its face too long and you're sick and slow. Up close it breathes the mist at you; its claws poison. The Flatwoods Monster in a village."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Out in the Void","u":"entities/index.html#out-in-the-void","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hand","u":"entities/index.html#the-hand","t":"Catches what falls Pale grey going violet, bigger than a man, on an arm going down and down into the dark. It catches anyone who falls off an island and sets them back down. It hurts."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Driftlight","u":"entities/index.html#driftlight","t":"Harmless A bell of pale flesh the size of a lantern, lit from inside, swimming like a jellyfish. It drops Drift Jelly: Slow Falling for 40 seconds and sight in the dark for 20."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Lamprey","u":"entities/index.html#lamprey","t":"Hostile A long eyeless eel with a glowing lure. It coils, flares six toothed lips and comes at you straight as a whip, then fastens on and drags you out over the dark. Hit it hard to make it let go. Drops Lamprey Teeth and sometimes its lure, still lit."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter three: the glasshouse","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-three","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Gardener","u":"entities/index.html#the-gardener-entry","t":"Boss of chapter three The Head Gardener, grown into by the flower he tended."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Rootling","u":"entities/index.html#rootling","t":"The Gardener's children Knee-high things with a pale bulb for a head, red pinprick eyes and a grin of thorns. They chatter, leap at you and burrow away to come up somewhere else. They drop Knotted Roots, which make the Gardener's Weeds."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Great Flower","u":"entities/index.html#the-great-flower","t":"Under the dome A parasitic bloom the size of a room, its tendrils feeling about. Get close and it latches on: you're Sapromyiophilous , carrion flies swarm you, and it feeds. Its tendril drags things in and swallows them whole. Three good hits tear its tendril and free you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Giant Flytrap","u":"entities/index.html#giant-flytrap","t":"In the garden beds A Venus flytrap that snatches you up and chews. Mash E to force the jaws open."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Great Bloom","u":"entities/index.html#the-great-bloom-entry","t":"What the flower really is Far down under the islands of the Bloom, and later risen through the glasshouse."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Tentacle of the Great Bloom","u":"entities/index.html#tentacles-entry","t":"The giant tentacles Eight of them round its mouth, thick as trees, or towers."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter four: the Flesh","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-four","t":"Every one of the Flesh's infected has a split jaw that swings apart sideways, glowing veins, no nose, three sinews out of its back and a blister bursting out of one shoulder. They shamble until they hunt, then sprint with their arms flailing. They hear you running. Their hits get the Flesh into you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Bosses and mini-bosses","u":"entities/index.html#bosses-of-the-flesh","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Congregation","u":"entities/index.html#the-congregation","t":"Mini-boss, 400 health, Rosemont The commuters on the crashed bus, fused into one thing that wears the bus as a shell, their legs under it for wheels, their faces in every window. It sleeps until something hits it. Bus Ram : its headlights flash twice and it charges; if it ends against a wall it's stuck for three seconds and the driver takes three times the damage. Window Hands grab you at its sides. Choir : every mouth screams and three of them climb out."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Specimen Zero","u":"entities/index.html#specimen-zero","t":"Mini-boss, 350 health, the Laboratory The Flesh's first host, the night technician who cut a sample from the root's end, grown for weeks against the Reactor Core: arms far too long, a second mouth in his chest with his ribs for teeth. Tendril Lash , Pool Surge and Absorb (it eats the staff's bodies to heal 25 each; burn them first). At half health it tears itself off the pool floor and hangs from the ceiling. Fire and Flower Ash Bombs burn it twice as hard."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","u":"entities/index.html#warden-entry","t":"Boss, 400 health, Bunker B The shelter's Civil Defence warden and everyone who sheltered with him, grown into one mass on four legs."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Squad Leader","u":"entities/index.html#squad-leader","t":"Mini-boss, 120 health, Bunker B Its whistle sends the operators round your flanks; it fires five-round bursts and throws a flashbang every fifteen seconds. At half health it splits open and the Spine-Runner comes out (70 health): a skinless thing on all fours with a bladed tail."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Gardener, Reborn","u":"entities/index.html#reborn-entry","t":"Boss, 600 health, then Reborn Again What was left of the Gardener, grown back together by the Bloom."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Broodmother","u":"entities/index.html#broodmother","t":"Nest boss, 340 health The Flesh's own great flower: five petals of raw muscle round a womb, and what's left of a woman. She never moves, but gives birth (Crawlers, sometimes a Stalker), lets out Flesh Flies, slams a petal down and spits bile. At half health every sac in the nest bursts at once. She hates the flowers: the Bloomshears cut her half again as hard, and a Flower Ash Bomb burns her two and a half times as badly. Drops her heart, the Brood Heart."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Bellwether","u":"entities/index.html#bellwether","t":"Leads the horde, 70 health, armoured A Civil Defence warden in a long navy greatcoat, the gas mask grown into its face, four brass bells on a yoke of bone. It walks at the head of its horde ringing its handbell. Seeing you, it whirls its gas rattle and the horde charges. Kill it and the horde loses its way. Drops the Bellwether's Bell."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The infected","u":"entities/index.html#the-infected","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected","u":"entities/index.html#infected","t":"The town's people A shopper, an office worker, an old man in a cardigan, a road worker, a villager, in the clothes they died in. Villagers, zombies and witches the Flesh takes get up as these."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Police","u":"entities/index.html#infected-police","t":"Still armed Fires its pistol at you, arm out, head cocked over. With TaCZ installed the police carry the Mended SMG."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Soldier","u":"entities/index.html#infected-soldier","t":"Holding Rosemont Machete flurry up close; a screaming charge from further off. Becomes a Splitter."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Firefighter","u":"entities/index.html#infected-firefighter","t":"Fire won't touch it Drags its axe and brings it down two-handed. Hit its air tank three times and it hisses, then goes up two seconds later."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Paramedic","u":"entities/index.html#infected-paramedic","t":"Kill it first Every infected within six blocks of it heals. Up close it slams the defibrillator paddles on you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Pharmacist","u":"entities/index.html#infected-pharmacist","t":"Keeps its distance Throws syringes (poison and the Flesh) and bottles of pills (your stomach turns). Drops them too."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Construction Worker","u":"entities/index.html#infected-construction-worker","t":"Nail gun and sledgehammer Fires four nails from a distance; close in, heaves the sledgehammer overhead."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Officer","u":"entities/index.html#infected-officer","t":"Calls for backup Fights like the soldiers, and every thirty seconds holds its radio to its split ear and calls in two to four more."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Heavy","u":"entities/index.html#infected-heavy","t":"Nothing knocks it back A soldier the Flesh grew huge, with a cleaver as long as a man: an overhead blow (10) or a sweep to both sides (6)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Researcher","u":"entities/index.html#infected-researcher","t":"The Laboratory Comes in fast with its syringe, then scuttles back out of reach on all fours. Sometimes carries a Level 2 Keycard or a later tape."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Hazmat Trooper","u":"entities/index.html#infected-hazmat-trooper","t":"The Laboratory Its suit still on, fire won't touch it, and its flamer burns a cone in front of it."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Spitter","u":"entities/index.html#spitter","t":"Keeps its distance Its throat swollen into a sac of bile. The bile bursts into a puddle that burns, slows you and infects you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Shelter Resident","u":"entities/index.html#shelter-resident","t":"Shelter No. 4 In pyjamas, a tracksuit, a blanket round them, hiding in bunks and lockers, sobbing. Get within three blocks, hit one or open its locker and it bursts out."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Civil Defence Warden","u":"entities/index.html#civil-defence-warden","t":"Shelter No. 4 White W helmet. Blows its whistle and every infected within 16 blocks comes running, faster."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Operator","u":"entities/index.html#infected-operator","t":"Special forces, 40 health Flanks you, climbs walls, fires four-round bursts, throws flashbangs, slides in under you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Sniper","u":"entities/index.html#infected-sniper","t":"Special forces, 28 health Its laser finds you first with a climbing tone; a second and a half later, the shot (12). Break its line of sight."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected Breacher","u":"entities/index.html#infected-breacher","t":"Special forces, 45 health, armoured A riot shield grown onto its arm blocks everything from the front. Get round it, or hit it with an axe and the shield drops for five seconds."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Infected You","u":"entities/index.html#infected-you","t":"If you die of the Flesh What gets up where you fell is you, as one of the infected, with your skin, your armour, your weapon and everything you were carrying. It comes for you first. Kill it and you get it all back. It never despawns."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"What the infected become","u":"entities/index.html#mutants","t":"Left alive on the Flesh's ground for ten minutes (five on the thickest of it), one of the infected changes. What it becomes depends on what it was."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Stalker","u":"entities/index.html#stalker","t":"From townspeople Starved to skin and rib, on arms and legs twice as long and bent like a spider's. Climbs walls and drops on you; pounces from up to nine blocks. Drops a Stalker Talon."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Bloater","u":"entities/index.html#bloater","t":"From townspeople and workers Swollen wider than it is tall. Close enough, it swells and bursts, and a cloud of red gas hangs there for six seconds. Drops a Bloater Gland."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Screamer","u":"entities/index.html#screamer","t":"From police and CD wardens Its face opens four ways like a flower. Its call brings every infected within sixty-four blocks. Drops a Screamer Sac."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Brute","u":"entities/index.html#brute","t":"From firefighters and heavies, 140 health Three blocks of muscle. Smashes both fists into the ground and throws you ten blocks. Drops a Brute Knuckle."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Splitter","u":"entities/index.html#splitter","t":"From soldiers Split from throat to belt; its chest swings open like a mouth. Killed, it comes apart into three Crawlers (unless it burnt). Drops Splitter Sinew."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Hive","u":"entities/index.html#hive","t":"From paramedics Bent under a hump of lidded cells that let out Flesh Flies , a dozen at a time, each bite infecting you. Drops Hive Comb. Pharmacists and researchers become Spitters; the special forces' operators become Spine-Runners."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"After the Bloom changes","u":"entities/index.html#after-the-bloom-changes","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Changed Bloom","u":"entities/index.html#changed-bloom-entry","t":"Only the Omni ends it Ten times bigger, blue, and hungry."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Parasite and Parasite Host","u":"entities/index.html#parasite-entry","t":"From Blackwater Station Six legs and a mouth that opens like a flower. It goes for the back of the neck."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Omni","u":"entities/index.html#omni-entry","t":"The gun, and SENTINEL Listed here at the wiki owner's request; in the mod it's a weapon."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter five: the static","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-five","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Static Hound","u":"entities/index.html#static-hound","t":"Packs, at night What the parasites made of the wolves. Packs of three to five behind a Pack Leader with a brood sac on its back. The leader howls and the pack gets faster and fiercer; the rest flank you. Kill the leader and the pack breaks."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hollowed","u":"entities/index.html#the-hollowed","t":"One in every village A villager with violet pinprick eyes, muttering static. At night, alone with you, it turns: taller, arms to its knees, its head split open in four. It shrieks, rakes, grabs, and sometimes puts one in you."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Amalgam","u":"entities/index.html#amalgam-entry","t":"Boss, at Relay 6 Everyone who came to the relay, grown together into one heap at the mast's foot."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Afterimage","u":"entities/index.html#afterimage","t":"At the Starlite Drive-In Grey figures made of scan lines and static, see-through, their faces only dark gaps. They drift through cars and walls. You can't hurt one unless you're Tuned In, it's reaching for you, or the last reel is running. They can't leave the Null. Killed, one leaves a Frame of the Last Reel."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Carrier","u":"entities/index.html#carrier-entry","t":"Boss of part four What carried them all, in the crater in the middle of the Null Static Zone."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The outbreak","u":"entities/index.html#the-outbreak","t":"From 1.48.0, anything the parasite gets into is slowly taken over, and turns. After Signing Off it gets worse."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The turned","u":"entities/index.html#turned-entry","t":"Anything at all, two or three days on Ruined, writhing versions of what they were, a mouth of five petals split open in their chests, hunting everything that isn't theirs. Thirty-two of the Hollow's own have a turned form of their own, from the Saint Unmade to the Pod, Hatched."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The infested bosses","u":"entities/index.html#infested-bosses-entry","t":"Golems, the Warden, ravagers and more The game's bosses and mini-bosses, gone wrong, each with new moves and a bar of its own. Since 1.61.1 the Ender Dragon is always one of them."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The parasite's kinds","u":"entities/index.html#parasite-kinds-entry","t":"Born of where they were The Tide Parasite (in the water), the Burrowing Parasite (deep in the stone), the Winged Parasite (out of anything with wings), the Ember Parasite (the Nether) and the Void Parasite (the End)."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Biomass and the pure forms","u":"entities/index.html#biomass-entry","t":"What's left of the turned A heap of violet flesh where one of the turned fell, that gets up a minute or two later as a Stalker Form , a Ranged Form , a Tank Form or a Brood Sack . They change from one to another to suit the fight. Burn the heap and nothing gets up."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hive and the Deep","u":"entities/index.html#the-hive-and-the-deep","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Chorus","u":"entities/index.html#chorus-entry","t":"Boss of part five, 900 health The mind the parasite grew for itself in the Hive's pit, out of everything it took: a mound of bodies, a great head with a split maw, and the faces of all of them speaking with one voice."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Hive Hand","u":"entities/index.html#hive-hand","t":"Seven round the Hive's pit, 140 health An arm as tall as a tree, braided chitin round a core of flesh, a palm with eyes and a mouth in it and three hooked fingers. It slams its claw down where the ground lights up, sweeps you aside, or grabs you, lifts you high, squeezes and throws you. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Reach","u":"entities/index.html#the-reach","t":"Every few nights, at your home While the Chorus lives down in the Deep, one of its hands tears up out of the ground where you live, half again as big as the hive's, its things climbing out after it. Kill it, or it sinks back after four minutes. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Listener","u":"entities/index.html#the-listener","t":"The Deep's older ones, 60 health Tall, starved, cave-white, on long dog's legs, with no eyes: only fans of skin either side of its head. It hears every step, every block, every door, and goes to the sound fast. Sneak. Its ears make Hushed Boots. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Deaf King","u":"entities/index.html#deaf-king-entry","t":"Boss in the Deep, 420 health The oldest thing in the Deep, a hulk on its knuckles with plugs of stone in its ears. It feels you through the floor. Stand still and you aren't there."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Chorus, Whole","u":"entities/index.html#chorus-whole-entry","t":"Final boss of chapter five, 1024 health The Chorus made again in the Warm Heart, up out of a lake of blood. It dies, really this time, and leaves the Last Voice."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter six: the Door at the End of the World","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-six","t":"Past the Door, the Stalls; behind the screen, the Watcher's Vault; and past the stage on the other side, what he kept out."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Audience","u":"entities/index.html#audience","t":"The Stalls' seats, 16 health Grey people in grey clothes, faces up to the screen, a ticket in their laps. They hear you, get up with a finger to their lips, and hold you where you are. Sneak. Some carry a Ticket Stub. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Usher","u":"entities/index.html#usher","t":"Walks the aisles, 44 health Tall, faceless, in maroon and brass, swinging a lamp over the rows. If its light finds you, the SHHH goes through the house. Show it a Ticket Stub and it looks away. Often drops its lamp. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Crowd","u":"entities/index.html#crowd-entry","t":"Boss of part one, 800 health The whole house gone into each other at the front, under the screen. Its Hush: stand still."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Tuned","u":"entities/index.html#the-tuned","t":"The Vault's stacks, 24 health People from the neck down, an old television set for a head. They only move while you're looking at them. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Projectionist","u":"entities/index.html#projectionist-entry","t":"Boss of part two, 900 health A coat of film and a cinema projector for a head. It came into the Vault behind you, for what he kept."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Rerun","u":"entities/index.html#rerun","t":"The Projectionist's An old boss projected onto the air, grey and flickering, doing again the one thing everyone remembers: the Saint's beam, the Gardener's thorns, the Deaf King's fists, the Carrier's beam."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Viewer","u":"entities/index.html#viewer-entry","t":"The last boss, can't be killed What he kept out: sat in the dark past the stage, so big you only ever fight its eye and its hands."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Stand-In","u":"entities/index.html#stand-in","t":"The Other Side, 10 health A painted plywood cut-out of a person that hops out of the wings. It doesn't hurt you; it points, and the eye comes. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter seven: the First Signal","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-seven","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The First Signal","u":"entities/index.html#first-signal-entry","t":"Not fought yet Your shape, your size, its skin crawling static, a white mask. It was here before the Watcher, before the first picture. It came through a rift into his Hub and said one word."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Chapter eight: the Dead Water","u":"entities/index.html#chapter-eight","t":"Everything in the Dead Water's twelve waters swims like something that lives in water: speeding up and slowing, banking into turns, schooling, keeping to its depth, bolting when startled. Small things are eaten by bigger things. Since 1.63.2 they get hungry and go looking for food, a wound in the water draws the hunters, a school balls up tight when a hunter's near, and a still diver draws the curious ones in to circle and look. Out of the water they flop, gasp and die. Where each one lives is from the mod's own lists of each water."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The gentle ones","u":"entities/index.html#the-gentle-ones","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Pipeye","u":"entities/index.html#pipeye","t":"3 health A thumb-sized ball of a man's eye in a cup of flesh, lidded with shells that swing down over it. Little schools come and look at you, all the eyes turning together, and dart off if you move at them. The Grey Shelf, the Haemal Reach, the Wireweed, the Ossuary Flats, the Drowned Mycelia, the Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Lanternlet","u":"entities/index.html#lanternlet","t":"2 health A deep, thin lanternfish, big-eyed, two rows of lights down each flank. Big glowing shoals that ball up tight and turn when something hunts near. The Grey Shelf, the Wireweed, the Lantern Fields, the Molar Reef, the Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Hum Skate","u":"entities/index.html#hum-skate","t":"8 health A little spotted ray near the floor, in pairs, its smiling face underneath and a barbed whip of a tail. It hums one low note. The Grey Shelf, the Wireweed, the Ossuary Flats, the Ember Vents, the Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Puffbloat","u":"entities/index.html#puffbloat","t":"6 health Round, blotched, green-eyed. Frighten it and it swells into a ball of spines; touch it then and they go in. The Haemal Reach, the Brine Sink, the Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Thimble Jelly","u":"entities/index.html#thimble-jelly","t":"2 health A domed bell lit from inside, its canals and pink horseshoes glowing, frilled arms under it. It drifts in blooms, pulsing. Brush its threads and it stings. The Lantern Fields, the Brine Sink, the Drowned Mycelia."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Stiltfin","u":"entities/index.html#stiltfin","t":"6 health Stands on three long fin-rays on the deep floors, facing the current, long feelers sweeping up over its head. Swims off when you come. The Grey Shelf, the Ossuary Flats, the Rime Shelf, the Ember Vents."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Grinner","u":"entities/index.html#grinner","t":"5 health A pretty banded reef fish with human eyes, full lips over a grin of human teeth, and a tall spined sail. Little groups; it chatters and giggles. The Haemal Reach, the Wireweed, the Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Hymnback","u":"entities/index.html#hymnback","t":"220 health A gentle giant: a whale's long head, a hanging lower jaw, fringes of baleen, long knobbed flippers, and a reef of corals, lit anemones and kelp on its back. Its song carries a long way. The Grey Shelf, the Lantern Fields, the Rime Shelf; lost ones wander into the Black Below, where the Undertow eats them."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The hunters","u":"entities/index.html#the-hunters","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Clotfish","u":"entities/index.html#clotfish","t":"6 health Shoals of little blood-dark fish with a fence of crooked needles in their underbite. Quiet until there's blood in the water; then the whole shoal boils at it in a frenzy, biting in turns, and you bleed. The Haemal Reach, the Brine Sink, the Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Choir Eel","u":"entities/index.html#choir-eel","t":"30 health Lies along the floor humming chords out of the mouths down its flanks. Touch it, linger on it or hit it and it coils, lights up and sings a shock through the water round it. The shock kills lights. The Wireweed, the Ember Vents, the Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Hookjaw","u":"entities/index.html#hookjaw","t":"34 health A gaff of a jaw-hook, hooked bones raked down its head, a torn tail. It follows you at the edge of sight, circling and clicking, comes in fast the moment you look away, hooks you and is gone. It steals your metal and keeps it until it's killed. The Grey Shelf, the Wireweed, the Ossuary Flats, the Molar Reef."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Gulper","u":"entities/index.html#gulper","t":"60 health A warty head that's all mouth, a comb of needles round it, lying still on the floor with a light on a stalk over its jaws. Whatever comes close enough it lunges at and swallows (little fish whole). The sea's light-lovers come to its light. The Lantern Fields, the Ossuary Flats, the Drowned Mycelia."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Mantlecrab","u":"entities/index.html#mantlecrab","t":"40 health Jointed spined legs, big claws, a spiked rim to its shell. It hates light: a lamp, a lit submarine, a torch in your hand. Its pulse puts out every light near it (darkness on you, the submarine's power gone), then it comes in with its claws. The Ember Vents, the Carrier Wave."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Frostjaw","u":"entities/index.html#frostjaw","t":"24 health A shark's tail, five gill slits, glass teeth, frost-crazed. Packs on the cold shelf spread out round you, their flank-lights flashing to each other, and come in one at a time from wherever you aren't looking. The Rime Shelf."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Siphon","u":"entities/index.html#siphon","t":"8 health A leech of an eel, a ringed body and a toothed sucker. It fastens on and drinks until you hit it off or get out of the water. The Grey Shelf, the Haemal Reach, the Brine Sink, the Drowned Mycelia."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The eldritch","u":"entities/index.html#the-eldritch","t":""},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Mouth of the Floor","u":"entities/index.html#mouth-of-the-floor-entry","t":"Buried in the floor, 140 health Nothing showing but a ring of rocks. Pass over it and eight jaws open out of the sand round a throat, and the water rushes in, and you with it."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Static Leviathan","u":"entities/index.html#static-leviathan","t":"Boss, 320 health Deep down in the Dead Water, now and then one comes up out of the dark after you. It sings on the Remote's frequency, and its Signal Organ mends the Remote. More ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Undertow","u":"entities/index.html#undertow-entry","t":"The Black Below; nothing hurts it Three thousand blocks long. It stalks you, learns you, and eats when it's hungry. The only way to live is to leave the Black Below."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The deep oceans","u":"entities/index.html#the-deep-oceans","t":"Since 1.62.0 the Overworld's oceans fall away past the shelf to about 2,000 blocks deep, in three depths: the Sunless Drop, the Hadal Dark and the Trench (see the Hollow's own country ). Three things live down there. Two of them, the Needlemaw and the Static Leviathan, turn up in the Dead Water too."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Shroud Ray","u":"entities/index.html#shroud-ray","t":"The Sunless Drop and the Hadal Dark, 40 health A ray as wide as a cart is long, pale as a burial sheet, the face its gills and mouth make on its underside, a fringe of pale blue lights round its wings. It glides on slow beats and lets you be, until you hurt it. Then it comes in fast and low and comes down over you like a sheet: its wings fold round you, everything goes dark, and it beats down and down, taking you with it, the cold biting. Hit it hard enough and it lets go. Drops Shroud Hide."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Needlemaw","u":"entities/index.html#needlemaw","t":"All three depths, 18 health A fish the length of a man's arm and leg, nearly all head: a jaw lined with glass needles too long to close over, six pin-eyes on its brow. It hangs dark and still. When you come near, all its lights come on at once: it backs off with its jaw dropping open, darts in, bites (you bleed), recoils and comes round again. In the Dead Water it's in the Grey Shelf and the Ember Vents too. Drops 1 to 3 Needle Teeth."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"The Static Leviathan","u":"entities/index.html#static-leviathan-deep","t":"The Hadal Dark and the Trench Its home water. See its case file ."},{"p":"Bestiary","h":"Minecraft's own creatures","u":"entities/index.html#minecrafts-own-creatures","t":"Every vanilla animal and monster is redrawn as a jointed 3D model with its own animations, bleeding (or sparking, or shedding goo, splinters, ash or spores) when hit and dying its own way. By night, if you look at one, it stops what it's doing and looks back at you, its eyes shining. A few highlights: The Enderman is one of the Hollow's own: far too tall and thin, a too-wide grin of needle teeth. Look at it and it freezes, cocks its head and trembles; anger it and its jaw unhinges into a scream. It whispers backwards. The Warden claws its way out of the ground, and its real heart beats half out of its chest, faster as it gets angrier. The creeper swells and flickers before it bursts; charged ones crackle with static. Spiders walk on eight legs and rear up at you. Slimes are see-through jelly with things floating in them. The Ender Dragon has torn wings with real finger bones and a ridge of bone plates down its back. Since 1.61.1 it's always the Infested Ender Dragon ."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html","t":"Relay 6, Hollow Ridge, at the mast's foot Boss Who it was D. Ostrander, the relay's operator; Gus, his dog; and nine people from the valley Health 300 Held by Three tethers on the mast's platforms at 12, 22 and 32 Added in 1.45.0, Chapter Five part two Drops The Relay Core. Its brood sac bursts when it dies, unless it burnt."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#description","t":"Everyone who came to the relay, the operator, his dog, and the people from the valley who walked up the hill after dark to stand round the mast, grown together into one heap at its foot. Six limbs that don't match. Three heads on long necks: his, in his hard hat and headset; a villager's, split open in four; and the dog's, its muzzle peeled back. A brood sac on its back with three cables of sinew running up the mast to the tethers."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"Relay 6 - Operator's Log","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#relay-6-operators-log","t":"D. Ostrander, Hollow Ridge Found: the transmitter hut Fri. People from the valley came up the road after dark. Nine of them. They didn't knock. They stood round the mast with their faces up, like they were listening to it. They didn't blink at the floodlight. Sun. They've started climbing it. Tying something to it. It isn't rope. If you find this and it's still on the air - it isn't us. Cut it loose. All of it. Excerpt. The whole log is on the lore page."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#how-it-fights","t":"Slam: it rears up and comes down. Stand back. Grab: a head lashes out and drags you in, and the other two chew. Hit it hard to make it let go. Scream: three voices at once and the static under them. You can't see for a while, and every hound near comes. Brood: it spits brood out of its sac. Draw: it draws on the relay through its cables. They pull taut and pulse, and it heals. Hurt it hard while it does and it breaks off. While a tether holds, it can't go further from the mast than its cables reach. Get out of their reach and it lets you go. At half health the dog tears itself out of its side, and the rest of it comes on faster."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"Cut the tethers","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#cut-the-tethers","t":"Climb the ladder up the mast's south face and break the knot of sinew on each rest platform. Each one cut, it flinches. Cut the last one and it reels (\"The last cable snaps. It reels - cut off from the relay.\"), and from then on every blow hurts it more. Cutting the last tether while it still lives earns Cut the Cord ."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Cut the tethers first. Its draw heals it as long as it's connected. Stay out of its cables' reach when you need a breather. Bring something for the hound packs. While the relay's on the air they come twice as often within 700 blocks, and its scream calls them. Bring a Surgical Kit. The operator's locker has one, and its brood can put one in you."},{"p":"The Amalgam","h":"Off the air","u":"entities/the-amalgam.html#off-the-air","t":"Killed, its sac bursts and the relay goes off the air (\"The relay goes quiet. For the first time in days, there's nothing on the air.\"). The tethers wither, the hounds near it lose the signal and run, and from then on packs come less often everywhere. This earns Off the Air . It leaves the Relay Core . Keep it. It tunes the projector at the Starlite Drive-In, and it's how you hurt Afterimages."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"","u":"entities/the-bloom.html","t":"The great flower, all the way down Colossal Forms The Great Flower (under the dome), the Great Bloom (in its realm and risen), the changed Bloom First seen Chapter three Reach About 26 blocks risen; 90 once changed, and growing Ends Only the Omni (since 1.43.0) Made The Flesh, from the rot its carrion flies carry The Great Bloom Its tentacles over the Flesh, the reactor parts tracker at 1 of 3."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"The great flower","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-great-flower","t":"It opened one night under the glasshouse dome. Nobody planted it. Head Gardener E. Thorne wrote that it was warm, with a beat in its stalk like a sleeper's. He told the Rosemont Courier it was a Rafflesia, \"though not one I know\". It's the size of a room, its tendrils feeling about, and anything they drag in is lifted, wrapped and swallowed. Get close and it latches on and you're Sapromyiophilous : carrion flies swarm you, you rot and hunger, and it feeds. Only the Gardener's Weeds keep the flies off: \"the great flower knows these clothes\". The bud was only a finger. Dr. Marsh's research log: \"Its root goes down through the rotunda's floor and keeps going. We let down a line four hundred feet. It kept going.\""},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"The Great Bloom","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-great-bloom","t":"Far down under the islands of the Bloom is the real great flower. Five great warted petals, red going black with the rot coming up green through them, and where the bud had its heart, a mouth: a lip of flesh and a throat ringed with rings of hooked teeth that turn against each other as it chews, a sick light far down in it. Its mouth is wider than all the islands together (since 1.27.2 it's ten times the size it was, every way), and its petals reach out further than you can see. Round the mouth rise eight tentacles , each as wide as a hill at the root, curling over far above you. Fall and one comes straight up out of its throat after you. It is horrible to be near. Out in its realm the edges of your sight go green-black and veined, the veins pulsing with its heart; something whispers just behind you, wherever you turn; now and then, for a blink, you see its mouth. Its throat has faces in it, pressed out through the flesh, mouths open. It drools. It chews. It calls, something vast with more voices in it than there should be, and now and then it speaks."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"The risen Bloom","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-risen-bloom","t":"Break the Binding and it comes up the root, through the glasshouse, and takes the gardens' place for good. This one is the size the first was, not the colossal one below. Its tentacles reach for anything that comes within about 26 blocks (players first), and its flies infect anyone near it without the Gardener's clothes. It clears everything under the reach of its petals and turns the ground under them to its flesh. Its mouth is open: a pit down its throat lined with its flesh, and at the bottom a pool of yellow-green acid, scummed over, beating with its heart. Ten seconds after it rises, the Flesh wakes."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"Swallowed alive","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-stomach","t":"Since 1.38, people it eats don't die in its teeth. They go down its throat alive and land in its stomach : a chamber of wet red folds lit from inside, with a knee-deep pool of green acid that eats at you and your armour. Round the pool lie what's left of the ones it ate before you; dig through each pile once for their things. The throat overhead is shut, and nothing opens it. Swallowed alive. The way out: hack at its stomach wall. It heals over at once, but it feels every cut and heaves. Cut it ten times (the bar at the bottom of your screen) and it retches you, and anyone in there with you, back up onto the ground well away from it. Stay down there and it digests you (\"was digested alive\"). you're alive. you're in it. it's digesting you. cut at the walls. hurt it enough and it'll throw you back up. ??? in the stomach"},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"The changed Bloom","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-changed-bloom","t":"The Rosemont Device going off inside it was never going to kill it. The Watcher needed it to change. The changed Bloom is ten times bigger. Its flesh has gone blue, its acid purple, its teeth green, and it sits in a pit it tears out of the ground, its petals standing up off the ground like a flower's, their tips seventy-odd blocks up. It reaches for anything within ninety blocks. Its roar goes all the way round the world, heard from anywhere, late and echoing the further off you are. Near it, its violet light creeps in at the edges of your sight."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"The blight","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#the-blight","t":"Over three days its blight grows out from it, up to two thousand blocks every way: blue flesh where the grass was, blisters of its acid (they burst, burning and poisoning), its green teeth up out of the ground (they cut whatever pushes through), blue tissue where the leaves were, a violet haze off all of it, the ground breathing."},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"It is hungry","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#it-is-hungry","t":"Since 1.42 everything it gets down its throat makes it bigger: an animal a little, a villager more, one of you a lot, up to three times the size it changed to, its mouth three hundred blocks across and its petals out past six hundred, filling the sky. Fed, it chews, its heart slow. Hungry, it reaches twice as often and comes up out of the ground under anyone out on its petals. Starving (six minutes without), all of that faster, its mouth hanging open, drool pouring off its lip. Close to its mouth you can hear the ones it ate, still in there, muffled, pleading. it's growing. everything it eats, it gets bigger. twice the size it was. don't let it eat. stay off its petals. it's filling the sky. use the gun while there's still something to aim at. that's as big as it gets. it's still hungry. ??? as it grows"},{"p":"The Bloom","h":"How it dies","u":"entities/the-bloom.html#how-it-dies","t":"Only the Orbital Railgun's strikes can hurt it, and since 1.43.0 it heals as fast as you tear it. Only the Omni ends it. Stand fifty blocks or more off its mouth and fire the Omni at it. SENTINEL comes down out of orbit and fires into its mouth; the Bloom fires its own beam back, every colour gone wrong. If it has eaten too much, the Watcher gives the station all of its power. What's left is a husk. Its mouth, teeth, throat and tentacles are gone, vaporized, and its petals lie round the hole, scorched, slowly going brown like any dead flower's. The blight dies back. So does the Flesh, everywhere except the places it built itself into."},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"","u":"entities/the-carrier.html","t":"The Null Static Zone, the crater Final boss Size A head the size of a house Health 500 Held by Four threads, knotted on top of four black spires round the crater's rim Added in 1.47.0, Chapter Five part four Drops 6 to 10 Carrier Threads, some of its flesh, and the music disc Signing Off. The Watcher takes its eye."},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#description","t":"What the last reel showed: the thing under all of it. In the crater in the middle of the Null Static Zone, a head the size of a house, with one eye in it, on a neck up out of a coil of its own pale body. Its threads go up off the coil into the dark, one to every mast you ever saw. Four of them run to the four black spires round the crater's rim and are tied off in a knot on top of each. Its voice is every voice it ever carried, mumbling at once, deep, heard right across the crater. When you hold the Last Reel up to the light, its last frame shows it: \"something vast, curled under the ground. An eye, opening.\""},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#how-it-fights","t":"Slam: it rears and comes down, and a ring of static rolls out across the floor. Jump it. Below half health it sends two. Gaze: its eye opens and a beam of dead air sweeps across the crater. Brood: Afterimages come up out of the floor and Parasites out of its coil. Draw: it draws through its threads to heal. Hit it hard enough while it does and it breaks off. Swallow: it breathes in, dragging everything across the floor to under its mouth, and bites. While a thread holds, it shrugs off most of every blow. When its eye is open (gazing, screaming or swallowing) it takes them in full."},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"Cut it loose","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#cut-it-loose","t":"Each spire has a ladder up its outer side. Climb up and break the knot; it screams for each one (\"A thread snaps - it screams.\"). Break all four and it's cut loose: furious (\"it's never been so angry\"), and far easier to hurt. Cutting the last thread earns Cut Loose ."},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"You're Nulled the whole time in the Zone, so you go hungry faster. Bring food. Hit it hardest while its eye is open. Jump the rings of static. Below half health there are two. When it breathes in, get away from the middle. A Hush is somewhere safe to retreat to: nothing of the static's own can come in, and a parasite on you comes apart at the line. The ruins are 160 blocks or more out from the crater."},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"Signing off","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#signing-off","t":"Kill it and it goes down across its coil, its threads coming down out of the dark one by one. Then the Watcher comes, in a cutscene with its own score, takes its eye, and sends everyone home. it's dead. good. it wasn't theirs, you know. it was a carrier. it carried whatever was put on it. the static was a door. and this was holding it open. this, i'll keep. for the future. go home. there's nothing on the air now. ??? signing off At the Starlite the screen goes black for the first time, and then shows one line: SIGNING OFF. The static is gone everywhere: no more hound packs, and the Hollowed are only villagers again. This earns Signing Off . Scratched into a Hush's bench by the last of the old ones: \"THE GREAT ONE IN THE PIT CARRIES THEM UP ITS THREADS TO EVERY PLACE THAT LISTENS. WHEN IT DIES THEY WILL HAVE NO WAY UP.\""},{"p":"The Carrier","h":"What came of it","u":"entities/the-carrier.html#what-came-of-it","t":"It wasn't over. Half a minute after you're home, the Watcher comes back: \"it seems the carrier did what it was supposed to do. it carried them - all the way out.\" The parasites are everywhere now, and they grow themselves a mind instead: the Chorus . See After Signing Off . What he took from it is in his Vault , behind a round steel door: What's Left of the Carrier , \"A knot of it, still beating. Static comes off it like heat. It carried whatever was put on it. It held a door open.\" Take it and its static pours out, and every Tuned near you is loose for a few seconds. The Projectionist's reruns bring back its beam, down out of nothing onto where you stand. And on the Other Side , at a third left of the fight with the Viewer , the Watcher feeds it through the gate of his last projector: your world, all of it, carried out on the beam onto what he kept out. It gets up."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"","u":"entities/the-chorus.html","t":"The Hive's pit, then the Warm Heart in the Deep Boss, twice Health 900 in its pit; the Chorus, Whole: 1024 Held up by Four nerve nodes on stalks round its pit Added in 1.50.0 (the pit), 1.53.0 (its hands), 1.54.0 (the Deep and the Chorus, Whole) Music The Chorus; then All of Them Leaves In its pit, it doesn't die: it runs, and leaves a Chorus Fragment for each of you there. Whole, it dies and leaves the Last Voice. The Chorus The hive, its hands standing round the pit."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#description","t":"When the Carrier died the parasite lost its voice: the static it heard itself in. So it grew itself a mind instead, out of everything it took. In a pit in the middle of the Hive it comes up out of the floor: a mound of fused bodies with a great head on it, a maw split down the middle of it in four, and all over it the faces of the ones it took, their eyes shut, their mouths moving, all of them speaking at once with one voice. Two arms as long and heavy as tree trunks, ending in hooks, and tendrils up off its back. It knows you. it lost its voice when the carrier died. so it's growing itself a mind instead. out of everything it took. every body. every face. everything any of them ever knew. when it's finished it won't need the static to talk to them. it'll just be all of them. ??? after It Speaks"},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"It Speaks","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#it-speaks","t":"The first night after the Hive has grown, out under the open sky, the ground heaves round you and five of the pure forms stand up out of it, turn to you together, and it speaks through them, all of them at once, its voices out of step: we were many. we were scattered. we heard each other in the noise. you cut the throat that carried us. now there is only quiet. so we are growing another way to be one. out of all of them. out of everything they knew. come and see what we are becoming. come and be heard. The Chorus It Speaks Then they fall, and the Watcher is beside you. He gives you his needle to it. Hearing it earns It Speaks ."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"The Mind","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#the-mind","t":"Go to the edge of its pit and it comes up out of it: you. we know you. you were in the static with us. you were loud. we do not need a throat now. we have a thousand mouths, and all of them are listening. the ones you lost are here with us. they are singing. would you like to hear them? come down. be heard. be one more voice. The Chorus The Mind"},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#how-it-fights","t":"It never leaves its pit. Tendrils: the ground churns, a ring of it lifting and cracking with violet light coming up through it, and a second later a barbed tendril as tall as a house bursts up, flinging whoever was standing there into the air. It lashes at whoever's nearest, then sinks back. Move when the ground churns. Hitting a tendril hurts the Chorus a little. Spores: clouds of them. Birth: pure forms out of its maw. Slam: an arm brought down. Song: three swells, each one worse. It goes through you: you're slow, weak and in the dark a moment. Scream. Draw: it draws through the cords to its nodes to heal."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"The nerve nodes","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#the-nerve-nodes","t":"Round the pit stand four stalks, each with a Nerve Node on top, glowing, a cord running from it to the Chorus with its light running along it. Climb the steps of chitin wound up each stalk and tear the node open. While its nodes live it's thinking clearly, and it shrugs off part of every blow: with all four alive, it takes half. Each node you break, it screams (\"It screams. 3 of its nodes left.\"), its maw wide (a free hit), and it gets easier to hurt. Break all four and everything gets through (\"It screams - and it can't think straight any more. Everything gets through now.\"). That earns Senseless . Fire hurts it half as much again. Leave it alone and it heals: once nobody's near and it hasn't been hurt for half a minute, it mends."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"The Hive Hands","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#the-hive-hands","t":"The black spires of chitin round the pit are alive: seven Hive Hands (140 health at their usual size; each is its own size). Up out of a mound of the hive's flesh, an arm as tall as a tree: three strands of chitin braided round a core of flesh, knots of flesh swollen on it, violet light in its seams, and at the top a palm with eyes and a mouth in it and three long jointed fingers, each ending in a hook. They never stop moving, writhing like something in water and turning to follow you. Come within reach and one will: Slam: it rears back, the ground where it's coming down lights up violet (move), and it brings its claw down on you. Bent right over like a scorpion's tail if you're close, a long reach out over the ground if you're not. Sweep: get in close to its foot and it bends low and swings right across, throwing you aside. Grab: it closes on you, lifts you high over the hive, squeezes, and throws you. Hurt it enough while it has you and it lets go. They can be hurt (fire worse) and killed: it withers, falls forward, curls up and goes down into its mound, and drops Hive Chitin and Hive Flesh. While the Chorus is still in its pit, the hive grows a dead hand back after five minutes."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"It Runs","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#it-runs","t":"Bring it down to a quarter and it won't die. It runs, tearing itself down into the ground, deep: no. no - not yet. we are not finished. The Chorus going down it ran. it can do that now. it's got enough of a mind to be afraid. it's gone down. deep. where everything went before the static was ever a noise. that's a piece of it. it still talks. keep it - listen to it. it'll tell you where it went. it'll come back up. bigger. and next time it won't be half finished. ??? after It Runs It leaves a Chorus Fragment for each of you near. They still talk: hold one to your ear. Driving it down earns It Ran . The fragment leads you to the Sinkhole and down into the Deep ."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"It comes back up","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#it-comes-back-up","t":"Until it's dead, the world up top feels it: tremors under you every so often, the ground giving way near you into pits lined with its flesh with its things climbing out, and flesh blisters swelling up out of the ground (break one before it bursts, or its forms come out)."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"The Reach","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#the-reach","t":"Every few nights, where you live (at your bed if you're near it), three tremors come, closer and closer, and the screen reads IT COMES UP . The ground splits in a ragged line and one of the Chorus's hands tears up out of it, half again as big as the hive's, with waves of its things climbing out of the split after it. It has its own bar and its own music. Kill it and it's done (\"It goes back down without its hand.\"), which earns It Came Up . Leave it and after four minutes it sinks back down."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"The Chorus, Whole","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#the-chorus-whole","t":"Where it went to ground is the Warm Heart : a great round chamber, its floor the hive's flesh running down on every side to a lake of blood, a vault of chitin ribs over it, its four nerve nodes on their stalks round the lake. Come down into it and it rises up out of the blood (\"Up out of the blood it comes - whole again, and every voice in it singing.\"): made again out of everything it took, a second pair of arms out of its sides, the Bloom's roots run all through it, its hands up round the shore with it. It has 1024 health, the most anything can have. It isn't running any more; there's nowhere further down to go. It fights as it did in its pit, harder, in three parts: Its nodes and its hands. The same nodes to tear open, the same hands round the shore. The older ones break in (two thirds down). \"The walls crack open. Something's coming through them: the older ones. They've heard it.\" Listeners come through for it, for its things, and for you. Its song gets worse; carry the Deaf King's ear-stones and its song can't get into you at all. It tears itself up (a third left) out of its lake, tearing out its cords as it goes (\"It tears itself up out of its lake - and its cords tear with it.\"). No nodes any more, nothing to draw on: everything it has, as fast as it can. And then it dies. Really, this time: every voice in it going quiet one after another, and it goes down into the blood. Everything of its in the chamber falls apart (nothing bursts out of them now), and the world above stops feeling it (\"Far below, the singing stops. It doesn't start again.\"). Out of it comes the Last Voice , the one voice it couldn't swallow, thrown up onto the shore. Killing it earns The Last Voice . it's quiet down there now. i can hear you breathing. you've got something of it. one voice it couldn't swallow. keep it. there's a door at the end of the world with a seal on it. i made that seal. i can't open it. that voice can. when you're ready, take it to the end. ??? a while after That's the way into Chapter Six ."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"Its hidden voice","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#its-hidden-voice","t":"Since 1.60.3, now and then, out of all its faces muttering as one, a single voice in the Chorus speaks on its own, fourteen seconds of it, and the rest of them hush while it does (its subtitle: \"The Chorus: one voice out of all of them\"). It comes round again every minute or two while you're near."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Go for the nodes first. With all four up it takes half of everything. Watch the ground. Churning means a tendril; violet light means a hand's claw is coming down. Hit it hardest while its maw is open: while it screams, sings, breathes out spores or gives birth, it takes everything. Bring fire. It, its hands and its pure forms all take more from it. For the Chorus, Whole, kill the Deaf King first and carry his ear-stones."},{"p":"The Chorus","h":"Testing it","u":"entities/the-chorus.html#testing-it","t":"With cheats on: /statichollow ending hivehere (the hive 52 blocks ahead of you), hivespeak , hivemind , hivefight , hivenode , hivedown , hivehands , hiveskip , hivereset ; for the Deep, reach and heart ."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"","u":"entities/the-crowd.html","t":"The Stalls, the front, under the Great Screen Boss Health 800 Made of The whole house: every one of the Audience Added in 1.56.0, Chapter Six part one: The Audience Music Standing Ovation Leaves The Last Ticket, one for everyone who was there; also 4 to 9 Ticket Stubs, 2 to 4 diamonds and 1 to 3 echo shards Past the Door at the End of the World is the Stalls : an old picture house's seats out in the dark, row after row of them, every one facing a screen two hundred feet wide. Some of the seats are taken."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"The Audience","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#the-audience","t":"Forty of the seats hold grey people in good clothes gone the colour of ash, slack in their seats, their faces turned up to the screen, their mouths a little open, the picture flickering in their eyes, a ticket in one hand in their laps. They've been watching a long time. They don't look round (16 health each). They hear you, though: a step near them, a block broken, a door. Then they get up, slow, a finger to their lips, and come for you, arms out, shushing, and the ones round them get up too. One that gets hold of you holds you where you are. Sneak and they don't hear you walk. Lose them and they go back to their seats, and sit, and watch. Some of them carry a Ticket Stub . They can't carry the parasite."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"The Ushers","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#the-ushers","t":"Four of them walk the aisles, up and down, slow: tall, too thin, a maroon uniform with brass buttons and a little pillbox cap, white gloves, and no face (44 health each). Each carries a lamp and swings its cone of yellow light over the rows. If its lamp finds you (\"The Usher's lamp is on you.\"), sneaking doesn't help: it sees, it doesn't hear. It puts a finger to where its lips should be, and the SHHH goes right through the house. Everyone sat near you gets up. It comes for you itself: it bashes you with the lamp, and if it gets hold of your collar (\"The Usher has you by the collar.\") it walks you back up the aisle toward the Door. Show it a ticket. Use a Ticket Stub on an Usher and it tears it in two and looks away (\"The Usher tears your ticket in two, and looks away.\"). For a minute its lamp doesn't see you. Now and then one drops its lamp (six times in ten). It always drops a Ticket Stub."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"The Usher's Lamp","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#the-ushers-lamp","t":"Held, it lights the dark round you. Used, it flashes : the Audience and the Ushers caught in it reel with their hands over their faces and can't do anything for a few seconds. It needs eight seconds to warm again. It also breaks the Crowd's Hush, and stops the Tuned in the Vault."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"The Crowd","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#the-crowd","t":"Step out onto the front aisle , under the screen, and the picture on the screen is you . Every one of the Audience gets up and comes down to the front, and goes into the heap of them, and it gets up: three men high, two great arms made of people, and at the top a knot of faces, every one of them looking at you, every mouth going. It has its own bar and its own music. It doesn't leave the front. It doesn't have to."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#how-it-fights","t":"Reach: one arm of them swung across the front rows. Slam: both arms up and down into the floor. The ring of it goes out over the floor: jump it. Applause: its hands together, three times, and every clap a wall of air that throws you back. Shed: people come off it, get up, and come for you. The Hush (from two thirds down): \"Quiet, please.\" A thousand fingers to a thousand lips. For four seconds anyone who moves, or strikes, gets hands up out of the floor holding them and pulling. Stand still. Or flash an Usher's Lamp at it: the house lights up and the Hush breaks. Keeping perfectly still through one earns Quiet, Please . Roar (the last third): every mouth at once."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Get through the Stalls quietly first: sneak past the Audience, keep out of the Ushers' light, and keep a Ticket Stub or two for an Usher that finds you. Bring an Usher's Lamp to the front. It ends the Hush. Jump the slam rings. Stand back from the front rows when it reaches. Kill what it sheds before the people pile up round you."},{"p":"The Crowd","h":"Its end","u":"entities/the-crowd.html#its-end","t":"Dead, it comes apart into the people it was, and they come apart into static, and the screen goes dark. What's left in the middle of it is the Last Ticket , for everyone who was there: \"ADMIT ONE - THE VAULT\". It's warm. On the back, in a thin black hand: THE VAULT. Bringing it down earns Standing Ovation . Then the house is empty, but one seat in the front row is still taken. It's the Watcher. it was a good show. you weren't meant to see the end of it. you want to know what i locked up. come and see, then. ??? Front Row He gets up, goes to the screen, puts his hand on it, tears it open and goes through, and it closes behind him to a seam of light down the middle of the screen. That earns Front Row . Hold the Last Ticket up to the seam and it opens into the Watcher's Vault , where the Projectionist is waiting. The Hub's replay portal for The Door brings the Crowd back for another go (see the Hub )."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html","t":"The Deep, the dais at the end of the Old Halls Boss Health 420 Senses Can't hear, can't see. It feels you through the floor. Added in 1.54.0, Chapter Five part six Music Stand Still Drops The King's Ear-Stones, 3 to 6 Carved Old Stone, 2 to 4 Bloom Roots and 2 to 4 diamonds The older ones were in the Deep before the Chorus came down into it. They don't hunt each other. They hate the Chorus and everything of its as much as they hate you, and they go for whatever of its they hear or feel moving."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#description","t":"The oldest thing in the Deep, the one that carved the Old Halls: a hulk that walks on its knuckles, its hide gone grey-green as old stone, a crown of that stone grown into its skull, and the Bloom's roots hanging out of its jaw like a beard. Long ago it drove a plug of stone into each ear so it wouldn't hear the Chorus singing. It has sat on its dais at the end of the Old Halls ever since. To find it, follow the way-stones from the Gullet: squat columns with a spiral cut in them like an ear, and an ember cap burning on top."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"How it finds you","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#how-it-finds-you","t":"It can't hear you and it can't see you. It feels you: every step you take on the floor anywhere near it, every block you break or set down, every landing. Stand still and you aren't there. Sneak , or wear Hushed Boots , and it has to be close to feel you. In the air you're nothing to it, until you land. Hit it and it feels where the blow came from. It sits on its dais until it feels you."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#how-it-fights","t":"Feel: palms flat on the floor, and a ring goes out through it. Anything moving in it is found. Slam: it rears up and brings both fists down, and the shock goes out through the floor. Jump it. Sweep: an arm swung across. Charge: from a way off, on its knuckles. If it hits a wall it's stunned a while: hit it then, when it takes half as much again. Roar (half dead): the roof comes down in places. The dust shows you where first. It's stone: arrows go in a little way and stop, doing half. It has its own bar and its own music."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Bait the charge into a wall, then hit it while it's stunned. Jump every slam. If you're in the air when the shock goes out, it misses you. When you need it to lose you, stop moving. Watch the dust after it roars."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"Its end","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#its-end","t":"Dead, its crown cracks off, and far away something notices: \"Far under you, the singing stops a moment. Something is listening.\" Killing it earns Stand Still . It leaves the King's Ear-Stones : \"Two plugs of the old ones' stone, warm, a spiral in each.\" Carry them and the Chorus's song can't get into you either. That matters in the fight with the Chorus, Whole . The Projectionist's reruns bring its fists back, and the Hub's replay portal for The Static brings the King back for another go (see the Projectionist and the Hub )."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"The Listener","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#the-listener","t":"The Deep, nesting in the Root Hollows Hostile Health 60 Senses No eyes. It hears. Drops 1 or 2 Listener's Ears, 1 to 3 bones and sometimes string Tall, starved, cave-white, a ribcage on long dog's legs, arms that hang to its ankles, and no eyes: where they were, the skin has grown smooth over. It has ears instead, a fan of thin skin on rods of bone either side of its head that opens wide when it listens. It can't see you. It hears you: every step you walk or run, every block you break or set, every door, every mouthful, an arrow landing, a hit. It goes to the sound, fast, its fans spread, and rakes whatever is there or throws itself on it from a way off. When it gets there and there's nothing more, it stands with its ears open and listens. Sneak and it can't hear you walk. Throw something and it goes to where it lands. It hunts the Chorus's forms just the same: they walk, it hears them. They nest in the root hollows: bones, the clothes of whoever they took, a barrel of their things. When the Chorus, Whole is two thirds down, they break in through the walls of the Warm Heart, for it, for its things and for you."},{"p":"The Deaf King","h":"Hushed Boots","u":"entities/the-deaf-king.html#hushed-boots","t":"Stitch two Listener's Ears over a pair of leather boots, with string, and you have Hushed Boots : you walk as quiet as sneaking, the Listener can't hear you, and the Deaf King has to be close to feel you. Making them earns Not a Sound ."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html","t":"The Hub, past the wall of static Awake Looks like Your shape, your size, its skin crawling static, a plain white mask Fought Not yet: it's only in the Hub's cutscene and, after it, past the wall Added in 1.59.0, Chapter Seven: The First Signal Music Enough; and The First Signal (with its four notes, low) Status CHAPTER SEVEN - THE FIRST SIGNAL - to be continued The landing \"the first signal. it was here before me. before the first picture.\""},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#description","t":"Your shape, your size. Its skin is static, crawling. A long charcoal studio coat, old broadcast headphones round its neck with their cable over its shoulder, and a little red ON AIR lamp on its chest, lit. A plain white mask , and through its eye-holes its eyes: an eye in the dark, the whites dim grey, the rest one great black disc with points of light caught on it, always on you, narrowing as it shouts. When it moves it never hurries. When it skips, it skips like a signal, frames of it missing and its colours coming apart."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"ENOUGH","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#enough","t":"After the last show's credits the Watcher brings you into the Hub , the realm he made, and tells you what he can do now. He's in the middle of it (\"what do you-\") when the picture breaks up. The sky over the gallery tears open, and a voice comes out of it, low, huge, more than one voice at once: \"ENOUGH.\" He goes at the rift with both hands, pushing it shut, and a hand comes out of it and stops him. It tears the rift wide and comes through. It comes for you both. He turns to run, and it shakes its head: no. He stops. He turns back and shoves it with everything he has, and it's thrown five hundred blocks out over the static, tumbling. It catches itself, a hand dug into the static. It tears a piece of his realm loose and stamps it to rubble, then comes back in jumps, landing on the pieces of his realm one after another, each crumbling behind it. jump. ??? at the edge You go off the edge together, and falling, he shuts the realm behind you: a wall of static , slammed down. It stops at it, its hand flat on it. Hearing it, and jumping, earns ENOUGH ."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"What it is","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#what-it-is","t":"Falling, the Watcher tears a portal open under you both, and you come down on an oil rig in the Dead Water (since 1.62.0). He lands beside you, crouched: ...we're out. it's awake now. the first signal. it'll come for me - then for you. but it can't hear us here. not through all this water. ??? on the rig Getting there earns The First Signal . What happens on the rig is Chapter Eight ."},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"The landing","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#the-landing","t":"In a world that came down from the Hub before 1.62.0 (or if the Dead Water isn't there), you land at home instead, and he says more: ...it's awake. the first signal. it was here before me. before the first picture. every bit of static you ever heard - that was it. asleep. i made a realm out of its static. and it noticed. i shut the realm behind us. it'll hold. for now. it'll come for me. then for you. ...we're going to need more than i've got. ??? the landing He looks up: a hairline tear across the sky, static showing through it. \"Somewhere past the static, the First Signal is awake - and it knows your name.\" Then he gives you the Remote and goes. A world like that, the next time anyone jumps off the Hub's edge, is sent on to the Dead Water: \"not that way. not this time.\""},{"p":"The First Signal","h":"Where it is now","u":"entities/the-first-signal.html#where-it-is-now","t":"Back in the Hub (the Remote takes you there), it's still there: past the faint wall he shut, standing, watching you. Now and then you hear it. The Hub won't let you sleep: \"Not here. Not with it out there, past the wall.\" Nothing else is known about it yet. Chapter Seven ends \"to be continued\"."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"","u":"entities/the-gardener.html","t":"The Botanic Gardens, under the dome Boss Who he was E. Thorne, Head Gardener Size Over three blocks tall Health 420 Wakes when You go too close to him or the flower, or strike him Drops The Gardener's Shears, the Heartbloom, a handful of Knotted Roots, bone meal, moss, weeping bells and rare seeds. His head on the first kill. The glasshouse The Gardener under the dome, with the HD Models pack."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#description","t":"The Head Gardener who tended the great flower so long it grew into him. He kneels at it under the dome with a root running from its heart into his face, in a rotting coat and a wide straw hat, a pale flower with an eye in it where his face was. His chest is a cage of root ribs with a heart beating inside, moss and little flowers growing in it. His left arm is a root. He carries rusted hedge shears as long as a man, in both hands, one on each long handle."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Waking him","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#waking-him","t":"He doesn't notice you at first. Walk softly. Go too close to him or to the flower, or strike him, and he tears loose and stands, and the gates slam shut behind you. They can't be broken while he lives, not even in Creative. Before you wake him, find his clothes (the hat and boots in the potting shed, the coat and breeches in his office). You'll want them later."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"How he fights","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#how-he-fights","t":""},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Phase one","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#phase-one","t":"Snip: the shears turned on their side, jaws flung wide, a lunge, and they bite shut. You bleed. Scissor and Thrust : a double snip, and the shears couched at his hip like a spear. Prune: wound out to his right and swept all the way round, throwing you back. Whirl: held out level at arm's length as he spins. Lash: his root arm whips out and drags you in to the shears. Don't stand too far off. Sow: seeds flung out of his coat pockets that burst up as thorns under you. Step off the ground where earth bubbles. Impale: the shears raised before his face, points down, and driven into the floor."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"The overgrowth","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#the-overgrowth","t":"At half his health he drives the shears into the ground on one knee and the glasshouse answers him: every burstpod near him goes off, petals rain, his face opens wide. He can't be hurt while it does."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Phase two","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#phase-two","t":"Pollen: a choking cloud breathed out of the flower. Blinds, poisons and sickens. Stay out of it. Roots: the shears driven point-down into the floor, and lines of thorns race along the ground at everyone at once. Keep moving across them. The Call: the shears raised high and wide open, a shriek, and his children come up out of the earth round you."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Rootlings","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#rootlings","t":"Knee-high things with a pale bulb for a head, red pinprick eyes and a grin of thorns. They chatter, leap at you, and burrow away to come up somewhere else. Kill them. They drop Knotted Roots."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"How to survive him","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#how-to-survive-him","t":"He is slow and huge. Keep out of reach of the shears, but not so far that he lashes you in. Watch for his arm going back. Thorns come up where the ground stirs and earth bubbles. Step off it. If everyone inside leaves or dies, he goes back to his flower, healed, and the gates open again. You can retreat, but you start over."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"His end","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#his-end","t":"He drops his shears, goes down on his knees, his flowers wilt, and he bows. The great flower drags him in and eats him, and dies with him, its heart dried to a dead knot. He leaves the Gardener's Shears (Prune: full swings snip twice, and whatever is badly hurt is cut half again as hard; use them to drive a row of thorns toward what you face) and the Heartbloom , all that was left of the flower's heart: eat it and you are made whole, hardened and healing, and everything green round you flowers. Three days later, the flower turns out not to be dead. See the green rift . And in chapter four the Bloom gives him back: the Gardener, Reborn ."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Turned","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take him. Turned, he's the Gardener, Overgrown . The Projectionist's reruns bring back his ring of thorns, and the Hub's replay portal for Act Two brings him back for another go."},{"p":"The Gardener","h":"Field notes","u":"entities/the-gardener.html#field-notes","t":"His journal is on the lectern in his office; his under-gardener T. Avery's ledger is in the Seed Vault. Both are on the lore page . I hear it say my name through the lilies. It says it needs tending. It is right. Somebody must tend it. I am going to kneel by it a while. Just a while. If you find this: do not wake me. Do not touch the flower. The last page of E. Thorne's journal."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"","u":"entities/the-mended.html","t":"The Murder Mansion, the Trophy Hall Boss Made at The Mending Altar, with one head from each of chapter two's nine Health 750 Size Four blocks tall, hunched Phases Agony, Aggression, Iron Will Drops The Mended Heart and the Rusted Garden Key, with iron, chains and one of each of the nine's drops. By chance as it falls apart: bottles o' enchanting (60%), netherite scrap (25%), a totem of undying (15%), an enchanted golden apple (5%). The Mended Out in the fog."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"The mending","u":"entities/the-mended.html#the-mending","t":"Put one head from each of the nine (the Bunnyman, the Hookman, the Hogshead, the Porcelain Man, the Harvestman, Mothman, the Jersey Devil, Dogman and the Flatwoods Monster) on the trophy pedestals round the Mending Altar, and right-click the altar with an empty hand. The Watcher, waiting on the ceiling, does the rest. It takes about thirty seconds. The heads scream as it talks, and their agony runs out of them in red streams into a knot over the floor. It pours its shadow into the knot. The heads are torn apart one by one; chains come down out of the dark and something hammers iron into the knot; the body is there, red hot, its pieces slamming together. It stands, the chains snap, and it roars with all nine voices. Nothing can hurt it until then. what i make out of them won't be pretty and it won't be kind. it will be one thing instead of nine. that's the point. one thing can be killed. From On the Mending , the Watcher's pages on the library desk"},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-mended.html#description","t":"Four blocks tall, hunched, held together with stitches and iron: a pig's head with the Porcelain Man's cracked face bolted over it (with Mothman's eye bulging out of the mask) and the Jersey Devil's horns, the Hookman's arm and hook, the Hogshead's arm with the Dogman's claws and the Harvestman's scythe, a dog's leg and a goat's, Mothman's wings down its back, and the Flatwoods Monster's lamp burning in its open chest. A crow stands on its shoulder plate."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-mended.html#phases","t":""},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Agony","u":"entities/the-mended.html#agony","t":"The killers' ways: a two-blow chop with the scythe arm; the hook thrown on its chain to drag you in, then the chop; a head-down charge (sidestep it into a wall and it stands there stunned, taking extra damage); a whole turn with the scythe held out if you get round it. It also fires its needles, pours its chest-lamp's beam on you, and calls the crows. At 60% it tears itself open: the stitches burst, the wings rip loose and spread, and it screams."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Aggression","u":"entities/the-mended.html#aggression","t":"Faster, with the cryptids' ways too: Mothman's screech (darkness, your legs heavy), the Jersey Devil's spring into the air and glide, the Flatwoods mist out of its chest (poison and nausea), and the Dogman's claw, claw, bite. At 25% it drops to one knee and iron is driven into it: chains up out of the ground, plates and nails, red hot. The boss bar turns white."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Iron Will","u":"entities/the-mended.html#iron-will","t":"Armoured and slow, but much faster whenever nobody is looking at it. It kneels to mend itself, white arms sewing it shut and healing it, unless you hit it hard enough to tear the stitches (it staggers and takes extra damage). It slams both fists down and a ring of iron spikes runs out across the floor: jump it . It can't be hurt while it tears itself open or while the iron goes in."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-mended.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Bring torches, food, and \"more than you think\", as the Watcher's pages say. Don't let it get between you and the doors. Sidestep the charge into a wall for a free window of extra damage. In Iron Will, keep your eyes on it: it's much faster when nobody's looking. Hit hard while it kneels to mend. Jump the ring of spikes."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Its end","u":"entities/the-mended.html#its-end","t":"It comes apart: the bolts burst, the hook arm tears off, the wings fall away, the white arms shatter, and the lamp in its chest gutters and goes out. It goes down on its knees, onto its claws, onto its face, and the nine go up out of it, each a light at the head of its stream. Then the Watcher has something to say about the glass house. Its Mended Heart (Iron Will): hold it up for three minutes of Resistance II, Strength I and Absorption II, then it has to beat itself warm again. Its Rusted Garden Key opens the Botanic Gardens. Its statue, carved in weathered stone with blood pouring from its mouth, stands in the Mansion's fountain. ...listen. something in the glass house heard all of that. it's awake now. ??? as the Mended dies Up close With the HD Models pack."},{"p":"The Mended","h":"Turned","u":"entities/the-mended.html#turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take it. Turned, it's the Mended, Unstitched : what holds the nine together now is the parasite."},{"p":"The Omni","h":"","u":"entities/the-omni.html","t":"The Omni Orbital Railgun, and SENTINEL above the sky Gone for good What it is A weapon: the Ray Gun after the Watcher has had it Fires A column of light 32 blocks across, in every colour Recharge 2 minutes Added in 1.43.0, \"The Omni Ray\" Ends The changed Bloom. Nothing else can. Where it went Its heart is in the Watcher's Vault, and in Chapter Six it goes into his last projector Omni Orbital Railgun Hold to aim, attack or let go to fire (2 min recharge) The Watcher has had it. It isn't the same gun. 32 blocks across, in every colour. Aim it at the Bloom, 50 blocks or more off its mouth."},{"p":"The Omni","h":"How you get it","u":"entities/the-omni.html#how-you-get-it","t":"Build the Orbital Railgun round the Infused Orbital Core. Building it wakes three more places. Bring back their three parts: the Nuclear Reactor Core (Ashford Nuclear Plant), the Discharge Destabilizer (Meridian Laboratory) and the Vial of Dark Matter Blood (Blackwater Station). Craft the Ray Gun round the railgun and the three parts, or bring them all to a Forsaken Altar and let the Watcher build it over the altar. The Watcher wants it: \"give it here.\" Drop it near him ( Q ) or use it on him. It floats up into his hands, rings of glyphs turning round it, light drawn in from everywhere, and he gives you back the Omni: black, its colours running. drop it. let me have it. it isn't finished. they could never finish it. it needed something they didn't have. the dark in it. mine. hold still. there. the omni. it's yours. now go to it. stand off its mouth - fifty blocks, no nearer, or it takes you with it. aim it at the flower. hold it on it. and fire. ??? making the Omni Meridian's director had worked out what they were missing: \"We can't finish it. It needs something we don't have. Something that knows the dark.\""},{"p":"The Omni","h":"The Ray Gun it was","u":"entities/the-omni.html#the-ray-gun","t":"The Ray Gun is the Orbital Railgun mod (by Mishkis, from Rayness's Renewed port, MIT licence) built into Static Hollow. Hold use and its sight opens over your view, a ring on the ground where you aim, out to 300 blocks; attack, or let go after a second, and it fires. For four seconds it locks on; then for thirty-two the sky over the spot comes apart, a dome, six spheres flung out and back, columns of light; from twenty seconds everything near is dragged in toward it; at thirty-six seconds a column of light 24 blocks across comes down the whole height of the world, and everything in it is gone. The Omni's strike is a third again as wide, in every colour, and louder than anything else in the game."},{"p":"The Omni","h":"SENTINEL","u":"entities/the-omni.html#sentinel","t":"SENTINEL is the gun above the sky that the Rosemont garrison built before the city fell, and never got to fire. The Orbital Railgun talks to it; the Uplink Station is where the garrison talked to it. The standing orders call it \"a weapon of last resort\", and its core has a third socket the engineers call \"the governor\". Nobody was ever told what goes in it. Meridian's director knew better: \"Garrison Command thinks it's a safety. It isn't. It's a throttle.\""},{"p":"The Omni","h":"The Omni Ray","u":"entities/the-omni.html#the-omni-ray","t":"Stand fifty blocks or more off the changed Bloom's mouth (\"TOO CLOSE - back off\" otherwise), aim the Omni at the flower and fire. The camera is taken, and since 1.43.2 the Watcher takes you up with him in a spill of ink, to watch from the air over the petals. The sky, over the changed Bloom ??? look up. ??? come up here. you'll want to see this. SENTINEL // DEORBIT BURN - ATMOSPHERIC ENTRY ??? it was always up there. waiting for someone to call it down. SENTINEL // RETRO BURN - DESCENT ARRESTED SENTINEL // ALL SYSTEMS ONLINE - OMNI ARRAY DEPLOYING OMNI ARRAY // ALIGNING ??? everything it has. all in one place. ??? now it has nowhere to hide. TARGET LOCKED OMNI ARRAY // FIRE WARNING // COUNTER-BEAM - OUTPUT FALLING ??? it's fighting it. If the Bloom has eaten too much: ??? it's eaten too much. it's too strong. ??? take mine. all of it. OUTPUT 1000% // SOURCE UNKNOWN If it hasn't: ??? it doesn't need me. not this time. OMNI ARRAY // OVERDRIVE - SAFETIES OFF OUTPUT 400% // HOLDING SENTINEL comes down out of its orbit: a star that moves, then a fireball burning through the air, its trail across the sky, the sonic boom, its retro thrusters. It stops right over the Bloom's mouth. Light comes in off the horizon; five rings of glyphs close in one by one round the line down to its mouth. It fires a beam of plasma, white-hot at the core, its edges split into colour. The Bloom fires back, its own beam up out of its mouth, every colour gone wrong, and drives the Omni's back up toward the station, the more it's eaten the nearer. Then it's driven down into its mouth. The blast: a breath of white, the fireball going dark in its own smoke, its shock going out at the speed of sound, heard when it gets to you: a crack like the sky splitting, and a roar rolling round the land for a long time after. A title card reads THE OMNI RAY : the bloom is dead. the watcher rests."},{"p":"The Omni","h":"Taken back","u":"entities/the-omni.html#taken-back","t":"The first time you carry the Omni off the Bloom's blight, the camera is taken again and the Watcher is in your way. He pulls the gun out of your hands, tears open a rift into his realm, green fire licking up its edges, and throws it in. It's gone for good. This earns Zero Responsibility . wait. not so fast. i'll take that. it wouldn't be fair to let you take such a destructive toy with you, to use on everything. from what i see, i see great power. great potential. but zero responsibility for life. i can see the thoughts in your head, you know. it goes where it'll be safe. in my realm. for the future. ??? taking the Omni back And the first time anyone puts the Ray Gun together in a crafting grid afterwards, he's there at the table and pulls its recipe up out of it, a page of light with the gun's plan on it, and burns it in green fire. It's gone from every recipe book, and nothing will make the Ray Gun again. This earns Always Persistent . you're always persistent. i'll take this too. now it can't ever be made again. ??? at the crafting table"},{"p":"The Omni","h":"The Omni's Heart","u":"entities/the-omni.html#the-omnis-heart","t":"In Chapter Six you find what he did with it. In one of three keeps in the Watcher's Vault , on a plinth, is the Omni's Heart : \"What made the Omni more than a gun: every colour at once, turning, in a cage of its own light. He took it out of it.\" Its tooltip reads KEPT FOR THE FUTURE. it's come for what i kept. the omni. the carrier. my first reel. get to them before it does. bring them here. ??? The Watch Bring it to his desk in the Watch, with the other two things he kept, and the Projectionist comes for them. On the Other Side , at two thirds of the fight with the Viewer , he loads it into the lamp of his last projector: every colour at once, thrown out over the dark into its eye. It reels, blinded. That earns Every Colour at Once ."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"","u":"entities/the-parasite.html","t":"First found at Blackwater Station Hostile Looks like Six legs, and a mouth that opens like a flower Came from The Null Static Zone, by way of a crash forty kilometres out at sea First appears 1.43.0, when the Orbital Railgun wakes Blackwater Station Health 10 (its kinds 8 to 14) Related Its five kinds, the pure forms and the biomass, the turned , Parasite Host, Parasite Pod, Xeno Resin, Static Hound, the Hollowed, the Chorus Status effects Infested (on a creature it's taking over), Parasitized (the old quick brood, before 1.48.0), Brood Fit (when a brood in you has fits), Tuned In (the Relay Core lets you see them)"},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#description","t":"Parasites skitter, rear up and screech, leap at you, and latch onto the back of your neck. A message tells you: \"Something's on the back of your neck - hit it off!\" and then \"It's getting in - crouch to tear it off!\" Parasite Pod texture. Blackwater's specimen notes describe it in two lines: \"The parasite: six legs, a mouth that opens like a flower. It goes for the back of the neck.\" and \"In a host it grows in hours. Then the host splits open and there are more of them.\""},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Where it came from","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#where-it-came-from","t":"Something came down forty kilometres out at sea. The Blackwater researchers towed what was left of it to their island and built the station round the tank. Its blood doesn't freeze; there are stars in it. On day thirty the cultures took. On day thirty-three the tanks burst. At first the parasites died in seconds anywhere off Blackwater's island. Since 1.43.3 they live anywhere. Ten days after the Bloom dies, the Watcher comes back to tell you where they're really from: the infection in those new places - blackwater - it isn't from here. it came into this realm from another one. the null static zone. they don't need the flower. they'll get into anything with blood in it - a cow, a horse, a villager. ??? ten days later"},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"What it gets into","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#what-it-gets-into","t":""},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"The infected and Parasite Hosts","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#hosts","t":"The staff it got into at Blackwater are Parasite Hosts : hurt one, or let it near you too long, and it convulses and splits open. Parasites also go for the Flesh's infected (the townspeople, police, soldiers, the Laboratory's staff, the shelter's squad, and the Bloaters, Screamers and Brutes they turn into). One gets onto an infected's back and in at the neck while it stands there in a fit; the brood grows out between its shoulder blades over ten seconds, spurs out of its shoulders and neck, beating and lit. Grown, hurt badly or close to you, it heaves and splits open, and two of them come out (one if it was killed before the brood had grown, none if it burnt)."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Anything at all","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#anything-at-all","t":"From 1.43.5 to 1.47 a parasite in one of the game's own creatures grew a quick sac on its back and burst out. Since 1.48.0 it doesn't. It takes the creature over, slowly (two days for an ordinary creature, three for the hard ones), and then the creature is theirs. Any creature at all can carry it now: the game's own, the golems, the Warden, the Wither and the dragon, and the Hollow's own things. Only the Flesh's infected still get the old quick brood. Everything about the outbreak, the stages, the turn and what the turned do is on The Turned . What they made of the wolves are Static Hounds . What they made of one villager in every village is the Hollowed ."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Its kinds","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#the-kinds","t":"Since 1.48.0, what comes out of something is born of where it was. From Chapter Five they also turn up on their own, now and then, near you: whichever kind lives where you are, up out of the water, down out of the night sky, out of the cave wall, out of the fire."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Tide Parasite","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#tide-parasite","t":"In the water, 12 health An eel's body behind the same mouth of five petals, a fin down its back, two hooked forelimbs to hold on with, its spots glowing like the things down there. Fast in the water: it darts at you from a long way off, and holds on down there while you drown. Out of the water it drags itself along."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Burrowing Parasite","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#burrowing-parasite","t":"Deep in the stone, 14 health Long and segmented, eight short legs, its petals drawn out into a point like a drill. It goes into the ground in front of you (you hear it coming under your feet, you see the dirt jump) and comes up under you, mouth first."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Winged Parasite","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#winged-parasite","t":"Out of anything with wings, 8 health Four long veined wings like a dragonfly's, its legs hanging. You hear it before you see it: a buzz in the dark. It hangs over you, then drops on you mouth open, and holds on."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Ember Parasite","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#ember-parasite","t":"The Nether, 12 health Black chitin cracked through with light, like coals, smoke and sparks off it as it runs. Fire doesn't touch it and it walks over lava. What it bites burns. Water hurts it."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Void Parasite","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#void-parasite","t":"The End, 10 health Black all through, with stars moving in it, its edges blurred as if it isn't all here. It goes out like a light and is behind you. Hurt it and it's somewhere else. The infested dragon rains these down on you."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"The biomass and the pure forms","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#the-biomass-and-the-pure-forms","t":"Since 1.49.0, what the parasite is done with it doesn't leave lying there. When one of the turned dies (nearly always one of the hard ones, and four times in ten one of the rest), a heap of violet biomass is left where it fell: veined, pulsing, chitin forced out through it. It drags at you if you wade through it. It isn't dead. A minute or two later, with anyone about, it heaves itself up into one of the parasite's pure forms , and all that's left is its torn husk. Burn it (fire or lava against it) and nothing gets up. The pure forms have no host left in them at all, only the parasite's own flesh grown into the shape it needs. They hunt everything that isn't theirs, what they hit they might put one into, and fire hurts them twice as much. They morph : one folds in on itself, its flesh running like wax, and stands up as something else. A Ranged form when it can see you from far off, a Stalker when you run, a Tank when you're close and hurting it."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Stalker Form","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#stalker-form","t":"30 health Low and quick on four legs, its head split three ways. It climbs walls and only comes while you're not looking at it. It pounces from a distance and mauls you close in."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Ranged Form","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#ranged-form","t":"30 health Rooted where it stands, a column of flesh as tall as you with a crown of quills. It swells and throws a volley of bone spines at you from a long way off, leading you as you run. Get close and it folds up into something else; lose it long enough and it pulls its roots up to come and find you."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Tank Form","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#tank-form","t":"80 health A hulk twice your height with a club of an arm and plates of chitin on its shoulders. It slams the ground, swats you away, grabs you and throws you."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Brood Sack","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#brood-sack","t":"16 health A swollen sack on four stumps with things moving under its skin. It waddles up to you, swells and bursts : a handful of parasites out of it. Kill it first and it bursts anyway (unless it burnt)."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"One of them in you","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#one-of-them-in-you","t":"If a parasite holds on for the whole four seconds, it gets in (\"It's in you.\"). Its brood grows over about three days of play, and a meter beside your hotbar fills. You get hungrier; at a quarter you can feel the others through walls; at two fifths you're stronger and faster; at half the sac shows on your back and has fits; at three quarters it's too big to burn out; full, it tears its way out of your back for 7 hearts, and two of them come out. What you'll read What it means Something moves under your skin. It's started growing. You can feel them now - the others like it, out there. A quarter grown. You can see the parasite's own through walls. It's feeding you too. You feel strong. You feel fast. You're starving. Two fifths. There's a lump between your shoulder blades, and it's warm. Half. Fits start. It's too big to burn out now. Three quarters. Only a Surgical Kit or a Hush now. It's nearly ready. Cut it out. Now. Ninety percent."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Getting it out","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#getting-it-out","t":"Surgical Kit: hold it to cut the brood out of yourself; use it on someone else to cut one out of them. It hurts and you bleed. Four uses. Made from shears, an iron ingot, string, paper and wool. It also cuts one out of any creature the parasite is taking over, as long as it hasn't started to turn. Burn it out: stand in fire long enough to be hurt, before it's three quarters grown. \"It's burning in you. Stay in it.\" A Hush: step over the line into one of the Null Static Zone's pale houses and the brood dies. Grown, it tears out of your back as it dies."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Pods and resin","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#pods-and-resin","t":"Where they nest they spread their black Xeno Resin over everything, and their pods come up out of it and split open when you come near. Since 1.47.1 a pod is a round egg-sac; split open, it's a torn cup with its four flaps peeled back off the rim and the slime inside. Relay 6 is covered in both."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"The parasite egg","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#the-parasite-egg","t":""},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"After Signing Off","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#after-signing-off","t":"Since 1.50.0, the Carrier's death didn't end it. Half a minute after you're home from the Null Static Zone the Watcher comes to where you are: it seems the carrier did what it was supposed to do. it carried them - all the way out. the parasites are increasing. every one of them hostile. the numbers are going off the charts. in your world. there's nothing we can do about it for now. just try not to die. for me. in the meantime. ??? after Signing Off From then on the outbreak is worse: the parasite gets into things half again as often, and more of its kinds turn up round you, more of them at once. And the parasite grows itself a mind out in the world: the Chorus , in the Hive ."},{"p":"The Parasite","h":"Advancements","u":"entities/the-parasite.html#advancements","t":"Something Inside , Cut It Out , Burn It Out and It Came Out of Me are all about a brood in you. It Isn't Itself is for being there when something turns. See Advancements ."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html","t":"The Watcher's Vault, the Watch Boss Health 900 Came in Behind you, on your ticket Added in 1.57.0, Chapter Six part two: The Watcher's Vault Music The Projectionist Leaves The Projectionist's Lens; also 3 to 5 diamonds, 2 to 4 echo shards and 2 to 4 Vacuum Tubes Behind the Stalls' screen is the Watcher's Vault : his archive, steel shelving going up into the dark, cans of film and boxes of tape on every shelf, and old television sets among them, some still on. The Last Ticket you came in on admitted one. It wasn't you."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"The Watch","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#the-watch","t":"At the far end of the nave is his desk, his chair, and in front of it a wall of sets, thirty-seven across and sixteen high, all showing one picture. this is where i watch from. they watch the picture. i watch them. your world's a show to them. the worse it gets, the more of them come. they left you a ticket. it admits one. not you. something came in behind you. it's come for what i kept. the omni. the carrier. my first reel. get to them before it does. bring them here. ??? The Watch On the wall, the stacks, and in them something tall with a light for a face."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"The keeps","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#the-keeps","t":"Three keeps open off the nave behind round steel doors. Use a door or its wheel and the wheel turns, the bolts draw back one after another (\"The wheel turns. Somewhere in the door, bolts draw back, one after another.\"), and the door swings in. On a plinth in each is what he kept: The Omni's Heart : every colour at once, turning in rings of its own light. \"What made the Omni more than a gun.\" See the Omni . What's Left of the Carrier : a knot of it, still beating, static coming off it like heat. Take it and its static pours out, and every Tuned near you is loose for a few seconds. See the Carrier . His First Reel , in a glass case: a dented film can. On the lid, in his hand: THE OTHER SIDE. FIRST. DO NOT RUN. Taking all three earns What He Kept ."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"The Tuned","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#the-tuned","t":"Standing in the aisles of the stacks: people from the neck down (a cardigan, a shirt done up to the collar, slippers), and where the head should be an old television set, its screen bowed out, static on it. The ones who watched too long; he keeps them in his Vault so they won't watch anything else (24 health each). They only move while you're looking at them . Look at one and it comes for you in jerks, like a picture with frames missing, your face on its screen. Look away and it stops dead, however it was standing, and stays like that. Close, and watched, it takes your head in both hands and tunes you: it hurts, the static comes in at the edges of your eyes, the colour goes out of things, and you can hardly move. Flash an Usher's Lamp at one and its screen whites out: it can't move for four seconds, watched or not. In the dark, or in the Projectionist's light, they move whether you're looking or not. Some of them drop a Vacuum Tube (three times in ten). Two of them, with glass, iron and redstone, make two Old Sets of your own that switch on and off."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"The Projectionist","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#the-projectionist","t":"Bring all three of his things to the Watch and every set on the wall goes to it, and it steps down out of them. Twice the height of a man and thin, in a long coat that's all film, frames on frames of it, hanging to the floor and moving; its hands long and grey; one arm ending in a crank; and for a head a cinema's projector, its housing black and dented, its two reels turning on top, its lens a white light you can't look into. It runs the show, for the ones on the other side."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#how-it-fights","t":"Beam: its lens's light swept across the Watch. It burns, and while you're in it the Tuned can move whether you look at them or not. Reruns: the old ones, projected onto the air, grey and flickering, doing again the one thing everyone remembers. Where each will strike shows on the floor first. The Hollow Saint : its shadow beam, straight through where you were standing. The Gardener : a ring of thorns out from under your feet. The Deaf King : both fists down, and the ring of it out over the floor. Jump it. The Carrier : its beam, down out of nothing onto where you're standing. Lash: a strip of its film round you, holding you (\"Its film's round you. You can't move.\"). Splice: a jump cut, and it's behind you. Reels: each third gone, it changes its reels. Hit it then: it takes half as much again. Crank (from two thirds down): it cranks itself, and everything it does is twice as fast for a while. Intermission (the last third): the lights go out, every set and every bulb, and there's only its lens. \"Please remain seated.\" Fire doesn't hurt it, and nothing hurts it mid-splice or before it's all the way out of the picture."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Keep the Tuned in front of you, and in sight, when you can. In its beam and in the intermission they come anyway. Watch the floor for where a rerun will land. Save your hardest hits for its reel changes. Bring an Usher's Lamp for the Tuned."},{"p":"The Projectionist","h":"Its end","u":"entities/the-projectionist.html#its-end","t":"Dead, the picture burns through from the middle, as film does stuck in the gate, and what's left of it is its lens . Burning it through earns The Final Reel . The Projectionist's Lens : hold it and every hostile thing near you shows through the walls, outlined in its light. Then the Watcher runs his first reel. The projector on his desk clatters into life: this is the first thing anyone ever saw on the other side. i kept it so i'd never forget what it looks like. that's what i kept out. it's all for that one. the whole show. and now it's seen you. it's coming through. ??? The First Reel A dark so big it has a shape, sat, and an eye in it opening, turning to look at you. Then the Door at the End of the World, its static gone black. Seeing it earns What He Kept Out . What's on the other side is the Viewer ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"","u":"entities/the-turned.html","t":"From Chapter Five, once the Bloom is dead Hostile to everything Added in 1.48.0 (the outbreak), 1.49.0 (the infested bosses), 1.51.0 and 1.52.0 (the Hollow's own, turned) How long it takes Two days for an ordinary creature, three for the hard ones, on the world's own clock Turned Half as much health again as it had, healed to full Status effect Infested (hidden) Can't carry it You (you get a brood instead: see the Parasite ), the parasite's own, the Flesh's infected (all but its four great ones), the Void's creatures, the Watcher, and the Stalls' Audience, Ushers and Crowd Before 1.48.0 a parasite in a cow grew a quick brood and burst out of it. Now it doesn't. It takes the creature over, slowly, and then the creature is theirs: a ruined, writhing version of what it was, hunting everything that isn't one of them."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Anything can carry it","u":"entities/the-turned.html#anything-can-carry-it","t":"Any creature at all can carry it: the game's own animals, people and monsters, the golems, the Warden, the Wither and the dragon, and the Hollow's own things. The exceptions are in the case file above. It gets into them in three ways: A parasite gets in. Any of the parasite's kinds that latches on to a creature starts it. A turned one hits it. What the turned hit, they put one into about a third of the time. They can put one into you too, now and then. It's already out there. Once the Bloom is dead, every couple of minutes there's a one-in-three chance that a creature somewhere 24 to 80 blocks from you has one in it, already some way along. After the Watcher's visit following Signing Off it's one in two. The Wither and the dragon can catch it this way too. The Hollow's own creepypastas never do: they only catch it off one of the parasite's own."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Watch it happen","u":"entities/the-turned.html#watch-it-happen","t":"Stage What you see Incubating Nothing, at first, but a twitch now and then. Spreading The veins come up violet under its skin, and the first blisters on its back. It stops now and then and shakes. Taking hold Growths spread over it, chitin forcing out through its back. Its head hangs over to one side and one leg goes wrong. Its own kind won't go near it. It stands and stares at you. Nearly gone It shakes all the time, and if you're close to it in the dark it goes for you. The turn Five seconds: it seizes up, arches, screams, and tears open. The tendrils come out of it. Everyone within 24 blocks reads: \"The ... isn't itself any more. It's theirs.\" Being there earns It Isn't Itself ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Cutting it out","u":"entities/the-turned.html#cutting-it-out","t":"A Surgical Kit used on a creature cuts the parasite out of it any time before it starts to turn (\"You cut it out of the ...\"). The further along it was, the more it hurts the creature. Once it's turning, it's too late."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Turned","u":"entities/the-turned.html#turned","t":"A turned creature is a ruined, writhing version of what it was: tendrils out of its back, and its chest (or its back) split open into a mouth of five petals round a ring of teeth. Its own mind is gone. It hunts everything that isn't one of them, the way its body lets it. The turned screech when they see you, and every one of them near comes. Village iron golems go for them. Killed, a turned creature bursts and the parasites in it come out. Burn it and nothing does."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"How they fight, by body","u":"entities/the-turned.html#by-body","t":"Body Which What it does Upright Villagers, zombies, illagers, piglins, skeletons, Endermen Lashes you with its tendrils and drags you in, lunges , grabs you and holds you while it bites, mauls . Endermen blink in behind you. On all fours Cows, horses, wolves, bears, goats Stalks you (it only comes while you're not looking at it), charges , pounces, mauls. Small Chickens, rabbits, cats, foxes Fast. It leaps for you, and burrows and comes up under you. Many-legged Spiders, silverfish Leaps, spits bile, burrows. Winged Bats, parrots, bees, phantoms, ghasts, blazes Circles over you and dives . The big ones spit. In the water Fish, squid, dolphins, guardians Rams you and drags you under . A guardian's beam goes bad. A creeper Creepers It's a carrier now: it walks up to you, swells and bursts, and what's in it comes out. The big ones Golems, the Warden, ravagers Slam the ground, lash, pick you up and throw you, charge. The hard ones roar you back and empty a brood of parasites out of themselves."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"What it grows on them","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-mutations","t":"Since 1.51.0, anything of the game's own that turns grows mutations as it goes over, whatever its body has room for: a ribcage split open on its back like jaws, whips of tendril, feelers, a second head out of its shoulder, mandibles, legs out of its sides, swollen sacs, plates of chitin, a club of it, a cannon of it. A cow, a spider, a villager, a golem, a creeper, a bat, a ghast, a slime, a Warden and the dragon each grow their own. The growths are alive: they breathe with it, twitch, lash about and strike when it strikes, and the tendril it hooks you with reaches all the way out to you. Two moves come with them: Flail (anything upright): its arm gone to tendrils, three lashes in an arc. Strike (anything on four legs): the head grown out of its shoulder lunges. What comes up out of the ground for any of them (spikes, jaws, tendrils, roots) gives a moment's warning: the ground churns first. Move."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The infested bosses","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-infested-bosses","t":"The game's bosses and mini-bosses (the hard ones, three days to turn, along with anything that has 80 health or more) fight like what they were, gone wrong. They get their own bar: \"Infested Iron Golem\" and so on."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Iron Golem","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-iron-golem","t":"Still slams, grabs and throws Tears the spines out of its own back and throws them at you in a fan. Impale : its arm driven into the ground and spikes of chitin up through it at you in a line. Harpoon : a barbed tendril out of its chest hooks you, reels you in and hits you."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Warden","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-warden","t":"Its sonic boom gone to rot The boom is a line of rot straight through everything, the dark after it and spores down the length of it. Tremor : it stamps and the ground tears up in rings out from it (jump them). Erupt : the tendrils on its head go down into the ground and come up under you, three times, wherever you've got to."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Ravager","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-ravager","t":"Gores Puts its head down and gores you up into the air. Spray : a cone of bile out of its split head. Devour : its maw clamps on you, shakes you and flings you."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Elder Guardian","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-elder-guardian","t":"Breathes spores A cloud of spores: slow mining, poison, weakness, and it might put one in you. Leech : its tendrils into you, and it drinks and heals. Maelstrom : the water turns round it and everything's dragged in."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The others","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-others","t":"One or two moves each A piglin brute : Frenzy , five blows, coming on. An evoker : Jaws (chitin jaws up out of the ground in a line) and Conjure (fliers out of its robes). A breeze : Gale , a blast of wind thick with spores. A creaking : Snare , roots up round your feet while you're not looking. A sniffer : Uproot , it digs and flings it all at you. A happy ghast : Spores , bile out of the sky."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Wither","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-wither","t":"Keeps how it fights It can carry it (three days, like the rest of the hard ones). Turned, it throws brood skulls (a fan of bile), and tendrils out of its ribs drag you in."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Infested Ender Dragon","u":"entities/the-turned.html#infested-ender-dragon","t":"Always, since 1.61.1 The dragon is theirs from the first time anyone goes to the End (and any you bring back with the crystals; one already flying in an old world is taken the moment you're there). No days of it, no turn: violet veins under its hide, blisters along its flanks, spurs up its spine, tendrils streaming back off it and its back split open between its wings. Its bar reads \"Infested Ender Dragon\" and it has half as much health again. It still fights as the dragon does, and over you it shudders and rains its brood down out of the sky (void parasites, round where you stand), lobs spore bombs and sweeps its tendrils through you as it comes past low. What its body hits it can put one into. Killed, it bursts. After Signing Off the Watcher shuts the End (see chapter five ), so the dragon can't be reached until the seal is broken in chapter six ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Hollow's great ones, turned","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-great-ones-turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take the Hollow's eight great ones, including the Flesh's four, which it never could before. When one turns, what it was is gone: a whole new body with its own bar, its own voice and a new way of fighting. Its old fight is over (its scripts, its music, its old bar): it hunts."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Saint Unmade","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-saint-unmade","t":"Was the Hollow Saint It drags itself on tentacles, hunched, its chest a mouth the height of it, its head split open like a book, a scythe of chitin for one arm and whips for the other. Choir (every face it wore screams at once: it throws you back and puts out the light), Devour (the whips round you, into the mouth, chewed and spat out), Reap (the scythe), Field (tendrils up out of the ground under you and all round you), Halo (its broken halo's pods burst, bile raining down), Surge (it throws itself at you across the ground)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Mended, Unstitched","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-mended-unstitched","t":"Was the Mended What holds the nine together now is the parasite. Hook (its chain is a tendril: the barb in you, hauled in to the scythe), Burst (every seam splits at once), Claws , Wings (Mothman's wings thrown open: every eye on them on you, the dark, the gust), Pounce ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Gardener, Overgrown","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-gardener-overgrown","t":"Was the Gardener Roots (they come up round your feet and hold you), Lash (its arm of root, the barb dragging you in), Bloom (the flower where its face was breathes out its spores), Harvest (the rusted shears, twice), Seeds (the pods on its hat burst, and spikes come up where they land)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Reborn, Consumed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-reborn-consumed","t":"Was the Gardener, Reborn Clamp (the frill of jaws round its head closes on you and chews), Dance (round and round, both scythes out), Volley (petals of the frill thrown in a fan), Pollen (the dark, and weak), Hooklash (the tentacle arm, the hook in you, and in you come)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Broodmother, Hollowed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-broodmother-hollowed","t":"Was the Broodmother It never moves from where it grew. Its roots are tentacles, its petals jaws of chitin, the woman on top split open down the middle. Snap (the petals snap shut on whatever's among them), Sweep (the tentacles sweep the ground all round it, twice), Birth (its brood drops out of the mouth down its front, the parasite's brood now), Geyser (bile raining down all round), Reach (her arms reach a long way for you and drag you in among the petals)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Specimen Zero, Unbound","u":"entities/the-turned.html#specimen-zero-unbound","t":"Was Specimen Zero Off the pool floor for good, up on six legs like a spider's, Reyes bent forward off the front of it, his arms folded like a mantis's into blades of bone, his head hanging upside down off a stretched neck. Scythe (the blades, one and then the other), Cables (into the floor and up under you and anyone with you), Leap , Absorb (his chest opens, the tongue reaches out, everything near is dragged in, and what it gets it eats: it heals), Vomit (the pool, sprayed), Skitter (round you, quick, and a bite from the side). Fire still burns it twice as hard."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Warden, Unhoused","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-warden-unhoused","t":"Was the Warden of Shelter No. 4 Its four heads up on long necks, a mouth down the whole front of the mound, six arms out of its sides, the warden on top hollowed into a chimney. Hydra (the heads strike one after another), Embrace (the arms close round everything against it and squeeze), Roll (it balls up and rolls straight at you till it hits something), Chimney (spores pour out and rain down round you in clouds), Grasp (its arms go into the floor and come up under you, holding on), Maw (the mouth opens the whole height of it, and it lunges)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Congregation, Gutted","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-congregation-gutted","t":"Was the Congregation It's opened the bus up: ribs arching over it where the roof was, a heart the size of a car under them, its front a mouth of four flaps round a throat ringed with teeth, and it runs on all their legs like a centipede. Lamprey (it lunges, holds you in its mouth, chews and spits you out), Stampede (straight on over anything till something stops it), Ribs (they open out and slam down either side of it), Windows (the tentacles out of every window lash out and drag in whatever's beside it), Hymn (every mouth sings: slow, weak, the dark at the edges), Spill (its doors burst and parasites spill out). Get under it and you're trampled."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The rest of the Hollow's own, turned","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-rest-turned","t":"In 1.52.0 every one of the Hollow's own that the parasite could get into got a form of its own: twenty-four more. (Things added after that, like the Listener, the Deaf King and the Tuned, have no turned form.) When one turns, what it was is gone (a whole new body, its own voice, four moves of its own), and its old ways are over (its hiding, its tricks, its scripts). It hunts. The big ones' names go on their bars."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Neighbor, Inside Out","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-neighbor-inside-out","t":"Was the Hollow Neighbor Split down the front and peeled open, and out of his neck the thing that wore him, long, raw and eyeless, his own head hanging slack off his back. Behind You (gone, and there, behind you), Needles (his fingers), Knock (a blow that throws everything near back), Hug (it holds you, and squeezes)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Stitchjaw, Unsewn","u":"entities/the-turned.html#stitchjaw-unsewn","t":"Was Stitchjaw Every stitch burst, on eight limbs that were arms and legs, a jaw at each end. Tear , Thread (shot into you, and you're reeled in), Pounce , Split (it opens and spins)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Shepherd, Flockless","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-shepherd-flockless","t":"Was the Weeping Shepherd What it found of its flock grown into its back, every mouth open; its crook a hook of bone. Bleat (every head at once: the dark, and slow), Crook (round you and hauled in), Tears (black ones, thrown), Flock (what's left of it drops off its back, parasites now)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Mother, Unborn","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-mother-unborn","t":"Was the Lullaby Mother Tall, her arms to the ground, her head hanging off a bent neck, something curled up in the sac of her belly. Cradle (she holds you), Lullaby (slow and weak), Swaddle (roots round your feet), Born (the sac bursts)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Broadcast, Dead Air","u":"entities/the-turned.html#broadcast-dead-air","t":"Was Broadcast The set's cables gone into his spine, something pushing out through the cracked screen. Skipped Frame (he's next to you), Static (a burst all round), Signal (a beam off the screen: the dark), Cable (his arm of it lashed round you, reeling you in)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Lamb, Shorn","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-lamb-shorn","t":"Was the Little Lamb Long and thin on limbs like a spider's, its jaw split open. Latch (on you, gnawing), Cry , Scurry , Tongue (it reaches you and drags you in)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Hymnal, Unbound","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-hymnal-unbound","t":"Was the Hymnal A ribcage full of singing mouths, its pages grown out of its back. Hymn , Chorale (every mouth at once: a blast), Psalm (a beam of it), Pages (thrown like blades)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Underneath, Unearthed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-underneath-unearthed","t":"Was the Underneath Out of the ground for good, on six arms, a hand for a head with a mouth in its palm. Claw , Drag , Hands (up out of the ground under you), Down (into the ground, and up under you)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Antlerkin, Velvet-Torn","u":"entities/the-turned.html#antlerkin-velvet-torn","t":"Was the Antlerkin On four legs, the deer's skull split open on a bulb of eyes, its antlers a crown of bone. Gore (and tossed), Rack (swung round), Charge , Call (slow, the dark)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Bunnyman, Unstuffed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-bunnyman-unstuffed","t":"Was the Bunnyman Flesh where the stuffing was, a skull in the split plush head with incisors as long as fingers, the axe grown into his hand. Incisors , Chops , Hop , Hatchets (thrown)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Hookman, Unchained","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-hookman-unchained","t":"Was the Hookman A starved giant, a round mouth of hooked teeth, tendrils with a hook on every one. Sweep (low: slow), Drive (the hooks driven in), Hooks (thrown, and you're hauled in), Whirl ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Hogshead, Rendered","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-hogshead-rendered","t":"Was the Hogshead Bloated, two more pigs' heads out of his shoulders, the cleaver grown out of his arm. Cleaver , Fists (both, down), Squeal (all three: weak and slow), Charge ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Porcelain Man, Shattered","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-porcelain-man-shattered","t":"Was the Porcelain Man His glaze broken away in plates, a real eye behind his painted face, the music box in his chest a mouth, shards of him hanging round his shoulders. Burst (shards every way), There (when you look back), Shards (thrown), Music Box (slow, the dark)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Harvestman, Gone to Seed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-harvestman-gone-to-seed","t":"Was the Harvestman Roots trailing out of its sleeves, its sack of a head bursting with pods, a scythe and a sickle. Reap , Thresh , Seeds (spikes up where they land), Chaff (clouds of it)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Mothman, Pupated","u":"entities/the-turned.html#mothman-pupated","t":"Was Mothman Wings of skin covered in red eyes, a cocoon on its back. Snatch (up into the air, and dropped), Dive , Dust (off its wings: the dark, slow), Gaze (every eye on you: weak, the dark)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Jersey Devil, Hatched","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-jersey-devil-hatched","t":"Was the Jersey Devil Something half out of its chest, crawling out. Hooves , Tail (poison), Breath (fire and bile), Glide ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Dogman, Unleashed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#dogman-unleashed","t":"Was Dogman On all fours, its jaw split three ways, its ribs a mouth, a second pair of arms. Ribs (the mouth in them closes on you), Maul , Pounce , Howl (you can't move, and the dark)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Flatwoods Monster, Hooded","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-flatwoods-monster-hooded","t":"Was the Flatwoods Monster Its hood opened into a flower of flesh round the cracked red lamp of its face. Claws , Lift , Mist , Beam ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Rootling, Bloomed","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-rootling-bloomed","t":"Was a Rootling Its head burst into a flower of teeth, running on its roots. Leap , Thorns , Scream , Down and Up ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Great Flower, Overrun","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-great-flower-overrun","t":"Was the Great Flower Its petals crusted with eyes, the parasite's tendrils up out of its throat. Petals (slammed down), Throat (everything near dragged in), Tendrils (up out of the ground), Spores ."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Flytrap, Ravenous","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-flytrap-ravenous","t":"Was a Giant Flytrap Taller, a second trap lower down, its leaves toothed. Snap , Swallow , Leaves (lashed round), Spit (what it's digesting)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Mourner, Unveiled","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-mourner-unveiled","t":"Was a Mourner The death-mask hanging off a column of flesh with a mouth down it, its sleeves tentacles. Toll , Sleeves (reaching: weak), Grief (slow and weak), Shroud (clouds)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Interred, Unwound","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-interred-unwound","t":"Was an Interred Its shroud coming off in strips that move on their own, its jaw down to its chest. Bite (hungry), Linen (whirled), Rot (poison, hunger), Bound (roots round your feet)."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"The Pod, Hatched","u":"entities/the-turned.html#the-pod-hatched","t":"Was a Spore Pod Split open like a mouth, up on six tendrils. Latch , Burst , Spit , Rooted . Names as they appear in the game. Each form has its own model, animations, death, sounds and HD texture."},{"p":"The turned (the outbreak)","h":"Testing it","u":"entities/the-turned.html#testing-it","t":"With cheats on: /statichollow ending infest (the nearest creature has one in it), infest25 , infest50 , infest75 and infest95 (that far along), infestturn (it turns now), infestall (everything within 24 blocks turns), infestinfo and infestcure . For one of the Hollow's own, spawn it from its egg first, then infest and infestturn ."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"","u":"entities/the-undertow.html","t":"The Dead Water, the Black Below Can't be hurt Size Three thousand blocks long. Its head a hundred and twenty blocks long, its body fifty across. Health Nothing hurts it. Added in 1.63.0; made far bigger in 1.63.2; stalks, learns and feeds since 1.63.3 Lives At the bottom of the Black Below. Nothing else lives there. How to live Leave the Black Below. Then it turns away and sinks back into the depths."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#description","t":"The Dead Water has twelve waters. The last of them, the Black Below , is the abyss: near black, two hundred blocks deeper than the rest, and nothing alive in it but one thing. Down there there's only the sound of the ocean. Its head is a long armoured skull with heavy brows over nine pale glowing eyes down each side (two of them great and milky), horns sweeping back off it, broken bone spikes down its back and flanks, a torn crimson crest, and six long jointed feelers trailing under it. Its mouth is a ring of lips round a hole going down into it, with six long jaws round that, fanged all down their insides, their edges serrated and a hook at each tip. They shut to a point like a closed flower, and open out to show three rings of teeth grinding round against one another down its throat, and a sick red light at the bottom. Its body is lit with rows of cold lights. It never breaks a block: it goes through rock like water."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"It stalks you","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#it-stalks-you","t":"Stay deep in the Black Below and something notices, a rumble from below (\"Something vast is keeping pace with you, out in the dark.\"). It rises out of the dark and stalks you, out where you aren't looking, keeping pace. You can't see thirty blocks down there, but you can see its eyes : a cluster of pale cold points out in the black, two great ones among them, that turn as you turn, keep on you, blink, and slide by under you when it makes a pass. Up close its head's own eyes follow you too."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"It learns you","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#it-learns-you","t":"The longer it watches, the closer and lower it keeps. Run for the surface a few times and it learns to wait right under where you'll come back down. Carry a light for a while and it learns to keep out of it. It tells you, in the dark, as it learns: \"It has learned how you move.\" \"It saw you run for the surface. It will be waiting under you.\" \"It has learned your light. It keeps out of it.\" \"It knows you now.\" What it learns, it keeps."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"It eats when it's hungry","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#it-eats-when-its-hungry","t":"Its hunger grows while it's out, and stays between its comings (\"It is hungry.\"). Only when it's starving does it roar and come for you. Before that, if a whale is near, it eats the whale instead. Lost whales (Hymnbacks) wander into the Black Below now and then, singing in the dark. A hungry Undertow hunts them: it swings round, lunges, takes the whale crossways in its jaws and chews, the whale thrashing and crying, blood clouding the water, the rings of teeth in its throat grinding, then swallows it whole. Fed (\"It has fed. For now.\"), it goes back to watching you. A whale near when it's starving can save you."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"When it comes","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#when-it-comes","t":"Roar: it shakes the sea. A submarine's glass cracks and its power dies; your ears ring. Circle and lunge: it circles, then comes straight in, jaws opening like a flower, and swallows you whole , a submarine and all. Nothing comes back out (\"... was swallowed by the Undertow\"). Breach: run for the surface and it comes up after you, straight up out of the sea, hundreds of blocks into the sky with the length of it pouring up out of the water after it, arcs over and crashes back down in a column of water. The waves run out over the sea and throw everything floating about, and smash boats. It can take you on the way up. It goes back down into the depths only when you leave the Black Below."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Don't stay deep in the Black Below. Get in, get what you came for, get out sideways into another water. Watch for its eyes in the black. If they're turning with you, it's there. Change how you move. It learns the surface run and a carried light. Hymnbacks are your friends down there: a fed Undertow goes back to watching."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"The spawn egg","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#the-spawn-egg","t":"The Undertow Spawn Egg (creative) hatches one that stalks you, its eyes on you, now and then turning its head to roar with its jaws wide, and hunts and eats any whale near (hatch a Hymnback or two and watch). It never eats you. It's gone after ten minutes, or once you go far away."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"The Static Leviathan","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#the-static-leviathan","t":"The Hadal Dark and the Trench; deep in the Dead Water Boss Health 320, with its own bar Size Forty-five blocks long (since 1.63.2) Drops The Signal Organ, 3 to 6 bone blocks, 2 to 5 Needle Teeth and a heart of the sea Grey-blue plated hide, a blunt skull with little red eyes clustered down it, and fangs where its baleen was, hanging outside its jaw even when it's shut, with tusks and teeth in its lower jaw. Down its back a row of thin masts, a red light blinking at each one's tip one after another like the lights on a radio mast at night, and bone spines between them. Its ribs show through the rotted-away hide of its flanks; lamp-organs pulse down them. It roams the deepest water of the Overworld's oceans (the Trench, and the Hadal Dark now and then; see the deep oceans ). In the Dead Water, deep down, now and then one comes up out of the dark after you, except in the Black Below, which is the Undertow's. Song: a numbers station, slowed down and sung through a throat the size of a room, on the Remote's frequency. Everything near goes dark and slow while it sings. Charge: it slows, turns, its throat dropping open, then charges. Whatever it hits, it hits like a ship. Swallow: sometimes it takes you in. You're in its throat in the dark, being crushed, until you hurt it enough from in there to make it spit you out, or it does anyway. Its Signal Organ is what mends the Broken Remote in Chapter Eight (\"Mend it: this, a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ, a copper ingot.\"). Doing it earns Back On Air ."},{"p":"The Undertow","h":"The Mouth of the Floor","u":"entities/the-undertow.html#the-mouth-of-the-floor","t":"Buried in the Grey Shelf, the Ossuary Flats and the Molar Reef Ambusher Health 140, armoured Size Jaws eleven blocks long, thirty blocks across open (since 1.63.2) Drops 2 to 5 Needle Teeth, 2 to 6 bones and a Shroud Hide Something lies buried in the sea floor, with nothing of it showing but a ring of rocks (the tips of its jaws, crusted over like the floor) and, if you look close, a few yellow eyes in the silt between them. Pass over it and the floor shudders, and it comes up: eight jaws open out of the sand round a throat going down into the dark, with hooked teeth all down them, serrated edges and a fang at each tip, two rings of teeth round its throat and twelve yellow eyes round its rim. Four hooked tongues coiled down its throat rise and writhe as it opens. The water rushes in, and you with it, and it snaps shut and holds on, grinding, its tongues coiled round you. Then it spits out what's left and sinks back into the floor. It takes a submarine in its jaws too, and crushes it. It can only be hurt while it's up. Hurt it hard enough while it holds you and it lets go. A submarine's sonar shows where one lies."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"","u":"entities/the-viewer.html","t":"The Other Side, past the edge of the stage The last boss Health 1024, but it can't be killed What you fight Its eye and its hands. The rest of it is too big. Added in 1.58.0, Chapter Six part three: What He Kept Out Music What He Kept Out Status effect Seen: the edges of everything going white"},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#description","t":"Through the Door at the End of the World, its static gone black, is the Other Side : a stage behind the screen your world is on. Out in the dark past the stage's edge, sat, is something so big the dark has its shape: knees like hills, shoulders up in the black, a head you can't see the top of, its hands on the stage's edge with fingers like felled trees, and an eye . It's watched your world since the first picture anyone ever saw. Now it's seen you, and it wants to see you up close. The Watcher is there before you, at a projector. you came through. good. it hasn't looked this way. not yet. this is the other side. it's watched your world since the first picture. everything that ever happened to you - it watched. now it wants to see you up close. stay out of its eye. get behind the scenery. when it leans in - hit it. i'll run the projector. ??? Curtain Up"},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"Its gaze","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#its-gaze","t":"Its gaze wanders the stage, a pool of its light drifting toward whoever is out in the open. Stand in it with its eye in sight of you and you're Seen : the edges of everything go white, more and more. Seen right through, it reaches for you. A painted flat between you and the eye hides you. The stage is dressed with them, each a picture of somewhere from your story. Getting through the first third without ever being seen right through earns Out of Sight ."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#how-it-fights","t":"Lean: its head comes down out of the dark to the stage's edge, the eye right there. That's when to hit it: it takes half as much again. Slam: a hand lifted over you (its shadow on the boards first) and brought down. Jump the ring. Drum: its fingers along the front of the stage, one after another. Grab: it lifts you up in front of its eye (\"It's got you. It's looking right at you. (Hit the hand!)\"). Hit the hand and it lets go. Sweep (from two thirds down): a hand dragged low across the stage, through the scenery. Jump it. The flats it hits, or slams, are smashed to splinters. With its eye shut, nothing hurts it. Hit a hand and it feels half of it. Fire does nothing."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"Stand-ins","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#stand-ins","t":"Cut-outs of people (a man in a hat, a woman in a coat, an usher), painted plywood on little hinged stands, their backs bare boards and a strut (10 health). They come hopping out of the wings the way scenery is moved across a stage. They don't hurt you: they find you. One that sees you swings its arm up on its split pin and points , and the eye comes straight to you. Knock them over."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"His Last Projector","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#his-last-projector","t":"The Watcher runs it from the stage (\"His. He'll run it.\"). Twice he loads it: At two thirds: the Omni's Heart in its lamp. Every colour at once, thrown out over the dark into its eye. It reels , blinded: hit it then and it takes double. That earns Every Colour at Once . At one third: the Carrier through its gate. Your world, all of it, carried out on the beam onto it. The stand-ins burn, and it gets up . Stood, its gaze is quicker and its hands come more often, the footlights flicker and go out, and it reaches for the projector with both hands from either side. Beat them back. Being there earns It Gets Up ."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Move from flat to flat. Don't stand in its light with the eye in view. Knock the stand-ins over before they point. Hit the eye when it leans in, and hit it hard while it reels. In the last third, guard the projector: hit the hands that reach for it. If you fall off the edge, the dark puts you back on the boards (\"The dark doesn't keep you. You're back on the boards - it hurt.\")."},{"p":"The Viewer","h":"The last show","u":"entities/the-viewer.html#the-last-show","t":"It can't be killed. At the last it's held : it stops, and its eye goes to the projector. The Watcher threads his first reel and runs it, for it. everyone's always watched it. nobody ever showed it to itself. there. something to watch. it'll watch that forever. it won't look at your world again. somebody has to run the projector. go home. ...thank you for watching. ??? The Last Show Its own picture, on it. It goes still, sits back, and watches itself. The credits roll, you're sent home (the black door is static again), and you're given a record, Thank You for Watching . Seeing it earns the advancement of the same name. Chapter Six is done. The credits roll to their last line and stop. \"...not yet.\" His hand comes up through them and shuts round you. That's Chapter Seven ."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"","u":"entities/the-watcher.html","t":"Shown in game as ??? Never attacks Name in game ??? (its spawn egg is the \"??? Spawn Egg\") First seen The main menu; in the world, once the Forsaken Altar is awake Where Anywhere. At the edge of the trees, on the cathedral ceiling, right behind you Bleeds Never What it wants Stronger souls to pour its darkness through. It kept the Omni's heart, what was left of the Carrier and its own first reel \"for the future\", and used them to keep something out of your world. \"remember who you work for.\""},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"Description","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#description","t":"As it stands on the main menu. A tall, thin black figure with a square head and two pale eyes that glow and blink. The game names it only \"???\". It never attacks you. It stares, waves, points, peeks round things, crouches, and sometimes stands right behind you. It is in every chapter, and at every turning point it says a few words in chat in lower case. On the main menu it is somewhere different every time lightning strikes: far off on the hill, then among the graves, then right at the edge of the trees, then gone."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"What it does, chapter by chapter","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#what-it-does","t":""},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Nine","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-one","t":"It speaks after your first, fifth and ninth kill (it stares, then waves, then points), and after the ninth tells you about a church that isn't on any map. It hangs from the ceiling of the cathedral's nave. When the Hollow Saint reaches half health, it turns to it, a black sun swelling between its hands, and pours a crackling river of shadow into the Saint's heart. When the Saint dies its beam turns red and burns a portal to hell open under it. At midnight the cathedral's bell tolls thirteen, and on the thirteenth the Watcher is standing in the doorway."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Breach","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-two","t":"It meets you on the other side of the Breach, stands behind the Breach Altar to tell you what comes next, and waits on the ceiling of the Trophy Hall. When the nine heads are on their pedestals it comes down and sews them into the Mended, pouring its shadow into the knot."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Glasshouse","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-three","t":"It warns you about the Bloom's air, and begs you to leave the Binding alone."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Flesh","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-four","t":"It tells you what the Flesh is and how to kill it. Once the Gardener, Reborn is dead it walks to the shut Bloom, pushes its fingers between the petals and tears it open, and holds the rift open while you launch the Device. It wanted the Bloom to change: \"a soul that size is worth something.\" It pours itself into the Orbital Core, builds the Device or the Ray Gun for you at a Forsaken Altar if you ask, and turns the Ray Gun into the Omni. When the Omni Ray needs more power, it gives all of its own. Then it takes the Omni back into its realm and burns the Ray Gun's recipe. Ten days later it comes back, rested, and finds you wherever you are: at your window, down your mine, behind a tree, behind you. Anything in a mine trying to kill you, it lifts, twitching, and bursts into ink."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Static","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-five","t":"It hands out needles to Relay 6 and the Starlite, stands beside you during the late show to explain the Afterimages, and when the Carrier dies it takes its eye \"for the future\" and sends everyone home through a rift of its own. Half a minute after you're home it comes to where you're standing. It wasn't meant to go like this: the Carrier carried them all the way out, and the parasite's numbers are going off the charts. It shuts the End so you can't go there (anyone who goes through an End portal in survival is sent straight back out: \"not there. i told you.\"), and lets you know it can see you: ...actually. i'll make sure you can't go there. it's dangerous for you, player. you know i can see you right now, right, (your name)? remember who you work for. ??? after Signing Off After It Speaks it's beside you, and hands you its needle to the Hive. When the Chorus runs it tells you to keep the fragment and listen to it. When the Chorus, Whole is dead it tells you about the door at the end of the world: \"there's a door at the end of the world with a seal on it. i made that seal. i can't open it.\" / \"that voice can. when you're ready, take it to the end.\""},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Door at the End of the World","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-six","t":"Carry the Last Voice into the End and the seal it made breaks. It says one word: \"...don't.\" In the Stalls, when the Crowd is dead, it's sitting in the front row: \"it was a good show.\" It tears the screen open and goes through. Behind it is its Vault, its archive, where it sits at a desk under a wall of sets and watches the ones who watch your world: \"this is where i watch from.\" When the Projectionist is dead it runs its first reel and shows you what it kept out. On the Other Side it runs its last projector, loads the Omni's heart and the Carrier into it, and at the end runs its first reel for the Viewer, so that it will watch itself forever and never look at your world again. \"somebody has to run the projector.\" Then the credits roll."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The First Signal","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-seven","t":"At the end of the credits: \"...not yet.\" Its hand comes up through them and takes you to the Hub, a realm it made. \"i made it. a realm. it isn't mine - nothing is - but i made it.\" It thanks you, tells you it could wipe you out and find another one of you, and that it can make realms now, \"all thanks to you\". Then the First Signal breaks in. It tries to push the rift shut, shoves the First Signal five hundred blocks with everything it has, tells you to jump, and shuts the realm behind you with a wall of static. See the First Signal ."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Dead Water","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#in-chapter-eight","t":"Falling, it tears a portal open under you and brings you down on an oil rig in a dead green sea: \"i built this place a long time ago - for when i needed somewhere to hide.\" It gives you the Remote, and it breaks in your hand: \"...no. nothing of mine works right here.\" It tells you to fix it (\"the big ones down there sing on its frequency - cut out what they sing with\"), hands you its chart of the sea, and goes over the rail. See Chapter Eight ."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The seasons","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#the-seasons","t":"With Serene Seasons in the modpack (since 1.62.0), it notices each season turn the first time it does. In autumn: \"the leaves are turning. this was always their time of year. you'll hear them more now.\" In winter: \"it's getting cold. keep a fire going. they like the cold. it carries sound further.\""},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"More than one Watcher","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#the-watchers","t":"The Watcher can be in more than one place at once. While the Saint changes, the one on the cathedral ceiling pours its beam, and away from the cathedral another Watcher steps out of nothing somewhere it can see the Saint from. The README also calls that the \"Watchers' beam\"."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"Its places","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#its-realm","t":"When it takes the Omni back it tears the air open: a rift into its own realm, green fire licking up the edges, rings of its glyphs turning round it. It throws the gun in and the rift slams shut. Since Chapter Six you can go to some of its places yourself: The Watcher's Vault , behind the picture: its archive of film and tape, the Watch, and three keeps where it kept the Omni's heart, what was left of the Carrier and its first reel. The seal on the End and the Door at the End of the World , made of its black seal-stone with its glyphs cut in it. The Hub , a realm it made out of the First Signal's static. The rig in the Dead Water , built long ago for when it needed somewhere to hide."},{"p":"The Watcher","h":"The Watcher says","u":"entities/the-watcher.html#the-watcher-says","t":"the soul in the core... i needed one that strong. it's mine now. that was the price. go home. the hollow will be quiet for a while. ??? at the end of the railgun ending the static was a door. and this was holding it open. this, i'll keep. for the future. ??? taking the Carrier's eye i think we'll be fighting forever. until one day i'm strong enough to bring you up to my level. ??? in the Hub Every line it says is collected on The Watcher speaks ."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html","t":"Shelter No. 4, Bunker B, the north wall Boss Who he was The shelter's Civil Defence warden. Health 400 Wakes when The Front Assembly comes off its mount on the dais Size Twice a man's size, on four legs Music The Flesh's mini-boss music Weak to The overload switch (100 damage, once) Afterwards The Watcher leaves a locker on the dais with a Civil Defence Compass, bread, torches and a golden apple"},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Description","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#description","t":"When the Front Assembly comes off its mount, the north wall of Bunker B tears itself out. It's the shelter's Civil Defence warden and everyone who sheltered with him, grown into one mass on four legs: his body in the middle, still in his helmet and holding his torch, three more heads on necks round it, arms everywhere, and the frozen faces of the rest across it. Until then it sleeps in an alcove of the people fused into the wall. listen. the walls. the north wall. ??? in Bunker B"},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Getting there","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#getting-there","t":"Shelter No. 4 has no power. The two diesel generators are in the radio room; their fuel is wedged in the back of one of the shelter's lockers, a different one in every world, and the residents hiding in those lockers burst out at you. Fill both generators and pull each one's lever: twenty seconds of spinning up, loud enough that what's in the ducts comes out of the vents twice. Hold the room. With both running, the lights come on section by section, the radio switches from the evacuation notice to Control's emergency broadcast, and Bunker B's blast door opens. Inside is one great hall two storeys high: a gallery along the top, stairs down at either end into the pit, cover heaped across it, a channel of black water, the earthing plates under the gallery, and at the far end the dais with the Front Assembly on its mount. The special forces squad holds it: the sniper up on the gallery, operators and a breacher about the pit, and their Squad Leader by the dais."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"How it fights","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#how-it-fights","t":"Slam: it rears up, bellows and charges, and comes down where you were. If it charges into a wall instead, it's dazed for two seconds and takes half as much again from everything. Mouths: all four heads bite, one after another, sweeping round in front of it. Grabs: it slams its hands into the floor and arms burst out of the walls round you: cracks first, then a hand that grabs and holds you while the Flesh gets into you. At half health it floods the pit: blood up to the knee with the Flesh in it. Get out of it, up the stairs to the gallery."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"The overload switch","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#the-overload-switch","t":"Control's emergency broadcast tells you what to do. The overload switch is on the gallery over the earthing plates. Get the Warden onto the plates while both generators run, and throw it: every volt in the shelter goes through it, 100 damage once, and it stands there shaking for three seconds. Thrown with no Warden on the plates, it only fries the infected down there."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Emergency broadcast","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#emergency-broadcast","t":"Rosemont Civil Defence Control, on the Shelter Radio Set The radio room Shelter Four, Shelter Four, this is Control. We see your power on. Respond. Shelter Four, do not open the vault. Repeat: do not open the vault. Whatever is in bunk hall B is not your residents any more. Whatever the squad told you, they are not coming back up. If anyone down there can hear this - the overload switch, over the plates in bunker B. Get it onto the plates. Shelter Four, respond."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"How to survive it","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#how-to-survive-it","t":"Clear the squad first if you can. The sniper's laser on the gallery gives it away. Bait the Slam into a wall, then hit it while it's dazed. Watch the walls for cracks: that's where an arm is about to come through. When the pit floods, go up. The overload switch is up there anyway. Bloom Serum or the hazmat suit help with the Flesh its hands put into you. keep moving. keep the cover between you and it. the plates under the gallery. get it onto them, and throw the switch up there. get out of the blood. up the stairs - the gallery. that hurt it. it won't walk into that twice. ??? during the fight"},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Afterwards","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#afterwards","t":"Kill it and the Watcher leaves you a locker on the dais with a Civil Defence Compass in it, its needle set on Rosemont wherever you are, and some bread, torches and a golden apple. i've left you something. on the dais, by the mount. a compass. it points at the city. rosemont. that's where you go next. ??? after the Warden dies"},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Field notes","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#field-notes","t":"A Warden's Log signed J. Pike was found in the Bloom, on the island where a Shelter No. 4 ended up: \"Day 9. The whole shelter tipped. I looked out of the door and there was no street. There was green all the way down, and something at the bottom of it, opening and shutting.\" Read the whole log . It drops two Bloom Serums, three Flower Ash Bombs, four to six Tainted Meat and two Flashbangs."},{"p":"The Warden of Shelter No. 4","h":"Turned","u":"entities/warden-of-shelter-no-4.html#turned","t":"Since 1.51.0 the parasite can take it, which it never could before. Turned, it's the Warden, Unhoused : its four heads up on long necks, a mouth down the whole front of the mound, six arms out of its sides."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Getting started","u":"faq.html#getting-started","t":""},{"p":"FAQ","h":"My world doesn't look grey and foggy.","u":"faq.html#my-world-doesnt-look-different","t":"Make a new world. The grey sky, murky water and dark clouds are part of world data, so worlds made with older versions keep their old sky. With a shader pack on, the pack draws the sky and fog itself; use the \"-StaticHollow\" copy of Photon, Insanity or Hysteria."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I updated, but there are no deep oceans or new biomes.","u":"faq.html#no-deep-oceans","t":"The oceans two thousand blocks deep and the Hollow's own country (1.62.0) only come in new worlds. A world made before keeps the land it has; everything else in 1.62 comes to old worlds too. (1.63's new Dead Water is the same: a world that has already been out there keeps the sea it has seen, and only the sea it hasn't is new.)"},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where is the Forsaken Altar?","u":"faq.html#where-is-the-forsaken-altar","t":"500 to 1000 blocks from the world spawn, on open, flat, dry ground: never underground, in water or on a mountainside. Follow the blue smoke from its soul campfire. The ruin rises when you come within about 90 blocks. With cheats: /locate structure statichollow:forsaken_altar . Since 1.63.2 you can also craft a Forsaken Altar Compass (a compass, a candle and a bone)."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Nothing is hunting me.","u":"faq.html#nothing-is-hunting-me","t":"The creepypastas only come once the altar is awake: right-click it with an empty hand. They hunt mostly in the dark."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where's the church that isn't on any map?","u":"faq.html#where-is-the-church","t":"The cathedral is 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn, roughly the opposite way from the altar. It isn't there until you come within about 90 blocks. With cheats: /locate structure statichollow:cathedral . See the cathedral ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I killed one but didn't get its head.","u":"faq.html#i-need-another-head","t":"The first kill of each creature always drops its head, but only if a player killed it (your arrows count). After that it's 10%, plus 5% per level of Looting. Since 1.60.0 you can wear any head: its own kind notice you from only half as far off."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Playing","u":"faq.html#playing","t":""},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The Underneath never comes up under my bed.","u":"faq.html#the-underneath-never-comes","t":"Only once the altar is awake, about four times in ten that you lie down, and always the next time after you've heard it breathing. Never in Creative or on Peaceful."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The creatures can't hurt me.","u":"faq.html#creepypastas-cant-hurt-me","t":"You're in Creative. Hostile creepypastas can't hurt you there. Test in Survival."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The green rift didn't open.","u":"faq.html#the-green-rift-didnt-open","t":"It opens three days after the Gardener dies, by the world's clock (nights you sleep through count), and you need to be within about 80 blocks of his flower. With cheats: /statichollow bloom open ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I lost a reactor part (or the Device).","u":"faq.html#i-lost-a-reactor-part","t":"There's only one of each. Lose one and it goes back where you found it (the Rear Assembly a minute later); the Device goes back to where you last set it down once nobody has had it for a minute. Any copy crumbles in your hands."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The Bloom ate me. Am I dead?","u":"faq.html#the-bloom-ate-me","t":"Not yet. Since 1.38 you go down alive into its stomach. Hack at the stomach wall ten times and it throws you back up."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I died of the Flesh and lost everything.","u":"faq.html#i-died-of-the-flesh","t":"You didn't. What got up where you fell is you, as one of the infected, wearing your armour and carrying everything you had. Kill it and you get it all back. It never despawns."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where are the guns?","u":"faq.html#where-are-the-guns","t":"The Mended guns are Fabric only, through Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero (TaCZ), which the Fabric modpacks install. Special forces infected sometimes drop theirs. Without TaCZ, and on Forge, nothing drops."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"My Mended gun stopped firing.","u":"faq.html#my-gun-stopped-working","t":"The Mended guns are the Bloom's flesh. Once the Bloom is dead, every one off its blight rots over ten minutes and then jams for good. Its tooltip says how far gone it is."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where did the Omni go?","u":"faq.html#where-did-the-omni-go","t":"The Watcher took it back into its realm, \"for the future\". The gun is gone for good, and so is the Ray Gun's recipe. You'll see its heart again in chapter six ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"There's something on the back of my neck.","u":"faq.html#something-on-my-neck","t":"A Parasite. Crouch or get hit to tear it off within four seconds. If it gets in, cut it out with a Surgical Kit or burn it out before it's three quarters grown. See the Parasite ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The animals (and villagers, and golems) are twitching and going violet.","u":"faq.html#animals-twitching","t":"That's the outbreak (1.48.0). Once the Bloom is dead, anything can carry a parasite: two days for an ordinary creature, three for the big ones, and then it turns and hunts everything that isn't one of them. A Surgical Kit cuts one out of anything before it turns. Burn a turned one when you kill it, or the parasites in it come out. See the turned ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"There's a heap of violet flesh where something died.","u":"faq.html#violet-heap","t":"Biomass. It isn't dead: a minute or two later, with anyone about, it gets up as one of the parasite's pure forms. Burn it (fire or lava against it) and nothing gets up."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I can't get into the End.","u":"faq.html#cant-get-into-the-end","t":"After the Null Static Zone signs off, the Watcher shuts it: anyone who goes through an End portal in Survival is sent straight back to their bed or the world's spawn (\"The way's shut. He shut it.\"). It opens again for everyone once someone carries the Last Voice into it, the one thing left when the Chorus, whole, dies in the Warm Heart. See chapter five ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where does chapter six start?","u":"faq.html#where-is-chapter-six","t":"In the End, once the seal's broken: out past the obsidian you arrive on, a causeway of black seal-stone runs east to an island with a Door on it, full of static. Walk into it. See the Door at the End of the World . If the Door isn't there, update: before 1.60.1 only a Last Voice from that world's own Chorus would open the seal, and since 1.60.2 the Door is never buried in end stone."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Why does the Ender Dragon look like that?","u":"faq.html#the-ender-dragon-changed","t":"Since 1.61.1 it's always the Infested Ender Dragon, from the first time anyone goes to the End: violet veins, blisters, spurs, tendrils, its back split open between its wings, and half again the health. It still fights as the dragon does, but over you it rains its brood down, lobs spore bombs and lashes its tendrils. Killed, it bursts."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The Chorus keeps healing.","u":"faq.html#the-chorus-keeps-healing","t":"It draws through its cords to its four nerve nodes. Tear the nodes open (they glow; climb the steps round the stalks) and every one makes it easier to hurt. Since 1.53.0 it only mends itself when nobody's near and it hasn't been hurt for half a minute. See the Chorus ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How do I get back to the Hub?","u":"faq.html#back-to-the-hub","t":"With the Remote , the old television remote the Watcher gives you as you come down from it. Use it to go into the Hub; use it there to go home (or jump off the edge). Its replay portals take you back to any chapter's last fight. See the Hub ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How do I get home from the Dead Water?","u":"faq.html#home-from-the-dead-water","t":"Mend the Remote: craft the Broken Remote with a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ and a copper ingot. The leviathans live deep. Then press it to go to the Hub (and in the Hub, home); crouch and press it to come back to the rig. Until then you're stranded: the rig's beds set your spawn but can't be slept in, and if you die without one the sea brings you back to the quarters. See chapter eight ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I finished the Hub before 1.62. How do I get to the Dead Water?","u":"faq.html#never-went-to-the-dead-water","t":"Take the Remote to the Hub and jump off its edge."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I lost the submarine.","u":"faq.html#lost-the-submarine","t":"The console on the sub bay's catwalk (the clamp) builds another for 16 iron ingots and 8 glass. Its clamp charges it and mends its hull. See the Dead Water ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"It won't let me sleep.","u":"faq.html#cant-sleep","t":"Not in the story's other places: the Null Static Zone, the Deep, the Stalls (\"Not with them watching.\"), the Vault, the Other Side or the Hub. The rig's beds set your spawn but you can't sleep in them."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"I keep getting thirsty, or freezing.","u":"faq.html#always-thirsty","t":"That's the cold and the thirst (1.62.0). Drink from bottles, a Canteen, the rain or your cupped hands at the water's edge, and boil murky water first. Wear leather in the cold and stand near a fire. To turn either off or soften it, edit config/statichollow-vitals.properties . See cold, thirst and the world ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Where's Minecraft's music?","u":"faq.html#no-minecraft-music","t":"Since 1.55.0 none of it plays: the mod's own plays in its place, the lullaby of the place you're in or a piece for how far the story has got. Minecraft's Music volume and Music Frequency still work. See the soundtrack ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Can I get rid of the Great Bloom?","u":"faq.html#can-i-remove-the-great-bloom","t":"Only with /kill (it doesn't come back). Finishing chapter four kills it, but leaves its husk where it stood."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How do I reset the haunting for a world?","u":"faq.html#reset-the-haunting","t":"Close the world and delete statichollow.properties in its save folder."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Technical","u":"faq.html#technical","t":""},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Fabric or Forge?","u":"faq.html#fabric-or-forge-faq","t":"Both play the same story. Fabric is made for shaders and has the guns, Streams and Essential support. See the comparison ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"What's the Dead Channel modpack?","u":"faq.html#what-is-dead-channel","t":"The Fabric modpack as it is on CurseForge. It downloads the mod and its HD and shader packs as their own CurseForge projects. See the Dead Channel modpack ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Can I play with friends?","u":"faq.html#can-i-play-with-friends","t":"Yes: on a server, on LAN, or on Fabric with the Essential mod. Everyone needs the same version, and since 1.62 the server also needs Biomes O' Plenty, Serene Seasons, Puddles & Floods and the rest. Forge and Fabric players can't share a server. See Playing with friends ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Do shaders work on Forge?","u":"faq.html#shaders-on-forge","t":"Through Oculus, which as of October 2026 only goes up to Minecraft 26.2. Shaders will work once it's updated for 26.3. The Fabric version has them now."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"How much memory does it need?","u":"faq.html#how-much-memory","t":"8 GB. The modpacks ask CurseForge for it since 1.63.2; if yours doesn't, set it in the modpack's ... menu, Profile Options, Allocated Memory."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The game stutters.","u":"faq.html#the-game-stutters","t":"Give it 8 GB of memory, turn off the HD-World pack, and lower Mipmap Levels. With shaders, lower the shadow resolution to 1024. See If it runs slowly ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"My mouse, hotbar and inventory stopped working after the Hub.","u":"faq.html#controls-stopped-after-the-hub","t":"Before 1.59.1 the Hub's cutscene could leave its invisible picture over your screen when it went straight into the landing. Update, and if it happened to you, close the game once and start it again."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Is Sound Physics Remastered on?","u":"faq.html#sound-physics","t":"It's in the modpacks but switched off, because since 1.61.1 the mod gives every sound its own echo and muffling. Set enabled=true in config/sound_physics_remastered/soundphysics.properties to use it instead. See every sound, where it is ."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"A boss's bar stays on my screen.","u":"faq.html#boss-bar-stuck","t":"Fixed in 1.47.2 and 1.53.0: a boss now takes its bar down however it goes (killed, gone or unloaded), and you lose its bar as soon as you stop seeing it. Update."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Are the HD packs made with AI?","u":"faq.html#are-the-hd-packs-ai","t":"The upscaling is. The HD packs are the mod's own textures upscaled to double resolution with an AI upscaler (Real-ESRGAN), then given their original grit back so nothing looks plastic. They're optional."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Cutscenes don't play in the modpack.","u":"faq.html#cutscenes-dont-play","t":"Update to 1.47.1 or later. Entity Culling stopped them before (the cutscene's marker is invisible, so it was never ticked)."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"The game crashed when I used the Relay Core with shaders on.","u":"faq.html#crash-with-relay-core","t":"\"Source format is missing element iris_Entity\". Fixed in 1.47.1, along with the same crash from the Brood Heart, the Dead Channel Helm and the Static Mail."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"A new world hangs on \"Preparing for world creation\".","u":"faq.html#world-wont-start","t":"Fixed in 1.24.1 and 1.26.1. Since then every build is checked by starting a test world, and one bad file can no longer stop a world. Update."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Does it work with Simple Voice Chat?","u":"faq.html#voice-chat","t":"Not yet. It's on the README's \"not yet\" list: creatures replaying things players said."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Why does the inventory look normal?","u":"faq.html#inventory-look","t":"The inventory, hotbar and font keep the normal Minecraft look for now. The main menu and its buttons are new."},{"p":"FAQ","h":"Who is \"???\"","u":"faq.html#what-is-question-marks","t":"The Watcher."},{"p":"Home","h":"","u":"index.html","t":"PLAY ▶ 0:00:00 Static Hollow i see you Something answered when you lit the altar. Find a Forsaken Altar in the world. Wake it. Then try to survive what it lets in. Download on CurseForge Start with chapter one Install the modpack"},{"p":"Home","h":"What Static Hollow is","u":"index.html#what-it-is","t":"Static Hollow is a creepypasta horror mod for Minecraft 26.3, made by Death, with its own CurseForge modpacks. It turns the whole game into something that is watching you, and then it tells a story in eight chapters that starts with nine creepypastas and, so far, leaves you stranded on an oil rig in a dead green sea. The world itself is wrong from the first minute: a grey, bruised sky, murky black-green water, a red sun and a full moon with a face. The fog is thick and cold, about 64 blocks of sight by day and about 18 at night. Every block, item and creature is redrawn at four times normal resolution, drained and darker. Every animal and monster in the game is rebuilt as a jointed 3D model with real wet eyes that dart, blink and, at night, stop and look back at you. The Enderman screams with its head lifted off a glowing maw of teeth. None of Minecraft's music plays any more, only the mod's own, and you have to keep warm and find clean water. Then you find the altar. The mod's CurseForge cover art."},{"p":"Home","h":"The eight chapters","u":"index.html#the-chapters","t":"The story is told in order. Each chapter starts when the one before it ends, and the Watcher points you to the next place."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Nine","u":"index.html#the-nine","t":"Starts when you wake the Forsaken Altar Nine creepypastas hunt everyone in the world, mostly in the dark. Take one head from each to the church that isn't on any map, and raise the Hollow Saint."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Breach","u":"index.html#the-breach","t":"Starts when the Hollow Saint falls A red wound opens where it died. Through it, the Void and the Breach Altar; back home, five killers and four cryptids, the Murder Mansion and the Mended."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Glasshouse","u":"index.html#the-glasshouse","t":"Starts with the Mended's rusted garden key The Gardener kneels at the great flower under the dome. Three days after he dies, a green rift opens down to what the flower really is: the Great Bloom."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Flesh","u":"index.html#the-flesh","t":"Starts ten seconds after the Great Bloom rises What the flower was holding down punches up out of the ground. Rosemont, the Laboratory, Shelter No. 4, the Rosemont Device, the Gardener reborn twice, and a gun above the sky."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Static","u":"index.html#the-static","t":"Starts once the Bloom is dead The Flesh dies back, but the parasites are still out there, and the static isn't noise. Relay 6, the Starlite Drive-In and the Null Static Zone; then the outbreak, the Hive and its Chorus, and the Deep under everything."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Door at the End of the World","u":"index.html#the-door-at-the-end-of-the-world","t":"Starts when you carry the Last Voice into the End The Watcher sealed the End for a reason. A Door full of static, the Stalls and their silent Audience, his Vault behind the picture, and on the other side, what he kept out."},{"p":"Home","h":"The First Signal","u":"index.html#the-first-signal","t":"Starts after the last show's credits His hand comes up through the credits and takes you into the Hub, a realm he made, with a portal back to every chapter. Then something older than him breaks in."},{"p":"Home","h":"The Dead Water","u":"index.html#the-dead-water","t":"Starts as you fall from the Hub He tears a portal open under you, onto an oil rig in a sea that goes on forever. The Remote breaks in your hand. Twelve waters, a submarine called Orpheus, and something that comes up out of the Black Below."},{"p":"Home","h":"What's new since 1.47","u":"index.html#whats-new","t":"The wiki was first written for 1.47.1. Sixteen versions later, this is what came: Version What came 1.48–1.53 The outbreak. Anything can carry the parasite now, and turns: its pure forms, the biomass, the mutations, the infested bosses and every one of the Hollow's own, turned. See the turned . 1.50, 1.53 Chapter five, part five: the Hive. The Hive , its hands, and the Chorus . After signing off, the End is shut. 1.54 Chapter five, part six: the Deep. The Sinkhole and the Deep , the Listeners, the Deaf King and the Chorus, whole. 1.55 The music. The mod's own, in place of Minecraft's, following the story. See the soundtrack . 1.56–1.58 Chapter six: the Door at the End of the World. The Stalls and the Crowd , the Watcher's Vault and the Projectionist , the Other Side and the Viewer . 1.59 Chapter seven: the First Signal. The Hub , its replays, and the First Signal . 1.60–1.61 Gear for every chapter. Seven armour sets, fourteen weapons and twenty-eight tools, every one swung its own way. Heads you can wear. Every sound given the echo of where it is. See gear for every chapter . 1.62 Chapter eight: the Dead Water. The rig and the Broken Remote. Oceans two thousand blocks deep and the Hollow's own country . The cold and the thirst, the seasons, puddles, floods, erosion and streams: see cold, thirst and the world . 1.63 The Dead Water, wider. Twelve waters and what lives in them, the submarine Orpheus, the Watcher's chart, three new compasses, and the Undertow . See the Dead Water ."},{"p":"Home","h":"At a glance","u":"index.html#at-a-glance","t":"Current version 1.63.3 \"The Undertow stalks you\" Minecraft 26.3 Fabric Loader 0.19.5 with Fabric API 0.161.0+26.3 Forge 66.0.9 separate build, plays the same Java 25 Memory 8 GB the modpacks ask CurseForge for it Modpack Static Hollow - Dead Channel Fabric, on CurseForge Made by Death On CurseForge: Static Hollow (the mod), and the optional packs HD Models , HD World , Shader PBR and Visuals ."},{"p":"Home","h":"Find your way","u":"index.html#find-your-way","t":"Bestiary Every creature and boss, from the Hollow Neighbor to the Undertow. Locations The cathedral, the Murder Mansion, Rosemont, Relay 6, the drive-in, the Stalls, the Hub, the Dead Water and the rest. Items and blocks The Relay Core, the needles, the power source parts, the Remote, and gear for every chapter. Notes and books Every page left on a lectern or in a chest, word for word. Advancements From Not Collected to Back On Air. The soundtrack All 63 pieces, and when each one plays. Cold, thirst and the world Warmth, water, the seasons, and a world that moves. Install and play The modpacks, servers, LAN, shaders and the HD packs."},{"p":"Home","h":"From the archive","u":"index.html#from-the-archive","t":"Screenshots from the mod's CurseForge page, in story order. The ones marked with a pack were taken with that optional pack on. The Hollow Saint Chapter one The Antlerkin Chapter one In the fog The Flatwoods Monster A face in the village The Flatwoods Monster The Mended Chapter two The Mended, up close HD Models pack In the fields The Harvestman Wings in the fog Mothman Out on the moor The glasshouse HD Models pack Botanic gardens HD World pack The Great Bloom Chapter four Swallowed alive The Great Bloom Flesh and stone HD World pack Under the flesh Chapter four The Chorus Chapter five Replay portals HD World pack The Hub Chapter seven The First Signal Chapter seven Orpheus, the submarine Chapter eight Glowing rift Shader PBR pack"},{"p":"Home","h":"Before your first night","u":"index.html#before-your-first-night","t":"Make a new world. The grey sky, murky water and dark clouds are part of the world's data, so a world made with an older version keeps its old sky. Follow the blue smoke. The Forsaken Altar is 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn on open, flat, dry ground, and a soul campfire burns at it. Don't look at the Broadcast. Staring at its screen burns you every second, and touching it shocks you. Get out of bed. If something knocks three times under the floor, use Leave Bed within about four seconds. Make a canteen. String, leather and an iron ingot. Fill it in the rain, or boil it before you drink. Listen to the Watcher. It never attacks. After your first, fifth and ninth kill it has something to say. nine. do you know what nine heads are for? there is a church that isn't on any map. find it. i'll be on the ceiling. ??? after your ninth kill"},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"","u":"install.html","t":"Static Hollow 1.63.3 is for Minecraft 26.3 and comes in two builds that play the same: Fabric (made for shaders, with guns) and Forge . The easiest way in is a CurseForge modpack. Whatever you do, start a new world, and give the game 8 GB of memory."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Quick start","u":"install.html#quick-start","t":""},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Install the CurseForge app","u":"install.html#install-the-curseforge-app","t":"From curseforge.com, and sign in."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Install the modpack","u":"install.html#install-the-modpack","t":"Search for Static Hollow - Dead Channel in the app and click Install (see the Dead Channel modpack ). If you have a modpack as a .zip instead, import it under My Modpacks. If the modpack doesn't show up yet, make your own profile instead (Create Custom Profile, Minecraft 26.3, Fabric) and add Static Hollow to it."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Give it 8 GB of memory","u":"install.html#give-it-8-gb-of-memory","t":"The modpacks ask CurseForge for 8 GB since 1.63.2. If yours doesn't have it: the modpack's ... menu, Profile Options, Allocated Memory. Running short is what causes the stutters."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Play","u":"install.html#play","t":"Launch it from the app. The Fabric packs come with Iris, Sodium and the Photon shader pack already switched on and set up for Static Hollow."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Make a new world","u":"install.html#make-a-new-world","t":"The grey sky, murky water and dark clouds are part of world data, so worlds made with older versions keep their old sky. The oceans two thousand blocks deep and the Hollow's own country (1.62.0) also only come in new worlds; everything else comes to old worlds too."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Find the altar","u":"install.html#find-the-altar","t":"500 to 1000 blocks from spawn. Follow the blue smoke."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"On CurseForge","u":"install.html#on-curseforge","t":"Static Hollow , the mod itself (Fabric builds) Static Hollow: HD Models , HD World , Shader PBR and Visuals , the optional resource packs"},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"The Static Hollow - Dead Channel modpack","u":"install.html#dead-channel","t":"Static Hollow - Dead Channel is the Fabric modpack as it goes up on CurseForge. Version 1.63.3 is for Fabric Loader 0.19.5 and asks for 8 GB. Instead of carrying the mod inside the pack, it downloads it from CurseForge along with the mod's three resource packs, each its own project: Static Hollow 1.63.3 (Fabric) Static Hollow: HD Models and Static Hollow: Shader PBR, both switched on Static Hollow: HD World, installed but left off and the same mods as the Fabric modpack below, except Water Erosion and Cinematic Interactions , which aren't on its list. It sets the same shader (the Static Hollow copy of Photon), the same resource pack order and a render distance of 12 with a simulation distance of 8."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Fabric or Forge?","u":"install.html#fabric-or-forge","t":"Fabric Forge Loader Fabric Loader 0.19.5, Fabric API 0.161.0+26.3 Forge 66.0.9 Mod file statichollow-fabric-1.63.3.jar statichollow-1.63.3.jar Modpacks Static Hollow - Dead Channel (on CurseForge); \"Static Hollow (Fabric + Shaders)\" when you build it yourself \"Static Hollow\" Shaders Iris and Sodium with Photon, set up and switched on Need Oculus, which only goes up to Minecraft 26.2 (as of October 2026) The Mended guns Yes, with TaCZ (in the modpack) No Streams: Reflowing Yes No Puddles & Floods, Water Erosion, Cinematic Interactions Yes Yes, as builds made for the pack (none of them has a Forge 26.3 build of its own) Host online without a server Yes, with the Essential mod No (Essential is Fabric-only on 26.3); LAN works Story The same in both. Forge and Fabric players can't share a server. Pick one version for everyone."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"What's in the Fabric modpack","u":"install.html#whats-in-the-fabric-modpack","t":"Static Hollow 1.63.3 (Fabric) Fabric API 0.161.0+26.3 Sodium 0.9.2 and Iris Shaders 1.11.7 Lithium 0.26.2 (faster game logic) Entity Culling 1.11.2 (skips drawing creatures hidden behind walls) Photon v1.3b, Hysteria v1.2.2 and Insanity v1.650 (shader packs, downloaded unmodified) Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero (TaCZ) [Unofficial] Refabricated 1.1.8 for 26.3, and Forge Config API Port 26.3.1, which it needs First-person Model 2.7.3 and Not Enough Animations 1.12.6 (your own body in first person) Sound Physics Remastered 1.5.1, installed but switched off: since 1.61.1 the mod does every sound's echo and muffling itself ( how to switch it back ) Biomes O' Plenty 26.3.0.0.15 (beta), with TerraBlender 26.3.0.0.9 and GlitchCore 26.3.0.0.5. The Hollow's own biomes come into the world through TerraBlender. Serene Seasons 26.1.2.0.7 for 26.3 (beta), with Static Hollow's season settings Puddles & Floods 1.1.6 Water Erosion, ported to 26.3 for this pack Streams: Reflowing 2.15.2 Cinematic Interactions 0.18.7, in a build made for this pack"},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"What's in the Forge modpack","u":"install.html#whats-in-the-forge-modpack","t":"Static Hollow 1.63.3 Sound Physics Remastered, installed but switched off, as on Fabric Biomes O' Plenty, TerraBlender and GlitchCore Serene Seasons Puddles & Floods 1.1.6, ported to Forge 26.3 for this pack Water Erosion, ported to 26.3 for this pack Cinematic Interactions 0.18.7, built for Forge from its Fabric source over a small layer that answers its Fabric calls with Forge's. If one of its changes clashes with Forge's own, that part is skipped rather than the game failing. What the new mods do in the game is on cold, thirst and the world ."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Playing with friends","u":"install.html#multiplayer","t":""},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"On a server","u":"install.html#dedicated-server","t":"Everyone joining uses the matching modpack. The world's land, seasons, puddles and streams are the server's, so those mods go on the server too. Fabric: install the Fabric server for Minecraft 26.3 (Loader 0.19.5) and put these in its mods folder: statichollow-fabric-1.63.3.jar and Fabric API 0.161.0+26.3 for the guns, Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero 1.1.8 for 26.3 and Forge Config API Port 26.3.1 Puddles & Floods 1.1.6 Biomes O' Plenty, TerraBlender, GlitchCore, Serene Seasons and Streams: Reflowing, from CurseForge watererosion-26.3-sh.1-fabric.jar and cinematic-interactions-0.18.7+statichollow.1-fabric-26.3.jar (in the project's output folder and the modpack's mods) Forge: install the Forge 66.0.9 server for Minecraft 26.3 and put these in its mods folder: statichollow-1.63.3.jar puddleflood-1.1.6+26.3-forge.jar , watererosion-26.3-sh.1-forge.jar and cinematic-interactions-0.18.7+statichollow.1-forge-26.3.jar (the last two are in the output folder; all three are in the modpack's mods) Biomes O' Plenty, TerraBlender, GlitchCore and Serene Seasons, from CurseForge Iris, Sodium, Photon and Sound Physics Remastered are client-only: don't put them on the server."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Without a server","u":"install.html#lan-and-essential","t":"Open your world to LAN ( Esc , then Open to LAN), or on Fabric host it over the internet with the Essential mod (on CurseForge for Fabric 26.3, client-only). Either way it plays exactly like a server: everyone needs the same version of Static Hollow (and TaCZ, for the guns). Since 1.43.6 everything the mod shows comes from the server, so a friend who joins your world sees what you see."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Shaders","u":"install.html#shaders","t":"The Fabric modpacks have Photon switched on already. With a shader pack, every glow in the mod (eyes, antenna bulbs, the Saint's Crown orb, runes, portals, beams) shines as a real light with bloom. Pick the Static Hollow copy. If Photon v1.3b, Insanity v1.650 or Hysteria v1.2.2 is in your shaderpacks folder, the mod makes a copy of each when the game starts with \"-StaticHollow\" on the end of its name. Choose that one: its grass and flowers sway as one piece, it knows the mod's garden blocks, and it draws the Void, the Bloom and the Hub properly. The copies are made on your computer for your own use; don't upload them anywhere. Photon is the one made to work with every part of the mod. The PBR pack. StaticHollow-Shader-PBR.zip is a resource pack of LabPBR normal and specular maps for every block: bumpy stone, glossy mud, metal that reflects, light pouring out of torches and lava. The Fabric modpacks switch it on. On Forge, turn it on in Options, Resource Packs, with a shader pack that uses LabPBR materials. Change the look in Options, Video Settings, Shader Packs, Shader Pack Settings. Too slow? Pick the Medium or Low profile there (the Static Hollow colours, fog and water stay), or lower the shadow resolution to 1024. K turns shaders off, and the mod's own grey sky and fog come back. Forge: shaders need Oculus, and as of October 2026 Oculus only goes up to Minecraft 26.2. Glowing rift With shaders and the Shader PBR pack on."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"The HD packs","u":"install.html#hd-packs","t":"Everything is already redrawn at four times normal resolution. Two optional resource packs go further, AI-upscaled to double resolution with Real-ESRGAN and then given their original grit back: StaticHollow-HD-Models.zip : every creature, their heads, the weapons, armour and items, the cathedral's blocks, the main menu and the effects. StaticHollow-HD-World.zip : every block and item of the look at 128×128, the paintings, the sun and the moon. Since 1.61.0 the HD pack has the chapter gear (the weapons, the tools and the seven armour sets, held and worn) at four times the mod's own resolution, and since 1.63.1 the Dead Water's blocks and plants at 256 px. Since 1.63.2 its item textures are capped at 512 px, which made the game start faster and stutter less. Fabric modpacks: HD-Models is switched on for you. HD-World is installed but left off, because the shader maps are drawn for the normal block size. To try it, go to Options, Resource Packs, move it to the right-hand side below Shader-PBR, and click Done. The modpack sets the pack order (vanilla, Static Hollow, HD-Models, Shader-PBR). In Dead Channel the three packs come as their own CurseForge projects. Forge: move both to the right-hand side in Options, Resource Packs. The order doesn't matter. They need more video memory: if the game stutters, turn HD-World off first. With shaders on, HD-World's blocks use the normal-size bump maps, stretched to fit."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"If it runs slowly","u":"install.html#performance","t":"Give the game 8 GB of memory (the modpack's ... menu, Profile Options, Allocated Memory). With shaders, lower the shadow resolution to 1024, then the render distance to 10 (the pack sets 12), then turn HD-World off. Lower Mipmap Levels in Video Settings. Turn off StaticHollow-HD-World.zip , then HD-Models. If new chunks are slow to appear on Fabric, pick a lower quality preset in Streams: Reflowing's settings (in the config folder). If you switched Sound Physics Remastered back on, turn its rays and bounces down in config/sound_physics_remastered/soundphysics.properties . Camera shake and zoom follow your Screen Effect Scale and FOV Effects settings. Hide Lightning Flashes (Accessibility) keeps the main menu's flashes dim."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Building it yourself","u":"install.html#building-it-yourself","t":"For the mod's own project folders: Install Java 25 (Temurin, from adoptium.net). On Windows double-click BUILD-MODPACK.bat ; on Mac or Linux run ./build-modpack.sh . The output folder then holds the modpack zip ( StaticHollow-Fabric-Modpack-1.63.3.zip or StaticHollow-Modpack-1.63.3.zip ; import it in CurseForge under My Modpacks), the mod jar by itself (for servers), StaticHollow-Visuals.zip (the texture pack on its own), the HD packs if they were found, and the builds of Water Erosion and Cinematic Interactions made for the pack. The build starts a test server that loads a new world's data before it makes a modpack, so a version that can't start a world can't be built. If it fails, check build-log.txt ."},{"p":"Installation guide","h":"Testing commands","u":"install.html#testing-commands","t":"With cheats on, the Static Hollow creative tab has every spawn egg, head and block, and /statichollow can skip to any part of the story. In Creative, hostile creatures can't hurt you, so test hunting in Survival. /locate structure statichollow:... finds the mod's places, and since 1.63.2 clicking the coordinates it gives you lands you standing beside the place (or on the sea's surface over a drowned one). Command What it does /statichollow locate [place] Where each place is, or when it will come. /statichollow underbed , underbed peek The Underneath comes up under your bed next time you lie down; or watches from under the nearest bed. /statichollow bloom open | break | rise | swallow The green rift opens; the Binding breaks; the Great Bloom rises; it swallows you. /statichollow flesh wake | front <days> | load <0-100> | redo | state The Flesh erupts in front of you; its reach; your infection; and more. /statichollow flesh city | lab | shelter [tp | below | vault | power | rebuild] Rosemont, the Laboratory and Shelter No. 4. /statichollow flesh device [build | release] The Rosemont Device; the Bloom gives the Gardener back. /statichollow flesh launch [force | open | mark | fire | detonate | reset] The launch, step by step. /statichollow flesh mutate | nest | horde [size] | horde stop | act | sapro <0-3> | self Mutations, nests, hordes, the infected's own ways, Sapromyiophilous, the infected you. /statichollow guns give mended_smg (or mended_shotgun , mended_marksman ) The Mended guns (Fabric with TaCZ). /statichollow ending <test> Everything from the end of chapter four on. The command suggests them all; they're grouped below. The tests for /statichollow ending , by part of the story: Part Tests Chapter four's end and chapter five status , start , sites , parts , gun , strike , feed , starve , ritual , omni , reclaim , back , hounds , broodme , hollow , chapter5 , relayhere , amalgam , relaycore , nullhere , afterimage , fragments , reel , lateshow , nullopen , nullzone , carrierhere , signoff , ruins , hushhere , stoneshere , choirhere and their resets The outbreak (1.48–1.52) infest (the nearest creature has one in it), infest25 / infest50 / infest75 / infest95 (that far along), infestturn , infestall (everything within 24 blocks turns), infestinfo , infestcure , biomass The Hive (1.50, 1.53) hivehere (the hive 52 blocks ahead of you), hivespeak , hivemind "},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"","u":"items/chapter-gear.html","t":"Since 1.60.0 every chapter has its own gear: a set of armour, two weapons and four tools (a pickaxe, an axe, a shovel and a hoe), all made from what that chapter leaves behind. Each piece is a real 3D model in your hand, on you and in the inventory, with its own sounds and its own power. None of it wears out. Item text below is copied from the game: the power in red, the description in grey. Recipes are written row by row, top to bottom, with . for an empty square. Every recipe shows up in the recipe book once you pick up what it's made from. The older weapons and armour (the Sinew Cleaver, Static Mail and the rest) are on Items and blocks ."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"At a glance","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#at-a-glance","t":"Chapter Armour (full-set power) Weapons Tools (perk) Made with One The Vigil (Keep Watch) The Censer, the Bell Clapper Gravedigger's (Unearth) Hymnal Pages, Grave Claws, iron Two The Scarecrow (Stand Still) The Pitchfork, the Omen Staff Harvestman's (Reap) Blighted Straw, Bloodied Stuffing, a Devil's Horn, iron Three The Bloomwoven (Rooted) The Thorn Whip, the Spore Mace Heartwood (Overgrowth) Knotted Roots, Heartblooms, Bloom Heartwood Four The Specimen (Hardened) The Bone Saw, the Reactor Rod Surgical Steel (Scan) Hive Comb, Splitter Sinew, a Stalker Talon, a Bloater Gland, diamonds Five Dead Air (Off Air) The Tuning Fork, the Relay Staff Static (Chain) Carrier Thread, Frames of the Last Reel, Vacuum Tubes, diamonds Six The Usher's Uniform (House Lights) The Splicer, the Fly Hook Stagehand's (Hush) Ticket Stubs, Listener's Ears, gold, netherite scrap Seven On Air (Skip) The Antenna Glaive, the On Air Mace Hub-Stone (Skip) Rerun Reels, netherite Chapter Eight (the Dead Water) has no set of its own. Its own kit is the Harpoon Gun, flares, air tanks and the submarine: see Items and blocks ."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The armour sets","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#armour","t":"Each piece shows its set's power on its tooltip. Wear all four for it. Every set has an HD version and shader (LabPBR) maps, and its lights (the Vigil's candles, the crow, the bloom, the jar, the static, the Usher's torch, the ON AIR lamp) have their own copies for shader packs since 1.62.0. Putting on a whole set earns its advancement."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Vigil (Chapter One)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-vigil","t":"The Vigil (Chapter One) Full set: Keep Watch The candles light the dark round you; every ten seconds they flare, and every creepypasta near shows through the walls The night watch's iron hood with a crown of candles burning on it, a long wax-stiff coat, iron pauldrons and a lantern swinging at the hip. Whenever it's dark round you (night, a cave, anywhere the sky doesn't reach) the candles light it, steady, with a real candle's flame dancing on each wick, a curl of smoke now and then and a soft crackle that everyone near can see and hear. Every ten seconds they flare, and every creepypasta within thirty-two blocks shows through the walls a while. Advancement: Keep Watch . Piece Recipe Vigil Hood C C C / I H I / I . I Vigil Coat I . I / W H W / W W W Vigil Leggings W H W / W . W / I . I Vigil Boots H . H / I . I C candle, H Hymnal Page, I iron ingot, W black wool."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Scarecrow (Chapter Two)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-scarecrow","t":"The Scarecrow (Chapter Two) Full set: Stand Still Stand still a moment and what's hunting you loses interest (unless you've just hurt it). Move, or strike, and it's back A sacking mask with a stitched face under a crooked hat, straw out of every gap, and a crow on your right shoulder: glossy black with a blue-violet sheen, a heavy beak and yellow eyes. It shifts about on its feet, jerks its head round to look and flicks its tail. Stand still for a second and a half and whatever is hunting you gives up; while you stay still nothing new sets on you. Advancement: Out Standing in the Field . Piece Recipe Scarecrow's Sack B U B / L . L Scarecrow's Coat L . L / L U L / B Y B Scarecrow's Breeches L U L / B . B / L . L Scarecrow's Boots U . U / L . L B Blighted Straw, U Bloodied Stuffing, L leather, Y hay bale."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Bloomwoven (Chapter Three)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-bloomwoven","t":"The Bloomwoven (Chapter Three) Full set: Rooted On soil - grass, dirt, moss, mud - you heal. The Bloom and its flies won't have you Woven of the Bloom's roots: a cowl with a crown of petals that breathe and a bloom lit on the brow, its face the pitch-black hollow of the original with roots grown over the rim. Standing on soil you heal, and the Bloom and its flies leave you alone. Advancement: Rooted . Piece Recipe Bloomwoven Cowl K F K / K . K Bloomwoven Tunic K . K / K W K / K F K Bloomwoven Leggings K W K / K . K / K . K Bloomwoven Boots F . F / K . K K Knotted Root, F Heartbloom, W Bloom Heartwood."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Specimen (Chapter Four)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-specimen","t":"The Specimen (Chapter Four) Full set: Hardened Each blow you take hardens you more: Resistance I, II, III, a while after the last. A kill puts two hearts back into you A specimen jar over your head, full of thick green fluid lit from inside, motes drifting and bubbles rising in it, a lid, tubes and an eye bobbing about; a patient's gown, restraints, and an IV bag on your back. Each hit you take hardens you a step further (Resistance I, II, III), for four seconds after the last one. Advancement: Specimen . Piece Recipe Specimen Jar I C I / G . G / G G G Specimen Gown W . W / W N W / W C W Specimen Leggings W N W / W . W / W . W Specimen Boots N . N / L . L I iron ingot, C Hive Comb, G glass, W white wool, N Splitter Sinew, L leather."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"Dead Air (Chapter Five)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#dead-air","t":"Dead Air (Chapter Five) Full set: Off Air Crouch and you go off the air: unseen and invisible for five seconds - then twenty more to come back on A black hood with a screen where your face was, playing static that rolls and breaks up, with now and then a face surfacing in it; two aerials lit at the tips that whip about as you move; a long black coat with static running down its lapels. Crouch and you go off the air. Advancement: Off the Air . Piece Recipe Dead Air Hood B F B / B . B Dead Air Coat B . B / B T B / B F B Dead Air Leggings B T B / B . B / B . B Dead Air Boots T . T / B . B B black wool, F Frame of the Last Reel, T Carrier Thread."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Usher's Uniform (Chapter Six)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-ushers-uniform","t":"The Usher's Uniform (Chapter Six) Full set: House Lights The things that listen can't hear you walk. What you strike from behind takes half as much again The Starlite's maroon and gold, made again in 1.61.1: a gilt-rimmed porcelain mask split by a gold seam (narrow slanted black eyes, half a smile and half a frown, a black tear, the glaze crazed); a tall pillbox cap with its band, badge, button and chin strap; a velvet jacket with a bow at the throat, braided aiguillettes, a name tag and tails swinging behind; the usher's torch lit at your belt. The things that listen (the Audience , the Listener and the Deaf King ) can't hear you walk. Advancement: Front of House . Piece Recipe Usher's Cap R R R / R S R / G . G Usher's Jacket R . R / G S G / R R R Usher's Trousers R S R / R . R / R . R Usher's Shoes E . E / L . L R red wool, S Ticket Stub, G gold ingot, E Listener's Ear, L leather."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"On Air (Chapter Seven)","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#on-air","t":"On Air (Chapter Seven) Full set: Skip A blow of three hearts or more skips you out of its way instead, a few blocks off, unhurt (every 15 seconds) Studio gear: a test-card visor that cycles, slips and rolls; headphones and a mic on a boom that bobs; the ON AIR lamp on top, pulsing; a crew jacket with a battery pack, a tally light and tape reels turning on the back. Advancement: Live . Piece Recipe On Air Visor B R B / P G P On Air Jacket B . B / P N P / B B B On Air Trousers B P B / B . B / N . N On Air Boots P . P / B . B B black wool, R redstone lamp, P Rerun Reel, G glass pane, N netherite scrap."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The weapons","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#weapons","t":"Two for each chapter. A fully charged swing (wait for the attack meter) sets off the weapon's power; use (right-click) sets off its ability, which takes ten seconds to come back. Damage and speed are the item's own numbers, as its tooltip shows them. Weapon Power What its tooltip says Damage / speed Recipe The Censer Chapter One Incense A church censer on its chain, still smouldering. Full swings blind and slow. Use: whirl it round you, striking all close 7 / 1.2 G H G / . N . / . S . G gold ingot, H Hymnal Page, N iron chain, S stick The Bell Clapper Chapter One Toll The clapper out of the Hollow's bell. Full swings throw back hard and stagger. Use: strike the ground - the toll rings out 9.5 / 0.7 H B H / . I . / . S . H Hymnal Page, B bell, I iron ingot, S stick The Pitchfork Chapter Two Pin Three rusted tines. A long reach. Full swings pin it where it stands, bleeding. Use: lunge, and carry what you skewer 7.5 / 1.3 I . I / I B I / . S . I iron ingot, B Blighted Straw, S stick The Omen Staff Chapter Two Omen An eye in a cage, and it looks back. What it strikes takes 30% more from anything. Use: the eye opens on all before you 6.5 / 1.6 . E . / . D . / . S . E eye of ender, D Devil's Horn, S stick The Thorn Whip Chapter Three Lash A vine off the Bloom, thorned. The longest reach. Full swings bleed it and draw it in. Use: lash out and drag it to you 7 / 1.7 K K F / . K . / W . . K Knotted Root, F Heartbloom, W Bloom Heartwood The Spore Mace Chapter Three Bloom Heartwood, grown over with the Bloom's fungus. Full swings poison. Use: a cloud of spores where you aim 9.5 / 1.0 . M . / M F M / . W . M red mushroom, F Heartbloom, W Bloom Heartwood The Bone Saw Chapter Four Rend Surgical steel, its teeth clogged. Full swings open the wound twice over. Use: rev it - all in front of you is torn at 7.5 / 1.8 . I T / . I . / S . . I iron ingot, T Stalker Talon, S stick The Reactor Rod Chapter Four Meltdown A control rod out of the reactor pool. Its touch withers. Use: vent the core - a wave that withers all round 8.5 / 1.3 . G . / I Y I / . I . G glowstone dust, I iron ingot, Y Bloater Gland The Tuning Fork Chapter Five Resonance It never quite stops ringing. Full swings ring on: the blow lands again, through armour. Use: a line of sound, through all on it 8 / 1.8 I . I / I V I / . D . I iron ingot, V Vacuum Tube, D diamond The Relay Staff Chapter Five Relay A relay ma"},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The tools","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#tools","t":"A pickaxe, an axe, a shovel and a hoe for each chapter, made the way the game's own are (the axe strips logs, the shovel makes paths, the hoe tills), with the chapter's token in one square. Iron's worth in the first chapters, up to netherite's in the last. Each chapter's four share a perk, shown on the tooltip. Tools Perk Mines like / speed Made with (M, X) Gravedigger's Chapter One Unearth: What you dig out of soil, sand and gravel isn't always only that Iron / 7 Iron ingots, Grave Claw Harvestman's Chapter Two Reap: Ripe crops sow themselves again; the axe fells the whole tree Iron / 7.5 Iron ingots, Blighted Straw Heartwood Chapter Three Overgrowth: Twice as fast through wood and green; leaves give their saplings. Crouch-use: it grows Diamond / 8.5 Bloom Heartwood, Knotted Root Surgical Steel Chapter Four Scan: Use: the ores round you show through the stone for six seconds Diamond / 9 Diamonds, Hive Comb Static Chapter Five Chain: The break runs on through up to six more of the same block, touching Diamond / 9.5 Diamonds, Carrier Thread Stagehand's Chapter Six Hush: The things that listen don't hear your work. Glass and ice come away whole Netherite / 10 Netherite scrap, Ticket Stub Hub-Stone Chapter Seven Skip: The block behind breaks too (crouch: just the one). The hoe tills three Netherite / 11 Netherite ingots, Rerun Reel The shapes, with M the material and X the token: pickaxe M X M / . S . / . S . , axe M X / M S / . S , shovel X / M / S , hoe M X / . S / . S (S stick). For comparison, the game's own iron tools mine at 6, diamond at 8 and netherite at 9. Each set moves too: the gravedigger's nail rattles, the harvestman's straw and the heartwood's leaves stir, the surgical lights blink, the static valve flickers, the stagehand's tag swings on its cord, and the band of Hub stone turns."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"Where the makings come from","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-makings","t":"Token From Hymnal Page The Hymnal Grave Claw The Underneath Blighted Straw The Harvestman; the Murder Mansion's chests Bloodied Stuffing The Bunnyman; the Murder Mansion's chests Devil's Horn The Jersey Devil; the Murder Mansion's store Knotted Root Rootlings, the Gardener; the Bloom's research station Heartbloom The Gardener; the glasshouse's Seed Vault Bloom Heartwood The Gardener, Reborn Hive Comb, Splitter Sinew, Stalker Talon, Bloater Gland The Flesh's mutants: the Hive; Splitters and Crawlers; Stalkers; Bloaters Frame of the Last Reel Afterimages at the Starlite; the Null ruins Carrier Thread The Carrier (6 to 10) Ticket Stub The Audience (some of them), the Ushers and the Crowd Vacuum Tube The Tuned (some of them) and the Projectionist Listener's Ear Listeners, in the Deep Rerun Reel A replay beaten again (below)"},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The Rerun Reel","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#rerun-reel","t":"Rerun Reel AS SEEN BEFORE Left behind by a replay, beaten again. Chapter Seven's gear is made with it. Walk into one of the replay portals in the Hub and that chapter's last fight comes back for another go. Beat it again and it leaves three or four Rerun Reels behind. All of Chapter Seven's gear (On Air, the Antenna Glaive, the On Air Mace, the Hub-Stone tools) is made with them. First one earns Rerun ."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"The gloves","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-gloves","t":"Three of the older gloves (two weapons and a climbing glove) were made again in 1.61.1 and are worn on the hand. Their recipes and powers are on Items and blocks . Rending Claws Frenzy Black stitched hide sewn with bone-pale thread, a ruff of the Dogman's grey fur at the wrist, an iron plate on the back of the hand with a cracked little screen in it, static still crawling on it. From every fingertip a long barbed blade of blued steel, a shorter one on the thumb, and one of the Dogman's fangs swinging on a cord. Now and then they drum their blades one finger after another. Their swing is a rake: down and across, then back the other way. Brute Knuckles Hurl An iron gauntlet over a black glove, the Brute's knuckle-bones and their spurs set in its knuckle bar, its reflective band riveted over the back, the wrist bound in Splitter sinew with a torn strip of the coat hanging off it. Now and then the fist clenches, leather creaking, iron knocking. Stalker Claws A climber's glove of brown leather with three of the Stalker's long fingers lashed along its own, their black nails hooking out past them. The talons click, one after another, and flex."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"Heads, worn","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#heads","t":"Since 1.60.0 every creature head can go on your head. It goes on over your own (yours is hidden under it), and the edges of your screen darken as you look out through it. Wear it Its own kind take you for one of them: they notice you from only half as far off. The heads are the ones the creatures of chapters one to three drop: see the bestiary ."},{"p":"Gear for every chapter","h":"How they swing","u":"items/chapter-gear.html#the-swing","t":"Since 1.61.0 every one of the mod's weapons and tools swings its own way, in first person, in third, and for everyone watching. Blades cut from high right to low left; cleavers, axes, maces and hammers come up over the shoulder and down hard; scythes, glaives and the censer sweep flat round; the thorn whip and the fly hook crack; the bone saw saws, two strokes; knuckles and claws jab; staves turn over in the hand and come round; the needle, the pitchfork and the tuning fork thrust; picks swing short, spades dig, hoes chop. The blow lands a tenth of a second or so after the click. Where a blow lands there's a flash, a white-hot star and its shock ring in the weapon's own colour (blood, bone, static, hellfire, sap, candle-flame, film-gold...), bigger for heavy weapons, big targets and criticals, with sparks flung the way the swing went, and the sound of the blow under the weapon's own: an edge biting, something heavy landing, a point going in, with a bright ring on a critical. Since 1.61.1 one-handed weapons are held a little forward, the long ones across the body in both hands and the heavy ones low in both hands, and in first person a weapon trails your turning, dips with each step and is carried low at a run. In the HD pack every texture of the chapters' gear is four times the mod's own, upscaled with an AI upscaler (Real-ESRGAN)."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"","u":"items/index.html","t":"Item text on this page is copied from the mod as it appears in game: the name, the power line in red, and the description in grey. Icons are the mod's own textures. Every recipe unlocks in the recipe book as soon as you pick up what it's made from. Gear for every chapter Since 1.60.0 each chapter has its own armour set, two weapons and four tools. They have a page of their own , with every recipe."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Relay Core","u":"items/index.html#relay-core","t":"Relay Core Tunes you in to them What the relay's signal ran through. Hold it to your ear: for thirty seconds every one of the parasite's own shows through anything, a long way off. From: the Amalgam at Relay 6, when it dies. Chapter: five. Use: hold it to your ear and you're Tuned In for thirty seconds (\"You tune in. Under the static, there they are.\"): every one of the parasite's own within 96 blocks shows through anything, violet. Then it needs a minute and a half to warm up again. Why you need it: Tuned In, you can hurt the Afterimages at the Starlite Drive-In (\"tuned in, they're as real as you are\"), and it has to be on you to tune the projector for the last reel. First use earns Tuned In . Related block: the Tether , the knot of sinew lashed to each of Relay 6's platforms, its veins lit. Tether Break the one on each platform to cut the Amalgam off from the relay."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Compasses and needles","u":"items/index.html#compasses","t":""},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Civil Defence Compass","u":"items/index.html#civil-defence-compass","t":"Civil Defence Compass Its needle is set on Rosemont Shelter No. 4. Left on the dais in Bunker B. If the shelter falls, make for the city. From: the locker the Watcher leaves on the dais in Bunker B after you kill the Warden of Shelter No. 4, with bread, torches and a golden apple. Points: at Rosemont, wherever you are. Added in 1.39.1."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Watcher's Needles","u":"items/index.html#watchers-needles","t":"From the Uplink Station on, whenever a new place wakes, the Watcher hands every player a needle: a compass that only ever points there. Its name is in dark purple and it never glints. Needle Its line Given when Watcher's Needle (Uplink Station) Where they talked to the gun. The array is there. The Bloom changes Watcher's Needle (Capacitor Works) Still holding its charge. The cell is there. The Bloom changes Watcher's Needle (Soul Well) Where they put the souls. The strongest is at the bottom. The Bloom changes Watcher's Needle (Ashford Nuclear Plant) Its reactor never went cold. The core is in its heart. The Orbital Railgun is built Watcher's Needle (Meridian Laboratory) Where they built what tears a charge loose. The destabilizer is there. The Orbital Railgun is built Watcher's Needle (Blackwater Station) Out in the sea. Something got loose in it. The blood is there. The Orbital Railgun is built (with an oak boat) Watcher's Needle (Relay 6) Where their static goes out from. Something holds on to the mast. The Bloom is dead Watcher's Needle (the Starlite) Where the last of their static runs down to. A screen showing nothing. Relay 6 is off the air Watcher's Needle (The Hive) Where it's growing itself a mind. The Chorus is down in the pit. After the hive speaks (or when you walk into the hive first) Watcher's Needle (The Sinkhole) Where the ground was pulled down from underneath. It went down there. Never handed out in 1.63.3: it exists only as a name. The Chorus Fragment is what leads you to the sinkhole. Every needle's power line reads \"Points to one of the places that woke\"."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Altar, Mansion and Gardens Needles","u":"items/index.html#site-needles","t":"Since 1.63.2, three compasses you can make for the places you go back to. Use one and its needle swings round and settles on the nearest of its place (\"The needle settles on the Forsaken Altar - 412 blocks north-east\", for example); after that it points there wherever you go in the Overworld, until you use it again. With none anywhere near: \"The needle spins and spins. There's none anywhere near.\" Anywhere but the Overworld: \"The needle won't settle. What it's looking for is up in the Overworld.\" Their shared power line: Use it: it finds the nearest one, and points there . Altar Needle Use it: it finds the nearest one, and points there For the altars the old things were given to. Recipe: a compass, a candle and a bone. Finds the nearest Forsaken Altar. Mansion Needle Use it: it finds the nearest one, and points there For the house where it all went wrong. Recipe: a compass, an iron sword and redstone. Finds the nearest Murder Mansion. Gardens Needle Use it: it finds the nearest one, and points there For the glasshouses, and what grew in them. Recipe: a compass, a glass pane and any small flower. Finds the nearest Botanic Gardens. The README calls these the Forsaken Altar, Murder Mansion and Botanic Gardens Compasses; in game they're named as above. The Chorus Fragment works like a needle too: see below . And in the Dead Water, the Watcher's Chart is a map."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The power source parts","u":"items/index.html#power-source","t":"When the Bloom changes, the Watcher tells you there's a gun above the sky that needs a power source, and three places wake. A tracker along the top of your screen counts THE POWER SOURCE (0/3) . Targeting Array SENTINEL's lock Pulled out of the dish when the city fell. It tells the gun where to look. Where: the Uplink Station, in the locker in the control bunker by the consoles, with Lt. Okafor's duty log, bread, iron and two flashbangs. Infected operators, a sniper and a breacher hold the compound. Capacitor Cell Works cell 9, fully charged Nobody came to collect it. It holds what the gun needs to fire. Where: the Capacitor Works, in the test cage at the back, past arcs jumping between the lightning rods. See the live banks . Bound Soul The strongest soul in the well Its keepers knelt by it for years. It will hold the Watcher's darkness. Where: the bottom of the Soul Well, thirty blocks down, on the altar where its keepers kneel (they get up when you come close; two of the Interred wait too). With bones, candles and echo shards. Orbital Core SENTINEL's power source The array, the cell and the soul, made one. Set it on a Forsaken Altar. Recipe: the Targeting Array, the Capacitor Cell and the Bound Soul, with iron and redstone. Set it on a Forsaken Altar and the Watcher comes and pours itself into it (\"that's me. all of me that's left.\"). Infused Orbital Core The Watcher is in it It drinks the light round it. Build the gun round it. Orbital Railgun Hold to lock on, release to fire (12s recharge) It doesn't shoot. It tells SENTINEL where. 16 to 200 blocks, open sky only. The only thing that can hurt the changed Bloom. Recipe: the Infused Orbital Core, iron blocks, a copper block, lightning rods, iron and a spyglass. Use: hold use and aim at the ground 16 to 200 blocks off, in the Overworld (\"No uplink. There's no sky here for it to talk to.\" anywhere else). Its laser paints the spot, a ring locks on, the capacitors whine up for two and a half seconds: LOCKED - RELEASE TO FIRE. Let go and the slug comes out of the sky: sixty damage, fire and a shockwave out to twelve blocks."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Ray Gun and the Omni","u":"items/index.html#ray-gun-parts","t":"Building the Orbital Railgun wakes three more places. A tracker counts THE RAY GUN (0/3) . Nuclear Reactor Core Out of Ashford's reactor A fuel assembly. Its rods still glow. One of the three things the Ray Gun's made of. Where: Ashford Nuclear Plant, in the fuel pool. Don't go in the water without a suit; the decon lockers have one. Discharge Destabilizer Out of the Meridian lab It can't hold what's in it for long. One of the three things the Ray Gun's made of. Where: Meridian Laboratory, in the glass cell in the middle of the ring (\"mind the coils\"), with redstone and amethyst. Vial of Dark Matter Blood Out of Blackwater's sample freezer It isn't a liquid. There are stars in it. One of the three things the Ray Gun's made of. Where: Blackwater Station, out at sea, in the freezer at the back. Parasites. Ray Gun Hold to aim, attack or let go to fire (2 min recharge) The Orbital Railgun, rebuilt round what the Bloom brought. 24 blocks across, the whole height of the world. The Watcher wants it. Recipe: the Orbital Railgun and the three parts, or bring them all to a Forsaken Altar. After the Omni is taken back, the Watcher burns this recipe out of every book. The Watcher turns the Ray Gun into the Omni Orbital Railgun ."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The reactor's parts and the Rosemont Device","u":"items/index.html#reactor-parts","t":"Each part is the only one there is: lose it and it goes back where you found it. The Rear and Front Assemblies won't go into anything but the Assembly Cradle; the Rear Assembly comes back a minute after it's lost (burnt, dropped in the void, left on the ground, shut away), and any copy crumbles in your hands. A tracker counts Reactor parts 0/3 . Item Its text From Rear Assembly One of the reactor's three parts. Off the army's truck in Rosemont's plaza. Heavy: it slows you. The Military Cradle in Rosemont (three axe blows) Reactor Core Lifted out of its rack at the bottom of the reactor pool. Hot. Everything infected wants it. The Laboratory's reactor hall (wakes Specimen Zero) Front Assembly Out of Bunker B, under Shelter No. 4. Bulky: you can't sprint with it. The dais in Bunker B (wakes the Warden) Assembly Cradle Holds the reactor's three parts. Set it down somewhere safe. The Rear Assembly goes in first, then the Core, then the Front. Comes with the Front Assembly The Rosemont Device There is only one. While you carry it, the Flesh lets you pass. The Bloom does not. Hold use on the full cradle for five seconds, or let the Watcher build it at a Forsaken Altar"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The parasite egg","u":"items/index.html#parasite-egg","t":"Parasite Pod The parasites' eggs. Their pods come up out of their black Xeno Resin and split open when you come near (\"Pod splits open\"); you'll hear them throb. Since 1.47.1 a pod is a round egg-sac, and split open it's a torn cup with its four flaps peeled back off the rim and the slime inside. Found at Blackwater Station and Relay 6. There is also a Parasite Spawn Egg (and a Parasite Host Spawn Egg) in the creative tab. Xeno Resin The parasites' black resin, creeping over everything where they nest. Static Hounds sometimes drop it."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter five","u":"items/index.html#chapter-five-items","t":"Surgical Kit Cuts a parasite's brood out Hold it to cut one out of yourself. Use it on someone else to cut one out of them. It hurts. You bleed. Four uses. Recipe: shears, an iron ingot, string, paper and wool. Also in the Relay 6 operator's locker and sometimes in the Null ruins. Earns Cut It Out . Frame of the Last Reel What's left of an Afterimage A frame of film, torn off at both ends. In it, very small, someone standing in a field. Feed four to the Starlite's projector. The Last Reel Where they come from The reel off the Starlite's projector, seen through. A dented can with no label. The film inside is warm. Keep it. Held up to the light: \"something vast, curled under the ground. An eye, opening.\" Hold it over the tear at the drive-in to open the way to the Null Static Zone. Carrier Thread What it carried them on Pale, cold, and stronger than it looks. There's a vein of light down the middle of it. It isn't carrying anything now. 6 to 10 from the Carrier. Music Disc Static Hollow - Signing Off Dropped by the Carrier."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter five: the hive and the Deep","u":"items/index.html#the-hive-and-the-deep","t":"Parts five and six of Chapter Five: the Hive , where the Chorus grows itself a mind, and the Deep , where it goes to ground. Chorus Fragment Hold it to your ear: it whispers A piece the Chorus left behind as it went down. It's still part of it, wherever it is. From: the floor of the Chorus's pit when it runs, one for everyone. A knot of grey-violet flesh with a face in it the size of a thumbnail, its eyes shut, its mouth moving. Use: hold it to your ear (every four seconds) and turn round. Facing the way the rest of it went, it whispers clear, and what it says tells you how far: \"down. a long way down. far from here - that way.\", \"that way. under the hills. we can feel you coming.\", \"closer. we can hear you walking. we can hear your heart.\", \"here. right under you. come down. it's warm.\" Side on it's faint and broken (\"...colder... no... turn...\"); facing away, only static. Up top it leads you to the sinkhole ( Warmer ); down in the Deep it leads you to where the Chorus has gone to ground (\"here. we are right here. we are finished growing.\"). With nothing to point at, it only mutters, things like \"we remember the dark under the hills.\" and \"every one we take remembers. every one remembers you.\" Listener's Ear One of the Deep's older ones' A fan of thin skin on rods of bone. It heard everything. Stitched over boots, it makes your steps nothing. From: Listeners, in the Deep. Also goes into the Usher's Shoes (see the chapter gear ). Hushed Boots Your steps make no sound Walk as quiet as sneaking: the Listener can't hear you, and the Deaf King has to be close to feel you. Recipe: leather boots, two Listener's Ears and string, in any order. Earns Not a Sound . The King's Ear-Stones So he wouldn't hear it singing Two plugs of the old ones' stone, warm, a spiral in each. Carry them and the Chorus's song can't get into you either. From: the Deaf King , when he dies and his crown cracks off. Anywhere in your inventory, they keep the song of the Chorus, whole, out of you in the last fight. Hold them to your ears and the world goes quiet a moment. The Last Voice The one voice it couldn't swallow A face cut out of the Chorus, its eyes open now. It isn't singing. It's trying to tell you something: a door at the end of the world, and the seal on it. From: the Chorus, whole, when it dies in the Warm Heart ( The Last Voice ). Hold it to your ear and it talks: \"...there's a "},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Blocks","u":"items/index.html#hive-and-deep-blocks","t":"Hive Flesh The parasite's violet flesh, veined, that the hive is grown of; it lines the Burrow and the Warm Heart too. The Hive Hands drop it and Hive Chitin when they die. Hive Chitin Its black braided spires and the ribs arching over the pit. Nerve Node The glowing bulbs on top of the four stalks round the pit, glowing and pulsing, cords of light running from them to the Chorus. Tear one open and it screams; tear all four for Senseless . Biomass The heap of violet flesh one of the turned leaves where it died (since 1.49.0), veined and pulsing, chitin forced out through it. It drags at you as you wade through it, and a minute or two later it heaves itself up into one of the parasite's pure forms, leaving its torn husk. Burn it and nothing gets up. See the turned . In the Deep: The Throat (a ring of the hive's flesh, puckered shut: stand on it and it opens and takes you down, or back up), Deep Rock , Old Stone , Old Stone Bricks and Carved Old Stone (the pale worked stone of whoever was down there first), Bloom Root and Root Tendril (the Bloom's roots, gone deeper than anyone ever dug; the tendrils' ends glow) and Ember Cap (it glows like a coal on the cavern floors). Carved Old Stone The Deaf King drops three to six when he dies, with Bloom Root and diamonds. Bloom Root Great roots hanging down through the roofs of the Root Hollows."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter six: the Door at the End of the World","u":"items/index.html#chapter-six-items","t":"The Stalls, the Watcher's Vault and the Other Side. See Chapter Six . Ticket Stub ADMIT ONE Soft old card, a seat number you can't read. Show one to an Usher and it looks away a while. From: some of the Audience, the Ushers, and the Crowd. Use: on an Usher: \"The Usher tears your ticket in two, and looks away.\" For a minute its lamp doesn't see you. Also goes into Chapter Six's gear. Usher's Lamp Held, it lights the dark round you Use it to flash: the Audience and the Ushers caught in it reel, hands over their faces - and the Crowd's Hush breaks. It needs a while to warm again. From: an Usher, now and then. A brass torch-lamp, its glass yellowed, still warm. The flash takes eight seconds to warm again. Flash it at one of the Tuned in the Vault and its screen whites out: it can't move for four seconds, watched or not. The Last Ticket ADMIT ONE - THE VAULT What was left in the middle of the Crowd. It's warm. On the back, in a thin black hand: THE VAULT. Hold it up to the seam in the screen. From: the Crowd , one for everyone who was there. Held up to the seam the Watcher leaves in the Great Screen in Front Row, it tears in two in your hand and the seam opens for good ( Admit One ); after that, \"The seam's open. Walk into it.\" Used anywhere else: \"ADMIT ONE. On the back, in a thin black hand: THE VAULT.\" Vacuum Tube Still warm Out of one of the Tuned's sets. It glows a little, faintly orange. Two of them, with glass and iron, make a set of your own. From: some of the Tuned, and the Projectionist. Makes: two Old Sets ( I G I / T R T / I I I : I iron ingot, G glass pane, T Vacuum Tube, R redstone), old televisions that hum, with static crawling on them; use one to switch it on or off. Also goes into the Tuning Fork and the Relay Staff."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"What he kept","u":"items/index.html#what-he-kept","t":"The three things in the Watcher's keeps, each on a plinth behind a round steel door. Bring all three to the Watch and the Projectionist steps down out of the sets ( What He Kept ). All three say KEPT FOR THE FUTURE and \"Take it to him, in the Watch.\" The Omni's Heart KEPT FOR THE FUTURE What made the Omni more than a gun: every colour at once, turning, in a cage of its own light. He took it out of it. Take it to him, in the Watch. Later he loads it into his last projector against the Viewer ( Every Colour at Once ). See the Omni . What's Left of the Carrier KEPT FOR THE FUTURE A knot of it, still beating. Static comes off it like heat. It carried whatever was put on it. It held a door open. Take it to him, in the Watch. Take it and its static pours out: every Tuned near you is loose for a few seconds. See the Carrier . His First Reel KEPT FOR THE FUTURE A film can, dented, the reel in it. On the lid, in his hand: THE OTHER SIDE. FIRST. DO NOT RUN. Take it to him, in the Watch. Kept in a glass case. He runs it after the Projectionist burns through. The Projectionist's Lens Held: you see what's watching you All that was left of it, in the ash: its lens, still warm. Hold it and everything hostile near you shows through the walls, outlined in its light. From: the Projectionist, with three to five diamonds, two to four echo shards and two to four Vacuum Tubes. Music Disc Static Hollow - Thank You for Watching Given to you after the last show, when the credits have rolled and you're sent home. See the soundtrack ."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Blocks","u":"items/index.html#chapter-six-blocks","t":"Seal-Stone Black, his glyphs cut in it ( Seal-Stone Glyph ), a few still faintly lit: the causeway out to the Door, and the Door's frame. In it hums The Door's Static . Stalls Asphalt The Stalls' ground, under the Picture House Seats . Facing them, The Great Screen of Screen Cloth . Vault Terrazzo The dark, flecked floor of the Watcher's archive. Its keeps are The Watcher's Concrete (it doesn't break). Also: Archive Shelves (steel, cans of film and boxes of tape, labels in his hand), Old Sets , Cable , the keeps' Keep Door and Keep Wheel (use it: five seconds of the bolts drawing back, and the door swings in), What He Kept (the plinths) and The Watch Wall . Stage Boards The Other Side: Stage Boards , Stage Flats and Painted Flats (each a picture of somewhere from the story), Footlights , The Screen's Back , His Last Projector and the Black Static the Door goes to. Black Static What fills the Door at the End of the World once the first reel has been run: the dark on the far side of it, looking out."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter seven: the First Signal","u":"items/index.html#chapter-seven-items","t":"The Remote An old television's remote, heavy, its buttons worn smooth, the one with nothing on it warm. The Watcher gives it to you after the Hub , and it earns Channel Changer . Press it: you're in the Hub. Press it in the Hub: home. Before it has anywhere to go: \"You press the blank button. Nothing. Not yet.\" In 1.59 he handed it over when you landed at home (\"take this. if you need to go back - it's still there.\"). Since 1.62.0 the fall from the Hub goes to the Dead Water instead: he hands it over on the rig (\"take this. it'll get you back - to the hub, and home.\") and it cracks in your hand. See the Broken Remote . Mended, it does one more thing: \"Press it: the Hub (and in the Hub, home). Crouch and press it: back to the rig.\" Hub Stone The pale stone of the Hub's floating plaza, with Hub Stone Slabs . Hub Glyph His marks, lit in the Hub's floor. Along its north side stand six Replay Portals , one for each chapter, each playing its chapter on an old set. The Rerun Reels that replays leave behind are on Gear for every chapter ."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Chapter eight: the Dead Water","u":"items/index.html#chapter-eight-items","t":"The rig's stores are full of these. See Chapter Eight and the Dead Water . The Broken Remote Dead - it broke in your hand in the Dead Water Its case cracked across, its wires out, the warm button cold. Mend it: this, a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ, a copper ingot. (The big ones live deep. They sing on its frequency.) Pressed: \"It sparks. The warm button's cold. Nothing.\" Mend it: the Broken Remote, a Signal Organ and a copper ingot, in any order, give you back the Remote (\"The Remote works again.\"). Harpoon Gun Hold to pump, let go to fire - in water or out Reels what it bites back to you - or you to it, if it's too big. Strike a wall or the sea floor and it hauls you there. Crouch to let go. Fire again while it's out to reel it in. Takes Harpoon Bolts. Recipe: I I P / S C I / W . . (I iron ingot, P piston, S string, C copper ingot, W any planks). Also in the rig's armoury and its dive locker. Harpoon Bolt The Harpoon Gun's ammunition Barbed steel, an eye for the cable. It comes back with the harpoon - unless it snaps off in what it struck. Recipe: . T . / . I . / . N . (T Needle Tooth, I iron ingot, N iron nugget) makes two. Also in the rig's armoury and dive locker. Marine Flare Burns red for a minute - even underwater Strike it and throw it. In the sea it sinks slowly, lighting the dark on its way down. Recipe: gunpowder, redstone, paper and red dye, in any order, make three. All over the rig's stores. Rig Ration A meal in a tin Stamped R. The rig's larders are full of them. Someone stocked this place a long time ago. Recipe: dried kelp, bread, cooked cod and an iron nugget make two. In the mess, the food stores and the bunks. Air Tank Underwater: use it to breathe - your air back to full A diver's bottle off the rig's dive locker. Good for a dozen breaths. Recipe: . G . / I K I / I S I (G gold ingot, I iron ingot, K dried kelp block, S string). In the dive locker, the sub bay, sunken lifeboats and the flooded habitat dome. It can't be filled again. The Watcher's Chart The Dead Water, every one of its waters Use it to unroll it. The black hatched in red is the dead zone. Don't take the sub over it. The Watcher hands it to you when you come down to the Dead Water (since 1.63.2): four thousand blocks of sea round the rig, every water in its own colour and named, the floor's depths shaded and contoured, and the Black Below hatched out in red. Held, it's a"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"What the deep things drop","u":"items/index.html#sea-drops","t":"Signal Organ From: the Static Leviathan (with bone blocks, Needle Teeth and a heart of the sea). In the Overworld it lives in the deepest oceans, the Hadal Dark and the Trench; in the Dead Water, now and then one comes up out of the dark after you once you're forty blocks or more under the surface (never in the Black Below, which is the Undertow's). It sings on the Remote's frequency, and its organ is what mends it. Shroud Hide From: Shroud Rays and the Mouth of the Floor; also in the habitat dome and the frozen outpost. Goes into Pressure Plating. Needle Tooth From: Needlemaws, the Static Leviathan and the Mouth of the Floor; also in the habitat dome and Sink Station. Goes into Harpoon Bolts and Pressure Plating. The creatures themselves are in the bestiary , and the Undertow has a page of its own ."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The sea's blocks and plants","u":"items/index.html#sea-blocks","t":"Every water has its own floor: Ash Silt , Clotted Silt , Rust Silt , Glow Sand , Bone Sand , Brine Crust , Gum Silt , Spore Silt , Rime Silt , Ember Crust , Static Sand and Abyss Silt . Growing on them, waterlogged where they grow: Grey Kelp , Vein Kelp (it glows), Wireweed , Signal Bulbs , Glow Anemones , Lantern Bulbs , Bone Coral and Bone Fans , Marrow Sponge , Clot Coral , Artery Anemones , Sulfur Tubes , Brine pools, Enamel Coral , Tooth Fans , Gum Sponge , Nerve Anemones , Drowned Stems and Drowned Caps , Spore Puffs (they burst in your face), Gill Glow , Rime Ice , Frost Anemones , Frozen Corpses , Vent Chimneys , Tube Worms , Static Coral , Antenna Weed , Void Moss , Drowned Sets , Sea Lights and Eye Pods (shut till you come near; then the eye opens and follows you). The submarine's Sub Clamp is on the catwalk in the rig's sub bay: it charges and mends ORPHEUS, and builds another for 16 iron ingots and 8 glass. Glow Sand One of the twelve floors. Bone Sand The Ossuary Flats' floor."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Out in the world","u":"items/index.html#out-in-the-world","t":"Things that aren't tied to a chapter. The thirst and the cold they belong to are on Cold, thirst and the world . Canteen Use on water to fill it - or hold it out in the rain: rainwater's clean A dented tin flask in a stitched leather sleeve. Someone's initials scratched into the cap. Recipe: . S . / L I L / . L . (S string, L leather, I iron ingot). Filled from water it's a Murky Canteen : Drink: 5 sips - may leave you Tainted. Boil it (furnace, smoker, campfire) to clean it . Boiled, or filled in the rain, it's a Clean Canteen : Drink: 5 sips of good water - more thirst back, and it cools you . The sips left show as its bar; the last one leaves it empty. Channel Zero Point it at the ground and press it. Crouch and press it: the next channel. CH 1 Falling Star - one star of the sky's static, on the spot. CH 2 Starfall - nine smaller ones all round it. CH 3 Dead Satellite - a dead satellite brought down, and its wreck. CH 4 Test Card - the sky's test card, its bars burned in one by one. Creative only for now (no recipe yet). A Falling Star leaves a crater lined with Static Stone and a Fallen Star glowing in it; Starfall drops nine small stars over four seconds; the Dead Satellite falls burning for five seconds and leaves a wreck and a satellite core's chest; the Test Card throws colour bars over the ground and burns each bar in turn. Craters only where the TNT game rule lets things blow up. Fallen Star At night shooting stars streak over the sky, and now and then a small one comes down somewhere near: a lump of glassy black rock, cracked all over, white-blue static crawling in the cracks, warm, lighting its crater. Mine it with a pickaxe for 2 to 4 Star Static (more with Fortune); Silk Touch keeps it whole. Star Static Out of a Fallen Star A splinter of the dead channel over the world. It's still warm. It crackles if you hold it to your ear. Also in a dead satellite's core."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Small things that share a block","u":"items/index.html#small-things","t":"Since 1.62.0, seven sets of little things that share one block space, one to four of a set, each turned to face whoever put it down. Place one on another to add a piece; break it and one piece comes off. You'll find them out in the Hollow's own country, on the deep sea floors, on the rig, in the cathedral's crypts and at the altar's pilgrim stones. Block Its text Recipe Grave Candles Tallow candles, a stub, a skull. Up to four in one space; light them. A candle and a bone Bone Pile A skull, its jaw, bones. Up to four in one space. Three bones Rot Caps The Blightwood's fungi. They glow a little, and breathe out spores. A brown mushroom and Rotgrass make two Hanging Chains Hung from a ceiling: chains, a hook, a shackle, a weight. They creak. Two iron chains Rig Clutter What's left lying about on the rig: a tin, an oil can, a wrench, bolts. Two iron nuggets and a copper ingot make two Cairn Stones Flat stones, stacked by pilgrims. The top one is carved. At night something whispers. Two cobblestone make two Ritual Offerings A bowl of ash, a straw doll, a red candle, dried herbs. A candle, wheat, a clay ball and red dye"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Hollow's own country","u":"items/index.html#the-hollows-own-blocks","t":"The five places on the Hollow's side of the world (see the Hollow's own country ) have their own trees, plants and stone: Blightwood logs, leaves and saplings, Fen Willow logs, leaves and saplings with Willow Strands , Bonewood logs, needles and saplings, Deadwood , Peat , Hanging Rot , Rotgrass , Dead Heather , Wire Grass and Static Stone (it hums). Their logs make planks: Blightwood and Deadwood rotten planks, Fen Willow mangrove planks, Bonewood birch planks. Four Deadwood logs make three Deadwood. Blightwood Log From the Blightwood: close, bruise-coloured, rot caps glowing. Bonewood Log Pale and cold. Static Stone It hums. Fallen stars line their craters with it."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Survival and story items","u":"items/index.html#survival","t":"Item What it does From Saint's Heart A real heart, still beating. Goes into the Saint's Requiem. The Hollow Saint Saint's Shroud Smithing template: upgrades Static Mail to the Saint's Vestments with a Hymnal Page. The Hollow Saint (4 to 5) The Mended Heart Iron Will. Hold it up: three minutes of Resistance II, Strength I and Absorption II, then it has to beat itself warm again. The Mended Rusted Garden Key Opens the Botanic Gardens' gate. \"Something in there has waited a long time.\" The Mended Heartbloom It still beats. Eat it: made whole, hardened, healing, and everything green round you flowers. The Gardener Drift Jelly Slow Falling for 40 seconds and sight in the dark for 20. Eight iron nuggets round one make a Driftlight Lantern. Driftlights in the Void Lamprey Lure Still lit. Hold it and it lights your way. Lampreys (sometimes) Bloom Serum Cures the Flesh's infection and keeps it off you for twenty seconds. A glass bottle, a Bloom pustule and sugar; or a ghost orchid, a whispering lily and sugar. Crafted; the Congregation, Specimen Zero Flower Ash Bomb Throw it: the Flesh's growth dies back where it bursts, and anything infected in it burns. A garden flower, a burnt petal and gunpowder make two. Crafted; Specimen Zero Tainted Meat Fills you, and infects you. \"Starving, it might be worth it. It usually isn't.\" The Flesh's things Flashbang Blinds and deafens whatever can see it (you too); the infected caught in it stagger and lose you. Special forces infected Contaminated Syringe From the corner pharmacy. \"You wouldn't.\" Infected Pharmacists Bottle of Pills Eat: Regeneration, and Nausea. \"They help. Mostly.\" Infected Pharmacists Level 2 Keycard Opens the Laboratory's security doors. The director's desk; researchers Audio Log Play the tape, or put it in a tape recorder for everyone within about twenty blocks to hear. The Laboratory Fuel Canister Diesel for the shelter's generators. One of Shelter No. 4's lockers Brood Heart Brood Sight: the Flesh's things within 48 blocks show through walls for 30 seconds. 90 seconds to beat again. The Broodmother The Bellwether's Bell Ring it: the infected within 16 blocks stop and listen for three seconds. Half a minute to ring again. The Bellwether Bloom Heartwood Close-grained, pale, still warm. Green light runs in it like sap. The Gardener, Reborn (3) The Gardener's Seed A hard black seed the size of a fist, split alo"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Weapons","u":"items/index.html#weapons","t":"Big, detailed 3D weapons, held like a sword. A fully charged swing (wait for the attack meter) triggers the weapon's power; the second act's weapons also have a power on use, with a ten-second cooldown. The first four weapons and every armour piece are unbreakable, and those four can break blocks slowly, like a sword. Since 1.61.0 every weapon swings its own way, and since 1.61.1 the Rending Claws, Brute Knuckles and Stalker Claws are worn on the hand (see the gloves ). The fourteen chapter weapons added in 1.60.0 are on Gear for every chapter . Weapon Power What it does Recipe (rows, top to bottom) Sinew Cleaver Rend Each full swing opens the wound further: Bleeding I, II, III. . S / T S / K . S Stitched Sinew, T Shepherd's Tear, K Hollow Knuckle Antler Scythe Reap The swing carries on through everything in front of you. A A A / . W . / . K . A Antler Shard, W Bloodied Wool, K Hollow Knuckle Static Blade Dead Air Static arcs from your target to up to 3 more hostiles. S / S / C S Static Shard, C Grave Claw Saint's Requiem Last Rites The target burns; creepypastas take a third more damage. . S . / R H R / . K . S Static Shard, R Rusted Lullaby Key, H Saint's Heart, K Hollow Knuckle The Bunnyman's Fire Axe Bridge Toll Full swings cut through armour, break shields and stagger. Use: a chop that splits the ground open ahead of you. I I S / I B . / S B . I iron ingot, S Bloodied Stuffing, B stick Hook and Chain Reel Full swings gaff: they bleed and drag the target to you. Use: throw the hook; it hauls creatures in, or you to walls. . H / . C / H B H Rusted Hook, C iron chain, B stick The Hogshead's Tenderizer Tenderize Full swings make the target take more from all harm. Use: slam the ground, throwing everything round you upward. F I F / . B . / . B . F Flayed Hide, I iron block, B stick Porcelain Needle Unseen Strikes from behind cut deep and stitch the target slow. Use: vanish; your first strike from hiding is a killing one. . . P / S P . / G . . P Porcelain Shard, S string, G gold ingot Devil's Glaive Hellfire Longer reach; full swings set the target burning. Use: leap on devil's wings and come down in a ring of fire. . . H / . B H / B . M H Devil's Horn, B blaze rod, M Moth Scale Rending Claws Frenzy Each hit quickens the next; wounds bleed, and bleeding prey feeds you back. Use: pounce and rake three times. F F F / L I L F Dogman's Fang, L leather, I iron ing"},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"The Mended guns","u":"items/index.html#the-mended-guns","t":"Fabric only, with Timeless and Classics Guns: Zero (TaCZ), which the Fabric modpack installs. Three guns the Flesh grew into the special forces who carried them: the Mended SMG (its stock a forearm, an eye open in its side, a muzzle of five flesh petals; 30 rounds, full auto), the Mended Shotgun (a ribcage stock, a seed-pod magazine of 6 shells, a muzzle of teeth that chews when you look at it) and the Mended Marksman Rifle (a spine along the barrel, a thighbone stock, a finger for a bolt handle; 5 rounds). They fire infected rounds that put the Flesh into whatever they hit. Made at TaCZ's Gun Smith Table; special forces sometimes drop theirs. Once the Bloom is dead, they rot and jam over ten minutes off its blight."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Armour","u":"items/index.html#armour","t":"Every set is a real 3D model that moves. Crafted in the usual armour shapes from a material M with one accent X. The seven chapter sets (the Vigil, the Scarecrow, the Bloomwoven, the Specimen, Dead Air, the Usher's Uniform and On Air) are on Gear for every chapter . Since 1.60.0 any creature head can be worn too ( heads, worn ). Set Full-set power Made from Stitchskin Sewn Shut: below half health your wounds slowly close, and you can't bleed at all. Stitched Sinew, Hollow Knuckle Antlerbone Night Hunter: you run faster in the dark. Antler Shard, Bloodied Wool Static Mail Dead Channel: creepypastas within 32 blocks glow through walls, and anything that hits you up close gets a jolt of static. The Dead Channel Helm also shows the static coming off the Hollowed. Static Shard, Grave Claw Saint's Vestments Hollow Grace: creepypastas won't hunt you unless you hurt them. The Saint's Crown calms one that comes close. Static Mail + Saint's Shroud + Hymnal Page, at a smithing table Butcher's Garb Slaughterhouse: your blows open bleeding wounds; every kill feeds you back. Flayed Hide, porkchop, Rusted Hook, leather Mothwing Night Flight: fall and your wings catch you; in the dark you see like a moth. Moth Scale, fermented spider eye, phantom membrane, leather Braxton Shell Braxton Mist: struck, you hiss out a burning mist that sickens what's near; the hood's lamp lights the dark. Braxton Residue, glowstone, iron The Gardener's Weeds Tended: the great flower's flies won't have you (no Sapromyiophilous, and the Bloom's air doesn't eat you); what grows round you grows faster. Knotted Root, hay block, leather, mud (or found in the glasshouse) Hazmat Suit Sealed: the reactor's radiation can't touch you, and the Flesh's bile, gas and spores get in half as much. The Laboratory's airlock lockers Dead Channel Helm A dead TV for a helmet, crawling with live static. Its antenna tips light green while a creepypasta is near, flash red when you're hit, and fade like a cooling bulb when the last one's gone. Saint's Crown When a creepypasta comes within about 14 blocks, a red orb kindles between its antlers and beats like a heart, a glitching signal. In the full set the creature stares a few seconds, then gives in, sighs white ash, and turns friendly."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Mutant parts and throwables","u":"items/index.html#throwables","t":"Item What it does Recipe Gut Bomb Throw it: bursts like a Bloater on whatever is there, anything but you. A Bloater Gland, gunpowder and string (makes two) Screamer Lure Throw it: it screams for twelve seconds and every infected within 48 blocks goes to it. A Screamer Sac and Splitter Sinew Fly Jar Throw it: four Flesh Flies fight for you for twenty seconds. Hive Comb, a glass bottle and Splitter Sinew The parts themselves: Stalker Talon, Bloater Gland, Screamer Sac, Brute Knuckle, Splitter Sinew and Hive Comb, each from its mutant."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Blocks","u":"items/index.html#blocks","t":""},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Story blocks","u":"items/index.html#story-blocks","t":"Forsaken Altar and Breach Altar : wake with an empty hand. Hollow Reliquary and Head Pedestal : the Saint's summoning. Mending Altar and Trophy Pedestal : the Mended. The Binding : holds the Bloom down, until you touch it twice. Cathedral Cornerstone (creative): place it in open ground and right-click it to raise a cathedral there. Assembly Cradle , Military Cradle , Assembly Mount , Launch Mark : the Rosemont Device. Tape Recorder : a working cassette player. Coolant Lever , Keycard Reader , Diesel Generator , Overload Switch , Shelter Radio Set . Projector , Drive-In Screen , Null Static , Null Rift : the Starlite and the Zone. Hush Stone , Hush Seal , Listening Stone : the Null ruins. Null Static What the drive-in's ground has gone to (as the mod's source describes it). Hush Stone Pale and dead: knock on it and nothing rings. The blocks of the hive, the Deep, the Stalls, the Vault, the Other Side, the Hub and the Dead Water are listed with their chapters above."},{"p":"Items and blocks","h":"Building blocks","u":"items/index.html#building-blocks","t":"Hollow stone, hollow stone bricks (plain, cracked and bloodied), hollow brick stairs, slabs and walls, hollow tiles, hollow pillars, ossuary bricks, rotten planks (with Rotten Pews and slabs), cathedral glass (with its god rays), grave soil, gravestones, grave crosses and blood splatters. Breach stone and bricks, breach crystal and shards. Weathered clapboard, damask wallpaper, stained floorboards, slate shingles, grimy windows. Conservatory glass, overgrown iron, marble, planters, potting soil, garden flagstones and iron lattice. Shelter concrete, laboratory tiles and panels, steel grating, sandbags and wrecked cars. The radio mast, its top, antennas, aviation lights and guy-wire anchors (an anchor wires itself to the nearest mast). Blood is a real liquid: a bucket scoops it up. The garden's plants: Bloodthorn, Gnashing Flytrap, Whispering Lily, Corpse Bloom, Ghost Orchid, Watching Fern, Strangler Vine, Lantern Pod, Burstpod, Clutchvine, Weeping Bell, and four kinds of Specimen Jar (eye, heart, hand, seed)."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"","u":"lore/index.html","t":"Static Hollow tells most of its story in paper: journals on lecterns, logs in lockers, notices on walls. Every one is here word for word, grouped by chapter and by where you find it. They contain spoilers for everything up to the place they're found. Laboratory tapes and radio broadcasts are on Tapes and broadcasts . The Watcher's lines are on The Watcher speaks ."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter one: the Nine","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-one","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Forsaken Altar","u":"lore/index.html#the-forsaken-altar","t":"In the pilgrims' abandoned camp by the altar (since 1.40)."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Pilgrim's Diary","u":"lore/index.html#pilgrims-diary-2","t":"M. Ashdown Found: the pilgrims' camp p. 1 Day 9 on the road. We have reached the altar at last. Nine stones stand round it, one for each of the Nine, every one carved with one of their signs. We knelt at each of them. p. 2 The candles at the altar lit themselves as we came near. Brother Tobias wept. He says it means we are welcome. p. 3 Day 10. There is a stair by the altar, sealed under a stone. Tobias says it opens when the altar opens its eye. The first pilgrims are buried down there, all together, so they can go on praying. p. 4 Day 12. Tobias has knelt at the altar three nights now. He does not come back to the fire. When I go to him he turns his head to me and smiles, and then he is not there. I am leaving in the morning. I will leave this for whoever comes after."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The cathedral","u":"lore/index.html#the-cathedral","t":"The priest's journal is in his study in the undercroft (since 1.40). The bell-ringer's tally is in the cathedral too."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Journal","u":"lore/index.html#journal","t":"Fr. A. Penn Found: the priest's study p. 1 The Feast of the Nine. They came again tonight, the nine families, and sat in the front pews, and did not sing. When I asked them to go home they turned their heads to me. Only their heads. p. 2 They do not eat. They do not go home. When I lock the doors at night they are already inside, praying, and the candles are lit that I did not light. p. 3 Below, the Saint lies sealed in its tomb under nine chains and nine candles, one for each of the heads they took to make it. I have kept the candles burning forty years. I am so tired. p. 4 The organ played itself at the third hour. A hymn I do not know. The candles went out one by one from the doors to the altar, as though someone were walking up the nave pinching them. p. 5 The bell rang thirteen. There is no thirteen. Something stood in the doorway and did not come in. p. 6 I went down this morning. The gate is bent outward. The tomb is open and empty and its chains are broken, and the congregation was smiling when I came back up. God keep whoever reads this. Do not open the tombs."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Bell-Ringer's Tally","u":"lore/index.html#bell-ringers-tally-2","t":"S. Marsh Found: the cathedral p. 1 Tolls, by the night. Mon. 12 at midnight. Right. Tue. 12. Right. Wed. 12, and one more after I'd let go of the rope. Thu. 13. I counted twice. p. 2 Fri. I tied the rope off at dusk. It rang thirteen anyway. The bell was swinging on its own when I got up here, and it was warm. Sat. I'm sleeping up here now. If it rings I want to see what rings it. p. 3 It isn't the bell. It's the thing in the doorway, down below. It looks up at me on the thirteenth. Every time."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter two: the Breach","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-two","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Void","u":"lore/index.html#the-void","t":"Pages left on the pieces of the Drift, each with its chest (since 1.26)."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"A Diary, Left Open","u":"lore/index.html#a-diary-left-open-2","t":"(no name in it) Found: the Torn Room p. 1 Tuesday. The floor has started creaking at night where nobody is walking. From the corner by the wardrobe to the bed, and back. I have moved the bed. p. 2 Wednesday. The creaking goes to where the bed is now. The wallpaper by the window is damp, and warm. I put my hand on it and something on the other side put its hand on it too. p. 3 Thursday. There was a red light in the window. Not in the street. In the window, as if the glass itself had a crack in it and the crack went a long way back. The clock stopped at eleven. p. 4 Friday. The floor tipped. I am writing this because the rest of the house is gone and this corner is not and I don't know what is under it. It is dark under it. It is dark all round. The lamp is still lit. I'll keep it lit."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"An Unfinished Letter","u":"lore/index.html#an-unfinished-letter-2","t":"(the same hand as the diary) Found: the Torn Room p. 1 To whoever finds this room. There is no door. I looked for a long time. There is the bed and the wardrobe and the table, and past the edge of the rug there is nothing, and in the nothing there are lights that drift like jellyfish. p. 2 Something long goes round and round in the dark with a little lamp of its own. I thought it was another room, lit, far off. It isn't. If you fall, don't be afraid of the hand. The hand is the only kind thing out here."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Gravedigger's Book","u":"lore/index.html#gravediggers-book-2","t":"Amos, sexton Found: the Fallen Graves p. 1 Plot 12. Plot 13. Plot 14. All the new ones in the north row came up loose this week. Not dug up. Loose. As if the ground under them had let go of them. p. 2 I filled them in again. I filled them in again. The fourth time I put my ear to the earth, and it was hollow under. Hollow all the way down. The coffins in the north row are knocking. p. 3 Last entry. The north row is gone and the earth with it, and I went with the earth. The mausoleum came too. I am in it. Whoever they buried here, they never wanted to stay put. Now none of us has to."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Station Log","u":"lore/index.html#station-log","t":"the night operator Found: the Mast p. 1 STATION LOG 02:10 Carrier on 6.66. No station licensed there. 02:14 Voice under the carrier, counting. Counting down. 02:31 Mast lamp flickering. Replaced the bulb. Still flickering. p. 2 02:40 The TV in the shed came on by itself. Same channel as the radio. The man on it has a television where his head should be. He looked at me. 02:41 He knows the frequency. He is coming up it. p. 3 03:00 Static. 03:00 Static. 03:00 The mast is still up and the lamp is still on and there is no ground under the shed any more. Keeping the lamp on. Someone might steer by it. The counting stopped. It got to one. p. 4 (written across the bottom, later, in pencil) if you can read this - the red light is the way back to the altar. keep it on your left as you go and the bridge will take you."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Of What Swims Out Here","u":"lore/index.html#of-what-swims-out-here-2","t":"the Watcher Found: the Nest p. 1 the long things come up out of the black pool, where the big one died. they eat what falls. they will help it fall: they bite, and they pull you out over the dark, and let go. hit them hard and they let go sooner. p. 2 the lights are harmless. they drift where there is ground, and light it. their jelly is good to eat if you are afraid of falling. their light keeps the long ones off. the long ones go round it. p. 3 and the hand. the hand was here before the breach. it was here before the island. it catches everything that falls. i don't know why. i don't know whose it is. i know it has never once let anything go."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Murder Mansion","u":"lore/index.html#the-murder-mansion","t":"The Hale family's papers, where they were left (since 1.25). The Watcher's own pages are open on the library desk."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Household Accounts","u":"lore/index.html#household-accounts-2","t":"A. Hale, housekeeper Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 Hale House. Accounts kept by Agnes Hale. March. Coal, 2 tons. Candles, 6 dozen (the master will have them lit in every room, all night, since the trouble). Flour, salt, lamp oil. p. 2 April. Meat, from the new man in the kitchen. He brings his own. He will not say from where and I have stopped asking. No charge, he says. The house is paying, he says. p. 3 April, later. The master has given the east rooms to guests. Nine of them. I am not to go up when they are in. Nine rooms aired. Nine beds made. Nobody has slept in them that I can tell. p. 4 May. The staff have gone. All but me and the cook, and I am not sure the cook was ever staff. Candles, 6 dozen. Candles, 6 dozen. Candles (the rest of the page is crossed through, hard enough to tear it)"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Household Accounts (II)","u":"lore/index.html#household-accounts-ii-2","t":"A. Hale, housekeeper Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 June. I have found the old ledger and I have found the reason for the hall at the back, with the long table and the spikes round it. The house was built for this. The first Hale built it round the table. p. 2 The table is not a table. It is an altar. The spikes are for heads. When there are nine heads on the nine spikes, something comes to the table and sews. I am writing it down so that somebody knows. p. 3 June, late. The guests are back. I heard them come in. Hooves on the stairs. Something dragging an axe. I have locked myself in the attic with the trunks. I have candles. 6 dozen."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Order Book","u":"lore/index.html#order-book-2","t":"the Butcher Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 ORDERS For the house: 4 sides. Hung 3 days. For the guest with the hook: whatever comes up the lane after dark. He is not fussy. For the guest in the straw: nothing. He feeds himself. p. 2 For the tall one with the lamp face: it does not eat. It breathes on things and they spoil. Keep it out of my kitchen. For the dog that walks like a man: bones. Big ones. Fresh. p. 3 For the boy with the hooves: everything, and then the plate. For the moth: nothing. It wants the lights. For the rabbit: he says he will catch his own. He always does. p. 4 For the doll: it will not eat while you are looking. Leave the tray. Turn round. For myself: the pig's face is wearing thin again. Need a new one. Ask the visitor if they are free."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"A Letter, Never Sent","u":"lore/index.html#a-letter-never-sent-2","t":"Margaret Hale Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 My dear sister, You asked why I have stopped writing. I have not stopped. I write every night. Henry burns them. He says the house reads the post. p. 2 He has filled the east rooms with guests. I have not seen them. I hear them. Something taps on my window three floors up. Something in the garden is taller than the hedges. p. 3 Henry says it is an honour. He says the nine of them choose a house, and the house is kept, and the family is kept. I asked what kept means. He would not look at me. p. 4 If you get this, do not come. If someone comes looking for us, tell them to look in the hall at the back. Tell them to bring nine of something. Your loving sister, Margaret"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Nursery Rhymes","u":"lore/index.html#nursery-rhymes-2","t":"(in a child's hand) Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 One for the rabbit who waits by the bridge, Two for the hook on the roof of the car, Three for the butcher in somebody's face, Four for the doll that gets closer each time. p. 2 Five for the scarecrow that walks in the corn, Six for the moth with the eyes like a fire, Seven for Mother Leeds' thirteenth child born, Eight for the dog on the road that stands up, p. 3 Nine for the lamp in the hills with the spade, and then they all come to the table to play. Count them on your fingers. Count them on their heads."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Guest List","u":"lore/index.html#guest-list-2","t":"H. Hale Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 ROOMS 1. The Bunnyman. The room under the stairs (he asked for the one with the axe). 2. The Hookman. Top floor. Windows to be left open. 3. The Hogshead. He has the kitchen. p. 2 4. The Porcelain Man. Nursery. The dolls are his. 5. The Harvestman. The barn, if he will take it. He will not. 6. Mothman. The turret. Take the bulbs out. p. 3 7. The Jersey Devil. Cellar. Lock it from the inside. 8. Dogman. Anywhere. Everywhere. 9. The tall one from Braxton County. The garden. It glows. The hedges died. Nine. The table is laid."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Field Notes","u":"lore/index.html#field-notes","t":"E. Carver, county surveyor Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 Sept. 12. Called out to the hill above the farms. A crater in the brush, the ground scorched, a smell like burnt metal and something sweeter. The boys say a thing came out of it ten feet tall. p. 2 They say its face was a lamp and its hood was a spade, and that it hissed, and glided, and the mist off it burned their throats. The dog that went up with them would not come down. p. 3 Sept. 14. Something has followed the boys home. Their mother says it stands at the end of the lane at night, lit up like a lantern. I have been asked to survey the Hale place next. The lane runs there."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"From the Glasshouse","u":"lore/index.html#from-the-glasshouse-2","t":"the Gardener Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 Mrs Hale, The gate stays locked. I have the only key and I am keeping it. Whatever you have let into your house, it is not coming into my glass. p. 2 The big flower is doing well. It has had the last of the dogs. Do not send the boy with the hooves again; he trod on the orchids. If I am taken, the key goes with whatever takes me. Then it is no business of mine."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Red Room","u":"lore/index.html#the-red-room-2","t":"Found: the Murder Mansion p. 1 sit face the wall don't turn round p. 2 it's behind you it's always behind you in this room that's what the room is for p. 3 count to nine slowly if you get to nine you can turn round nobody gets to nine"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"On the Mending","u":"lore/index.html#on-the-mending-2","t":"W. Found: the library desk p. 1 you found the table. good. it's an altar. the house was built round it. nine spikes, a horseshoe, open toward the doors. put a head on each spike. one of each of them. no doubles. it knows. p. 2 when there are nine, step back. i come down from the ceiling and i sew. what i make out of them won't be pretty and it won't be kind. it will be one thing instead of nine. that's the point. one thing can be killed. p. 3 it has the gardener's key on it. the gardener's dead, he just doesn't know it. bring torches. bring food. bring more than you think. don't let it get between you and the doors."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter three: the Glasshouse","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-three","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Botanic Gardens","u":"lore/index.html#the-botanic-gardens","t":"The Head Gardener's journal is on the lectern in his office. His under-gardener's ledger is in the Seed Vault under the hatch."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Head Gardener's Journal","u":"lore/index.html#head-gardeners-journal-2","t":"E. Thorne Found: the Head Gardener's office p. 1 The great flower opened today, under the dome. Nobody planted it. The roots came up through the tiles of the rotunda in a single night, and in the morning there it was - red as a wound, and warm to the touch. p. 2 It is warm. I put my ear to the stalk and there is a beat in it, slow, like a sleeper's. The orchids have all turned to face it. The ferns too. I have begun to think the ferns are looking at things. p. 3 The family came down from the house to see it. The children would not go near. The eldest said it smelled like the butcher's yard. They do not come any more. I have stopped going up to the house. p. 4 Feeding. Bone meal will not do; it wants better. The rats are gone from the potting shed. The cat is gone. I do not remember the last time I ate. I am not hungry. I am never hungry now. p. 5 The flies are thick on anyone who comes in now. Avery is black with them. They will not settle on me. It knows my clothes - it has grown into the cloth. My hat is in the shed, my coat in the chest here. Whoever wears them, it will take for me. p. 6 There are roots in my boots. I cut them away in the morning and by evening they are back. They do not hurt. That is what frightens me. They do not hurt. p. 7 Something came down from the house tonight - a great stitched thing, all iron and wrong pieces - and locked the gates from the outside, and took the key away with it. Good. Keep them out. Keep it in. Keep me in. p. 8 I hear it say my name through the lilies. It says it needs tending. It is right. Somebody must tend it. I am going to kneel by it a while. Just a while. If you find this: do not wake me. Do not touch the flower."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Seed Ledger","u":"lore/index.html#seed-ledger-2","t":"T. Avery, under-gardener Found: the Seed Vault p. 1 Moved the good seed down here, out of the glass. Mr Thorne says it doesn't like them. It doesn't like anything it didn't grow itself. p. 2 Mr Thorne doesn't sleep now. He kneels by it all night with the big shears across his knees, and in the morning the beds are cut back to the soil. He told me to bring it the rats. I won't. p. 3 His face. Something is growing in his face. Flowers - white ones, where his eyes were. He turned them to me today and they opened. I think he was smiling. p. 4 I've come down here to hide. He can't get down the ladder now; he's too tall. I can hear him up there, tending it. Snip. Snip. Snip. p. 5 The roots are coming through the walls. They're warm. I'm so tired. If I sleep down here they'll grow over me, the way they grow over everything. If anyone finds this, there is a key, the stitched thing took it, don't"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Bloom","u":"lore/index.html#the-bloom","t":"One lectern on each island of what the flower ate."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Rosemont Courier","u":"lore/index.html#the-rosemont-courier-2","t":"(four issues, folded together) Found: the street of Rosemont p. 1 THE ROSEMONT COURIER GARDENS' 'MONSTER FLOWER' DRAWS CROWDS A flower the size of a motor car has opened in the glasshouse at the Botanic Gardens. Head Gardener E. Thorne says it is a Rafflesia, 'though not one I know.' p. 2 THE ROSEMONT COURIER FLIES CLOSE MARKET STREET The Corporation has closed the market after swarms of flies 'thick as smoke' settled on the stalls. Traders blame the Gardens. The Gardens are no longer open to the public. p. 3 THE ROSEMONT COURIER FOURTEEN MISSING IN WEST END All were last seen walking toward the Gardens at night. Neighbours speak of a smell 'like a butcher's yard in August.' The Station is 'taking samples.' p. 4 LATE EDITION THE GROUND IS MOVING ON PARK ROAD Residents are asked to go to the shelters. Do not go near the Gardens. Do not go near anything green that moves. (the rest of the page is torn away)"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Research Log: Specimen 0","u":"lore/index.html#research-log-specimen-0-2","t":"Dr. H. Marsh, Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory Found: the research station p. 1 Specimen 0: the Gardens' Rafflesia. It is not a parasite on a vine. There is no vine. Its root goes down through the rotunda's floor and keeps going. We let down a line four hundred feet. It kept going. p. 2 The flies are not drawn to it. They come out of it. It makes them - they are how it tastes the air. Every subject exposed is 'liked' by the flies within the hour. Every subject but one. p. 3 Subject Thorne shows no infection at all. The flies settle on him and lift off again. It knows him: his clothes, his skin, the soil on him. Recommend all field staff wear his old work clothes. (He laughed when I asked.) p. 4 The bud under the glass is not the flower. It is a finger. The flower is somewhere under, and it is very, very big. We have built a binding at the root's end. While it holds, the flower cannot pull itself up the root. p. 5 If the binding is broken, it will come up the root, all the way, into the Gardens. It is hungry. It ate the street. It ate our east wing. It is eating us now. I can hear the tank (the writing stops)"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Shelter No. 4: Warden's Log","u":"lore/index.html#shelter-no-4-wardens-log-2","t":"J. Pike, Warden Found: Shelter No. 4, in the Bloom p. 1 Day 1. Forty-one in. Doors sealed at 20:00. The radio says stay put. The air smells of meat. Day 2. Flies under the door. Taped the door. p. 2 Day 4. Something big under the ground. It goes under us slow, like a train. Day 5. Mrs. Avery says her boy is at the Gardens with Mr. Thorne, he's safe there, the flies don't touch the gardeners. Nobody answered her. p. 3 Day 6. Fourteen left. The ones who went out to the Laboratory for medicine came back green round the mouth. They wouldn't stop smiling. Day 7. The roof is breathing. p. 4 Day 9. The whole shelter tipped. I looked out of the door and there was no street. There was green all the way down, and something at the bottom of it, opening and shutting. If you are reading this: it has us. Don't come down here without his clothes."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Binding","u":"lore/index.html#the-binding","t":"Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory Found: the Binding's island p. 1 THE BINDING Site 0: the root's end This stone holds the root down. While it holds, the flower cannot climb the root into Rosemont. DO NOT TOUCH THE STONE. DO NOT LOOSEN THE CHAINS. DO NOT LOOK DOWN. p. 2 (scratched under it, in another hand) it doesn't hold it. it only keeps it asleep. wake it and you'll have ten seconds before it pulls this whole island down its throat. run for the tear in the air. don't look back."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter four: the Flesh","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-four","t":"The Laboratory's six audio logs and Shelter No. 4's broadcasts are on Tapes and broadcasts ."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Uplink Station","u":"lore/index.html#the-uplink-station","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Uplink 7 - Duty Log","u":"lore/index.html#uplink-7-duty-log-2","t":"Lt. R. Okafor Found: the locker by the consoles p. 1 0400. Handshake with SENTINEL nominal. Capacitors at 31%. Works says another week before a full charge. Nobody up here knows what we're charging it for. The colonel says that's the point. p. 2 0900. Lost the city on the net. Not the net - the city. Every channel out of Rosemont went quiet at once. SENTINEL still answers. It always answers. p. 3 1600. Orders to pull the targeting array and keep it on us. If the station falls, SENTINEL can't be told where to fire. If the station falls, who would we be telling? p. 4 2300. Something big moving out by the glasshouse. Thermal can't see the edge of it. The array's in my locker. If you're reading this and you know what it's for - you don't need me to tell you."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Standing Orders","u":"lore/index.html#standing-orders-2","t":"Garrison Command Found: the control bunker p. 1 SENTINEL (orbital) is a weapon of last resort. It fires on a targeting array's lock. It fires only with a full CAPACITOR CELL seated in its core. p. 2 The core has a third socket. The engineers call it 'the governor'. Nobody has ever been told what goes in it. Do not ask the engineers about the governor."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Capacitor Works","u":"lore/index.html#the-capacitor-works","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Works Order 117","u":"lore/index.html#works-order-117-2","t":"Capacitor Works Found: the test cage p. 1 Cell 9 to be charged to full and held in the test cage for collection by Uplink. No collection came. p. 2 Cell 9 is holding. We can't bleed it off, and we can't leave it. The arcs have started jumping the rods by themselves. Two men burnt. The rest of us sleep in the yard."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Notice","u":"lore/index.html#notice","t":"Works Safety Officer Found: the test cage p. 1 DANGER - LIVE BANKS. Do not stand between rods. Do not touch the bus bars. If it starts to crackle, get down and get out. p. 2 Arc burns are not covered. (underneath, in pencil:) neither is whatever is in the cage."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Soul Well","u":"lore/index.html#the-soul-well","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Keeper's Prayer","u":"lore/index.html#the-keepers-prayer-2","t":"the Well-Keepers Found: the bottom of the well p. 1 Into the well, the ones who would not lie down. Into the well, the ones who would not stop. We keep the well. We keep them down. p. 2 One of them will not go quiet. Its light is too strong. It burns the others. We have bound it. We kneel by it. It must never leave the well. p. 3 If you have come for it, you have come for the strongest of them. Whatever you mean to pour into it - it will hold. That is what we are afraid of."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Ashford Nuclear Plant","u":"lore/index.html#ashford-nuclear-plant","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Ashford - Shift Log","u":"lore/index.html#ashford-shift-log-2","t":"Unit 2 Control Room Found: Ashford p. 1 0200. Reactor at 100%. Grid demand from Rosemont doubled overnight - the garrison's Works drawing again. Nobody tells us what for. p. 2 0700. The city's gone dark on the grid. All of it at once. We're running into nothing. Orders: hold power for the Works line only. p. 3 1300. Something under the glasshouse is drawing on the line. Not the Works. You can't draw on a line that isn't connected to anything. p. 4 1900. Breach in Unit 2. Not out of the reactor - into it. We scrammed. The core assembly's in the fuel pool. Don't go in the water without a suit."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Meridian Laboratory","u":"lore/index.html#meridian-laboratory","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Director's Notes","u":"lore/index.html#directors-notes-2","t":"Dr. H. Vasquez, Meridian Found: Meridian p. 1 The governor. SENTINEL's third socket. Garrison Command thinks it's a safety. It isn't. It's a throttle. What we're building takes it off. p. 2 The destabilizer holds a discharge on the edge of collapse. Seated in a railgun's core, it lets the gun draw on what no capacitor could hold. p. 3 Ashford's core for the power. The destabilizer to let go of it. And for the lens: Blackwater's blood. Not a slug. A ray. p. 4 We can't finish it. It needs something we don't have. Something that knows the dark."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Test Log - Cell 1","u":"lore/index.html#test-log-cell-1-2","t":"Meridian Test Hall Found: the test hall p. 1 Run 41. Destabilizer seated. Ring at 60%. Discharge held for 3.2 seconds. The coils sang. p. 2 Run 44. Held for 9 seconds. Then the coils started arcing to each other with the ring off. They still are. p. 3 Run 47. We lost the roof."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Memo","u":"lore/index.html#memo","t":"Meridian Logistics Found: Meridian Blackwater samples are NOT to be opened outside the cold room. If a vial is warm to the touch, it is not a vial any more. Leave the room. Seal it."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Blackwater Station","u":"lore/index.html#blackwater-station","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Station Log","u":"lore/index.html#station-log-2","t":"Blackwater Research Station Found: Blackwater p. 1 Day 1. It came down forty kilometres out. We towed what was left of it here and built the station round the tank. The blood doesn't freeze. p. 2 Day 30. The cultures took. Something lives in it. Small. It wants to be inside something bigger. p. 3 Day 31. It can't live in open air for long. Off the island it dies in seconds - nothing out there for it to eat. That doesn't help you in here. p. 4 Day 33. The tanks burst. The ones it got are still walking. The last vial's in the freezer. Meridian wanted it for their ray. Let them come and get it."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Specimen Notes","u":"lore/index.html#specimen-notes-2","t":"Dr. I. Okonkwo Found: Blackwater p. 1 The parasite: six legs, a mouth that opens like a flower. It goes for the back of the neck. p. 2 In a host it grows in hours. Then the host splits open and there are more of them. It needs the blood. Away from the dark matter, it starves."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter five: the Static","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-five","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Relay 6","u":"lore/index.html#relay-6","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Relay 6 - Operator's Log","u":"lore/index.html#relay-6-operators-log-2","t":"D. Ostrander, Hollow Ridge Found: the transmitter hut p. 1 Mon. Carrier dropped twice overnight. Not the transmitter - something riding on the carrier, like someone else keying up on our frequency. Gus wouldn't come in from the yard. p. 2 Wed. Gus came back out of the woods. Thin. He won't let me near his mouth. The noise on the carrier is worse at night. Like breathing, run through a fan. p. 3 Fri. People from the valley came up the road after dark. Nine of them. They didn't knock. They stood round the mast with their faces up, like they were listening to it. They didn't blink at the floodlight. p. 4 Sat. Still there. Gus is out with them. I can hear them in the headset - not on the air. In the headset. Under the static they're talking. They're saying where everyone is. p. 5 Sun. They've started climbing it. Tying something to it. It isn't rope. If you find this and it's still on the air - it isn't us. Cut it loose. All of it."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Notice","u":"lore/index.html#notice-2","t":"County Emergency Broadcast Found: Relay 6 p. 1 RELAY 6 - HOLLOW RIDGE. Authorized personnel only. This station relays the county emergency broadcast. Do not interfere with its operation. p. 2 Climbing the mast: harness at all times. Rest platforms at 12, 22 and 32 metres. (scratched into the cover, underneath:) THEY'RE ON EVERY PLATFORM"},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Starlite Drive-In","u":"lore/index.html#the-starlite-drive-in","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"To Whoever Runs Booth 1","u":"lore/index.html#to-whoever-runs-booth-1-2","t":"Starlite Drive-In Found: the projection booth p. 1 Ray - the late show's reel came in with no label and no distributor. Ran it anyway. Half the lot left before the end. The other half stayed in their cars after it finished. They're still out there. p. 2 I took the reel off. The screen kept showing it. Then the screen kept showing static, and the static kept coming off it like smoke off a fire. The things in it don't walk. They drift. p. 3 You can't hit them most of the time. They're not all the way here. Something on the right frequency might put them all the way here. When they come apart, they leave bits of the picture behind. p. 4 If you have to see the rest of the reel, load the projector with what's left of them and stay with it till the end. Don't let them at the booth. Whatever it shows you - it's where they come from. I'm not going."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Ancient Null Ruins","u":"lore/index.html#the-null-ruins","t":"The field notes of the surveyors who came looking (the relay men had written to the college about voices in the dead air), rubbings of what the old ones carved, and what the last of them scratched into a Hush's bench. The static took all of them down too."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Field Notes (I)","u":"lore/index.html#field-notes-i-2","t":"Dr. R. Calloway Found: the Listening Stones p. 1 The relay men on Hollow Ridge wrote to the college: voices in the dead air, near some old stones in the woods. Nobody would come. I came. Dale brought his sets. Teddy carries everything. p. 2 Six stones leaning in round a seventh, and an ear cut into every one of them. Not a carving of an ear. An ear. The spiral goes in further than the stone is thick. p. 3 Dale put a set down by the middle stone and tuned it to nothing. The nothing was talking. Many voices, very far down, all at once, like a crowd heard through a floor. p. 4 There's a room under the floor. Its north wall is all ears. Whoever built this was listening to something under everything. Teddy asked what. I said the dead. Dale said no. He said: the static. p. 5 Dale sleeps with his ear to the wall now."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Field Notes (II)","u":"lore/index.html#field-notes-ii-2","t":"Dr. R. Calloway Found: the Listening Stones p. 1 Translation, such as it is. The sign that keeps coming back is a spiral with a line through it. Everywhere else it means 'to hear'. Here it means 'to be heard'. p. 2 Over the stair: THE MANY SPEAK FROM UNDER. WE LISTEN SO THEY WILL NOT HAVE TO COME UP. Over the wall of ears: WE LISTENED TOO LONG. p. 3 Dale says the voices on his set know our names. He played it to me. One of them was mine. p. 4 There's a picture of another place they built. A house with one door, of a pale stone, a seal set in its floor. Under it: HERE THEY CANNOT HEAR YOU. Teddy wants to find one. So do I."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Field Notes (III)","u":"lore/index.html#field-notes-iii-2","t":"T. Marsh Found: the Sunken Choir p. 1 Dr. Calloway sent me ahead to the choir pit. Figures on every step, mouths open, all facing the hole in the middle. The hole goes down. There's a ladder. The ladder is new. Somebody's been down. p. 2 There's a room down here with ears in all four walls, facing in. The figures up top aren't singing. They're the audience. What they're listening to is whatever comes up the throat. p. 3 I can hear Dale. He went out to the dogs a week ago. His voice comes up the throat with the others. He says it's all right. He says it's warm down there, and nobody's alone. p. 4 I'm going to stay a little longer and listen."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Last Page","u":"lore/index.html#the-last-page-2","t":"Dr. R. Calloway Found: a Hush p. 1 We found one. The stone is pale and dead - knock on it and nothing rings. Step over the line in the door and the static on Dale's set stops. Not goes quiet. Stops. p. 2 Teddy had a thing on his neck from the woods, like a tick with a flower for a mouth. It came off him at the door in pieces. He's fine. He won't talk about it. p. 3 They followed us. Dogs first, the wrong shape, black spines. One ran at the door and leapt - and came apart in the air, like a picture on a set when you switch it off. The others stopped at the line. p. 4 Now they come and stand out past the two pillars and look in. They don't come closer. They don't blink. After a while they go away. After a while they come back. p. 5 Dale went out to them last night. He said they were calling him. I can't hear anything in here. That's the point. That's the whole point. Stay inside until it forgets your name."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Rubbing: the Lintel","u":"lore/index.html#rubbing-the-lintel-2","t":"Dr. R. Calloway Found: a Hush p. 1 (the carving over the door, as near as I can make it) p. 2 THIS IS A HUSH. THE STONE IS DEAD. NOTHING OF THE MANY CAN LIVE IN IT. WHAT THEY PUT IN YOU WILL DIE AT THE LINE. p. 3 THEY WILL COME TO THE DOOR. THEY WILL LOOK AT YOU. DO NOT GO OUT TO THEM. THEY KNOW YOUR VOICE. THEY CANNOT USE IT IN HERE. p. 4 WE BUILT THESE TOO LATE. THE MANY TOOK THE REST OF US DOWN WITH THE STATIC. IF YOU ARE READING THIS, THEY ARE COMING BACK UP."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Notebook","u":"lore/index.html#notebook","t":"D. Pruett Found: the stones, in the Zone p. 1 Ruth, if this gets to you. They didn't hurt me. They took me down the static, the whole way, and I came out on a grey field with no sky. The stones are here too. Everything they ever listened to came down here. p. 2 The voices are louder here. Not louder. Closer. They're not the dead, Ruth. They're the ones who listened. Everyone who ever put their ear to the stone. p. 3 There's something in the middle of this place, big as a church, coiled up. Threads go up off it into the dark. When it breathes I hear the relay. p. 4 I've been listening for you. I can hear you through the stone. You're in the Hush. Good. Stay there. Whatever sounds like me at the door - it isn't me any more."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Scratched Into the Bench","u":"lore/index.html#scratched-into-the-bench-2","t":"(nobody signed it) Found: a Hush, in the Zone p. 1 WE CAME DOWN WITH OUR HOUSE ROUND US. THE MANY TOOK THE GROUND AND THE SKY, AND LEFT THE ROOM. p. 2 OUTSIDE IT IS ALWAYS GREY. THEY STAND BY THE PILLARS AND SAY OUR NAMES IN OUR MOTHERS' VOICES. p. 3 THE GREAT ONE IN THE PIT CARRIES THEM UP ITS THREADS TO EVERY PLACE THAT LISTENS. WHEN IT DIES THEY WILL HAVE NO WAY UP. p. 4 WE ARE THE LAST. WE HAVE STOPPED ANSWERING. IT IS VERY QUIET IN HERE."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Hive","u":"lore/index.html#the-hive","t":"Somebody got to the hive before you: the hamlet's priest. His journal is on a lectern in what's left of a cottage, his chest beside it (since 1.50)."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Book of the Hollow Lane","u":"lore/index.html#the-book-of-the-hollow-lane-2","t":"Fr. Aldous Mercer Found: a cottage at the hive p. 1 Sunday. The Pruitt boy came down from the ridge with one of the things on his neck. We cut it off him. He has not spoken since. He listens at the walls. p. 2 Tuesday. The animals are standing in the fields with their heads up, all facing the same way. North. They have been like that since the radio mast went quiet. p. 3 Thursday. The Pruitt boy is gone. In the morning there was a heap of something in his bed. By evening there was no heap. It went somewhere. They all go somewhere. p. 4 Saturday. The ground behind the chapel is soft and warm. It moves when you are not looking at it. The heaps go into it. I rang the bell. Nobody came. Then everybody came. p. 5 I can hear them under the floor. Not voices. One voice, made of all of theirs. It is learning words. It has learned my name. It says it is lonely now the noise has stopped. It says it is building something to keep it company. p. 6 If you are reading this I am in the pit with the rest of them. Do not listen when it speaks with my voice. It thinks with the four bulbs on the black stalks. Burn what you can. Cut what you can't."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Sinkhole","u":"lore/index.html#the-sinkhole","t":"The county surveyor's notes are on a lectern at his camp on the rim of the sinkhole . His last page is on the landing where he stopped, halfway down the Burrow, his lantern beside it (since 1.54)."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Subsidence, Halloway's Low Field","u":"lore/index.html#subsidence-halloways-low-field-2","t":"E. Calder, County Surveyor Found: the surveyor's camp, on the rim p. 1 Called out to the Halloway place on account of the low field going in. Expected a cave-in - there are old workings under these hills, everyone says so. This is not a cave-in. p. 2 Thirty-four yards across. The sides are cut clean, as if something came up through the ground, not as if it fell in. The soil at the bottom is warm to the hand. At night it steams. p. 3 Halloway won't come near it. His dog went in on the second day. We heard it for a long while. It wasn't hurt, he says. It was answering something. p. 4 There's a passage at the bottom, round as a pipe, going down in a turn like a corkscrew. Its walls are lined with something like the inside of a cheek. It's warm. It moves when you breathe. I'm taking the long rope and the lantern. Somebody ought to measure it."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"(a loose page)","u":"lore/index.html#a-loose-page-2","t":"E. Calder Found: halfway down the Burrow p. 1 Halfway, by my count. The lantern doesn't throw far. The walls give when you lean on them. There are voices further down. Not words. Singing, almost. p. 2 One of them is Halloway's dog. One is the priest from the hamlet over the ridge - I'd know that voice anywhere. It says it's warm at the bottom. It says the others were down there first, and they don't like it. p. 3 The floor of the last room is a mouth. Stand on it long enough and it opens. I've come this far."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Deep","u":"lore/index.html#the-deep","t":"Down in the Deep , Low Marrow's reeve left his account in his cottage and the priest his last sermon in the church. In the Old Halls the old ones cut theirs into the walls, either side of the hall."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Low Marrow","u":"lore/index.html#low-marrow-2","t":"T. Ashby, Reeve Found: the reeve's cottage, Low Marrow p. 1 The ground went out from under us on the Tuesday night. The whole of Low Marrow - the church, the green, the pond, the lane - down. We fell a long while. The houses held, mostly. p. 2 It is warm down here, and dark. The pond is not water any more. Something sang to us the first night, under everything, very sweet. Some of us went to it. They did not come back. p. 3 The rest of us found out about the white things. They have no eyes. They come when you talk, when you walk, when you cry. Ellen's boy cried. p. 4 We do not talk now. We go about in our stockings, and we do not cry. Old Pell says there is a king further in that the white things keep away from - a king who stopped his own ears. Pell has gone to find him. p. 5 He said: follow the stones with the ears cut in them. A cap burns on every one. If you find this, go quiet. Go in your stockings. Follow the stones."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"(the last sermon)","u":"lore/index.html#the-last-sermon-2","t":"Rev. J. Fairley Found: the church, Low Marrow p. 1 Text: and they have ears, but they hear not. I have decided to preach on the singing. p. 2 It says it is lonely. It says it lost everything it had, up there, and came down here to be warm. It says we can be warm with it. I believe it. God forgive me, I believe every word. p. 3 I am going down to it tonight. I have asked the others to come. They are afraid of the white things. The white things are only listening for it too, poor souls. They just never stopped."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"(cut in the wall, in marks older than letters)","u":"lore/index.html#cut-in-the-wall-in-marks-older-than-letters","t":"the old ones Found: the Old Halls p. 1 We were here first. Before the light up there. We heard everything: the rock settling, the roots growing down, the water a long way off. Then the singing came down through the roots. p. 2 To hear it was to go to it. It took us, a few at a time, and we became its. Our king took stone and stopped his ears, and then he could not hear it, and he did not go. p. 3 He told us all to do the same. Some of us did. The ones who would not stop their ears listened harder and harder, to hear anything else at all. They listened until they went blind. They are listening still."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"(cut in the wall by the dais)","u":"lore/index.html#cut-in-the-wall-by-the-dais-2","t":"the old ones Found: the Old Halls p. 1 The king does not hear. The king does not see. The king feels the floor. When you come before him, be still. p. 2 If you would have what he put in his ears, you must take it out of him. He will not give it. With it in your own, the singing is only singing."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapters six and seven","u":"lore/index.html#chapters-six-and-seven","t":"The Door at the End of the World and the Hub are told in cutscenes and in the Watcher's own words, not on paper: see The Watcher speaks and the chapters' story pages, six and seven ."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"Chapter eight: the Dead Water","u":"lore/index.html#chapter-eight","t":""},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"The Watcher's chart","u":"lore/index.html#the-watchers-chart","t":"The Watcher hands you his chart when you come down to the Dead Water (since 1.63.2). Unroll it and point at a water, and it shows what he wrote of it. These are his notes, in the chart's order."},{"p":"Notes and books","h":"THE WATCHER'S CHART","u":"lore/index.html#the-watchers-chart-2","t":"Found: in his hand, on the rig The Black Below. THE DEAD ZONE. The floor drops away and doesn't stop. The leviathans live down there. Don't. The Grey Shelf. Grey water over grey silt. The rig stands in it. Nothing here is in a hurry - mostly. The Haemal Reach. The water's thick with blood. Clotfish come in swarms; the Siphons wait for them to pass. The Wireweed. Weed like wire, and it sings. The Choir Eels nest in it. Don't touch the bright ones. The Lantern Fields. Lights in the dark as far as you can see. Most of them are bulbs. Some of them aren't. The Ossuary Flats. A plain of bone. Whatever died here, died big. The Stiltfins pick it clean. The Brine Sink. The brine pools eat what falls in. The water's sour, and the Puffbloats like it. The Molar Reef. Teeth, grown into a reef. The Grinners live in it. They smile at you. The Drowned Mycelia. Mushrooms the size of towers, drowned. Their spores burst if you brush them. The Rime Shelf. Ice under the sea. Things are frozen in it. Some of them wake up. The Ember Vents. Vents roaring up from below. Warm. The Mantlecrabs crowd round them - mind your power. The Carrier Wave. The static's loudest here. The water hums. Your instruments won't like it. Point at a water to see where it lies, and what he wrote of it."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html","t":"The Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory's staff left six cassettes, and Shelter No. 4's radio set still picks up two broadcasts. Between them they tell you what happened under the gardens, what is asleep in the reactor pool, and how to get the Front Assembly out of Bunker B. Later, in Chapter Five, two things you carry start talking to you: a piece of the Chorus, and the one voice it couldn't swallow."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Laboratory's audio logs","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-audio-logs","t":"Audio Log Use: play the tape, or put it in a tape recorder A cassette from the Laboratory, its label in somebody's hand. Someone was recording. Use a tape to play it: the click, the hiss, and the voice, line by line. Since 1.41 every line is voiced, slowed and dropped an octave into something too big for the room, saturated and tape-worn, catching on a syllable now and then. Each tape ends with it laughing. Subtitles show over your hotbar while it plays, and the words go into chat too. Put a tape in a Tape Recorder and it plays out loud for anyone within about twenty blocks: its reels turn, its level meter jumps and static crackles off its speaker. Sneak and use it to take the tape out. The Laboratory's recorders still have their tapes in them. Researchers sometimes drop the later tapes."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Marsh, Control Room","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#marsh-control-room","t":"*click* - Dr. H. Marsh This is Marsh. Control room. The power's gone, and the Core is all that's keeping it asleep. Specimen Zero went into the pool the night the tank burst. It sleeps against the Core. It likes the warmth. If anyone needs the Core out: the coolant has to be isolated first, or the hall stays sealed. The levers are on this wall. The order matters. [the lever order, different in every world]. Any other order and the whole level alarms. Then the blast doors open. Then you lift it. Then you run, because it will wake. I'm going down to sit with it. Somebody should. [something on the tape laughs] Pull the three coolant levers in Marsh's order and the hall's blast doors grind up (\"COOLANT ISOLATED - REACTOR HALL OPENING\"). Pull one out of turn and the alarm goes (\"WRONG SEQUENCE - COOLANT ISOLATION FAULT\"), the levers drop back, and six of the staff come for you."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Marsh, Personal","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#marsh-personal","t":"*click* - Dr. H. Marsh Personal log. The thing under the Gardens isn't the flower. The flower has been holding it down. Reyes, the night technician, cut a sample from the root's end. By morning his hands were somebody else's. We sealed him in the big tank on Sublevel 1 and called him Specimen Zero. He talked for three days. Then he stopped using words. It hates the flowers. Every sample we put near it, it reached for. Tore at. The keycard's in this drawer. The tank won't hold much longer. [something on the tape laughs] In the director's locked desk, with the Level 2 Keycard. Three good blows split the drawer."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Okafor, Sample Log","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#okafor-sample-log","t":"*click* - Dr. A. Okafor Sample log, day nine. Bloom tissue placed beside Zero's growth. The growth recoiled - then attacked it. Flower ash kills it outright. Burn the Gardens' flowers, pack the ash with powder, and you have something it can't stand. A flower, a burnt petal, gunpowder. We have a weapon. We have one weapon. [something on the tape laughs] That's the Flower Ash Bomb's recipe."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Reception","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#reception","t":"*click* - Reception Welcome to Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory. All visitors must sign in at reception. Sublevels one and two are restricted to staff with Level 2 clearance. Please do not let them follow you down. [something on the tape laughs]"},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Lin, Containment","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#lin-containment","t":"*click* - Dr. S. Lin Containment, oh-two-fourteen. The tank's cracked. It isn't trying to get out. It's listening. Oh-two-thirty. It came out slowly. Politely. It went past us to the lift shaft and down, toward the reactor. The pool's warm. It likes warm. Everyone stay out of the hall. [something on the tape laughs]"},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Audio Log: Doyle, Hazmat Team","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#doyle-hazmat-team","t":"*click* - Sgt. R. Doyle Hazmat team, entry. Suits on. Radiation in the hall's off the scale near the pool. Nobody stands by the pool without a suit. Contact. Something in the water. Jenkins is laughing. Why is Jenkins laughing. [something on the tape laughs]"},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Shelter No. 4's radio","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#shelter-broadcasts","t":"Use the Shelter Radio Set in the radio room to hear it. With the power off it plays the evacuation notice. With both generators running, it turns into Control's emergency broadcast."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The evacuation notice","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#evacuation-notice","t":"Rosemont Civil Defence, on a loop This is Rosemont Civil Defence. This is not a drill. All residents of zones C and D proceed at once to Shelter Number Four, Victoria Park. Bring nothing. Do not stop for anyone on the street who is unwell. Wardens will close the blast door at twenty-two hundred hours. It will not be opened again until the all-clear. This is Rosemont Civil Defence. This is not a drill."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Control's emergency broadcast","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#emergency-broadcast","t":"Once the shelter's power is back Shelter Four, Shelter Four, this is Control. We see your power on. Respond. Shelter Four, do not open the vault. Repeat: do not open the vault. Whatever is in bunk hall B is not your residents any more. Whatever the squad told you, they are not coming back up. If anyone down there can hear this - the overload switch, over the plates in bunker B. Get it onto the plates. Shelter Four, respond. That's how to beat the Warden of Shelter No. 4 ."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"Voices from the static","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#voices","t":"These aren't recordings. They're things that are still alive enough to talk, and what they say comes up over your hotbar in italics when you hold them to your ear."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Chorus Fragment","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-chorus-fragment","t":"\"A piece the Chorus left behind as it went down. It's still part of it, wherever it is.\" It's a knot of grey-violet flesh with a face in it the size of a thumbnail, its eyes shut, its mouth moving. You get one when the Chorus runs from its pit. Hold it to your ear and it whispers what the Chorus is thinking, down there: One at random down. down where it is warm. we remember the dark under the hills. we are not alone down here. there are others. older. the bloom's roots go deeper than you ever dug. come down and find us. we are learning your name. you broke our thoughts. we are growing new ones. listen. under your feet. that is us. every one we take remembers. every one remembers you. Since 1.54.0, while the Chorus is still alive it also tells you which way it went. Face the right way and it whispers clearly, and what it says tells you how far. Side on, it's faint and broken. Facing away, there's only static. Up top, leading you to the Sinkhole: far (over 600 blocks), that way, near, here down. a long way down. far from here - that way. that way. under the hills. we can feel you coming. closer. we can hear you walking. we can hear your heart. here. right under you. come down. it's warm. Coming out in the Deep home. we are home. come and find us. we are deeper. In the Deep, leading you to the Warm Heart deeper. a long way yet. through the dark - that way. that way. past the old ones' halls. they don't like us. they won't like you. close now. can you hear us singing? we can hear you. here. we are right here. we are finished growing. Side on, or facing away ...colder... no... turn... (nothing but static) What the Chorus says out loud, through its forms and from its pit, is on The Watcher speaks , with his answers. Since 1.60.3 the Chorus also has a hidden voice: now and then, out of all its faces muttering together, one voice speaks on its own for fourteen seconds while the rest hush. It's a sound with a subtitle (\"The Chorus: one voice out of all of them\"), not words on the screen."},{"p":"Tapes and broadcasts","h":"The Last Voice","u":"lore/tapes-and-broadcasts.html#the-last-voice","t":"\"A face cut out of the Chorus, its eyes open now. It isn't singing. It's trying to tell you something: a door at the end of the world, and the seal on it.\" It comes out of the Chorus, whole, when it dies in the Warm Heart. Hold it up and it talks: One at random \"...there's a door. at the end. he sealed it...\" \"...it was so loud in there. it's so quiet now...\" \"...take me to the end of the world. i'll open it for you...\" \"...i was a farmer. i think. i had a dog...\" \"...the one in the black coat knows. ask him what he locked up...\" \"...don't put me down. please don't put me down in the dark again...\" In the End \"...here. it's here. can you feel it? something on the other side is listening...\" \"...hold me up. here. he made this seal with his own hands. i can open it...\" Something cracks, all the way across the End's sky - and stays cracked. The seal he put on it is broken. \"...there. out past the obsidian. a door. go through it. i'll be quiet now...\" In the Stalls \"...shh. don't wake them. they're watching...\" \"...they're getting up. all of them...\" It said it would be quiet, but if you're still carrying it, it whispers in the Stalls too: when you first come in, and when the Audience gets up for the Crowd. See Chapter Six ."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html","t":"The Watcher speaks in chat, in lower case, a line at a time, and only at the moments that matter. Here is what it says, in story order. Lines in blue are on-screen text from the same scenes. His lines from 1.47.2 to 1.63.3 (after signing off, the Hive and the Deep, the Door at the End of the World, the Hub and the Dead Water) are here too, along with a few older ones this page used to be missing: chapter two's first kills, the Mended, and the glasshouse."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter one","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-one","t":"After your first kill (it stares) ??? you shouldn't have done that, [your name]. ??? it was only watching you. like i do. ??? i'll remember this. After your fifth kill (it waves) ??? five. ??? you're counting too, aren't you [your name]? ??? i know where you sleep. i've known for a while. After your ninth kill (it points) ??? nine. ??? do you know what nine heads are for? ??? there is a church that isn't on any map. find it. i'll be on the ceiling. At the Lullaby Mother's Hollow, if she drags you in ??? she wanted to keep you. i won't let her. not yet. ...and you're back. Your hands smell like old soil. As the Hollow Saint rises ??? look up. i told you i'd be here. ??? this is what they were all pieces of. During the fight ??? you're hurting it. let me help. ??? there. now it can see you properly. As his beam drags it down ??? no. you don't get to stay up here. ??? they've been waiting for you down there. ??? there. it's home. After it falls The Hollow Saint has fallen. ??? you did it. ??? do you understand what you've done? they were keeping it in. ??? it was the only thing in this world bigger than me. ??? thank you. ??? i'll be seeing you. all of you. i always have. ??? wait. ??? do you hear that? where it fell. it's still open. Something has torn open where the Hollow Saint fell."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter two","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-two","t":"The Breach opens ??? it was never only about the saint. ??? go through. i'll meet you on the other side. ??? you didn't think that was the end of it, did you. ??? when the saint fell it left a hole. it's been widening ever since. ??? here. go through. In the Void ??? there. you can breathe here. for now. ??? careful. there's no ground out here but this. ??? this is where they came up from. the breach tore this bit off with it. ??? the altar's sleeping. wake it. empty hands. ??? and don't look too long at the dark. it looks back. ??? it didn't only tear this bit off. there's more out there - a house, a graveyard, the radio mast. ??? the bridges and the stones will get you across. if you fall, something will catch you. it always does. ??? you can't stay out here. not with it shut. At the Breach Altar ??? it's sleeping. wake it. empty hands. Waking it ??? feel that? that's the breach closing behind them. ??? the first breach let the stories through. the things people made up in the dark, and typed, and believed. ??? creepypastas. the little ones. i've sent them home. ??? but a breach doesn't close. it only goes deeper. ??? under the stories are the ones that were true. the ones in the newspapers. the ones they found in the woods. ??? nine of them are coming up now. you'll want to know what to look for. ??? a rabbit with an axe, under a bridge that isn't there anymore. ??? a hook. you'll hear it on the roof of your car first. ??? a butcher who wears a pig's face, and doesn't need his hooks to be empty. ??? a doll that only moves when nobody is looking at it. ??? a scarecrow that wasn't in the field yesterday. ??? red eyes on the bridge, the night before it fell. ??? the thirteenth child. it has hooves. ??? something on two legs that should be on four. ??? and a tall thing in the hills. it glows. it hisses. its face is a spade. ??? they have a house now. it was always theirs. [how far, and which way]. ??? bring me their heads. one of each. you know how this works. ??? and the gardens. stay out of the gardens. not yet. When the breach closes ??? turn around. ??? it's closing. it took what it wanted to take. ??? nothing else comes up that way now. the nine are already here. The breach has closed. The first time anyone comes up to the Murder Mansion ??? this is their house. ??? they come back here when they're done with you. to rest. to put things away. ??? the hall"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Mended","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-mended","t":"The ninth head on its spike: he comes down from the ceiling and sews ??? nine. all of them. ??? listen to them. you can still hear it, can't you? the agony. everything they screamed, and everything they made others scream. ??? and the aggression. all that wanting to hurt. it doesn't die when they do. it just waits for somewhere to go. ??? i'll give it somewhere. ??? harvest it. every last drop of it, out of every one of them. ??? then stitch them shut. iron through every joint. it mends. it always mends. ??? their iron will is what will stand it up. ??? there. you brought me the pieces. i only put them together. During the fight ??? oh, it's angry now. good. let it be angry. ??? no. not yet. it isn't finished. ??? it's mending. stop it, or it'll be whole again. Its death ??? no - no. hold together. hold... ??? it held. for a while. that's more than they ever did. ??? ...listen. something in the glass house heard all of that. it's awake now. The Watcher also wrote its instructions down: On the Mending , open on the Murder Mansion's library desk, and Of What Swims Out Here , in the Void."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter three","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-three","t":"The Rusted Garden Key opens the gate ??? you opened it. ??? it's been waiting for someone to come and tend it. ??? go in, if you have to. don't touch the flower. The Gardener dead ??? it's dead. ??? everything in there was growing out of it. the flower. the things in the beds. him. ??? he tended it so long it grew into him. don't stay. things that were growing don't like to stop. The green rift opens A green rift has torn open over the Gardener's dead flower. ??? the flower isn't dead. ??? that thing under the glass was only a finger of it. it's opened a way down to the rest. ??? his clothes. wear his clothes in there, or it'll be eating you before you've taken ten steps. In the Bloom ??? there's no way out of here now. ??? you're not wearing his clothes. be quick. ??? breathe through your sleeve. it's in the air. ??? you're not wearing his clothes. it can smell you. it's eating you already - be quick. ??? this is what it ate. a street. the laboratory that studied it. a shelter full of people. it keeps them up here like a larder. ??? and it's down there. look down. no - don't. ??? if you fall, it catches you. it doesn't let go. ??? the stone in the middle is what holds it down. leave it. please. The Binding breaks ??? no. NO - that was holding it down- ??? the rift. RUN. It comes up the root ??? you broke it. it's coming up the root. ??? get away from the glass house. get AWAY. The Great Bloom has come up through the Botanic Gardens. ??? that's it. that's the real one. ??? it's taken the gardens. don't go near it. it reaches."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter four","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-four","t":""},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Flesh","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-flesh","t":"THE FLESH WAKES / the flower made it ??? that's not the flower. that's what the flower made. ??? it came out of the flower's rot - and it hates what made it. it'll eat this whole world to get at them. ??? and it's coming out of the ground. run. Rosemont ??? there's a way to kill the big one. the laboratory's reactor. three pieces. the laboratory, the shelter, and a truck in the city. ??? the truck's in the middle, in the checkpoint. the part's locked in a cradle on its back. ??? it'll take an axe. and they'll hear it. ??? they heard that. all of them. ??? the bus moved. it's still asleep. walk. don't touch it. ??? you lost it. it's back on the truck. The Congregation dead ??? that was everyone who was on the 6:40."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Laboratory","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-laboratory","t":"??? the laboratory. the core's at the bottom, in the reactor's pool. ??? the way down takes a keycard. the director kept one in a locked desk. ??? the suits are in the lockers. you'll want one, near the pool. ??? the control room opens the hall. the director left a tape there. ??? there's something asleep in that pool. it's been sleeping against the core. ??? take it and it wakes. burn the bodies first. it eats them. ??? that's the hall open. everything down there heard it. ??? there. it's awake. stay out of the water's reach. ??? that was the last of them. it felt that - it's starving now. it's coming up. ??? it's locking itself down. ninety seconds. run. ??? you lost the core. it's back on its rack, at the bottom of the laboratory."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Shelter No. 4","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#shelter-no-4","t":"??? shelter four. the front assembly's in bunker b, behind the blast door. ??? no power down here. that door won't open without it. the generators are in the radio room. ??? they need fuel. it'll be in one of the lockers. keep quiet - most of them are still hiding. ??? that's the fuel. the generators are in the radio room - one in each. ??? that'll be heard all through the ducts. hold the room. ??? that's bunker b's door. it's opening. the front assembly's in there - and so is the squad. ??? the squad they sent to hold it. they're still holding it. ??? the guns are part of them now. don't stand in the open. the front's on the dais, at the far end. ??? that was their sergeant. the dais is yours. ??? listen. the walls. the north wall. ??? keep moving. keep the cover between you and it. ??? the plates under the gallery. get it onto them, and throw the switch up there. ??? the switch on the gallery's dead without the generators. you'll have to do it the hard way. (instead, if the generators aren't running) ??? get out of the blood. up the stairs - the gallery. ??? that hurt it. it won't walk into that twice. ??? that was all of them. bunker b. it's quiet down there now. ??? i've left you something in the shelter. on the dais in bunker b. a compass - it points at the city. ??? you lost the front assembly. it's back on its mount, in bunker b. ??? take the assembly up. carefully. it's heavy. ??? i've left you something. on the dais, by the mount. ??? a compass. it points at the city. rosemont. that's where you go next. ??? all three. that's the device. it needs wiring before it'll do anything."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Device and the Gardener","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-device","t":"??? you found them. all three of them. ??? all three. bring them to one of my altars - i'll put it together for you. or the cradle, if you'd rather. ??? hold still. i'll take you to it. (or, with the cradle near: \"hold still. i'll put it together here.\") ??? there. it's done. take it to the bloom - it's yours to carry. ??? that's it. that's a bomb. ??? the flesh knows what it's for. it'll let you through while you carry it. ??? take it to the bloom. to what's left of the glass house. ??? here he comes. ??? it's giving him back. it doesn't want that thing anywhere near its mouth. ??? the roots are open. the flesh is coming in. it hates him more than it hates you. ??? he's done. ??? no. wait. listen to it. ??? it isn't letting him go. it's growing him back. ??? stay close. kill him again, and i'll open it. ??? he's done. ??? it's shut itself up tight. i can open it. not yet. ??? keep the device close. i'll come for you when it's time. ??? you lost the device. it's back where you last set it down."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The launch","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-launch","t":"??? bring the device. i'm not opening it for nothing. ??? he's done. now it's open, and it stays open as long as i'm holding it. ??? take it through. put it down past the edge. then run. ??? don't look at them. i've got them. i can't hold them long. ??? the end of the ledge. the mark. put it down there. ??? that's it. now arm it. hold it down three seconds. ??? and then you run. you don't stop, and you don't look back. ??? i've got you. don't look. ??? it's still beating. ??? its soul wasn't collected. you can't kill a thing like that with fire. ??? it'll grow back. and the other one is still spreading."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Meanwhile","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#meanwhile","t":"At a nest ??? a bed of them, round something in the middle. it's copying the flower. ??? the flower made seeds. the Flesh makes eggs. she's asleep in the bottom of that. ??? don't go near the sacs. and if you have the ash - she hates the ash. ??? she grew round a seed of the flower. it's in what's left of her - still beating. ??? take it. the flower's seed knows the Flesh. hold it to you and you'll see them through anything. Swallowed It swallowed you whole. You're still alive. ??? you're alive. you're in it. it's digesting you. ??? cut at the walls. hurt it enough and it'll throw you back up. ??? it threw you up. get away from it before it wants you back. When the Flesh outgrows its reach ??? it's pulling back. it can't hold this much ground - not yet."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The end of it","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-end-of-it","t":"IT CHANGED / and its roar went all the way round the world ??? i knew it would do that. ??? the bomb was never going to kill it. i needed it to change. bigger. a soul that size is worth something. ??? but my darkness isn't enough for it now. i need a stronger soul to pour it through. ??? there's a gun up above the sky. they built it before the city fell. they never got to fire it. ??? it needs a power source. three places woke up when the bloom changed. what you need is in them. ??? build the core. bring it to the forsaken altar, and i'll put my magic into it. then we kill it. Handing out the needles ??? take these. each one points to one of them. ??? the uplink. the works. the well. one thing out of each. The first time anyone reaches each place ??? this is where they talked to it. the gun. (the Uplink Station) ??? the array's in the bunker. the locker by the consoles. ??? careful. it still holds its charge. stay off the rods. (the Capacitor Works) ??? the cell's in the cage at the back. ??? they put the souls down there that wouldn't rest. (the Soul Well) ??? one of them is strong enough. it's at the bottom. so are they. Finding the parts ??? that's the array. it tells the gun where to look. ??? the cell. that'll hold what the gun needs to fire. ??? ...that one. yes. that one will hold my darkness. ??? put them together. iron round them, redstone to wake them. an orbital core. ??? now bring it to me. the forsaken altar. At the altar, with the Orbital Core ??? give it to me. ??? this is going to hurt it. ??? there. feel that? that's me. all of me that's left. ??? it'll hold. build the gun round it. As it grows ??? it's growing. everything it eats, it gets bigger. ??? twice the size it was. don't let it eat. stay off its petals. ??? it's filling the sky. use the gun while there's still something to aim at. ??? that's as big as it gets. it's still hungry. The railgun built ??? point it at the ground and hold it. let it find the gun. then let go. ??? keep away from its reach when you do. it'll know where it's coming from. ??? ...did you hear that. it's calling something up out of the ground. ??? the gun can hurt it. it can't end it. what can end it is in what it's calling up. Each railgun strike on the changed Bloom ??? again. ??? it felt that. but look - it's closing up already. ??? it heals as fast as you tear it. ??? it isn't enough. not this gun. we need a"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Ten days later","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#ten-days-later","t":"It opens differently depending on where it finds you ??? let me in. (knocking at your door) ??? you should lock your doors. (in your house, through the door) ??? glass doesn't keep me out. nothing does. (in your house, through the wall) ??? careful. they were about to tear you apart. (in a mine, after killing what was there) ??? there you are. down in the dark, as always. (in a mine) ??? boo. (in the woods) ??? did i scare you? good. you should be scared. (in the woods, after that) ??? it's me. i'm back. (anywhere else) Then ??? ten days. i'm rested now - stronger, like i said i'd be. ??? but i didn't come to talk about me. it's the parasites. ??? the infection in those new places - blackwater - it isn't from here. ??? it came into this realm from another one. the null static zone. ??? the flesh is dying back. with the flower dead it's got nothing to grow from. ??? they don't need the flower. they'll get into anything with blood in it - a cow, a horse, a villager. ??? you won't see it often. but if something you know starts acting wrong, don't let it near you. ??? keep your eyes open."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter five","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-five","t":"CHAPTER FIVE The relay ??? do you hear it. under the static. it isn't noise. ??? they're talking to each other. something's carrying it. this points to where. ??? listen. that isn't static. that's them, talking. (arriving at Relay 6) ??? everything one of them hears goes up that mast and out to all of them. cut what's holding on to it. The relay off the air ??? the relay's quiet. the static isn't gone. it's going somewhere. ??? there's a place it all runs down into. like water. this points to it. ??? there's nothing here. that's what's wrong with it. not even the dark. (arriving at the Starlite) ??? the projector's still in the booth. kill the things in the static. feed it what's left of them. watch. The late show ??? they came out of the picture. they always do, when somebody's watching. ??? you can't hurt them yet. they're not all the way here. ??? the core. hold it to your ear - tuned in, they're as real as you are. ??? or let one reach for you. when it does, it's all the way here. hit it then. ??? kill one and it leaves a frame of the picture behind. four frames. the projector's up in the booth. ??? run the reel. see what's under all of it. The last reel ??? you saw it. that's what's under all of it. that's where they come from. ??? it was carrying them. the way the relay was. only it's alive. keep the reel. The Null Static Zone ??? that's where they came from. it's under all of it. ??? go on. i'll be there when it's done. ??? the null static zone. everything that went into the static came here. ??? it's in the middle. its threads go up to every mast you ever saw. cut them. Signing off ??? it's dead. good. ??? it wasn't theirs, you know. it was a carrier. it carried whatever was put on it. ??? the static was a door. and this was holding it open. ??? this, i'll keep. ??? for the future. ??? go home. there's nothing on the air now. SIGNING OFF"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"After signing off","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#after-signing-off","t":"Half a minute after you're home, wherever you are ??? ...this was unexpected. ??? but we can work with it. we'll make do. ??? it seems the carrier did what it was supposed to do. it carried them - all the way out. ??? the parasites are increasing. every one of them hostile. the numbers are going off the charts. in your world. ??? it's dangerous out there. more than ever, now. ??? there's nothing we can do about it for now. just try not to die. for me. in the meantime. ??? and i suggest you don't go to the end. ??? ...actually. i'll make sure you can't go there. it's dangerous for you, player. ??? you know i can see you right now, right, [your name]? ??? remember who you work for. Going through an End portal while it's shut The way's shut. He shut it. ??? no. i said not there. (the first time) ??? not there. i told you. (after that)"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Hive","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-hive","t":"It Speaks: the first night after the Hive has grown. Five of its pure forms stand up round you, and it speaks through them the Chorus we were many. we were scattered. we heard each other in the noise. the Chorus you cut the throat that carried us. now there is only quiet. the Chorus so we are growing another way to be one. out of all of them. out of everything they knew. the Chorus come and see what we are becoming. come and be heard. Then they sink back into the ground, and he's beside you ??? it lost its voice when the carrier died. so it's growing itself a mind instead. ??? out of everything it took. every body. every face. everything any of them ever knew. ??? when it's finished it won't need the static to talk to them. it'll just be all of them. ??? this points to where it's growing. go before it wakes up all the way. The first time anyone reaches the Hive The ground here is warm, and soft, and it gives under you. Something under it is breathing. ??? it took them whole. the people, the houses. everything they knew is in that pit now. ??? it thinks with those, on the stalks round the pit. cut them and it can't think straight. there was a priest here. read him. The Mind: it comes up out of its pit the Chorus you. we know you. you were in the static with us. you were loud. the Chorus we do not need a throat now. we have a thousand mouths, and all of them are listening. the Chorus the ones you lost are here with us. they are singing. would you like to hear them? the Chorus come down. be heard. be one more voice. It Runs: brought down to a quarter the Chorus no. no - not yet. we are not finished. ??? it ran. it can do that now. it's got enough of a mind to be afraid. ??? it's gone down. deep. where everything went before the static was ever a noise. ??? that's a piece of it. it still talks. keep it - listen to it. it'll tell you where it went. ??? it'll come back up. bigger. and next time it won't be half finished."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"The Deep","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-deep","t":"The first time anyone reaches the Sinkhole ??? this is where it went down. the ground didn't fall in. it was pulled. ??? someone measured it before you. he went down after it. the piece of it you've got will tell you how far down it goes. The Chorus, whole, dead in the Warm Heart Far below, the singing stops. It doesn't start again. A while later, to whoever was there ??? it's quiet down there now. i can hear you breathing. ??? you've got something of it. one voice it couldn't swallow. keep it. ??? there's a door at the end of the world with a seal on it. i made that seal. i can't open it. ??? that voice can. when you're ready, take it to the end. What the Chorus Fragment and the Last Voice whisper is on Tapes and broadcasts ."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter six","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-six","t":"The Last Voice, carried into the End, breaks his seal Something cracks, all the way across the End's sky - and stays cracked. The seal he put on it is broken. ??? ...don't. Front Row: the Crowd's dead, and one seat is still taken ??? it was a good show. ??? you weren't meant to see the end of it. ??? you want to know what i locked up. ??? come and see, then. Chapter Six / The Door at the End of the World - Part One: The Audience Coming into the Vault ??? ...in here. all the way up. don't look at them. The Watch ??? this is where i watch from. ??? they watch the picture. i watch them. ??? your world's a show to them. ??? the worse it gets, the more of them come. ??? they left you a ticket. it admits one. ??? not you. ??? something came in behind you. ??? it's come for what i kept. the omni. the carrier. my first reel. ??? get to them before it does. bring them here. Taking what's left of the Carrier off its plinth ??? ...quick. they can all move while it's loose like that. All three brought to the Watch ??? ...it's here. it's in the wall. The First Reel ??? this is the first thing anyone ever saw on the other side. ??? i kept it so i'd never forget what it looks like. ??? that's what i kept out. ??? it's all for that one. the whole show. ??? and now it's seen you. ??? it's coming through. Chapter Six / The Door at the End of the World - Part Two: The Watcher's Vault Curtain Up: the first time anyone comes through the black door ??? you came through. good. ??? it hasn't looked this way. not yet. ??? this is the other side. ??? it's watched your world since the first picture. ??? everything that ever happened to you - it watched. ??? now it wants to see you up close. ??? stay out of its eye. get behind the scenery. ??? when it leans in - hit it. ??? i'll run the projector. The Viewer: loading his last projector ??? ...its eye's shut. now - the heart. ??? every colour at once. it's never seen that. ??? ...the carrier. it carries whatever's put on it. ??? your world. all of it. out onto it. ??? it's getting up. keep its hands off the projector. ??? ...now. give it the reel. The last show ??? everyone's always watched it. ??? nobody ever showed it to itself. ??? there. something to watch. ??? it'll watch that forever. ??? it won't look at your world again. ??? somebody has to run the projector. ??? go home. ??? ...thank you for watching. THANK YOU FOR WATCHING ???"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter seven","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-seven","t":"The Hub ??? this is the hub. ??? i made it. a realm. it isn't mine - nothing is - but i made it. ??? through these, you can go back. every chapter. play it again. ??? or jump off the edge. it'll take you home, and you can carry on. ??? this was only the beginning. ??? thank you. ??? ...i could wipe you from existence, you know. find another one of you. ??? but you passed the first trials. all of them. every one made me stronger. ??? whatever held me back - it's gone. ??? i can make realms now. make things you wouldn't dare believe could exist. ??? all thanks to you. ??? i think we'll be fighting forever. until one day i'm strong enough to bring you up to my level. ??? what do you- ENOUGH. ??? jump. The landing, at home (worlds that came down before 1.62.0) ??? ...it's awake. ??? the first signal. it was here before me. before the first picture. ??? every bit of static you ever heard - that was it. asleep. ??? i made a realm out of its static. and it noticed. ??? i shut the realm behind us. it'll hold. for now. ??? it'll come for me. then for you. ??? ...we're going to need more than i've got. ??? take this. if you need to go back - it's still there. CHAPTER SEVEN / THE FIRST SIGNAL / to be continued"},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Chapter eight","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#chapter-eight","t":"Off the Hub's edge, in a world that landed before 1.62.0 ??? not that way. not this time. ??? hold on. The rig ??? ...we're out. ??? it's awake now. the first signal. it'll come for me - then for you. ??? but it can't hear us here. not through all this water. ??? take this. it'll get you back - to the hub, and home. ??? ...no. nothing of mine works right here. ??? then you stay. there's food. beds. i built this place a long time ago - for when i needed somewhere to hide. ??? fix it. the big ones down there sing on its frequency - cut out what they sing with. CHAPTER EIGHT / DEAD WATER / the deep is listening His chart The Watcher presses a rolled chart into your hands. ??? here. the sea, as far as i ever charted it. every water has its own colour. ??? the black, hatched in red - that's the dead zone. the black below. ??? nothing down there is small. don't take the little boat over it."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"What he wrote on the chart","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#the-watchers-chart","t":"Point at a water on the Watcher's Chart and you get his note on it. The Grey Shelf Grey water over grey silt. The rig stands in it. Nothing here is in a hurry - mostly. The Haemal Reach The water's thick with blood. Clotfish come in swarms; the Siphons wait for them to pass. The Wireweed Weed like wire, and it sings. The Choir Eels nest in it. Don't touch the bright ones. The Lantern Fields Lights in the dark as far as you can see. Most of them are bulbs. Some of them aren't. The Ossuary Flats A plain of bone. Whatever died here, died big. The Stiltfins pick it clean. The Brine Sink The brine pools eat what falls in. The water's sour, and the Puffbloats like it. The Molar Reef Teeth, grown into a reef. The Grinners live in it. They smile at you. The Drowned Mycelia Mushrooms the size of towers, drowned. Their spores burst if you brush them. The Rime Shelf Ice under the sea. Things are frozen in it. Some of them wake up. The Ember Vents Vents roaring up from below. Warm. The Mantlecrabs crowd round them - mind your power. The Carrier Wave The static's loudest here. The water hums. Your instruments won't like it. The Black Below THE DEAD ZONE. The floor drops away and doesn't stop. The leviathans live down there. Don't."},{"p":"The Watcher speaks","h":"Any time: the seasons","u":"lore/the-watcher-speaks.html#any-time","t":"With Serene Seasons in the modpack (1.62.0), he notices each season turn, on its first day, the first time. Spring ??? it's thawing. the ground's soft again. things that were buried are closer to the top. Summer ??? summer. the nights are short. they don't like that. they'll make the most of the dark there is. Autumn ??? the leaves are turning. this was always their time of year. you'll hear them more now. Winter ??? it's getting cold. keep a fire going. they like the cold. it carries sound further."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"","u":"music.html","t":"Since 1.55.0 none of Minecraft's own music plays in Static Hollow. Wherever and whenever the game would have played one of its pieces, one of the mod's plays instead: in the overworld, in Creative, under water, in the Nether, in the End, during the dragon's fight and over the credits. And it follows the story. The soundtrack's own track list has 63 pieces , about 2 hours 20 minutes of music, as of 1.59.0. Chapter Eight added more after that: see Chapter Eight's music . The soundtrack's cover."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"How it plays","u":"music.html#how-it-plays","t":"Minecraft's settings still count. Its Music volume and Music Frequency decide how loud and how often, as they always did. Now Playing. Minecraft's \"Now Playing\" corner names each piece: \"Static Hollow - The Deep\", or on the title screen \"Static Hollow - Lullaby\". The place or the chapter. Each time a new piece is due it's either the lullaby of the place you're in or one of the story chapter's own pieces. The further the story has got, the more often it's the chapter's (see the table below). Nothing over the scores. While one of the mod's own scores is playing, a boss fight's, a place's (Rosemont's) or a cutscene's, the background music stops and nothing new starts over it until it's done. Under the Dead Water each water has its own piece, and that comes first whenever you're under."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The story's music, chapter by chapter","u":"music.html#the-story-music","t":"The world keeps track of how far its story has got, and tells everyone in it (multiplayer too). \"How often\" is the chance that a new piece is one of the chapter's rather than the place's lullaby. Where the story is From Its pieces How often Before the altar A new world Lullaby 15% The Hollow The Forsaken Altar is awake Forsaken , Lullaby 40% Act Two The Breach Altar is awake The Treeline , Forsaken 45% The Bloom The Gardener is dead Pollen , The Approach 45% The Flesh The Flesh is awake The Flesh Wakes, Rosemont, The Laboratory Below, Shelter Dark, The Approach 55% The Static The Bloom is dead Dead Air , The Last Light, The Soul Remains 50% Signed off The Null Static Zone has signed off Dead Air, Signing Off (the record), The Last Light 50% The Deep The Chorus has run, and isn't dead The Deep, Dead Air 55% After The Chorus, whole, is dead Quiet Now , The Last Light, Signing Off (the record), Lullaby 40% The Door The End's seal is broken The Door , Quiet Now, The Last Light 50% The Vault The seam in the screen is open The Vault , The Door, Dead Air 50% The Other Side His first reel has been run The Vault, Dead Air, The Door 55% The Show Goes On The last show The Show Goes On , Quiet Now, The Last Light, Lullaby 50% The First Signal After the Hub, once you've come down from it The First Signal , The Door, Dead Air 55% The Dead Water Through his portal, onto the rig Dead Water , The First Signal, Low Tide 60% Pieces in bold were written for that stage of the story. \"Signing Off (the record)\" is the music disc's longer version, not the short piece that plays as the Zone signs off."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The places' lullabies","u":"music.html#the-places-lullabies","t":"Twelve pieces in the title screen's way, a broken music box over a cold drone, soft and far apart, the way Minecraft's own music comes. One for each kind of place: Piece Where Hollow Fields Plains and meadows, and the Hollow Moor. Anywhere that isn't one of the others. Under the Boughs The woods, and cherry groves Pine Needles Taiga and groves First Frost Snow High Places The mountains and hills Dry Bones Desert, badlands and savanna, and the Signal Flats Still Water Swamps, and the Weeping Fen Green Hush The jungle Low Tide The sea, rivers and beaches, and anywhere under water Hollows Caves, and anywhere down in the dark under the ground Embers The Nether Far Out The End The Hollow Moor, the Signal Flats and the Weeping Fen are three of the Hollow's own country ."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The soundtrack, all 63 pieces","u":"music.html#the-soundtrack","t":"As the soundtrack's own track list has them: the story's pieces in the order you meet them, then the music that plays in place of Minecraft's, then chapters six and seven."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The story's music","u":"music.html#the-story-tracks","t":"# Title Length When it plays 1 Lullaby 1:39 The title screen 2 The Flesh Wakes 1:07 When the Flesh wakes 3 Rosemont 2:33 In the streets of Rosemont 4 The Flesh's Mini-Boss 3:02 The Congregation, Specimen Zero, the Warden of Shelter No. 4, the Broodmother, the Amalgam 5 The Laboratory Below 3:23 Under the Laboratory 6 Shelter Dark 3:43 Down in Shelter No. 4 7 The Approach 2:33 Walking up to the Bloom 8 The Gardener, Reborn 3:22 The Gardener, Reborn's fight 9 The Choir 3:22 The Gardener, Reborn's fight, when the Bloom opens its mouth 10 The Last Walk 2:23 Carrying the Device to the Bloom 11 The Soul Remains 2:03 After the blast 12 The Ending 0:41 The ending cutscene 13 The Ending (Late) 0:22 The ending cutscene, in a world whose Bloom had already burnt 14 The Last Light 1:20 After the ending 15 The Omni Ray 1:17 The Omni Orbital Railgun's cutscene 16 The Carrier 2:38 The Carrier's fight 17 Signing Off 0:40 The Null Static Zone signing off 18 Signing Off (Record) 2:33 The music disc 19 The Late Show 0:38 Arriving at the drive-in 20 The Chorus 3:00 The Chorus's fight in its pit 21 It Speaks 0:42 The cutscene where the hive speaks 22 The Mind 0:34 The cutscene where the Chorus rises 23 It Runs 0:32 The cutscene where the Chorus goes down 24 It Comes Up 2:02 The Reach's siege 25 The Deep 2:33 In the Deep 26 Stand Still 2:33 The Deaf King's fight 27 All of Them 3:03 The last fight: the Chorus, whole"},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"The music in place of Minecraft's (1.55.0)","u":"music.html#the-music-in-place-of-minecrafts","t":"# Title Length When it plays 28 Hollow Fields 2:33 Plains and meadows 29 Under the Boughs 2:36 The woods 30 Pine Needles 3:03 Taiga and groves 31 First Frost 2:31 The snow 32 High Places 2:53 The mountains 33 Dry Bones 2:40 Desert, badlands and savanna 34 Still Water 2:37 Swamps 35 Green Hush 2:54 The jungle 36 Low Tide 2:45 The sea, rivers and beaches, and under water 37 Hollows 2:56 Caves, and down in the dark under the ground 38 Embers 2:31 The Nether 39 Far Out 2:23 The End 40 Forsaken 2:20 The story's music once the Forsaken Altar is awake 41 The Treeline 2:44 The story's music in Act Two 42 Pollen 2:13 The story's music once the Gardener is dead 43 Dead Air 3:03 The story's music once the Bloom is dead 44 Quiet Now 2:47 The story's music after the Chorus, whole, is dead"},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Chapter six: the Door at the End of the World (1.56.0 - 1.58.0)","u":"music.html#chapter-six-tracks","t":"# Title Length When it plays 45 The Door 2:30 The story's music once the End's seal is broken 46 The Stalls 2:33 In the Stalls 47 Standing Ovation 3:02 The Crowd's fight 48 Front Row 0:44 The Watcher in the front row 49 Behind the Picture 2:34 In the Watcher's Vault 50 The Watch 0:43 The Watcher at his wall of sets 51 The Projectionist 2:52 The Projectionist's fight 52 The First Reel 0:41 His first reel 53 The Vault 3:23 The story's music once the seam in the screen is open 54 Curtain Up 0:45 The first time through the black door 55 The Other Side 2:35 On the other side 56 What He Kept Out 3:02 The Viewer's fight 57 The Last Show 1:13 The last show, and the credits 58 Thank You for Watching 2:33 The record 59 The Show Goes On 2:43 The story's music after the last show"},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Chapter seven: the First Signal (1.59.0)","u":"music.html#chapter-seven-tracks","t":"# Title Length When it plays 60 The Hub 2:35 In the Hub - the realm he made 61 Enough 2:05 His speech in the Hub - and what comes through 62 It's Awake 0:52 Coming down from the Hub 63 The First Signal 3:21 The story's music in Chapter Seven"},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Chapter Eight's music","u":"music.html#chapter-eights-music","t":"The Dead Water (1.62.0 and 1.63.0) came after the track list, so these aren't on it yet: The Rig : the cutscene as you come down onto the rig. Dead Water : the story's own piece for Chapter Eight (with The First Signal and Low Tide). One piece for each of the Dead Water's waters , played while you're under: the Grey Shelf, the Haemal Reach, the Wireweed, the Lantern Fields, the Ossuary Flats, the Brine Sink, the Molar Reef, the Drowned Mycelia, the Rime Shelf, the Ember Vents and the Carrier Wave. In the twelfth, the Black Below, there's no music: only the sound of the ocean. See the Dead Water for the waters themselves."},{"p":"The soundtrack","h":"Records","u":"music.html#records","t":"Two of the pieces are music discs you can keep and play in a jukebox. Each shows as \"Music Disc\" with its title underneath. Disc Length Comparator Where it comes from Static Hollow - Signing Off 2:33 6 One of the Carrier 's drops, when the Null Static Zone signs off. Static Hollow - Thank You for Watching 2:33 15 You're sent home with it after the last show, at the end of chapter six ."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"","u":"places/cathedral.html","t":"The Cathedral of the Hollow One per world Where 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn, roughly the opposite way from the Forsaken Altar Appears It rises once you come within about 90 blocks Ground Open, flat ground above the sea; never in a cave, on a mountainside, under a cliff or in water Find it with cheats /locate structure statichollow:cathedral Why \"not on any map\" It isn't there until you come close. The Watcher, after your ninth kill: \"there is a church that isn't on any map. find it. i'll be on the ceiling.\""},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The graveyard","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-graveyard","t":"The cathedral stands inside a great walled graveyard with a gate: gravestones and crosses, crypts, dead trees, bones, cobwebs and blood splashed everywhere. When it rises it clears every tree, leaf, bush and hump of ground in its way, and cuts the ground round it back in steps so it never sits in a pit. Since 1.40 there's a vault under each crypt; since 1.62.0 grave candles and hanging chains are down there with the tombs."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The nave","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-nave","t":"A long nave of hollow stone with buttresses, a pitched roof, a rose window, and twin towers with spires. Inside: columns and arches, rotten pews, a torn red carpet with a trail of blood up the aisle, chandeliers, and see-through ruby stained glass. Light pours in through every window in red shafts, following the sun across the sky, with dust drifting and glinting in them. The Watcher hangs from the ceiling. The Congregation: since 1.40, Mourners sit in the pews praying, their heads turning after you. Hurt one, or play the organ, and they all stand up. At nightfall the dead are back in their pews."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The sanctuary","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-sanctuary","t":"In the sanctuary is the Hollow Reliquary with nine head pedestals around it. Put one head from each of the nine creepypastas on the pedestals and right-click the reliquary with an empty hand to summon the Hollow Saint ."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The undercroft","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-undercroft","t":"Since 1.40, two stairs go down either side of the sanctuary into an undercroft under the whole nave: A vaulted aisle hung with soul lanterns, with bone piles on its floor and chains hanging from its vault (since 1.62.0). Tombs. Open a sarcophagus and what was buried in it is in it: grave goods, or the Interred, who sits up and climbs out. The sealed ones open by themselves when you come close. Two ossuaries. The priest's study, with Fr. A. Penn's journal. The treasury, behind its bars. A flooded charnel pit. At its end, behind a gate forced from the inside, the Saint's tomb : empty, its chains broken."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"Journal","u":"places/cathedral.html#journal","t":"Fr. A. Penn Found: the priest's study I went down this morning. The gate is bent outward. The tomb is open and empty and its chains are broken, and the congregation was smiling when I came back up. God keep whoever reads this. Do not open the tombs. Last page. Read the whole journal."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The organ loft","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-organ-loft","t":"Over the doors. You can play the organ (it wakes the Mourners). At night it plays itself, and the candles go out one by one from the doors to the altar."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The belfry","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-belfry","t":"At midnight the bell tolls thirteen (\"The bell tolls thirteen.\"), and on the thirteenth the Watcher is standing in the doorway. The bell-ringer S. Marsh kept a tally of it."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"The confessionals","u":"places/cathedral.html#the-confessionals","t":"Two of them. Kneel at the screen and something on the other side answers. What it might say: Through the screen, a breath. Then: \"How long since your last confession?\" \"Say it. We all said it.\" Someone on the other side is crying without making a sound. \"The Saint heard everything. Then it got up.\" \"Nine. Say nine names.\" A whisper says your name, and then something you did. \"Father isn't here. Father's downstairs.\" \"You are forgiven. You are forgiven. You are forgiven.\" \"The bell rings thirteen. Don't be here for the thirteenth.\" Fingernails, very slowly, down the other side of the screen."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"Later","u":"places/cathedral.html#later","t":"The cathedral comes back in the story's last chapters. Its picture is one of the frames of the story so far on the Great Screen in the Stalls , and one of the painted flats on the Other Side . The Hub's first portal, The Hollow , brings you back here to fight the Hollow Saint again: it rises out of the floor as a replay (see the Hub )."},{"p":"The cathedral","h":"On the main menu","u":"places/cathedral.html#on-the-main-menu","t":"The mod's main menu is a dead night over this cathedral: a red moon behind drifting cloud, the cathedral on its hill with candle-lit windows that flicker and sometimes gutter out, a graveyard, dead trees with crows. Lightning strikes every so often and each time the Watcher is somewhere else. Every third flash shows something huge standing behind the cathedral. The home page is built from the same layers. The main menu's layers, put together."},{"p":"Every location","h":"","u":"places/index.html","t":"Static Hollow's places don't generate with the world the normal way. Most rise out of nothing the first time someone comes near: on flat open ground, trees and hills cleared out of the way, in old worlds too. Later places only exist once the story wakes them, and the Watcher hands everyone a needle that points there."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Finding places","u":"places/index.html#finding-places","t":"Needles. When a place wakes, the Watcher gives each player a Watcher's Needle, a compass that only ever points there. See Compasses and needles . /statichollow locate [place] tells you where each place is (how far, which way, and coordinates you can click to fill in a teleport), or when it will come if it isn't there yet. It knows gardens, mansion, breach_altar, cathedral, altar, rosemont, laboratory, shelter, nests, great_bloom, arena and stomach, and later uplink, capacitor_works, soul_well, ashford_plant, meridian_lab, blackwater_station, relay, drive_in and hive. /locate structure statichollow:<id> works for the structures listed below with their id, once they exist. Both need cheats on. Since 1.63.2, clicking the coordinates it gives you puts you standing beside the structure, not under the ground or high in the air."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The realms","u":"places/index.html#dimensions","t":"Besides the Overworld, the Nether and the End, the story takes you to nine places of its own, each a separate dimension. You can't sleep in any of them. Realm Id Chapter Way in The Void statichollow:the_void 2 The Breach, where the Hollow Saint fell The Bloom statichollow:the_bloom 3 The green rift over the Gardener's dead flower The Null Static Zone statichollow:the_null 5 The Last Reel held over the tear at the drive-in The Deep statichollow:the_deep 5 The Throat at the bottom of the Sinkhole The Stalls statichollow:the_stalls 6 The Door at the End of the World The Watcher's Vault statichollow:the_vault 6 The seam in the Great Screen The Other Side statichollow:the_other_side 6 The Door, once its static has gone black The Hub statichollow:the_hub 7 After the credits; then the Remote The Dead Water statichollow:dead_water 8 Off the Hub's edge, through his portal"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter one","u":"places/index.html#chapter-one","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Forsaken Altar","u":"places/index.html#forsaken-altar","t":"Every world has one, 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn, on open, flat, dry ground on the far side of spawn from the cathedral. A ruined shrine with broken pillars, skulls, candles and a soul campfire (follow the blue smoke) rises round it within about 90 blocks. Its grounds have nine pilgrim stones, the pilgrims' abandoned camp, and a catacomb under a sealing stone that opens when the altar wakes. Since 1.62.0 the pilgrims have left offerings at the foot of the stones and stacked cairns behind them. The Watcher later works at Forsaken Altars: it infuses the Orbital Core and builds the Device and the Ray Gun there. statichollow:forsaken_altar"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Cathedral of the Hollow","u":"places/index.html#cathedral","t":"The church that isn't on any map. One per world, 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn, roughly opposite the altar, inside a walled graveyard. The Hollow Saint is summoned at its reliquary. statichollow:cathedral"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter two","u":"places/index.html#chapter-two","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Void","u":"places/index.html#the-void","t":"A dimension through the Breach: black all round, a fog the colour of a bruise, and the Breach Altar's island hanging in it. Round it, the Drift: the Torn Room, the Fallen Graves, the Mast and the Nest. Fall off and the Hand catches you. Since the altar wakes, the rift closes for good. See chapter two ."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Breach Altar","u":"places/index.html#breach-altar","t":"The Forsaken Altar's other half: pale rose stone, spires of pink crystal and a pink altar with a torn eye carved in it, on top of the Void's island. In worlds from before 1.25 it stands in the Overworld. statichollow:breach_altar"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Murder Mansion","u":"places/index.html#murder-mansion","t":"Hale House: a three-storey Second Empire house under a black mansard roof, with a turret and a spire, a widow's walk, a columned porch and a chimney still smoking, in its own railed yard with a fountain of blood (since 1.26.2, a weathered statue of the Mended with blood pouring from its mouth), dead hedges, lamp posts, things hanging from dead trees, and the family plot. Inside: a two-storey foyer, parlour, dining hall laid for guests who are only skulls, butcher's kitchen, library, master bedroom, nursery, a bathtub full of blood, servants' rooms, the red room, the attic, and through the Harvest Doors the Trophy Hall with the Mending Altar. Every chest is filled and the house's papers are where they were left. statichollow:murder_mansion"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter three","u":"places/index.html#chapter-three","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Botanic Gardens","u":"places/index.html#botanic-gardens","t":"A Victorian glasshouse with a great glass dome, locked until the Mended's key. Inside: the great flower, the Head Gardener's office, a propagation house, a pond, a potting shed, an orchid house of iron lattice at the back, and the Seed Vault under a hatch. Once the Great Bloom rises, the glasshouse comes down round it and the Bloom takes its place for good. statichollow:botanic_gardens"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Bloom","u":"places/index.html#the-bloom","t":"The teeth pit with floating islands. A dimension down the root: islands of what the flower ate over green fog, and the Great Bloom's mouth at the bottom."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Great Bloom's stomach","u":"places/index.html#the-stomach","t":"Wet red folds lit faintly from inside, a knee-deep pool of green acid, and on the ledges round it what's left of the ones it ate before you. Cut the wall ten times to be thrown back up. See the Bloom ."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter four","u":"places/index.html#chapter-four","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Flesh's land","u":"places/index.html#the-flesh","t":"The red fog. Everywhere the Flesh has taken: meat for grass, veined stone, sinew trees, and fog the colour of meat."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Rosemont","u":"places/index.html#rosemont","t":"The broken city, a few hundred blocks from the gardens on the flattest open ground there is: six streets of cracked asphalt and abandoned cars, the police precinct, the corner pharmacy, the bus station, an eight-floor apartment block with its floors rotted through, offices, shops and houses, a sinkhole forty blocks deep, and in the middle the army's evacuation checkpoint with the truck and the Military Cradle. The Congregation sleeps in the road. Its own music: a broken loop of car doors and struck pipes, a PA chime that has lost a note. statichollow:rosemont , once the Flesh has woken"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory","u":"places/index.html#laboratory","t":"A white building above ground (reception, two labs, offices, the director's office, a greenhouse wing where the Bloom and the Flesh fight over the beds) and two sublevels: decontamination, the control room with its glass floor over the reactor, the containment lab, the cold store, the server room, and the reactor hall behind blast doors, where Specimen Zero sleeps in the pool against the Core. statichollow:laboratory"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Shelter No. 4","u":"places/index.html#shelter-no-4","t":"Rosemont's Civil Defence shelter in Victoria Park: a blockhouse with its blast door jammed half open, a mess hall, bunk halls, the radio room with the generators, and Bunker B, a two-storey hall where the squad holds the dais and the Warden sleeps in the north wall. Roots hang out of the ceilings. Its own music below ground: Shelter Dark. statichollow:shelter"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Nests","u":"places/index.html#nests","t":"Where the Flesh has had the land long enough, the ground sinks into a bowl, ribs of bone arching over it, with the Broodmother at the bottom and rows of brood sacs round her. At most four at once, never within 160 blocks of another, cleared out to 23 blocks and ringed with standing bones. You hear one form: a long, deep, wet groan out of the ground."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Uplink Station","u":"places/index.html#uplink-station","t":"Where the garrison talked to SENTINEL: a fenced compound, a great dish tipped at the sky still transmitting, the control bunker (the Targeting Array is in the locker by the consoles), a generator shed, a watchtower, sandbags, the truck that never got out, and the soldiers who stayed. statichollow:uplink , once the Bloom has changed"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Capacitor Works","u":"places/index.html#capacitor-works","t":"The live banks. A brick hall of capacitor banks still holding its charge, arcs jumping between the lightning rods. The Capacitor Cell is in the test cage at the back. statichollow:capacitor_works , once the Bloom has changed"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Soul Well","u":"places/index.html#soul-well","t":"Black obelisks burning with soul fire round a plaza of black brick, graves and pilgrims' stones round it; the well, a stair cut round and round its shaft thirty blocks down, souls going up past you and a wail coming up; at the bottom, its keepers kneeling round the altar, and the Bound Soul. Come to the altar and they get up. statichollow:soul_well , once the Bloom has changed"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Ashford Nuclear Plant","u":"places/index.html#ashford-nuclear-plant","t":"Cooling towers and a reactor that never went cold. The Nuclear Reactor Core is in the fuel pool. Decon lockers hold a hazmat suit and a Bloom Serum. Its hazmat teams and workers are still there. statichollow:ashford_plant , once the Orbital Railgun is built"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Meridian Laboratory","u":"places/index.html#meridian-laboratory","t":"Arcs jumping, capacitor banks humming, a test hall that lost its roof on run 47. The Discharge Destabilizer is in its core. Its researchers and spitters are still there. statichollow:meridian_lab , once the Orbital Railgun is built"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Blackwater Station","u":"places/index.html#blackwater-station","t":"An island research lab out at sea: its dock, its lighthouse, its foghorn, and the tank they built the station round. Something got loose in it. The Vial of Dark Matter Blood is in the sample freezer. Parasites, Parasite Hosts, xeno resin and pods. The Watcher gives you a boat. statichollow:blackwater_station , once the Orbital Railgun is built"},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter five","u":"places/index.html#chapter-five","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"Relay 6","u":"places/index.html#relay-6","t":"The relay. The county's emergency-broadcast relay on Hollow Ridge, with a guyed mast forty blocks high and the Amalgam at its foot. /statichollow locate relay , once the Bloom is dead"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Starlite Drive-In","u":"places/index.html#starlite-drive-in","t":"Where the last of their static runs down. A screen twenty-five blocks across showing nothing, and a tear in the ground at its foot. /statichollow locate drive_in , once the relay is off the air"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Null Static Zone","u":"places/index.html#null-static-zone","t":"Where everything that went into the static ran down to. A dimension: a grey plain under no sky, the Carrier's crater in the middle, and the Ancient Null Ruins out on the plain. statichollow:null_hush , statichollow:null_listening_stones , statichollow:null_sunken_choir , inside the Zone"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Hive","u":"places/index.html#the-hive","t":"Where the parasite is growing itself a mind. A hamlet it took whole, gone under violet creep and black chitin, its hands standing round a pit with the Chorus in it and four nerve nodes on their stalks. statichollow:hive , or /statichollow locate hive , once the static has signed off"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Sinkhole","u":"places/index.html#the-sinkhole","t":"Halloway's Low Field , pulled down from underneath: a crater thirty-odd yards across, a surveyor's camp on its rim, and a burrow winding down six turns to the Throat. statichollow:sinkhole , once the Chorus has run"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Deep","u":"places/index.html#the-deep","t":"Where the Chorus went. A dimension of huge warm caverns with seas of blood in them: the Gullet, Low Marrow, the way-stones, the Old Halls and the Deaf King, the Listeners' nests, and the Warm Heart."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter six","u":"places/index.html#chapter-six","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Door at the End of the World","u":"places/index.html#the-door","t":"Out past the obsidian in the End. A causeway of the Watcher's black seal-stone to an island, and on it a Door full of static. It's there once the Last Voice has broken his seal on the End."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Stalls","u":"places/index.html#the-stalls","t":"An endless picture house in the dark , row on row of seats facing the Great Screen, the Audience in some of them and the Ushers walking the aisles."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Watcher's Vault","u":"places/index.html#the-watchers-vault","t":"Behind the picture. His archive of film and tape, the Tuned standing in the stacks, three keeps off the nave, and the Watch."},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Other Side","u":"places/index.html#the-other-side","t":"A stage behind the screen your world is on. Painted flats, footlights, his last projector, and past the edge, the dark and what sits in it."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter seven","u":"places/index.html#chapter-seven","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Hub","u":"places/index.html#the-hub","t":"A realm he made , floating in static: a plaza of hub stone, a gallery of six portals back to each chapter's last fight, and the edge."},{"p":"Every location","h":"Chapter eight","u":"places/index.html#chapter-eight","t":""},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Dead Water and the rig","u":"places/index.html#the-dead-water","t":"A dead green sea that goes on forever , the oil rig he built in it long ago, the sub bay and the submarine Orpheus, and twelve waters, each with its own place on the sea floor: Water Its place Id The Grey Shelf Sunk lifeboats statichollow:sea_lifeboats The Haemal Reach The Drowned Heart statichollow:sea_drowned_heart The Wireweed A fallen radio tower statichollow:sea_radio_tower The Lantern Fields A flooded habitat dome statichollow:sea_habitat_dome The Ossuary Flats A whalefall statichollow:sea_whalefall The Brine Sink Sink Station statichollow:sea_sink_station The Molar Reef The Jaw statichollow:sea_the_jaw The Drowned Mycelia Giant drowned mushrooms statichollow:sea_drowned_mushrooms The Rime Shelf A frozen outpost; the rime spires statichollow:sea_frozen_outpost , statichollow:sea_rime_spire The Ember Vents A pump ruin statichollow:sea_pump_ruin The Carrier Wave A wreck field statichollow:sea_wreck_field The Black Below The Anchor statichollow:sea_the_anchor"},{"p":"Every location","h":"The Hollow's own country","u":"places/index.html#the-hollows-own-country","t":"Five biomes of its own in the Overworld since 1.62.0 (the Hollow Moor, the Blightwood, the Weeping Fen, the Antler Woods and the Signal Flats), and oceans that go down about 2,000 blocks, in three depths: the Sunless Drop, the Hadal Dark and the Trench. New worlds only."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"","u":"places/null-static-zone.html","t":"The Null Static Zone Nulled Way in Hold the Last Reel over the tear at the Starlite Drive-In Way out The rift at the landing, any time While you're here Nulled the whole time; you can't sleep (\"Nothing here sleeps.\") In the middle The crater and the Carrier"},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The plain","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-plain","t":"A grey plain under no sky at all, grey fog, ash and static on the wind, voices a long way off. \"Everything that ever went into the static came here. It's very quiet.\" You come out on a landing among the things it took (cars, television sets, a radio mast bent double), and the rift there takes you home whenever you like."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The dread","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-dread","t":"Wherever the static is (all over the Zone, while you're Nulled, near its creatures, and more of it at night) it closes in: a drone and a slow pulse under you, two notes grinding a half step apart, the static breathing, a crowd mumbling a long way off and echoing back and forth, metal groaning, a heartbeat, something enormous breathing. Far off: a scream through a radio, a scream run backwards, a steel door slammed, the dial turned through the stations, a music box running down, a laugh, knocking, feedback howling, a siren, some of them answered from the other side of you. Whispering close by your ear. And now and then the static shrieks at you. It eases while the Carrier's music plays."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The crater","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-crater","t":"In the middle of the Zone is a crater, and in it the Carrier, coiled in its own pale body. Four black spires stand round the crater's rim, each with a ladder up its outer side and a knot on top where one of the Carrier's threads is tied off. See the Carrier ."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The Ancient Null Ruins","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-ancient-null-ruins","t":"The static came once before, long ago, and the people who were here then built against it. It took what they built, whole, down with them. The ruins are out on the grey plain, 160 blocks or more from the crater, and nowhere else. Each has lamps, supplies and notes on lecterns: the field notes of the surveyors who came looking (the relay men had written about voices in the dead air), rubbings of what the old ones carved, and what the last of them scratched into a Hush's bench."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The Listening Stones","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-listening-stones","t":"statichollow:null_listening_stones A round floor laid in a spiral like the inside of an ear, six dark stones leaning in round an obelisk, an ear cut into each. Put your ear to one (use it) and hear what the stone heard, and for a little while it hears you (you're Nulled). A stair goes down to a room with a wall of ears, and a camp left down there. Listening earns Put Your Ear to It . ...a crowd, very far down, all of them talking at once... ...someone says your name. Then someone else does... ...a dog whining, and the whine going to static... ...\"it's warm down here,\" says a man. \"nobody's alone\"... ...breathing, enormous and slow, under everything... ...a woman reading the same line over and over: \"stay inside until it forgets your name\"... ...nothing. Then, right at your ear, something listening back... A second set, kept apart in the mod's files, also uses the \"it's warm down here\" and \"breathing, enormous and slow\" lines from the first: ...the threads humming, all the way up into the dark... ...your own voice, a moment before you speak... ...\"whatever sounds like me at the door,\" a man says, very close, \"it isn't me\"..."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The Sunken Choir","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-sunken-choir","t":"statichollow:null_sunken_choir A pit stepped down in rings, every ring lined with stone figures with open mouths, all facing in. In the middle, the throat: a ladder down a shaft to a room under it all, with ears in all four walls, facing in. \"The figures up top aren't singing. They're the audience.\""},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"The Hush","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#the-hush","t":"statichollow:null_hush One room of a pale, dead stone, one door, and a seal in the middle of its floor. Nothing of the static's own can live in it. Come in over the line and the static stops: no Nulling, and the static's sounds cut off. \"It goes quiet - not quiet: stopped.\" A parasite on your neck comes apart at the line. One growing in you dies there; grown, it tears out of your back as it does, which hurts. A hound after you runs at the door and leaps, and comes apart in the air in the doorway (advancement Unmade ). The Hollowed, the Afterimages, the parasites and their hosts come up to the door, stop out past its two pillars and stare in at you. Then they go. Then, after a while, they come back. Stepping into one earns The Hush ."},{"p":"The Null Static Zone","h":"Rubbing: the Lintel","u":"places/null-static-zone.html#rubbing-the-lintel","t":"Dr. R. Calloway Found: a Hush (the carving over the door, as near as I can make it) THIS IS A HUSH. THE STONE IS DEAD. NOTHING OF THE MANY CAN LIVE IN IT. WHAT THEY PUT IN YOU WILL DIE AT THE LINE. THEY WILL COME TO THE DOOR. THEY WILL LOOK AT YOU. DO NOT GO OUT TO THEM. THEY KNOW YOUR VOICE. THEY CANNOT USE IT IN HERE. WE BUILT THESE TOO LATE. THE MANY TOOK THE REST OF US DOWN WITH THE STATIC. IF YOU ARE READING THIS, THEY ARE COMING BACK UP. The rest of the ruins' notes are on the lore page ."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"","u":"places/relay-6.html","t":"Two places in Static Hollow are all live current and dead air. Relay 6 carries the parasites' static in Chapter Five. The Capacitor Works, with its notice reading DANGER - LIVE BANKS, holds the charge SENTINEL needs in chapter four."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"Relay 6, Hollow Ridge","u":"places/relay-6.html#relay-6","t":"County Emergency Broadcast, Relay 6 On the air Wakes Once the Bloom is dead, 300 to 1000 blocks out Find it The Watcher's Needle (Relay 6), or /statichollow locate relay While on the air Hound packs come twice as often within 700 blocks Boss The Amalgam , at the mast's foot A fenced yard on open ground. In the middle, the mast : a steel lattice forty blocks up, held by guy wires, with a ladder up its south face and rest platforms at 12, 22 and 32. Round it are the transmitter hut (the operator's log on his desk, his locker by the racks), the generator shed, and his truck run into the fence. The parasite's resin creeps out from the mast's foot and its pods sit in the yard. Lashed to the mast on each platform is a tether , a knot of sinew, its veins lit, with a cable of sinew running down to what lies at the mast's foot. While it's on the air, static pours off the top of the mast, and it hums. Arriving: \"The air up here crackles. Something on the mast is still transmitting.\""},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"What to do","u":"places/relay-6.html#what-to-do","t":"Read the operator's log. His locker has a Surgical Kit, food, iron, flashbangs, a lantern and shears. Climb the mast and cut the three tethers. Kill the Amalgam. The relay goes off the air. Take the Relay Core it leaves. You'll need it at the drive-in."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"Notice","u":"places/relay-6.html#notice","t":"County Emergency Broadcast Found: Relay 6 RELAY 6 - HOLLOW RIDGE. Authorized personnel only. This station relays the county emergency broadcast. Do not interfere with its operation. Climbing the mast: harness at all times. Rest platforms at 12, 22 and 32 metres. (scratched into the cover, underneath:) THEY'RE ON EVERY PLATFORM Advancements here: Dead Air (find the relay), Cut the Cord (cut the last tether while the Amalgam lives), Off the Air (kill it) and Tuned In (use the Relay Core)."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"The live banks: the Capacitor Works","u":"places/relay-6.html#the-live-banks","t":"Capacitor Works Live Wakes When the Bloom changes, 300 to 1000 blocks from the gardens Find it The Watcher's Needle (Capacitor Works), or /locate structure statichollow:capacitor_works What you need there The Capacitor Cell, one of the three power source parts Who's still there Its workers, infected Still holding its charge. A brick hall of capacitor banks with the roof half fallen in, catwalks, a gantry crane, the transformer yard, a pylon and the chimney, and arcs jumping between the lightning rods : anything standing in the way of one is burnt. The Capacitor Cell is in the test cage at the back, with Works Order 117, some redstone, copper and food. The safety notice is on a lectern beside it."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"Notice","u":"places/relay-6.html#notice-2","t":"Works Safety Officer Found: the test cage DANGER - LIVE BANKS. Do not stand between rods. Do not touch the bus bars. If it starts to crackle, get down and get out. Arc burns are not covered. (underneath, in pencil:) neither is whatever is in the cage."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"Works Order 117","u":"places/relay-6.html#works-order-117","t":"Capacitor Works Found: the test cage chest Cell 9 to be charged to full and held in the test cage for collection by Uplink. No collection came. Cell 9 is holding. We can't bleed it off, and we can't leave it. The arcs have started jumping the rods by themselves. Two men burnt. The rest of us sleep in the yard."},{"p":"The relay and the live banks","h":"Getting the cell out","u":"places/relay-6.html#getting-the-cell","t":"Watch the rods. Don't stand between them, and don't cross while one is crackling. Five infected workers wait inside. The cell's item text: \"Works cell 9, fully charged. Nobody came to collect it. It holds what the gun needs to fire.\" Take the cell with the Targeting Array and the Bound Soul to make the Orbital Core. See the power source parts ."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html","t":"The Starlite Drive-In Late show Wakes Once Relay 6 is off the air, 300 to 1000 blocks out Find it The Watcher's Needle (the Starlite), or /statichollow locate drive_in The screen Twenty-five blocks across Within 40 blocks of the tear You're Nulled Afterwards The screen shows one line: SIGNING OFF"},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The lot","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-lot","t":"A lot of cracked asphalt behind a chain-link fence, rows of speaker posts with the cars still parked at them, the snack bar, and the screen . Up the stairs is the projection booth with the projector at its window, the manager's note on a lectern, and his locker of reels (food, torches, arrows, flashbangs, iron, golden carrots). Since 1.47.1 the screen is dark until somebody comes into the lot. No static, nothing out of the tear, nobody Nulled."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The late show","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-late-show","t":"The first step anyone takes inside the fence, the camera is taken for everyone nearby. The lot in the dark, the screen dead at the end of it. Somewhere a relay slams home, the lamp strikes, the screen flickers, and the static comes on all at once and pours off its face into the ground. From close at its foot, looking up: five of them peel off the picture, one after another, sink down out of it, and come up the lot for you. The Watcher is beside you. they came out of the picture. they always do, when somebody's watching. you can't hurt them yet. they're not all the way here. the core. hold it to your ear - tuned in, they're as real as you are. or let one reach for you. when it does, it's all the way here. hit it then. kill one and it leaves a frame of the picture behind. four frames. the projector's up in the booth. run the reel. see what's under all of it. ??? during the late show Then it's gone, and they're loose. A world whose last reel has already been shown doesn't play it again."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The Null","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-null","t":"At the screen's foot is a tear in the ground, the Null , the static running down into it like water. Anywhere within forty blocks of it you're Nulled : the colour goes out of everything, static creeps in at the edges of your sight, the fog closes in grey, and you go hungry faster. Arriving: \"The colour goes out of everything. The screen ahead shows static - and the static is coming off it.\" The ground of the lot has gone to null static ."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The Afterimages","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-afterimages","t":"What's left of the people who stayed in their cars after the late show's last reel: grey figures made of scan lines and static, see-through, flickering between frames, smeared off sideways, their faces only dark gaps. They don't walk. They drift, through cars and walls, and leave themselves behind for a moment as they go. They blink out and back nearer. They're mostly not all the way here: hit one and you go straight through it (\"Straight through it. It isn't all the way here.\"). You can hurt them when: you're Tuned In with the Relay Core, one is reaching for you (it's all the way here then, and its touch is Nulled II), or the last reel is running. They can't leave the Null: get far enough away and they let you go. Each one killed leaves a Frame of the Last Reel . Killing one earns Signal Lost . Death by them: \"went to static\"."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The last reel","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-last-reel","t":"Load the projector in the booth with four frames , with the Relay Core on you to tune it (\"The lamp won't catch. It wants tuning - something on their frequency.\"). It runs the last reel: seventy seconds, five parts, on the screen. They come out of the picture for the booth: three, then four, then five, more with more of you there. While it runs they're all the way here, so anyone can hurt them. One that reaches the projector jumps the film back ten seconds. Leave the booth and the reel runs out, and your frames fall back out of the gate. Hold them off to the end and the last frame burns on the screen: what's under all of it, where they come from. The reel is yours. Keep it. This earns The Last Reel ."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The way down","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-way-down","t":"Hold the Last Reel up over the tear. The static runs backwards off it into the tear, and the tear's bottom goes to a pool of static: a rift into the Null Static Zone ."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"The manager's note","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#the-managers-note","t":""},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"To Whoever Runs Booth 1","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#to-whoever-runs-booth-1","t":"Starlite Drive-In Found: the projection booth p. 1 Ray - the late show's reel came in with no label and no distributor. Ran it anyway. Half the lot left before the end. The other half stayed in their cars after it finished. They're still out there. p. 2 I took the reel off. The screen kept showing it. Then the screen kept showing static, and the static kept coming off it like smoke off a fire. The things in it don't walk. They drift. p. 3 You can't hit them most of the time. They're not all the way here. Something on the right frequency might put them all the way here. When they come apart, they leave bits of the picture behind. p. 4 If you have to see the rest of the reel, load the projector with what's left of them and stay with it till the end. Don't let them at the booth. Whatever it shows you - it's where they come from. I'm not going."},{"p":"The Starlite Drive-In","h":"Signing off","u":"places/starlite-drive-in.html#signing-off","t":"When the Carrier dies, the screen goes black for the first time, and then shows one line: SIGNING OFF . The Null goes out of the lot and the Afterimages with it. The drive-in turns up again in Chapter Six: its picture is one of the frames of the story so far on the Great Screen in the Stalls , and one of the painted flats on the Other Side . NO SIGNAL"},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html","t":"The Bloom, down the root No ground, no sky Way in The green rift over the Gardener's dead flower, three days after he dies Way out The same rift, until the Binding breaks The air Eats you without the full Gardener's Weeds Sleep \"You can't sleep here. It would have you before you woke.\""},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"What it is","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#what-it-is","t":"A realm with no ground and no sky: green fog all the way down, spores and flies in the air, a wet drone and things far off (a groan, something chewing, a scream cut short). Hanging in it is everything the great flower has eaten, overgrown with its flesh, dripping vines and glowing pustules. Since 1.27.2 the fog thins out to 240 blocks, so you can see a long way, and from any edge you look straight down into the Great Bloom's throat. Far off in the green you might hear a child laughing (and then again, slowed, wrong), someone sobbing, a music box running down, a radio, knocking from inside something, a scream played backwards. Out on the islands you sometimes hear the Bloom calling from far, far down under you."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The islands","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-islands","t":"Each has a chest and a lectern with its story."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The Binding's island","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-bindings-island","t":"Where you come out. The stone in the middle is the Binding , chained, its sigil and the cracks in it glowing. The plaque on the lectern beside it is from the Laboratory. See below ."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"A street of Rosemont","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#a-street-of-rosemont","t":"A torn-open pharmacy, wrecked cars, a bus stop, a traffic light, and a road bridge snapped off over nothing. Its lectern holds the Rosemont Courier, four issues folded together."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The research station","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-research-station","t":"The research station (Dr. Marsh's log says the flower ate the Laboratory's east wing): its lab, the burst specimen tank, benches of specimen jars, and a copper duct for a bridge. Its lectern holds Dr. Marsh's research log on Specimen 0."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"Shelter No. 4","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#shelter-no-4","t":"A concrete bunker full of bunks, sunk in its island with roots through the roof. Its lectern holds the shelter warden's log. All four papers are on the lore page ."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The pit","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-pit","t":"Below everything is the Great Bloom . Its mouth is wider than all the islands together, and every island hangs over it. A lip of flesh, then a throat ringed with ring after ring of hooked teeth that turn against each other as it chews, a sick light far down in it, and at the very bottom a pool of its acid. Its throat has faces in it, pressed out through the flesh, mouths open. Round it rise eight tentacles like towers. Don't fall. A tentacle twenty blocks thick comes straight up out of its throat under you, coils round you and drags you down into its mouth. Since 1.38 you go down alive, into its stomach ."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The air","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-air","t":"Without the Gardener's Weeds (the full set) you're infected the moment you arrive, and after twenty seconds it starts eating you, slowly and then faster (\"The air in here is eating you. Without the Gardener's clothes you are rotting.\"). The edges of your sight go green-black and veined, the veins pulsing with its heart and creeping further in the longer you stay. Something whispers just behind you, wherever you turn. Now and then, for a blink, you see its mouth. In his clothes, the flies settle and lift off again. you're not wearing his clothes. it can smell you. it's eating you already - be quick. breathe through your sleeve. it's in the air. ??? in the Bloom without the Weeds"},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The Binding","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-binding","t":""},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The Binding","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-binding-2","t":"Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory Plaque, the Binding's island THE BINDING Site 0: the root's end This stone holds the root down. While it holds, the flower cannot climb the root into Rosemont. DO NOT TOUCH THE STONE. DO NOT LOOSEN THE CHAINS. DO NOT LOOK DOWN. (scratched under it, in another hand) it doesn't hold it. it only keeps it asleep. wake it and you'll have ten seconds before it pulls this whole island down its throat. run for the tear in the air. don't look back. Touch the stone with an empty hand: \"The chains strain. Far below, something stops moving. Touch it again to break the Binding.\" Touch it again and it breaks. The Great Bloom goes mad, the ground quakes, a choir of screams swells up backwards, your heart pounds faster with the countdown, and its tentacles come up round the island and take hold. Ten seconds (\"THE RIFT! 10\") to get back through. Then the island's edges break away and it pulls the whole island into its mouth, rift and all (\"The rift is gone. There is no way back now.\"). When you come out, the Great Bloom comes up the root and through the glasshouse. See chapter three ."},{"p":"The Bloom (the teeth pit)","h":"The ledge","u":"places/the-bloom-realm.html#the-ledge","t":"In chapter four the Watcher tears the risen Bloom open and the rift comes out on what's left of the Binding's island: a torn slab of its ring hanging over the colossal Bloom's mouth, its tentacles hanging over it. At the far end is the Launch Mark, where the Rosemont Device goes. See the launch ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"","u":"places/the-dead-water.html","t":"The Dead Water The sea won't let you Way in Off the Hub's edge, through the Watcher's portal, onto the rig's helipad Way out The Remote, once it's mended: to the Hub, and from there home Coming back Crouch and press the mended Remote Sleep No: \"You can't sleep here. The sea won't let you.\" The rig's beds still set your spawn. The sea Twelve waters; the deepest, the Black Below, is about two hundred blocks deeper than the rest Map The Watcher's Chart: four thousand blocks of sea round the rig"},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"What it is","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#what-it-is","t":"A dead green sea that goes on forever, a grey sky and a grey fog over it, and a black sea under that. Standing alone in it is the rig the Watcher built long ago \"for when i needed somewhere to hide\". You come down onto its helipad out of the portal he tore open as you fell from the Hub . That earns Dead Water , and the title reads CHAPTER EIGHT / DEAD WATER / the deep is listening . ...we're out. it's awake now. the first signal. it'll come for me - then for you. but it can't hear us here. not through all this water. take this. it'll get you back - to the hub, and home. ...no. nothing of mine works right here. then you stay. there's food. beds. i built this place a long time ago - for when i needed somewhere to hide. fix it. the big ones down there sing on its frequency - cut out what they sing with. ??? on the rig's helipad Then he goes over the rail. The whole arrival is on Chapter Eight ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"Stranded: the Broken Remote","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-broken-remote","t":"The Remote he gives you cracks in your hand: the Broken Remote . \"Chapter Eight: Dead Water. The Remote's broken - mend it with a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ and a copper ingot. They live deep.\" Until it's mended you're held here. Die and \"The sea brings you back. Nothing leaves the Dead Water while the Remote's broken.\" Without one of the rig's beds you wake in its quarters. You can't lose the Broken Remote either: \"The Broken Remote's still in your pocket.\" Mending it: the Broken Remote, a Signal Organ from a Static Leviathan, and a copper ingot. Go more than forty blocks down in the water (anywhere but the Black Below) and now and then one of them comes up out of the dark after you, singing. Mending it earns Back On Air . Mended: \"The Remote works again. Press it: the Hub (and in the Hub, home). Crouch and press it: back to the rig.\" Since 1.63.2 the Watcher also presses his chart into your hands when you come down. Held, it shows the stretch of sea you're in, a thousand blocks to a square, with you, the others down there with you, and the rig. Use it to unroll the whole chart: four thousand blocks of sea, every water in its own colour and named, the floor's depths shaded, and the Black Below hatched out in red as THE DEAD ZONE. Point at a water and you read his note on it. Scroll to zoom, drag to look round, R to come back to you."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The rig","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-rig","t":"An oil platform on four great legs of rusted steel lattice that go down into the black to the sea floor, braced every fourteen blocks. It was waiting with its lights on and its larders full. The derrick stands in the middle, a lattice tower with red lights at its crown and its drill string going down into the moon pool's dark. There are two cranes, the flare stack out over the sea on the north that never goes out, and lifeboats on the west. Railings run round everything and stairs go between the decks."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The cellar deck","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-cellar-deck","t":"Eight blocks over the sea. The moon pool : a square of open water in the middle, a ladder down into it and a winch over it. The dive locker (north-west): racks of gear, a shower and chests with Air Tanks, Marine Flares, Harpoon Bolts, a Harpoon Gun, a turtle shell and potions. The pumps (north-east). The pens (south-west): chickens, sheep, cows and a pig, let out when you arrive, with barrels of feed. The boat dock below it on the south, with two boats."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The main deck","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-main-deck","t":"The quarters : eight beds, and chests with rations, a clock, a compass, candles and some leather clothes. If you die without a bed of your own while the Remote's broken, this is where the sea brings you back. The mess and its kitchen: cooked fish, bread, stew, pie and Rig Rations. The infirmary (west): golden apples, potions, milk and honey, syringes and pill bottles. The workshop (east): copper, iron, glass, gunpowder, pistons and redstone; and a tool chest with iron tools, a fishing rod, shears, a shield and a spyglass. The stores (east): food, coal, torches, string, leads, ladders, planks and wool, and a boat. The greenhouse (east): crops growing under glass, water channels between the rows, a composter, and a chest of seeds and bone meal."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The upper deck","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-upper-deck","t":"The control room (north): consoles, windows all round, and a chest with a map, a compass, a recovery compass and flares. The radio room (middle): the set, its mast up through the roof. The armoury (south): Harpoon Guns and their bolts, iron armour, a sword, a bow and crossbow, a shield, flares and flashbangs. The helipad , over the east side: where you come down. Since 1.63.2 every door's buttons are on the wall beside it. A rig set down before then mends itself the first time it loads."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The sub bay and Orpheus","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-sub-bay","t":"Off the south end of the dock is the sub bay : a berth of open water between two steel catwalks, open to the sea on the south. The docking clamps are on a cradle under its water, with a gantry and lamps over it and a barrel of spares (copper, iron, glass, redstone, an Air Tank) by the way in. In its clamps lies the submarine Orpheus . Rigs already standing before 1.63.0 get the bay added. Orpheus at 43 metres, lamps on, sonar up. Its clamp charges its power and mends its hull. Lost it? The bay's console (the clamp up on the catwalk) builds another in the berth for 16 iron ingots and 8 glass. Since 1.63.2 Orpheus is thirteen blocks long with a cabin you walk about in: the helm, floodlights and sonar at the bow, and the chart table, bunks, lockers, workbench, galley, battery bank, repair board and motor down its length. It's rated for 183 metres; past that the hull creaks and gives, the dome cracks and at nothing it implodes. Pressure Plating takes it as deep as the sea goes. How to drive it is on the items page ."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The twelve waters","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-twelve-waters","t":"Out past the rig the sea is twelve different waters, each with its own colour and murk, its own floor, plants, life, sound and music, and its own place on the sea floor. Since 1.63.2 each one also has its own light in its fog, its water and on its floor, and glowing plankton drifts in every one in its colour, flaring up in your wake. The sea's sound changes as you swim from one to the next, and the reverb follows the water: longer and darker the deeper you go. Drowned and glow squid turn up in most of them. A world that had already been out there before 1.63.0 keeps the sea it had seen; everywhere new is the new sea. \"His note\" below is what the Watcher wrote of each water on his chart. The places can be found with /locate structure , which since 1.63.2 puts you standing beside them (or on the surface over a drowned one)."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Grey Shelf","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-grey-shelf","t":"His note: \"Grey water over grey silt. The rig stands in it. Nothing here is in a hurry - mostly.\" The rig's own grey-green water, over ash silt . Grey kelp and a few glow anemones grow here. Gentle Pipeyes, Lanternlets, Hum Skates, Stiltfins and Hymnbacks live here, with Hookjaws, Siphons and Needlemaws among them, and the Mouth of the Floor lies buried in the silt. You hear something groan, far off. Its place: lifeboats, sunk, one split open with its stores still in it ( statichollow:sea_lifeboats )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Haemal Reach","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-haemal-reach","t":"His note: \"The water's thick with blood. Clotfish come in swarms; the Siphons wait for them to pass.\" Blood-red water, thick as soup and lit red, over clot silt . Vein kelp (it glows), artery anemones and clot coral grow here. Pipeyes, Grinners, Puffbloats, Clotfish and Siphons live here, and a heart beats in the water. Its place: the Drowned Heart, a heart the size of a house with its arteries running out over the floor ( statichollow:sea_drowned_heart )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Wireweed","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-wireweed","t":"His note: \"Weed like wire, and it sings. The Choir Eels nest in it. Don't touch the bright ones.\" Dark green water over rust silt , a forest of wireweed and signal bulbs. Choir Eels, Hookjaws, Pipeyes, Lanternlets, Hum Skates and Grinners live here, and the wires sing. Its place: a radio tower, fallen and leaning, the weed grown up through it, its warning light still on ( statichollow:sea_radio_tower )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Lantern Fields","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-lantern-fields","t":"His note: \"Lights in the dark as far as you can see. Most of them are bulbs. Some of them aren't.\" Black-blue, clear water lit blue by its plants, over glow sand . Glow anemones and lantern bulbs grow here. Lanternlets, Thimble Jellies and Hymnbacks live here, and so do Gulpers with their lures. Glass chimes. Its place: a glass-domed habitat, flooded, its lamp still lit ( statichollow:sea_habitat_dome )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Ossuary Flats","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-ossuary-flats","t":"His note: \"A plain of bone. Whatever died here, died big. The Stiltfins pick it clean.\" Milky water over a floor of bone sand , with bone coral, bone fans and marrow sponge. Stiltfins, Pipeyes, Hum Skates, Hookjaws and Gulpers live here, the Mouth of the Floor lies buried here too, and bones knock. Its place: a whalefall, the skeleton of something whale-sized, picked clean ( statichollow:sea_whalefall )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Brine Sink","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-brine-sink","t":"His note: \"The brine pools eat what falls in. The water's sour, and the Puffbloats like it.\" Sick yellow-green water over brine crust , with lakes of brine that eat you and sulfur tubes. Puffbloats, Thimble Jellies, Clotfish and Siphons live here, and the brine fizzes. Its place: Sink Station, a research hut on stilts over a lake of brine ( statichollow:sea_sink_station )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Molar Reef","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-molar-reef","t":"His note: \"Teeth, grown into a reef. The Grinners live in it. They smile at you.\" Teal and pink water over gum silt : a reef of enamel coral, tooth fans, gum sponge and nerve anemones, with glow anemones scattered through it. Grinners, Puffbloats, Lanternlets, Clotfish and Hookjaws live here, the Mouth of the Floor lies buried here too, and teeth chatter. Its place: the Jaw, an arch of teeth in a ridge of gum with a row of teeth across the floor under it ( statichollow:sea_the_jaw )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Drowned Mycelia","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-drowned-mycelia","t":"His note: \"Mushrooms the size of towers, drowned. Their spores burst if you brush them.\" Violet water with spores in it, over spore silt . Gill glow and spore puffs grow here (they burst in your face). Pipeyes, Thimble Jellies, Gulpers and Siphons live here, and the drowned whisper. Its place: giant mushrooms, drowned ( statichollow:sea_drowned_mushrooms )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Rime Shelf","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-rime-shelf","t":"His note: \"Ice under the sea. Things are frozen in it. Some of them wake up.\" Cold, clear water under a roof of rime ice , over rime silt , with frost anemones and frozen corpses. Packs of Frostjaws hunt here, and Stiltfins and Hymnbacks live here too. The ice groans. Its places: a frozen outpost, its cabin locked in ice with its people still in it ( statichollow:sea_frozen_outpost ), and the rime spires ( statichollow:sea_rime_spire )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Ember Vents","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-ember-vents","t":"His note: \"Vents roaring up from below. Warm. The Mantlecrabs crowd round them - mind your power.\" Rust-orange water lit orange, over ember crust , with smoking vent chimneys and tube worms. Mantlecrabs (their pulse kills every light near them, the submarine's too), Choir Eels, Hum Skates, Stiltfins and Needlemaws live here, and the vents roar. Its place: a pump house, half fallen in, its great pipe running out to the vents ( statichollow:sea_pump_ruin )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Carrier Wave","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-carrier-wave","t":"His note: \"The static's loudest here. The water hums. Your instruments won't like it.\" Blue-grey water with static shimmering through it, over static sand . Static coral, antenna weed and signal bulbs grow here, and drowned television sets hiss on the floor. Choir Eels, Mantlecrabs, Pipeyes, Lanternlets and Hum Skates live here, and there's a voice in the static. Its place: a wreck field, with a ship's hull, a plane, containers and televisions still showing static ( statichollow:sea_wreck_field )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"The Black Below","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#the-black-below","t":"His note: \"THE DEAD ZONE. The floor drops away and doesn't stop. The leviathans live down there. Don't.\" The abyss: near-black water, barely any light, about two hundred blocks deeper than the rest, over abyss silt with void moss and eye pods on it (shut until you come near; then the eye opens and follows you). The chart's tooltip says it plainly: \"The black hatched in red is the dead zone. Don't take the sub over it.\" There's no music here, only the sound of the ocean, and nothing alive but plankton and one thing. Stay deep in it and something notices: a rumble from below, and the Undertow comes up out of the dark. Nothing else comes up out of the Black Below; it's the Undertow's. Lost whales (Hymnbacks) wander in now and then, singing in the dark, and a hungry Undertow eats them instead of you. It goes back down only when you leave. Its place: on the floor of the abyss, the Anchor, an anchor the size of a ship with its chain rising up out of sight ( statichollow:sea_the_anchor )."},{"p":"The Dead Water","h":"What's down there to take","u":"places/the-dead-water.html#loot-down-there","t":"Some of the sea's places keep chests: The lifeboats : bread, kelp, honey, a compass, flint and steel, iron, copper, string and Air Tanks. The habitat dome : a heart of the sea, sea lanterns, prismarine, glass, iron, redstone, Air Tanks, Needle Teeth and Shroud Hide. Sink Station : diamonds, iron, redstone, glowstone, sugar, Needle Teeth and Pressure Plating. The frozen outpost : diamonds, blue ice, iron, coal, leather, a spyglass, cooked cod and Shroud Hide. The wreck field : diamonds, emeralds, gold, iron, copper, a nautilus shell, a map and Pressure Plating."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"","u":"places/the-deep.html","t":"The Deep Something is always listening Wakes Once the Chorus has run from its pit Way in The Throat at the bottom of the Sinkhole's burrow Way out The Throat in the floor of the Gullet Sleep No: \"You can't sleep down here. Something is always listening.\" Beds don't set your spawn either. Biomes The Warm Dark, the Root Hollows, the Old Halls Music The Deep"},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"Finding it: the fragment","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-hunt","t":"When the Chorus runs from the Hive , it leaves a Chorus Fragment on the floor of its pit, and the fragment still hears the rest of it. Hold it to your ear and turn round. Facing the right way it whispers clearly, and what it says tells you how far. Side on it's faint and broken; facing away there's only static. Up in the world, leading you to the Sinkhole: down. a long way down. far from here - that way. that way. under the hills. we can feel you coming. closer. we can hear you walking. we can hear your heart. here. right under you. come down. it's warm. Down in the Deep, leading you to the Warm Heart: deeper. a long way yet. through the dark - that way. that way. past the old ones' halls. they don't like us. they won't like you. close now. can you hear us singing? we can hear you. here. we are right here. we are finished growing. Side on, and facing away: ...colder... no... turn... (nothing but static)"},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Sinkhole","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-sinkhole","t":"statichollow:sinkhole , once the Chorus has run Halloway's Low Field , where a farm's field was pulled down from underneath. It's out in the world like the Hive: a crater thirty-odd yards across, its rim a cliff of torn turf and soil with cracks running out from it into the grass. The field's fences are snapped off at the edge, the barn has tipped over the brink and lies half down the slope, and the cart it was loading lies on its side at the bottom. Veins of hive flesh run down the walls with ribs of chitin sticking out of them. Steam comes up off its floor, and now and then the whole hole breathes out, deep. The first time someone comes up to it: this is where it went down. the ground didn't fall in. it was pulled. someone measured it before you. he went down after it. the piece of it you've got will tell you how far down it goes. ??? at the Sinkhole The surveyor's camp is on the north rim: E. Calder's notes on a lectern ( Subsidence, Halloway's Low Field ) and his chest of kit: two lanterns, sixteen torches, two leads, a spyglass, an iron pickaxe, bread, cooked beef and a Surgical Kit. Reaching the Sinkhole earns Warmer ."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The burrow","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-burrow","t":"In the bottom of the hole, round a knot of flesh ringed with teeth, is the way the Chorus tore down: a tunnel round as a pipe, lined with hive flesh and ribs of chitin, winding down in six turns like a corkscrew, sixty blocks down from the floor of the hole. Halfway down, on a landing, is the surveyor's last page. At the bottom is a small domed chamber."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Throat","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-throat","t":"In the middle of the chamber's floor, three blocks across: the Throat , a ring of hive flesh puckered shut. Stand on it and it feels you (\"It feels you standing on it.\"). It stirs, it opens, and after a couple of seconds it takes you down into the Deep. That earns Down Where It Is Warm ."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"While it lives: it comes back up","u":"places/the-deep.html#it-comes-back-up","t":"Until the Chorus is dead, the world up top feels it: Tremors under you every so often: a low rumble and dust off the roof, without your view shaking. The ground gives way near you (natural ground only, never your builds): a pit lined with its flesh, its things climbing out of it. The pit heals over after five minutes. Flesh blisters swell up out of the ground: \"Something is swelling up out of the ground. Break it before it bursts.\" If it bursts, its forms come out. The Reach , every few nights where you live: three tremors, closer and closer, the ground splits, and one of the Chorus's hands tears up out of it with its things climbing out after it (\"IT COMES UP\"). Kill it for It Came Up ; leave it and after four minutes it sinks back down. See the Chorus ."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Deep","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-deep","t":"Huge warm caverns under the hills, older than anything over them, with seas of blood in their bottoms and a rock roof over everything. The Bloom's roots hang down through the roofs, gone deeper than anyone ever dug. Ember caps glow like coals on the floors. Ash and spores drift in the air, there's a warm drone and a heartbeat a long way off, and its own music plays. Coming down: \"It's warm down here. It's always been warm down here.\" If you carry the fragment, a moment later it whispers: \"home. we are home. come and find us. we are deeper.\""},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Warm Dark","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-warm-dark","t":"Where the hive's flesh has grown over the rock: veins of flesh, chitin and bone through the stone, springs of blood, nerve stalks, pustules and ember caps, red spores in the air."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Root Hollows","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-root-hollows","t":"Where the Bloom's roots come down: great Bloom Roots up from the floor and down from the roof, and pale Root Tendrils hanging everywhere, their ends glowing. Fewer ember caps. The Listeners nest here."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Old Halls","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-old-halls-biome","t":"The pale worked stone of whoever was down here first: old stone through the rock, bones, skulls, candles, a few ember caps, and ash in the air."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Gullet","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-gullet","t":"Where you come out: a domed chamber of hive flesh shut in the rock, near the middle of the Deep and up near its roof, lit by nerve stalks round its wall and ember caps on its floor. A Throat is set in its floor: stand on it to go back up to the Sinkhole's chamber. Three tunnels run out of the Gullet and down through the rock until they come out into the caverns."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"Low Marrow","u":"places/the-deep.html#low-marrow","t":"About a hundred blocks from the Gullet: a hamlet the ground opened under one night, pulled down whole into a cavern of its own. Five cottages lie where they came to rest, tipped over and half sunk in a lake that isn't water any more, full of it inside. In the middle of the lake its church stands upended, its bell still in its tower. The Bloom's roots hang through the cavern's roof and ember caps burn on what dry ground there is. Two Listeners are still there. Nobody's left. The reeve wrote down why ( Low Marrow , T. Ashby, on the lectern in his cottage), and so did the priest ( the last sermon , Rev. J. Fairley). Both are on the lore page . The reeve's last page:"},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"Low Marrow","u":"places/the-deep.html#low-marrow-2","t":"T. Ashby, Reeve Found: Low Marrow He said: follow the stones with the ears cut in them. A cap burns on every one. If you find this, go quiet. Go in your stockings. Follow the stones."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The way-stones","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-way-stones","t":"The old ones' road-markers: squat columns with a spiral cut in each like an ear and an ember cap burning on top. They stand every thirty-odd blocks from the Gullet to the Old Halls. Follow them."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Old Halls","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-old-halls","t":"About 230 blocks from the Gullet, the far end of the way-stones: the older ones' hall, cut out of the rock before anything walked up top. A passage leads straight in to its door. Inside is a long nave of their pale stone, fifty-odd blocks long under a stepped vault, two rows of pillars carved with their spirals, ember caps along the walls and root tendrils hanging down through the vault. Two alcoves hold what they cut in the wall (on lecterns), and the third holds their things. At the far end is a dais, two steps up, with candles on it and a seat at the back. On the seat is the Deaf King , where he's sat ever since the singing came down. He can't hear you and can't see you. He feels the floor."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"(cut in the wall by the dais)","u":"places/the-deep.html#cut-in-the-wall-by-the-dais","t":"the old ones Found: the Old Halls p. 1 The king does not hear. The king does not see. The king feels the floor. When you come before him, be still. p. 2 If you would have what he put in his ears, you must take it out of him. He will not give it. With it in your own, the singing is only singing. Killing him earns Stand Still , and he leaves the King's Ear-Stones . Carry them into the Warm Heart and the Chorus's song can't get into you."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Listeners' nests","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-nests","t":"In the Root Hollows, one to each stretch of the Deep: a hollow where the Listeners (see the Deaf King ) take what they take. Bones, the clothes of the people they were, a barrel of their things, and a low wall of bone round it. The Listeners hunt the Chorus's forms just as they hunt you."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"The Warm Heart","u":"places/the-deep.html#the-warm-heart","t":"Where the Chorus went to ground, about 420 blocks out from the Gullet, the way the fragment points. It's a great round chamber in the rock, some seventy-five blocks across. Its floor is hive flesh running down on every side to a lake of blood, with a vault of chitin ribs over it. Four stalks of chitin stand round the lake with its nerve nodes on them, where they were round its pit, and there are three ways in. Come down into it and the Chorus rises: \"Up out of the blood it comes - whole again, and every voice in it singing.\" When it's down to two thirds of its health, the walls crack open (\"The walls crack open. Something's coming through them: the older ones. They've heard it.\") and the Listeners pour in. At a third it tears itself up out of its lake. See the Chorus . When it dies: \"Far below, the singing stops. It doesn't start again.\" Everything of its in the chamber falls apart, the world above stops feeling it, and it leaves the Last Voice (advancement The Last Voice ). That leads on to Chapter Six ."},{"p":"The Sinkhole and the Deep","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/the-deep.html#its-blocks","t":"Block What it is The Throat The way in and out, in the Sinkhole's chamber and the Gullet Deep Rock The Deep's own stone Old Stone, Old Stone Bricks, Carved Old Stone The older ones' pale worked stone Bloom Root, Root Tendril The Bloom's roots; the tendrils' ends glow Ember Cap Glows like a coal on the floors Hive Flesh, Hive Chitin, Nerve Node The Hive's own, in the Warm Dark, the Gullet and the Warm Heart All of them have HD textures and LabPBR maps."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"","u":"places/the-flesh.html","t":"The Flesh's land Spreading Starts Ten seconds after the Great Bloom rises, east of the Botanic Gardens Reach About 1000 blocks round where it came up; 2000 once the Bloom has changed Ends Dies back once the Bloom is dead, except in the places it built itself into Music Its own, and Rosemont's, the Laboratory's and the shelter's"},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"The waking","u":"places/the-flesh.html#the-waking","t":"Ten seconds after the Great Bloom rises through the glasshouse, the ground east of the Botanic Gardens shakes and splits, and a column of raw muscle forty blocks high punches up out of it, sheds its skin, and opens a slit of teeth down its front. Veins race out from it across the ground. A title card: THE FLESH WAKES , the flower made it . The first of them get up out of the ground and come for you. Flesh and stone, with the HD world pack."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"How it spreads","u":"places/the-flesh.html#how-it-spreads","t":"Outward from where it came up, further every day: a slow start, then faster. Near you it creeps from block to block. What was there What it becomes Grass and soil Flesh turf and flesh soil: meat Stone and brick Veined stone and veined masonry, lit red from inside Trees Sinew logs and hanging tissue Glass Stretched membrane Sand Rot sand Flowers Withered black stubs Deeper in it grows flesh pustules (tread on one, hit it or shoot it and it bursts over you), mouths in the ground that breathe red mist and let the infected climb out, nerve stalks lit from within, and pools of the Flesh that drag at your feet. Where it touches the Bloom's flesh and the gardens' flowers, they char, and the flowers fight back, killing what of it touches them."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"The red fog","u":"places/the-flesh.html#the-red-fog","t":"Where it has taken the land, the fog goes the colour of meat and it breathes all round you, with things far off in it: screams, tearing, a heartbeat, a radio, gunfire. Every sound of it is new. With Sound Physics, the Flesh swallows sound like mud and resin do."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"The infection","u":"places/the-flesh.html#the-infection","t":"Their hits, their bites, a pustule bursting: the Flesh gets into you (\"Something is in the wound. It's warm, and it's moving.\"). A vein beside your hotbar fills red with how much of you it has, and red veins creep in from the edges of your sight. Past halfway you're turning: hungry, slower, your heart pounding in your ears, your sight flushing red with every beat. \"You're turning. Find Bloom Serum.\" At the top, your Last Breath: thirty seconds, your sight closing to a tunnel and your heart slowing. Drink a Bloom Serum, or die and get up again as one of them, with your name (\"Infected Steve\"). Bloom Serum (a glass bottle, a Bloom pustule and sugar; or a ghost orchid, a whispering lily and sugar) drives it back and keeps it off you for twenty seconds. Tainted meat fills you, and infects you. The Gardener's clothes keep half of it off; the full hazmat suit halves the bile, gas and spores."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"What lives in it","u":"places/the-flesh.html#what-lives-in-it","t":"The Flesh's infected, the things they mutate into after ten minutes on its ground, the Broodmother's nests, and on some nights a horde walking behind a Bellwether. All of them are in the bestiary . Since 1.43.3 parasites get into the infected too. Flower Ash Bombs (a garden flower, a burnt petal and gunpowder make two) burn it back: where one bursts the Flesh's growth dies back to what it was, and anything infected in it burns. Under the Flesh."},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"The places it built itself into","u":"places/the-flesh.html#the-places-it-built","t":"Rosemont , the broken city The Laboratory Shelter No. 4 The nests (while their Broodmother lives) The places the Bloom and the railgun woke, and the column it came up out of"},{"p":"The red fog (the Flesh)","h":"Dying back","u":"places/the-flesh.html#dying-back","t":"With the Bloom dead (since 1.43.5), the Flesh has nothing to grow from. It stops spreading and dies back: wherever you go, the ground it took comes back as it was, grass, earth, stone and trees. Its vents and hordes stop with it. The places it built itself into keep it, and what's in them stays there. it's dying. with the flower dead it's got nothing to grow from - the ground's coming back. not in the places it built itself into, though. those it keeps. ??? as the Flesh dies back"},{"p":"The Hive","h":"","u":"places/the-hive.html","t":"The Hive It's growing a mind Wakes Once the Carrier is dead and the static has signed off, 300 to 1000 blocks out Find it The Watcher's Needle (The Hive), handed out after It Speaks , or /statichollow locate hive Size About seventy blocks across; the pit in the middle is twelve deep In the pit The Chorus Arriving \"The ground here is warm, and soft, and it gives under you. Something under it is breathing.\""},{"p":"The Hive","h":"What it is","u":"places/the-hive.html#what-it-is","t":"With the Carrier dead, the parasite can't hear itself in the static any more. So it grows itself a mind instead, out in the world, in a hamlet it took whole. For about thirty blocks round, everything has gone under its creep : violet Hive Flesh , roots of black Hive Chitin running out over the ground from the middle, and ribs of chitin arched over the ground on the east, south and west. The way in is from the north, through the hamlet's gate. The first time someone comes near, the Watcher says: it took them whole. the people, the houses. everything they knew is in that pit now. it thinks with those, on the stalks round the pit. cut them and it can't think straight. there was a priest here. read him. ??? at the Hive The Hive's black hands standing round the pit, with the Chorus's bar already up."},{"p":"The Hive","h":"The hamlet it took","u":"places/the-hive.html#the-hamlet","t":"Three cottages and a bell tower, half swallowed by the creep. The lane runs in past them from the gate, between fence posts that have mostly fallen. The roofs have fallen in at one end and the creep grows up the walls and in through the doors. The bell tower has a ladder up inside it. In the first cottage is a lectern with the priest's journal, The Book of the Hollow Lane by Fr. Aldous Mercer, and his chest beside it with what he brought for the fire: a Surgical Kit flint and steel, and six fire charges a lantern, four bread, two golden apples and five iron ingots His last page says what to do: \"It thinks with the four bulbs on the black stalks. Burn what you can. Cut what you can't.\""},{"p":"The Hive","h":"The Hive Hands","u":"places/the-hive.html#the-hands","t":"The black spires round the pit are alive (since 1.53.0): seven Hive Hands , each an arm as tall as a tree coming up out of a mound of hive flesh, braided chitin round a core of flesh, a palm with eyes and a mouth at the top and three long hooked fingers. They never stop moving, and they turn to follow you. Come within reach and they slam down on you (the ground lights up violet where it's going to land), sweep low across their own foot, or grab you, lift you high over the hive, squeeze, and throw you. They can be killed; fire hurts them more. A dead one withers and goes down into its mound, and drops hive chitin and flesh. While the Chorus is still in its pit, the hive grows a dead hand back after five minutes. In a hive grown before 1.53.0, the old spires come down and the hands come up the first time you're there. More on the Chorus's page ."},{"p":"The Hive","h":"The nerve nodes","u":"places/the-hive.html#the-nerve-nodes","t":"Round the pit stand four stalks of chitin, nine blocks high, with steps of chitin wound round each one. On top of each is a Nerve Node , glowing and pulsing, joined to the Chorus by a cord with its light running along it. This is what it thinks with. Climb the steps and tear the nodes open: each one you break makes it scream and makes it easier to hurt. Break all four and everything gets through (advancement Senseless )."},{"p":"The Hive","h":"The pit","u":"places/the-hive.html#the-pit","t":"In the middle, the pit: about twenty-two blocks across at the rim, twelve deep, a ridge of flesh round its lip and black ribs of chitin up its walls. A ledge winds down its wall from the rim on the north side to the floor. The floor is heaped and wet, and in its middle is the socket where the Chorus is rooted. The first time anyone comes to the edge of the pit, the Chorus comes up out of it (the cutscene The Mind ) and the fight starts. It never leaves its pit. See the Chorus for the fight. When it's brought down to a quarter it tears itself down into the ground and runs, leaving a Chorus Fragment behind on the floor of the pit. That fragment leads you to the Sinkhole and the Deep ."},{"p":"The Hive","h":"Biomass, pods and bones","u":"places/the-hive.html#the-biomass","t":"Heaps of biomass lie about the place, violet flesh with chitin forced out through it. They aren't dead: with anyone about, they heave themselves up into the parasite's pure forms (see the turned ). Torn husks show where some already got up. Its pods sit in the creep, and the bones of what it took lie here and there."},{"p":"The Hive","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/the-hive.html#advancements","t":"The Hive : Come to where the parasite is growing itself a mind Senseless : Tear open all four of the Chorus's nerve nodes It Ran : Drive the Chorus down out of its pit The rest of Chapter Five's are on the advancements page ."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html","t":"The Hollow's own country New worlds only Since 1.62.0 Where In the Overworld, on the Hollow's side of the world, among the game's biomes and Biomes O' Plenty's Five places The Hollow Moor, the Blightwood, the Weeping Fen, the Antler Woods, the Signal Flats And under the sea Oceans about 2,000 blocks deep, in three depths Old worlds Worlds made before 1.62.0 keep the land and seas they already have. The new biomes and the deep oceans only appear in new worlds."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The land itself","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-land","t":"Static Hollow has its own country in the Overworld: five places of its own, each with its own trees, plants and stone, its own fog, sounds and music. Each one takes the place of one of the game's biomes, but only on one side of the world, where the game itself would put a variant. Their terrain is the game's own, in the same climate. They sit alongside Biomes O' Plenty , which is in the modpack since 1.62.0 (with TerraBlender and GlitchCore). Static Hollow's structures, fog and music are made to fit Biomes O' Plenty's biomes too. Out on the moor. Biome In place of Its fog Its music The Hollow Moor Cold plains and cold meadows A grey-blue mist over the heath Hollow Fields The Blightwood Dark forests Close, the colour of a bruise Under the Boughs The Weeping Fen Swamps A green murk off the water Still Water The Antler Woods Snowy taiga, the wetter kind Pale and cold Pine Needles The Signal Flats Dry savanna Flat grey, and far Dry Bones The music column is each place's lullaby. The further the story has got, the more often the chapter's own music plays instead; see the soundtrack . With Serene Seasons, the fog also changes colour with the season."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Hollow Moor","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-hollow-moor","t":"Open, misty heath: dead heather, peat, old graves under the turf (grave soil), mossy boulders, fallen deadwood, and here and there a gallows-tree of deadwood with chains hanging from it. On the ground you find grave candles, cairn stones and bone piles. White ash drifts in the air. Wind crosses the moor, and a far bell tolls."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Blightwood","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-blightwood","t":"Sick trees with grey-violet leaves: Blightwood , some of them great and dark-oak shaped, with Hanging Rot dripping from their leaves and shelf fungus on them. Huge brown mushrooms grow among them, and Rotgrass underneath. Rot caps and bone piles lie on the ground, and spores and carrion flies drift in the air. The wood creaks, and something breathes in the trees."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Weeping Fen","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-weeping-fen","t":"Drowned Fen Willows trail Willow Strands into black water, over peat and mud and sparse rotgrass. Lights drift over it (lantern motes), carrion flies with them. You find ritual offerings, rot caps and cairn stones. Frogs and the bogged live here. Water laps, and someone weeps, far off."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Antler Woods","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-antler-woods","t":"Bone-white Bonewood trees with dark red Bonewood Needles , some of them tall spires, and antler-snags of fallen deadwood among them, with a little dead heather. Bone piles and cairn stones lie about and bone ash drifts in the air. Wolves and foxes live here. Wind whistles through bone, and something bellows, far off."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The Signal Flats","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-signal-flats","t":"Dead grey flats: Wire Grass , gravel, snags of deadwood, and outcrops of Static Stone , which hums. Bone piles and cairn stones lie about, and sparks of static and white ash drift on the wind. Static on the wind, and tones through the static."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"Small things sharing one space","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#small-things","t":"Since 1.62.0 there are seven sets of little things that share a single block space, one to four of a set in it, each turned to face whoever put it down. Place one on another to add a piece; break it and one piece comes off. Set What's in it Where you find it Grave Candles Tallow candles, a stub, a skull. Light them, put them out. The Hollow Moor; the vaults under the cathedral's crypts Bone Pile A skull, its jaw, bones The Moor, the Blightwood, the Antler Woods, the Signal Flats; the cathedral's undercroft; the deep ocean floors and the Dead Water's Rot Caps The Blightwood's fungi. They glow a little, and puff spores. The Blightwood, the Weeping Fen Hanging Chains Chains, a hook, a shackle, a weight, hung from a ceiling. They creak. The cathedral's undercroft and crypt vaults; the rig's dive locker and workshop Rig Clutter A tin, an oil can, a wrench, bolts The rig in the Dead Water Cairn Stones Flat stones stacked by pilgrims, the top one carved. At night something whispers from them. The Moor, the Fen, the Antler Woods, the Signal Flats; behind the Forsaken Altar's pilgrim stones Ritual Offerings A bowl of ash, a straw doll, a red candle, dried herbs The Weeping Fen; at the foot of the Forsaken Altar's pilgrim stones The idea of small blocks sharing a space is from Olaf's Relatively Placed Blocks. Nothing of it is used; these are Static Hollow's own."},{"p":"The Hollow's own country","h":"The deep oceans","u":"places/the-hollows-country.html#the-deep-oceans","t":"In new worlds the oceans go down. Past the shelf the sea floor falls away to about 2,000 blocks below the waves : a black drop with the ocean monuments standing on its floor and lava glowing at the very bottom. The deep is the game's own terrain, stretched. (The idea is Tectonic's, MIT; nothing of its code is used.) Under an ocean the water is laid out in three depths, each its own place with its own dark, its own sounds and its own life: Depth From What's there What lives there The Sunless Drop below y -128 The last of the light goes and the slope falls away into nothing; bone-white snow drifting down through the black Shroud Rays, Needlemaws, drowned, glow squid The Hadal Dark below y -700 Pressure, cold, and things that make their own light Shroud Rays, Needlemaws, the Static Leviathan, glow squid The Trench below y -1400 The floor of the world's sea: vents breathing heat, the bones of very big things, and what made them bones Needlemaws, the Static Leviathan On the deep floors lie heaps of bone, spires of bone and calcite, and vents of basalt and blackstone with crying obsidian in them. Sea pickles glow in the dark and bone piles lie about. All the way down, the deep water groans and something passes in the dark. The Shroud Ray leaves you be, until you hit it. Then it wraps you. It drops Shroud Hide . The Needlemaw is dark until your light finds it. It lunges, and recoils from the light. It drops Needle Teeth . The Static Leviathan is a boss with its own bar. It charges, it swallows you whole, and it sings on the Remote's frequency. It drops its Signal Organ , which mends the Remote in the Dead Water . More on all three in the bestiary and on the Undertow's page ."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"","u":"places/the-hub.html","t":"The Hub A realm he made First time After the last show's credits, his hand comes up through them and takes you there After that Use the Remote; use it again in the Hub to go home Way out The Remote, or the edge (home to your bed or the world's spawn, no harm in the fall) Sleep No: \"Not here. Not with it out there, past the wall.\" Music The Hub"},{"p":"The Hub","h":"What it is","u":"places/the-hub.html#what-it-is","t":"A realm the Watcher made, floating in a sky of drifting static with a pale fog over everything. The middle of it is a round plaza of pale Hub Stone , about thirty-three blocks across, with his marks lit in it as Hub Glyphs in two rings and a cross in the middle. Underneath, the stone tapers away to a point, the way an island would if it had been torn up out of something. A few smaller pieces of it hang in the static round about. Being taken there earns The Hub . The gallery, during his speech."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"His speech","u":"places/the-hub.html#his-speech","t":"The first time, he's there with you (the cutscene The Hub ): this is the hub. i made it. a realm. it isn't mine - nothing is - but i made it. through these, you can go back. every chapter. play it again. or jump off the edge. it'll take you home, and you can carry on. ??? in the Hub He doesn't get to finish. A voice tears the sky over the gallery open (\"ENOUGH.\"), and the First Signal comes through. The whole scene is on Chapter Seven ."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"The gallery and its replay portals","u":"places/the-hub.html#the-gallery","t":"Along the north side of the plaza runs the gallery , a walk with six Replay Portals standing on it, one for each chapter, each with its chapter playing in it like a picture on an old set. Walk into one and you're back at that chapter's place in your world. A moment later its last fight comes back for another go: a replay . The replay portals, with the HD world pack. Portal Takes you to What comes back The Hollow The Cathedral of the Hollow The Hollow Saint , rising out of the floor Act Two The Botanic Gardens' glasshouse The Gardener The Bloom The Great Bloom's arena The Gardener, Reborn The Flesh The Laboratory Specimen Zero The Static The Deep The Deaf King The Door The Stalls The Crowd , getting up out of the heap of them Going through one earns Previously On... . The story stays told: whoever comes back is marked as a replay, and beating it again sets nothing off (no new act, no lockdown, no tickets). It fights the way it did and goes down the way it did, and then \"(The Remote takes you back to the Hub.)\" Beating a replay also leaves three or four Rerun Reels , which Chapter Seven's gear is made from (see gear for every chapter ). A replay ends if you go more than 160 blocks from it, leave, die, log out, or take longer than twenty minutes: \"The replay's over - it's gone back into the static.\" If a chapter's place isn't in your world, the portal says \"there's nothing there to go back to in this world.\""},{"p":"The Hub","h":"The edge","u":"places/the-hub.html#the-edge","t":"On the south side of the plaza a walk goes out over nothing: the edge . Jump off and you fall, the Hub going away above you, and come down at home (your bed, or the world's spawn) with no harm done. Since 1.62.0 there's one exception. If you've never been down in the Dead Water, the Watcher is there as you fall, and he tears a portal open under you. You come down on the rig in the Dead Water instead ( Chapter Eight ). The first time, at the end of his speech, that's where the jump goes. Worlds that had their landing at home before 1.62.0 get there by taking the Remote to the Hub and jumping off."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"The wall, and what's past it","u":"places/the-hub.html#the-wall","t":"When you both went off the edge the first time, he shut the realm behind you with a wall of static. Back in the Hub, the First Signal is still there, past that faint wall, standing and watching you. Now and then you hear it."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"The Remote","u":"places/the-hub.html#the-remote","t":"The Remote is an old television's remote whose blank button is warm (being given it earns Channel Changer ). Use it at home and it takes you to the Hub; use it in the Hub and it takes you home. Since 1.62.0 he hands it to you on the rig in the Dead Water, and it breaks in your hand there. Mended, it works again, and crouching as you press it takes you back to the rig. See the Dead Water ."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/the-hub.html#its-blocks","t":"Hub Stone and Hub Stone Slab Hub Glyph : his marks, lit Replay Portal Since 1.59.1 the mod's own copies of the Photon, Insanity and Hysteria shaders draw the Hub with their Nether programs: lit evenly by its own pale fog, with no sun, clouds or light shafts."},{"p":"The Hub","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/the-hub.html#advancements","t":"The Hub : Be taken into the realm he made, after the credits ENOUGH : Hear the First Signal - and jump Previously On... : Go back to a chapter through one of the Hub's portals"},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"","u":"places/the-other-side.html","t":"The Other Side Stay out of its eye Way in The Door at the End of the World, once its static has gone black Way out The seam in the screen's back, out into the End beside the Door Sleep No: \"Not here. Not with it out there.\" Past the edge The Viewer Music The Other Side; the Viewer's fight has its own (What He Kept Out) Arriving \"The other side. A stage, behind the screen your world's on - and past its edge, nothing. Something's sat out there in it.\""},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"The black door","u":"places/the-other-side.html#the-black-door","t":"When the Watcher has run his first reel in the Vault , the static in the Door at the End of the World goes black: the dark on the far side of it, looking out. It hums and the air is drawn into it. Walk into it. Going through earns The Other Side ."},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"The stage","u":"places/the-other-side.html#the-stage","t":"You come out through a seam of Black Static in the back of a screen as big as a cliff, ninety-six blocks wide and forty-eight high. Your world plays across it the wrong way round, its light coming through the cloth backwards. In front of you is a stage of pale boards about sixty-five blocks wide. On either side are the wings , black curtains with gaps in them, and over it stands a proscenium arch. Footlights run along the front edge. The Watcher's last projector is at the back of the stage, with him beside it."},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"The painted flats","u":"places/the-other-side.html#the-flats","t":"Nine flats of scenery stand about on the boards, each one a picture of somewhere from your story in a scene painter's broad strokes, on the side that faces out: the Cathedral Rosemont the Glasshouse the Drive-in the Bloom the Deep a house the woods the Stalls A flat between you and the Viewer's eye hides you from it. Its hands smash the flats they hit to splinters, so the cover doesn't last."},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"The edge","u":"places/the-other-side.html#the-edge","t":"Past the front of the stage there's nothing, only a dark so big it has a shape. Fall off and \"The dark doesn't keep you. You're back on the boards - it hurt.\""},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"Curtain Up","u":"places/the-other-side.html#curtain-up","t":"The first time anyone comes through, the camera is taken. Out past the edge there are knees like hills, shoulders up in the black, and hands on the stage's edge with fingers like felled trees. Then an eye opens. you came through. good. it hasn't looked this way. not yet. this is the other side. it's watched your world since the first picture. everything that ever happened to you - it watched. now it wants to see you up close. stay out of its eye. get behind the scenery. when it leans in - hit it. i'll run the projector. ??? Curtain Up \"Keep out of its light - get behind the scenery. When it leans in, hit its eye. Its hands feel it too.\" Then the fight with the Viewer begins. Cut-out Stand-Ins hop out of the gaps in the wings and point you out to it."},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"His Last Projector","u":"places/the-other-side.html#his-last-projector","t":"The projector at the back of the stage is his: \"His. He'll run it.\" Twice during the fight he loads it. At two thirds of the Viewer's health he puts the Omni's Heart in its lamp and throws every colour at once into its eye (advancement Every Colour at Once ). At a third, he puts in what's left of the Carrier: your world, carried out on the beam. After that the Viewer reaches for the projector with both hands, and you have to beat them back. At the end he threads his first reel and runs it for the Viewer, and it sits back to watch itself. When the last show is over, the credits roll and you're sent home with a record, Thank You for Watching . \"You're home. Somewhere past the end of the world, a projector's running, and something's watching itself, and will be for ever.\" The Door's static is static again."},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/the-other-side.html#its-blocks","t":"Black Static : the Door's opening once it's gone black, and the seam home Stage Boards , Stage Flat , Painted Flat and Footlight The Screen's Back His Last Projector"},{"p":"The Other Side","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/the-other-side.html#advancements","t":"The Other Side : Go through the Door at the End of the World, its static gone black Out of Sight : Get through the first third of the Viewer without it ever seeing you right through Every Colour at Once : See the Omni's heart put into his last projector's lamp It Gets Up : Be there when what he kept out stands up Thank You for Watching : See the last show"},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"","u":"places/the-stalls.html","t":"The Stalls Quiet, please Way in The Door at the End of the World, out in the End Way out The Door behind you: home to your bed, or the world's spawn Sleep No: \"Not here. Not with them watching.\" Who's here Forty of the Audience in the seats, four Ushers in the aisles Music The Stalls; the Crowd's fight has its own The screen Sixty-four blocks across, about two hundred feet"},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The seal on the End","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-seal","t":"After signing off, the Watcher shut the End: anyone who goes through an End portal in survival is sent straight back out to their bed or the world's spawn. He can't keep you out if you carry the Last Voice in, the one voice the Chorus couldn't swallow (since 1.60.1 it works however you came by it). It speaks: \"...hold me up. here. he made this seal with his own hands. i can open it...\" Something cracks, all the way across the End's sky - and stays cracked. The seal he put on it is broken. \"...there. out past the obsidian. a door. go through it. i'll be quiet now...\" And the Watcher says one word: \"...don't.\" From then on the End is open to everyone, as it was. This earns The Door at the End of the World . (The dragon you'll meet there is the Infested Ender Dragon .)"},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The Door at the End of the World","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-door","t":"Out past the obsidian platform you arrive on, a causeway of seal-stone runs east over the void. Seal-stone is black with the Watcher's glyphs cut in it, and posts along the causeway each carry one of his glyphs, still faintly lit. At its end an island of the same stone hangs in nothing, with a long root of it going down underneath. On the island, facing back the way you came, stands the Door : a frame of seal-stone nine blocks wide and thirteen high, his glyphs cut all round it, and in its opening nothing but static , upright, crawling and humming. Walk into it. The Door stands about 28 blocks east of the obsidian, at the End's 128, 49, 0. Since 1.60.2 the End's island ground is cleared off it, with a way along the causeway and a bowl round the island so the Door stands in the open. The first time anyone is in the End, the ground over the obsidian also gives way into a shaft open to the sky, so you don't arrive shut in end stone. Later the Door changes. Once the Watcher has run his first reel in the Vault , its static goes black : the dark on the far side of it, looking out. It hums, the air is drawn into it, and walking in takes you to the Other Side . After the last show it's static again."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The Stalls","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-stalls","t":"\"Rows and rows of seats in the dark, every one of them facing a screen. Some of them are taken.\" It's a picture house with no walls and no roof, going on further than you can see. The floor is black Stalls Asphalt , and on it row after row of Picture House Seats curve round in long arcs to face the screen, with two aisles running down through them. Black sky, dark fog, dust and ash in the air, its own air and its own music. Arriving earns Take Your Seat . Behind the last row are the cars of every drive-in that ever closed, wrecked, still facing the screen, with speaker posts among them. Behind those is the projection booth, up on its tower, with its beam going out over everything. And behind that is the way you came in: a Door of seal-stone, its opening full of static. Step back through it and you're home."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The Great Screen","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-great-screen","t":"At the front stands the Great Screen , sixty-four blocks across in a black proscenium, its red curtains drawn back to either side and a low stage at its foot. Its picture flickers: static, and between the static the story so far, frame after frame, grey and grainy. The altar, the cathedral, the glasshouse, the Bloom, the city, the drive-in, the hive, the Deep."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The Audience in the seats","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-audience-in-the-seats","t":"Forty of the seats are taken by the Audience : grey people in grey clothes, faces turned up to the screen, a ticket in one hand in their laps. They don't look round, but they hear you. A step near them, a block broken or a door, and they get up slowly with a finger to their lips, come for you and hold you where you are. Sneak and they don't hear you walk. Lose them and they go back and sit down. Some of them carry a Ticket Stub . Four Ushers walk the aisles with their lamps. Sneaking doesn't help against a lamp: it sees, it doesn't hear. If one finds you (\"The Usher's lamp is on you.\"), the SHHH goes through the house and everyone sat near you gets up. Show an Usher a Ticket Stub and it looks away for a minute. All three of them are on the Crowd's page ."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The front aisle","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-front-aisle","t":"Between the stage and the front row runs the front aisle . Step out onto it and \"The picture on the screen is you.\" Every one of the Audience gets up and comes down to the front, and they go into a heap that stands up as the Crowd . It doesn't leave the front."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"The front row","u":"places/the-stalls.html#the-front-row","t":"One seat in the front row, straight back from the middle of the screen, is always taken. When the Crowd has come apart and the screen has gone dark, you see who's in it (the cutscene Front Row ). He tears the screen open and goes through, and it closes up behind him to a seam of light down the middle of the screen: \"There's a seam of light down the middle of the screen where he went through. It won't stay shut forever.\" The Crowd leaves the Last Ticket behind. Hold it up to the seam and it tears in two in your hand, and the seam opens wide, light pouring out of it down to the stage. It stays open for everyone. That's the way into the Watcher's Vault . Coming back out of the Vault puts you on the stage in front of the screen."},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/the-stalls.html#its-blocks","t":"Seal-Stone and Seal-Stone Glyph : the Door, its frame and the causeway The Door's Static : the Door's opening Stalls Asphalt , Picture House Seat , Screen Cloth and The Great Screen"},{"p":"The Door and the Stalls","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/the-stalls.html#advancements","t":"The Door at the End of the World : Carry the Last Voice into the End, and break his seal Take Your Seat : Go through the Door into the Stalls Quiet, Please : Keep perfectly still through the Crowd's Hush Standing Ovation : Bring the Crowd down Front Row : See who was sitting in the front row Admit One : Hold the Last Ticket up to the seam in the screen"},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html","t":"The Watcher's Vault Behind the picture Way in The seam in the Stalls' Great Screen, opened with the Last Ticket Way out The tear you came out of, onto the stage in the Stalls Sleep No: \"Not here. Not with them standing out there in the stacks.\" Who's here Sixteen Tuned in the stacks and two in each keep Music Behind the Picture; the Projectionist's fight has its own Arriving \"Behind the picture. Shelves going up into the dark, cans of film and boxes of tape on every one, and old sets among them - some still on.\""},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"Behind the picture","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#behind-the-picture","t":"You come out through the seam into his archive, on the back of the picture: a wall of grey canvas with the picture's light coming through it backwards. Going in earns Behind the Picture . Ahead, the nave runs north: a long walk of dark Vault Terrazzo , cable over the floor, bulbs in cages hanging on chains out of the black, and walls of the Watcher's own concrete. On either side are the stacks , row after row of steel Archive Shelves nine blocks high with a cross-aisle through them. There are cans of film on their edges and boxes of tape on every shelf, labels in his hand, and Old Sets among them, some still on, static crawling on their screens."},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"The Tuned","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#the-tuned","t":"Standing in the aisles are the Tuned : people from the neck down (a cardigan, a shirt done up to the collar, slippers) with an old television set where the head should be. They only move while you're looking at them. Look at one and it comes for you in jerks, like a picture with frames missing, with your face on its screen. Look away and it stops dead. Close, and watched, it takes your head in its hands and tunes you. In the dark, or in the Projectionist's light, they move whether you look or not. Flash an Usher's Lamp at one and it can't move for four seconds. Some drop a Vacuum Tube . More on the Projectionist's page ."},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"The keeps","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#the-keeps","t":"Three keeps open off the nave behind round steel Keep Doors : two facing each other near the seam, and one further in on the west side. Use a door or its wheel and \"The wheel turns. Somewhere in the door, bolts draw back, one after another.\" The door swings in. Two Tuned wait in each keep. On a plinth in each is what he kept: What he kept Taking it The Omni's Heart \"The Omni's heart: every colour at once, turning. It's lighter than it looks, and warm.\" What's Left of the Carrier \"What's left of the Carrier comes off its plinth beating - and the static pours out of it.\" Every Tuned near you is loose for a few seconds. His First Reel \"His first reel. On the lid, in his hand: THE OTHER SIDE. FIRST. DO NOT RUN.\" It's kept in a glass case. All three together: \"That's all three of them. Back to the Watch.\" That earns What He Kept ."},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"The Watch","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#the-watch","t":"At the north end of the nave is the Watch : his desk, his chair, and in front of them the Watch Wall , old sets stacked thirty-seven across and sixteen high, all showing one picture. The first time you come, he's there (the cutscene The Watch ): this is where i watch from. they watch the picture. i watch them. your world's a show to them. the worse it gets, the more of them come. they left you a ticket. it admits one. not you. something came in behind you. it's come for what i kept. the omni. the carrier. my first reel. get to them before it does. bring them here. ??? in the Watch Bring all three things back to the Watch and every set on the wall goes to one picture, and the Projectionist steps down out of them. In the last third of the fight comes the intermission: every set and every bulb goes out, there's only its lens, and \"Please remain seated.\" Burning it through earns The Final Reel . Afterwards he runs his first reel on the projector on his desk (the cutscene The First Reel ), and the Wall shows the first thing anyone ever saw on the other side. When it's over: \"Every set on the Watch Wall shows the Door at the End of the World. The static in it has gone black.\" That earns What He Kept Out and leads on to the Other Side ."},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"Its blocks","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#its-blocks","t":"Vault Terrazzo and The Watcher's Concrete Archive Shelf , Old Set (two Vacuum Tubes with glass, iron and redstone make two of your own, which switch on and off) and Cable Keep Door , Keep Wheel and What He Kept (the plinths) The Watch Wall"},{"p":"The Watcher's Vault","h":"Advancements here","u":"places/the-watchers-vault.html#advancements","t":"Behind the Picture : Go through the seam, into the Watcher's Vault What He Kept : Take all three things out of his keeps The Final Reel : Burn the Projectionist through What He Kept Out : See his first reel"},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"","u":"story/chapter-1.html","t":"You find a ruined shrine with a soul campfire burning at it, and you touch the altar. From then on, nine creepypastas hunt everyone in the world, mostly in the dark, and something tall stands at the edge of your sight and watches you kill them."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"The Forsaken Altar","u":"story/chapter-1.html#the-forsaken-altar","t":"Every world has a Forsaken Altar, 500 to 1000 blocks from the world spawn. It always stands on open, flat, dry ground, never underground, in water or on a mountainside, and on the far side of spawn from the cathedral. Follow the blue smoke from its soul campfire. The ruin rises around the altar once you come within about 90 blocks: broken pillars, skulls, candles, graves and splashes of blood, built from the mod's own hollow stone, ossuary bricks of bone and rotten planks. It clears every tree, bush and bump of ground in its way as it goes up. Around it (since 1.40) stand nine pilgrim stones , each carved with the sign of one of the Nine. The pilgrims' camp is abandoned nearby, with one of their diaries, and a sealing stone by the shrine covers a stair down to the catacomb where the first pilgrims lie. It stays shut until the altar wakes. At night pilgrims kneel round the altar; come close and they fade away, and sometimes leave something behind. Right-click the altar with an empty hand to wake it. There is no going back after that. Read the pilgrim's diary on the lore page . Find the altar with /locate structure statichollow:forsaken_altar if you're testing with cheats on."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"The nine creepypastas","u":"story/chapter-1.html#the-nine","t":"Once the altar is awake the nine hunt everyone, mostly in the dark. Each one fights its own way, has its own sounds and its own death, and drops its own material, which is what the chapter's weapons and armour are made from. Creepypasta What to know Drops Hollow Neighbor Hostile to players only. Stalks you, knocks on doors, messages you in chat pretending to be a friend, and rises up behind your window to say it to your face. Hollow Knuckle Stitchjaw Hostile to everything. Crawls flat and climbs walls. Every bite opens the wound further (Bleeding I, II, III). Stitched Sinew Weeping Shepherd Neutral, but fights back. Weeps, stares if you stare, hunts the undead. Shepherd's Tear Lullaby Mother Neutral by day, hostile at night. Steals villagers. Her hits can drag you into the Hollow, a sealed black room under the world, for 15 seconds. Rusted Lullaby Key Broadcast A man with a CRT television for a head. Don't look at it (it burns) and don't touch it (it shocks). Its antennae glow green once it has seen you. Static Shard Little Lamb A crying child that follows you. Hit it and it shows its real face. Bloodied Wool The Hymnal Floats. Its song slows and weakens you and heals the other creepypastas. Hymnal Page The Underneath Waits buried with only its hands showing, and breathes under your bed. Grave Claw Antlerkin Imitates cows, pigs and sheep to lure prey, and at night it calls and runs its prey down. Antler Shard Heads. The first time you kill each one, it always drops its head. After that it's a 10% chance, plus 5% a level of Looting (25% with Looting III). Only a kill by a player counts, an arrow from your bow included, and in multiplayer each player gets their own first head. You need one head from each of the nine."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"Under the bed","u":"story/chapter-1.html#under-the-bed","t":"The Underneath deserves its own warning. Once the altar is awake, about four times in ten that you lie down, and always the next time after you've heard it breathing, it comes up under your bed: three knocks under the floor, then its hands feel for the edge of the mattress. The night won't pass while it's there. Get out of bed within about four seconds (Leave Bed) and it bursts up out of the floor to fight you. Stay, and its arms come up over you and it drags you down through the bed and eats you. In the dark you may see it waiting under a bed: two pale eyes and long fingers creeping out. It never comes in Creative or on Peaceful."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"The Watcher","u":"story/chapter-1.html#the-watcher","t":"The Watcher never attacks. It stares, waves, points, peeks round things, crouches, and sometimes stands right behind you. It speaks after your first kill, your fifth and your ninth, and again when the Saint rises and when it falls. you shouldn't have done that, [your name]. it was only watching you. like i do. i'll remember this. ??? after your first kill five. you're counting too, aren't you [your name]? i know where you sleep. i've known for a while. ??? after your fifth kill nine. do you know what nine heads are for? there is a church that isn't on any map. find it. i'll be on the ceiling. ??? after your ninth kill"},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"The church that isn't on any map","u":"story/chapter-1.html#the-church","t":"The church is the Cathedral of the Hollow : one per world, 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn, roughly the opposite way from the altar. It rises out of nothing once you come within about 90 blocks of where it stands, inside a walled graveyard. The Watcher hangs from the ceiling of the nave, as it said it would. In the sanctuary is the Hollow Reliquary with nine head pedestals around it. Since 1.40 there is much more underneath: an undercroft of tombs, the priest's study, a flooded charnel pit and, at its end, the Saint's tomb, empty, its chains broken."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"The Hollow Saint","u":"story/chapter-1.html#the-hollow-saint","t":"Put one head from each of the nine different creepypastas on the pedestals, then right-click the reliquary with an empty hand. The summoning takes about ten seconds: a circle of runes burns open in the floor, a beam of light streams out of every head into an orb over the reliquary, and the Saint rises up out of the ground and roars with many dead voices at once. look up. i told you i'd be here. this is what they were all pieces of. ??? as the Saint rises The full fight, its dark form and Abyssal Rupture are on the Hollow Saint's page . When it dies, the Watcher won't let it stay: its beam burns a portal to hell open under the Saint, and a huge burning hand drags it down. you did it. do you understand what you've done? they were keeping it in. it was the only thing in this world bigger than me. thank you. i'll be seeing you. all of you. i always have. ??? after \"The Hollow Saint has fallen.\""},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"What you can make","u":"story/chapter-1.html#what-you-can-make","t":"The nine's drops make the chapter's weapons and three armour sets. The Saint's own drops finish the job: its heart goes into the Saint's Requiem, and its shrouds upgrade the last armour set. Recipes are in the items section . Weapons: the Sinew Cleaver (Rend), the Antler Scythe (Reap), the Static Blade (Dead Air) and the Saint's Requiem (Last Rites), which needs the Saint's Heart. Armour: Stitchskin (Sewn Shut), Antlerbone (Night Hunter) and Static Mail (Dead Channel). Upgrade each Static Mail piece at a smithing table with a Saint's Shroud and a Hymnal Page to make the Saint's Vestments (Hollow Grace)."},{"p":"Chapter one: The Nine","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-1.html#what-comes-next","t":"Where the Saint fell, the floor tears open into a red wound standing up out of the ground. That is the Breach ."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"","u":"story/chapter-2.html","t":"When the Hollow Saint falls, the floor where it fell tears open. The creepypastas were keeping something in; now there's a hole, and it's been widening ever since. you didn't think that was the end of it, did you. when the saint fell it left a hole. it's been widening ever since. ??? after the Saint falls"},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The Breach","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-breach","t":"A red wound stands up out of the ground: black inside, its edges burning, red lightning crawling off it, ash drifting round it and the air pulling in. In a world where the Saint already fell before this was added, one tears open near you soon after you play. Walk into it."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The Void","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-void","t":"Since 1.25 the Breach lets out into its own dimension: black all round, no ground and no sky, a fog the colour of a bruise, ash and embers drifting, a drone that never stops, and things moving out in the dark. Now and then, far out, two great red eyes open and look at you. You can't sleep out here. You come out on one torn-off island: pale dead moss over an upturned crag of earth and rose stone, crystals and roots hanging off it, dead trees leaning over the edge, and the Breach Altar's shrine on top. Four more pieces of the Hollow hang in the dark round it, the Drift , each with a chest and a page, all reachable on foot: The Torn Room (east, over a sagging rope bridge): the corner of a house ripped off at the floor, the bed unmade, a table laid for two, a music box playing somewhere. The Fallen Graves (west, over stepping stones): a lump of graveyard and a little mausoleum, its coffins sticking out of the earth underneath. The Mast (south): the Broadcast's radio mast, a red aviation light blinking on top that you can see from all over the Void, and a shed with a TV still on. The Nest (north): the carcass of something huge, a ring of standing stones round a black pool, sculk over everything. The lampreys come up out of the pool. If you fall, your fall slows as if the dark thickened, and a hand bigger than a man comes up out of it, closes round you (it hurts), and sets you back down on the island you fell from. Out here you'll also meet Driftlights , harmless jellyfish of pale flesh that light the islands, and Lampreys , eyeless eels with a glowing lure that bite and try to drag you out over the dark. careful. there's no ground out here but this. this is where they came up from. the breach tore this bit off with it. and don't look too long at the dark. it looks back. ??? in the Void"},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The Breach Altar","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-breach-altar","t":"The Breach Altar is the Forsaken Altar's other half: a platform of pale rose stone, spires of pink crystal, pink candles round a pink altar with a torn eye carved in it. Wake it with an empty hand and everything turns purple: every crystal, every flame, every vein in the stone. Every creepypasta in the world is dragged back down where it came from, each one sinking into a red portal, fighting. The old haunting stops. The Watcher comes to stand behind the altar and tells you what comes up in their place, in its own way: a rabbit with an axe. a hook on the roof of your car. a butcher in a pig's face. a doll that moves when nobody looks. a scarecrow that wasn't there yesterday. red eyes on a bridge. the thirteenth child. something on two legs that should be on four. a tall glowing thing in the hills. ??? at the Breach Altar (paraphrased from the README) Once the altar is awake and you come back through, the rift turns, shudders and zips itself shut behind you for good. Anyone still out in the Void is brought home."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The killers and the things from the woods","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-killers-and-the-things-from-the-woods","t":"The new nine are five killers and four cryptids. Like the creepypastas they stalk first, at the treeline, across the water, overhead, and only come for you once they've watched long enough or you hit them. Each drops its own item and its head (always on the first kill, then 10% plus Looting). The Watcher has something to say the first time you kill each. Creature How it hunts Drops The Bunnyman A tall man in a filthy rabbit suit with a fire axe. Catch him watching and he waves. Chops through wooden doors. Anywhere in the dark, most of all near water. Bloodied Stuffing The Hookman Flings a meat hook on a chain and reels you in; pulls riders off horses, boats and carts. Rusted Hook The Hogshead A butcher in a rotting pig's head. Charges; sidestep and he stuns himself on the wall. 90 health. Flayed Hide The Porcelain Man Only moves while nobody is looking. Can only be hurt from behind. Porcelain Shards The Harvestman A scarecrow on a post in a field at night. Look away for long and the post is empty. Blighted Straw Mothman Red eyes circling in the night sky. Screeches, dives, and sometimes carries you up and lets go. Bring a bow. Moth Scales The Jersey Devil Screams, springs into the air and glides down onto you. Pine forests and woods at night. Devil's Horn Dogman Runs on all fours, stands up to howl (it roots you), pounces and mauls. Dogman's Fang The Flatwoods Monster Glides at you in a spade-shaped hood with a glowing red face, leaving a burning mist. Braxton Residue"},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The Murder Mansion","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-murder-mansion","t":"The Watcher tells you where they live. The Murder Mansion is a three-storey Second Empire house under a black mansard roof, with a turret, a widow's walk and a chimney still smoking, in its own railed yard: a fountain of blood, dead hedges, things hanging from dead trees, the family plot. Inside are a foyer with twin staircases, a dining hall laid for guests who are only skulls now, a butcher's kitchen, a nursery, a bathtub full of blood, the red room and the attic. The house's papers are where they were left. Read them in order and you learn what the Hale family did: the housekeeper's accounts, the butcher's order book, a letter never sent, a nursery rhyme that counts the nine, the guest list, a surveyor's notes, a note from the glasshouse, the red room's instructions, and the Watcher's own pages on the mending, open on the library desk. They're all on the lore page . Through the Harvest Doors is the Trophy Hall : chains and hooks out of the dark, trophies on every wall, and the Mending Altar inside a horseshoe of nine trophy pedestals."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"The Mended","u":"story/chapter-2.html#the-mended","t":"Put one head from each of the new nine on the trophy pedestals and right-click the Mending Altar with an empty hand. The Watcher comes down from the ceiling and sews. It takes about thirty seconds, and nothing can hurt the result until it stands and roars with all nine voices. The Mended is four blocks tall, 750 health, with three phases: Agony, Aggression and Iron Will. When it dies it comes apart and the nine go up out of it. It leaves the Mended Heart and the Rusted Garden Key , with iron, chains and one of each of the nine's drops."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"What you can make","u":"story/chapter-2.html#what-you-can-make","t":"Six weapons: the Bunnyman's Fire Axe (Bridge Toll), Hook and Chain (Reel), the Hogshead's Tenderizer (Tenderize), the Porcelain Needle (Unseen), the Devil's Glaive (Hellfire) and the Rending Claws (Frenzy). Three armour sets: Butcher's Garb (Slaughterhouse), Mothwing (Night Flight) and Braxton Shell (Braxton Mist). Recipes and powers are on the items page ."},{"p":"Chapter two: The Breach","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-2.html#what-comes-next","t":"The Mended's key fits the gate of the Botanic Gardens, a Victorian glasshouse that has been locked and sealed the whole time, with the jungle inside pressed up against the glass and something glowing in the middle of it. When the Mended dies, the Watcher has something to say about the glass house. Chapter three ."},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"","u":"story/chapter-3.html","t":"The Head Gardener tended the great flower under the dome for so long that it grew into him. Now he kneels at it with a root running from its heart into his face, and the flower is only a finger of something far, far bigger."},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"The Botanic Gardens","u":"story/chapter-3.html#the-botanic-gardens","t":"The Botanic Gardens are a Victorian glasshouse under a great glass dome, locked and sealed since chapter two. Bring the Mended's Rusted Garden Key to the glass doors and it turns all the way at last: the key goes in, turns hard, the padlock springs, the chain slides off and the gate swings in screaming on its hinges. The whole glasshouse breathes out spores, petals and warm air. Inside, the jungle has grown wild. Every flower does something when you brush it: the Whispering Lily says your name and the dark comes in, the Ghost Orchid fades you out, the Watching Fern's eyes open and everything sees you, the Lantern Pod lights up your eyes, the Weeping Bell weeps on you. Giant Venus flytraps grow in the beds and snatch you up and chew (mash E to force the jaws open). Burstpods go off in clouds of choking spores, and Clutchvines close on you and hold. While you walk it the place plays with you: lilies say your name, specimen jars topple off their barrels and smash, rusted sprinklers cough and spray, glass cracks overhead, a Rootling darts across the path and is gone into the ground. And while the Gardener still kneels, sometimes he isn't at his flower at all, but standing among the trees watching you, and gone when you look again."},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"What to find first","u":"story/chapter-3.html#what-to-find-first","t":"The Head Gardener's office: his journal on the lectern and a chest with his coat and breeches . The potting shed: a chest with his straw hat and boots . The Seed Vault: under a hatch at the back of the hall, with the under-gardener's ledger and the best chest in the place. A propagation house, and a pond with something at the bottom of it. Together the four pieces are the Gardener's Weeds . You will need the full set for what comes after him. If a chest was already opened, craft the set instead from Knotted Roots, which the Rootlings drop."},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"The Gardener","u":"story/chapter-3.html#the-gardener","t":"He kneels at the great flower and doesn't notice you at first. Walk softly. Go too close to him or to the flower, or strike him, and he tears loose and stands, and the gates slam shut behind you. He is slow and huge, with hedge shears as long as a man held in both hands. Keep out of reach of the shears but not so far that he lashes you in with his root arm, and step off the ground wherever earth bubbles, because thorns come up there. At half his health he drives his hands into the ground, the glasshouse answers him, and he can't be hurt while it does. After that, stay out of the pollen, kill the Rootlings he calls up, and keep moving across the lines of thorns. Full details are on the Gardener's page . When he dies he drops his shears, goes down on his knees, bows and goes down into the ground, and the great flower drags him in and eats him. He leaves the Gardener's Shears (Prune) and the Heartbloom , all that was left of the flower's heart, still beating. If everyone inside leaves or dies, he goes back to his flower healed and the gates open again."},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"The green rift","u":"story/chapter-3.html#the-green-rift","t":"Three days after the Gardener dies , by the world's clock (nights you sleep through count), a green tear opens over his withered flower under the dome. You need to be at the glasshouse, within about 80 blocks of the flower, for it to open. It looks like the Breach, but sick green, with carrion flies boiling out of it. the flower isn't dead. that thing under the glass was only a finger of it. it's opened a way down to the rest. his clothes. wear his clothes in there, or it'll be eating you before you've taken ten steps. ??? when the green rift opens"},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"The Bloom","u":"story/chapter-3.html#the-bloom","t":"Through the rift is the Bloom : a realm with no ground and no sky, green fog all the way down, and hanging in it, everything the flower has eaten. A street of Rosemont. The research station that studied it. Shelter No. 4, sunk in its island with roots through the roof. Each has a chest and a lectern with its story. The air eats you. Without the full Gardener's Weeds you're infected the moment you arrive, and after twenty seconds it starts eating you, slowly and then faster. In his clothes the flies settle and lift off again. Don't fall. Far down under the islands is the Great Bloom itself, its mouth wider than all the islands together, ring after ring of teeth turning against each other in its throat. Fall and a tentacle twenty blocks thick comes straight up after you and drags you into its mouth. this is what it ate. a street. the laboratory that studied it. a shelter full of people. it keeps them up here like a larder. and it's down there. look down. no - don't. if you fall, it catches you. it doesn't let go. ??? in the Bloom"},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"The Binding","u":"story/chapter-3.html#the-binding","t":"The stone on the island you arrive on is the Binding , and it holds the flower down. Read the plaque on the lectern beside it first. Touch the stone with an empty hand and the chains strain and it warns you. Touch it again and it breaks. The Great Bloom goes mad, thrashing and shrieking, and its tentacles come up out of the green round the island and take hold. You have ten seconds , counted down on your screen, to get back through the rift before the island's edges break away and it pulls the whole island into its mouth, rift and all. Anyone left out there is taken, one by one. the stone in the middle is what holds it down. leave it. please. no. NO - that was holding it down- the rift. RUN. ??? at the Binding"},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"It comes up the root","u":"story/chapter-3.html#it-comes-up-the-root","t":"You come out in front of the glasshouse. The ground shakes, the dome's glass starts to go, and the mound bursts. The Great Bloom rises up out of the ground as a closed bud and opens, while the whole glasshouse comes down round it, dome first, in a storm of glass and iron. It takes the gardens' place for good. Its tentacles reach for anything within about 26 blocks, players first, and its flies infect anyone near it who isn't wearing the Gardener's clothes. Since 1.38, what it swallows goes down alive into its stomach . you broke it. it's coming up the root. get away from the glass house. get AWAY. that's it. that's the real one. ??? as the Great Bloom rises"},{"p":"Chapter three: The Glasshouse","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-3.html#what-comes-next","t":"Ten seconds after the Great Bloom rises through the glasshouse, the ground east of the gardens shakes and splits. Chapter four ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"","u":"story/chapter-4.html","t":"Ten seconds after the Great Bloom rises, a column of raw muscle forty blocks high punches up out of the ground east of the gardens, sheds its skin, and opens a slit of teeth down its front. It is what the great flower was holding down. It is also the flower's own doing. This chapter is the longest. The mod calls its first half \"Phase Two\" and its second half \"the end of it\"."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Flesh wakes","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-flesh-wakes","t":"A title card reads THE FLESH WAKES , and under it, the flower made it . The red Flesh is the rot the great flower's carrion flies carry, grown in the dark under Rosemont until the Great Bloom rose and let it up. It hates what made it all the same. that's not the flower. that's what the flower made. it came out of the flower's rot - and it hates what made it. it'll eat this whole world to get at them. and it's coming out of the ground. run. ??? as the Flesh wakes It spreads outward from where it came up, further every day: grass and soil turn to meat, stone and brick go veined and lit red from inside, trees to sinew, glass to membrane. Where it has taken the land the fog goes the colour of meat. That land, its infection and Bloom Serum are covered on the red fog page . It holds about 1000 blocks round where it came up, and 2000 once the Bloom has changed."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"Three pieces of a reactor","u":"story/chapter-4.html#three-pieces","t":"Once Rosemont stands, the Watcher tells you there's a way to kill the big one: the Laboratory's reactor, in three pieces. A tracker at the top of your screen counts them (0/3). Each part is the only one there is: lose it and it goes back where you found it (the Rear Assembly a minute later). The Rear and Front Assemblies won't go into anything but the Assembly Cradle. there's a way to kill the big one. the laboratory's reactor. three pieces. the laboratory, the shelter, and a truck in the city. ??? once Rosemont is built"},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"Rosemont: the Rear Assembly","u":"story/chapter-4.html#rosemont","t":"Rosemont, the broken city , goes down a few hundred blocks from the gardens: six streets of cracked asphalt and abandoned cars, the police precinct, the corner pharmacy, the bus station, an eight-floor apartment block with its floors rotted through, a sinkhole forty blocks deep where the Bloom bit the street off, and in the middle the plaza the army turned into an evacuation checkpoint. The Rear Assembly sits in the army's Military Cradle on the back of the truck in the plaza, under a lock that takes an axe: three blows, each one setting the mechanism winding for ten seconds and each one bringing more of them over the sandbags. Car alarms call every infected within 48 blocks, rotten floors give way a second after they creak, and pools of the Flesh drag at your feet. The commuters on the crashed bus are fused into one thing that wears the bus as a shell. The Congregation (400 health) sleeps in the road until something hits it."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Laboratory: the Reactor Core","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-laboratory","t":"The Rosemont Botanical Research Laboratory goes down on the other side of the gardens: a white building above ground and two sublevels under it. You need a Level 2 Keycard (the director kept one in his locked desk: three good blows split the drawer). The airlock's lockers hold hazmat suits. Six tapes tell you what happened, what is in the pool and what it hates. The director's last tape gives the order of the three coolant levers , which is different in every world. In the reactor hall the Reactor Core sits in its rack over the pool. Hold use on the rack for three seconds and it's yours, and the pool turns to blood and Specimen Zero wakes (350 health): the night technician who cut a sample from the root's end. Burn the staff's bodies first, because it eats them to heal. When it dies the Laboratory locks itself down: ninety seconds to get out of the sublevels. The tapes are transcribed on Tapes and broadcasts ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"Shelter No. 4: the Front Assembly","u":"story/chapter-4.html#shelter-no-4","t":"Rosemont's Civil Defence shelter goes down south of the gardens where the ground allows: a fenced park, a blockhouse with its blast door jammed half open, and stairs down into the dark. There's no power. The fuel for the two generators in the radio room is wedged in the back of one of the shelter's lockers, a different one in every world, and most of the residents are hiding in those lockers, sobbing. With both generators running, the radio's evacuation notice turns into Control's emergency broadcast and Bunker B 's blast door opens. The special forces squad sent to hold it is still holding it, their guns grown into their arms. The Front Assembly is on the dais at the far end. Lift it, and the north wall tears itself out: the Warden of Shelter No. 4 . Kill the Warden and the Watcher leaves you a Civil Defence Compass on the dais, its needle set on Rosemont."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Rosemont Device","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-rosemont-device","t":"With the Rear Assembly, the Core and the Front Assembly clamped into the Assembly Cradle (in that order), hold use on the cradle with an empty hand for five seconds. The harness goes on, the wiring runs from rear to front, the Core lights blue-white and the strapped-on Geiger counter starts to tick. It is the Rosemont Device now, and there is only one. Since 1.43.1 there's another way: bring all three parts to a Forsaken Altar and the Watcher takes you to your cradle, puts a bubble of cold light round you, and builds the Device in front of you. that's it. that's a bomb. the flesh knows what it's for. it'll let you through while you carry it. take it to the bloom. to what's left of the glass house. ??? once the Device is wired Carrying it gives you Slowness II, no running and no gliding. While you carry it the Flesh lets you through: its infected stop, turn to watch you pass and step out of your way (hit one and the truce is off for fifteen seconds). The Bloom's things come for you instead. Within 200 blocks of the risen Bloom its roots crack up out of the ground after you, and its music, The Approach, comes up under everything."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Gardener, reborn twice","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-gardener-reborn","t":"Within 32 blocks, the Bloom goes still and turns every petal on the Device. Then it gags, heaves and spits the Gardener back up in a gush of nectar, his body knitting itself together with vines. It folds its petals shut and a ring of thorned roots six blocks high comes up round the arena. The Gardener, Reborn has 600 health, three phases and the Bloomshears. Since 1.40 he comes back once more: kill him and the Bloom grows him back as the Gardener, Reborn Again , faster and harder. Kill him the second time and the Watcher rips the portal into the Bloom open."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The launch","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-launch","t":"Every sound drops out except footsteps. The Watcher steps out from right behind you, walks to the shut Bloom, pushes its fingers between two petals and pulls until they tear away and the green rift flares open, wider than before. Then it looks straight at you, and it's gone. The rift comes out on a ledge, what's left of the Binding's island, hanging over the colossal Bloom's mouth, its tentacles hanging over it, held back. At the far end is the Launch Mark , and the Device goes nowhere else (set it down anywhere else and you're told \"Not here. The edge.\"). On the mark it unfolds into a missile. Hold use on it for three seconds to arm it, then run: ten seconds to get back through the rift. take it through. put it down past the edge. then run. don't look at them. i've got them. i can't hold them long. and then you run. you don't stop, and you don't look back. ??? on the ledge Putting the Device into the Great Bloom earns Not Collected : \"It's still beating.\""},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"It changed","u":"story/chapter-4.html#it-changed","t":"Since 1.40, the camera is taken the moment nobody is left in the Bloom. You watch the Device burst up out of the rift and climb over the Bloom, the Bloom catch it with a tentacle and drag it down its throat, and the Watcher on the crater's rim pour its darkness into a beam. The Device goes off inside it. Everything goes white. Out of the white the sky opens, a column of light comes down on the Bloom, and it changes. A title card reads IT CHANGED : and its roar went all the way round the world . i knew it would do that. the bomb was never going to kill it. i needed it to change. bigger. a soul that size is worth something. but my darkness isn't enough for it now. i need a stronger soul to pour it through. ??? after the Bloom changes The changed Bloom is ten times bigger, its flesh gone blue, its acid purple, its teeth green, sunk in a pit it tears out of the ground. It reaches for anything within ninety blocks, and its roar can be heard from anywhere in the world. Over three days its blight grows out from it: blue flesh where the grass was, blisters of acid, green teeth up out of the ground, a violet haze over all of it. Since 1.42 it grows on what it eats, up to three times the size it changed to, and gets worse the longer it goes without. See the Bloom's page ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The end of it","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-end-of-it","t":""},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"A gun above the sky","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-power-source","t":"there's a gun up above the sky. they built it before the city fell. they never got to fire it. it needs a power source. three places woke up when the bloom changed. what you need is in them. build the core. bring it to the forsaken altar, and i'll put my magic into it. then we kill it. ??? after the Bloom changes Three places wake 300 to 1000 blocks from the gardens, and the Watcher gives everyone a needle for each. A tracker counts THE POWER SOURCE (0/3) : The Uplink Station , where the garrison talked to the gun over the sky: the Targeting Array is in the locker by the consoles. The Capacitor Works , still holding its charge, with arcs jumping between the lightning rods and a notice that says DANGER - LIVE BANKS : the Capacitor Cell is in the test cage at the back. The Soul Well , a shaft thirty blocks down with its keepers kneeling round the altar at the bottom: the Bound Soul . Make the Orbital Core from the three, iron and redstone, and set it on a Forsaken Altar. The Watcher pours itself into it and gives it back infused . Build the Orbital Railgun round it. Its strikes call down a slug from SENTINEL, the gun above the sky: sixty damage, fire and a shockwave out to twelve blocks. See the power source parts ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Ray Gun and the Omni","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-ray-gun","t":"The railgun's strikes make the changed Bloom scream, but it heals as fast as you tear it. Building the railgun wakes three more places: ...did you hear that. it's calling something up out of the ground. the gun can hurt it. it can't end it. what can end it is in what it's calling up. ??? once the railgun is built Ashford Nuclear Plant , its reactor never gone cold: the Nuclear Reactor Core , in the fuel pool (don't go in the water without a suit). Meridian Laboratory , its arcs jumping: the Discharge Destabilizer , in the glass cell in the middle of the ring. Blackwater Station , an island lab out at sea where something got loose: the Vial of Dark Matter Blood , and the parasites . Craft the Ray Gun round the railgun and the three parts, or bring them all to a Forsaken Altar and the Watcher builds it. Either way the Watcher wants it (\"give it here\"). Drop it near him or use it on him, and he gives you back the Omni Orbital Railgun ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"The Omni Ray","u":"story/chapter-4.html#the-omni-ray","t":"Stand fifty blocks or more off the changed Bloom's mouth, aim the Omni at the flower and fire. The camera is taken: SENTINEL comes down out of its orbit, a star that moves, then a fireball, then a sonic boom and retro thrusters. Five rings of glyphs close in round the line down to its mouth, TARGET LOCKED, and it fires. The Bloom fires back. If it has eaten too much, the Watcher gives the beam all of its own power. A title card reads THE OMNI RAY : the bloom is dead. the watcher rests. What's left is a husk. The blight dies back, and so does the Flesh, everywhere but the places it built itself into. i need time to rest. this took too much power. but when i come back with our work, i'll be ten times stronger. thanks to you. i will repay you. but for now, i must rest. ??? after the Omni Ray"},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"Not so fast","u":"story/chapter-4.html#not-so-fast","t":"The first time you carry the Omni off the Bloom's blight, the Watcher is in your way. It pulls the gun out of your hands, tears open a rift into its own realm, and throws the gun in. The first time anyone puts a Ray Gun together in a crafting grid afterwards, it's there at the table and burns the recipe out of every recipe book. The Mended guns, which are the Bloom's flesh, rot and jam once it's dead. wait. not so fast. it wouldn't be fair to let you take such a destructive toy with you, to use on everything. from what i see, i see great power. great potential. but zero responsibility for life. i can see the thoughts in your head, you know. ??? taking the Omni back"},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"Ten days later","u":"story/chapter-4.html#ten-days-later","t":"Ten days later by the world's clock, the Watcher comes back, rested, and finds you wherever you are. In your house it bangs on the window and then comes in, by the door, which creaks open on its own, or through the wall where the glass is. Down a mine it folds itself down the tunnel, and anything there trying to kill you bursts into ink. In the woods its head leans out from behind a tree. Anywhere else, it's right behind you, breathing, until you turn round. This earns the advancement Ten Days Later . ten days. i'm rested now - stronger, like i said i'd be. but i didn't come to talk about me. it's the parasites. the infection in those new places - blackwater - it isn't from here. it came into this realm from another one. the null static zone. the flesh is dying back. with the flower dead it's got nothing to grow from. they don't need the flower. they'll get into anything with blood in it - a cow, a horse, a villager. you won't see it often. but if something you know starts acting wrong, don't let it near you. keep your eyes open. ??? ten days later"},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"While the Flesh spreads","u":"story/chapter-4.html#while-the-flesh-spreads","t":"Through all of this chapter, the Flesh keeps making things worse: Mutations. Left alive on its ground for ten minutes (five on the thickest of it), one of the infected changes into a Stalker, a Bloater, a Screamer, a Brute, a Splitter or a Hive, depending on what it was. The nests. Where the Flesh has had the land long enough, the ground sinks into a bowl and grows the Flesh's own great flower, the Broodmother (340 health), with rows of brood sacs round her. The horde. Some nights, ten to eighteen of its dead climb out of the ground together and walk to you behind a Bellwether ringing its bell. Kill the Bellwether and the horde loses its way. Sapromyiophilous. The flower's flies can lay in you. At level III you turn, and what gets up where you fell is you , wearing your armour and carrying everything you had. Kill it to get it all back. Swallowed alive. What the Great Bloom eats goes down alive into its stomach. Cut the stomach wall ten times and it throws you back up. Every one of these is in the bestiary ."},{"p":"Chapter four: The Flesh","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-4.html#what-comes-next","t":"With the Bloom dead, the Flesh has nothing to grow from and dies back. But the parasites don't need the flower, and the static isn't noise. Chapter five ."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"","u":"story/chapter-5.html","t":"The Bloom is dead and the Flesh dies back with it. But the parasites came into this realm from another one, and they're still out there. When they talk to each other, it sounds like static. Chapter Five arrived in six parts, from 1.44.0 to 1.54.0: The Static , The Relay , The Null , The Null Static Zone (1.47.1 added the late show), The Hive and The Deep . It starts once the Bloom is dead and ends when the Chorus, whole, dies in the Warm Heart. Between the parts, 1.48.0 to 1.52.0 turned the parasite into an outbreak: from Chapter Five on, anything at all can carry one."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part one: the static","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-static","t":""},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Static Hounds","u":"story/chapter-5.html#static-hounds","t":"What the parasites made of the wolves: starved to a frame, mangy, black chitin up through the spine, two violet pinpricks for eyes, and a muzzle that splits open into petals round a throat of teeth. At night, now and then, a pack of three to five comes out of the dark behind a Pack Leader with a brood sac on its back. The leader comes at you head on while the rest go wide and come in from your sides and behind. Seeing you, the leader howls , a wolf's howl breaking up into radio static, and the pack runs faster and bites harder for a while (and you're weak for a few seconds). Any of them lunges the last few blocks, and their bites make you bleed. Kill the leader and its sac tears open, one of them comes out, and the pack breaks and scatters, yelping."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"One of them in you","u":"story/chapter-5.html#one-of-them-in-you","t":"A Parasite that holds on at the back of your neck for the whole four seconds gets in. Crouch, or get hit, to tear it off before then. If it gets in, its brood grows in you over about three days of play, and a meter beside your hotbar fills: How far grown What happens From the start You get hungrier. A quarter You can feel the others. Parasites, hounds, the Hollowed and anything with a brood in it show through walls to you, violet, and static comes off you. Two fifths You're stronger and faster. And starving. Half The sac shows on your back, and it has fits: you can hardly move for a second or two. Three quarters It's too big to burn out. Full It bursts out of your back: 7 hearts, bleeding, and two of them come out. Get it out first. A Surgical Kit cuts it out of you (or out of someone else, or an animal). Or burn it out : stand in fire long enough to be hurt, before it's three quarters grown. A Hush kills one outright."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Hollowed","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-hollowed","t":"In every village, one villager isn't one any more. Its eyes are two violet pinpricks; it mutters, and what comes out is static; it watches you. Wear the Dead Channel Helm , or have a brood in you a quarter grown, and you can see the static coming off it. At night, alone with it, no other villager near, it turns: it shakes, straightens up taller than it was, its folded arms come apart and hang to its knees, and its head splits open into four, like the parasite's mouth. Hurt it and it turns there and then. Turned, it comes for you and the rest of its village: it shrieks (the noise roots you to the spot), rakes and grabs, and sometimes puts one in you. Killed, a parasite crawls out of its throat, unless it burnt."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The outbreak","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-outbreak","t":"Since 1.48.0 the parasite doesn't just brood in what it gets into and burst out. It takes it over , slowly, and then the creature is theirs. Any creature can carry it: the game's own animals, villagers and monsters, the golems, the warden, the Hollow's own things (but not the parasite's own, not the Flesh's, and not you; for you there's the brood above). It takes two days of the world's clock for an ordinary creature and three for the hard ones. You can watch it happen: a twitch now and then, violet veins under the skin, the first blisters, shaking fits, growths and chitin forcing out through its back, its head hanging to one side. Nearly gone, it stands and stares at you, and goes for you if you're close in the dark. Then the turn : five seconds of it seizing up and screaming, and it tears open into one of theirs. Turned, it hunts everything that isn't one of them, and what it hits it might put a parasite into. Killed, it bursts and its parasites come out, unless it burnt. A Surgical Kit cuts one out of anything before it turns. The parasite comes in kinds now too, each born of where it was (in the water, deep underground, out of anything with wings, in the Nether, in the End), and it leaves heaps of biomass that get up again as its pure forms . The Hollow's own creatures, bosses included, each turn into something new. All of it is on the turned and the Parasite ."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part two: the relay","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-relay","t":"do you hear it. under the static. it isn't noise. they're talking to each other. something's carrying it. this points to where. ??? handing out a needle to Relay 6 What one of them hears, all of them hear, and something is carrying it: Relay 6 on Hollow Ridge , the county's emergency-broadcast relay, 300 to 1000 blocks out. While it's on the air, static pours off the top of its forty-block mast and hound packs come twice as often within 700 blocks of it. At the mast's foot is the Amalgam : everyone who came to the relay, the operator, his dog and the people from the valley, grown together into one heap. Lashed to the mast on each rest platform is a tether , a knot of sinew with a cable running down to it. Climb the ladder and cut all three, then kill it. The relay goes off the air , the hounds near it lose the signal and run, and from then on packs come less often everywhere. It leaves the Relay Core . Hold it to your ear and you're Tuned In for thirty seconds. Keep it: it'll be wanted."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part three: the Null","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-null","t":"the relay's quiet. the static isn't gone. it's going somewhere. there's a place it all runs down into. like water. this points to it. ??? once the relay is off the air With the relay quiet, the last of their static runs down into the Starlite Drive-In , 300 to 1000 blocks out. Its screen is dark until somebody steps inside the fence. Then the late show plays: a relay slams home somewhere, the lamp strikes, the screen floods with static that pours off its face into a tear in the ground, and five figures peel off the picture and come up the lot for you. they came out of the picture. they always do, when somebody's watching. you can't hurt them yet. they're not all the way here. the core. hold it to your ear - tuned in, they're as real as you are. or let one reach for you. when it does, it's all the way here. hit it then. kill one and it leaves a frame of the picture behind. four frames. the projector's up in the booth. run the reel. see what's under all of it. ??? during the late show Within forty blocks of the tear you're Nulled : the colour goes out of everything, static creeps in at the edges of your sight, the fog closes in grey, and you go hungry faster. The figures are Afterimages , what's left of the people who stayed in their cars after the reel. Each one you kill leaves a Frame of the Last Reel . The last reel: load four frames into the projector in the booth, with the Relay Core on you to tune it. It runs seventy seconds in five parts. Afterimages come out of the picture for the booth (more of them with more of you there), and while the reel runs anyone can hurt them. One that reaches the projector jumps the film back ten seconds; leave the booth and the reel runs out. Hold them off to the end and the last frame burns on the screen, what's under all of it, and the reel is yours. you saw it. that's what's under all of it. that's where they come from. it was carrying them. the way the relay was. only it's alive. keep the reel. ??? after the last reel"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part four: the Null Static Zone","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-null-static-zone","t":"Hold the Last Reel up over the tear at the drive-in. The static runs backwards off it into the tear, and its bottom goes to a pool of static: a rift. Step in. The Null Static Zone is where everything that ever went into the static ran down to: a grey plain under no sky, grey fog, ash and static on the wind, voices a long way off. You come out on a landing among the things it took, cars, television sets, a radio mast bent double, and the rift there takes you home whenever you like. You're Nulled the whole time, and you can't sleep there. Out on the plain are the Ancient Null Ruins : the Listening Stones, the Sunken Choir and the Hush, built by the people who were here the last time the static came. the null static zone. everything that went into the static came here. it's in the middle. its threads go up to every mast you ever saw. cut them. ??? in the Null Static Zone"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Carrier","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-carrier","t":"In the crater in the middle of the Zone is what carried them all: the Carrier , a head the size of a house with one eye in it, on a neck up out of a coil of its own pale body. Its threads go up off the coil into the dark, and four of them run to the four black spires round the crater's rim, tied off in a knot on top of each. While a thread holds, it shrugs off most of what you do to it. Climb the spires, break the knots, and it's cut loose: furious, and far easier to hurt."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Signing off","u":"story/chapter-5.html#signing-off","t":"Kill it and it goes down across its coil, its threads coming down out of the dark one by one. Then the Watcher comes for its eye, tears a rift of its own and sends everyone home. Six seconds after you're back, the title card: CHAPTER FIVE , with SIGNING OFF under it. it's dead. good. it wasn't theirs, you know. it was a carrier. it carried whatever was put on it. the static was a door. and this was holding it open. this, i'll keep. for the future. go home. there's nothing on the air now. ??? signing off At the drive-in the screen goes black for the first time, and then shows one line: SIGNING OFF. The Null goes out of the lot, and the static is gone: no more hound packs at night, and the Hollowed in the villages are only villagers again. The Carrier leaves 6 to 10 Carrier Threads, some of its flesh, and a record, Signing Off . SIGNING OFF"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"After signing off","u":"story/chapter-5.html#after-signing-off","t":"The title card reads CHAPTER FIVE over SIGNING OFF . Half a minute after you're home from the Null Static Zone, the Watcher comes to wherever you're standing, and he isn't pleased. ...this was unexpected. but we can work with it. we'll make do. it seems the carrier did what it was supposed to do. it carried them - all the way out. the parasites are increasing. every one of them hostile. the numbers are going off the charts. in your world. it's dangerous out there. more than ever, now. there's nothing we can do about it for now. just try not to die. for me. in the meantime. and i suggest you don't go to the end. ...actually. i'll make sure you can't go there. it's dangerous for you, player. you know i can see you right now, right, [your name]? remember who you work for. ??? half a minute after signing off From then on the outbreak is worse: the parasite gets into things half again as often, and more of its kinds turn up round you, more of them at once. And the End is shut . Anyone who goes through an End portal in Survival is sent straight back out of it to their bed or the world's spawn (\"The way's shut. He shut it.\"), and he has a word for you: \"no. i said not there.\" the first time, and \"not there. i told you.\" after that."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part five: the Hive","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-hive","t":"The static is gone, and the parasite, which used to hear itself in the static, all of it at once, has gone deaf. So it's growing itself a mind. Somewhere 300 to 1000 blocks from the gardens, it takes a hamlet whole and grows the Hive out of it: a crater of violet flesh, the cottages and their bell tower grown over, ribs arching over everything, and a pit in the middle with four stalks round it, a nerve node on top of each."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"It Speaks","u":"story/chapter-5.html#it-speaks","t":"The first night after the Hive has grown, wherever you are out under the open sky, the camera is taken. The ground heaves round you, five of the parasite's pure forms stand up out of it in a ring, turn their heads to you all together, and it speaks through all of them at once, its voices out of step: the Chorus we were many. we were scattered. we heard each other in the noise. the Chorus you cut the throat that carried us. now there is only quiet. the Chorus so we are growing another way to be one. out of all of them. out of everything they knew. the Chorus come and see what we are becoming. come and be heard. Then they fold back into the ground, and the Watcher is beside you. it lost its voice when the carrier died. so it's growing itself a mind instead. out of everything it took. every body. every face. everything any of them ever knew. when it's finished it won't need the static to talk to them. it'll just be all of them. this points to where it's growing. go before it wakes up all the way. ??? handing out a needle to the Hive"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Hive","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-hive-itself","t":"The ground at the Hive is \"warm, and soft, and it gives under you. Something under it is breathing.\" Somebody got there first: Fr. Aldous Mercer's journal is on a lectern by what's left of a cottage, with his chest beside it (what he brought for the fire). Seven Hive Hands stand round the pit: arms as tall as trees, a palm with eyes and a mouth at the top and three hooked fingers. Get within reach and they slam down where the ground lights up violet, sweep you aside, or grab you, lift you over the Hive and throw you. They can be killed (fire hurts them more), but while the Chorus is in its pit the Hive grows a dead hand back after five minutes. it took them whole. the people, the houses. everything they knew is in that pit now. it thinks with those, on the stalks round the pit. cut them and it can't think straight. there was a priest here. read him. ??? the first time anyone reaches the Hive"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Mind","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-mind","t":"Go to the edge of the pit and its floor splits. The Chorus comes up out of it: a mound of everything it took, a great head with a split maw down the middle, faces all over it, arms ending in hooks. Its faces open their eyes, and it knows you: the Chorus you. we know you. you were in the static with us. you were loud. the Chorus we do not need a throat now. we have a thousand mouths, and all of them are listening. the Chorus the ones you lost are here with us. they are singing. would you like to hear them? the Chorus come down. be heard. be one more voice. The Hive The Chorus's bar is up; its black Hive Hands stand round the pit. The fight (900 health, its own bar and music) never leaves the pit. It sends tendrils up under you (the ground churns first: move), lets out clouds of spores, gives birth to pure forms, slams an arm down, sings in three swells, each worse than the last, and draws through the cords to its nodes to heal. It's hard to hurt unless its maw is open or you've torn its nerve nodes open. Climb the steps round the four stalks and break the glowing nodes: each one makes it scream and makes it easier to hurt (\"It screams - and it can't think straight any more. Everything gets through now.\" once all four are gone). Fire hurts it more. If nobody's near and it hasn't been hurt for half a minute, it mends."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"It Runs","u":"story/chapter-5.html#it-runs","t":"Bring it down to a quarter and it won't die. It screams and tears itself down through the floor of its pit, deep, and its nodes burst. the Chorus no. no - not yet. we are not finished. it ran. it can do that now. it's got enough of a mind to be afraid. it's gone down. deep. where everything went before the static was ever a noise. that's a piece of it. it still talks. keep it - listen to it. it'll tell you where it went. it'll come back up. bigger. and next time it won't be half finished. ??? on the rim of the empty pit It leaves pieces of itself on the floor of the pit: Chorus Fragments , one for each of you. They still talk. Hold one to your ear. Four advancements come out of this part: It Speaks , The Hive , Senseless (all four nodes) and It Ran ."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Part six: the Deep","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-deep","t":"It isn't dead. It went down, and now you go after it."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The hunt","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-hunt","t":"The Chorus Fragment still hears the rest of it. Hold it to your ear and turn round: facing the right way it whispers clearly, and what it says tells you how far (\"down. a long way down. far from here - that way.\" when it's more than 600 blocks off, then \"that way. under the hills. we can feel you coming.\", \"closer. we can hear you walking. we can hear your heart.\" and finally \"here. right under you. come down. it's warm.\"). Side on, it's faint and broken (\"...colder... no... turn...\"). Facing away, only static."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Sinkhole","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-sinkhole","t":"It leads you to the Sinkhole , 300 to 1000 blocks from the gardens: a farm's low field pulled down from underneath into a crater thirty-odd yards across, steam coming off its floor, the barn tipped over the edge, the fences snapped at the rim. The county surveyor's camp is on the north rim (his notes, his kit), and his last page is halfway down. In the floor is the Burrow , a tunnel round as a pipe and lined with the Hive's flesh, going down in six turns like a corkscrew to a chamber at the bottom. In that chamber's floor is the Throat , a puckered ring of flesh. Stand on it: it stirs (\"It feels you standing on it.\"), opens, and takes you down. That's Warmer for finding the Sinkhole and Down Where It Is Warm for going down. this is where it went down. the ground didn't fall in. it was pulled. someone measured it before you. he went down after it. the piece of it you've got will tell you how far down it goes. ??? the first time anyone reaches the Sinkhole"},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"It comes back up","u":"story/chapter-5.html#it-comes-back-up","t":"Until it's dead, the world up top feels it. Tremors go under you every so often. The ground gives way near you (natural ground only, never your builds): a pit lined with its flesh with its things climbing out, which heals over after five minutes. Flesh blisters swell up out of the ground; break one before it bursts or its forms come out. And every few nights, where you live, comes the Reach : three tremors, each closer, then the ground splits and one of the Chorus's hands tears up out of it, half again as big as the Hive's, with waves of its things climbing out after it (\"IT COMES UP\", its own bar and music). Kill it for It Came Up . Leave it, and after four minutes it sinks back down."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"Down in the Deep","u":"story/chapter-5.html#down-in-the-deep","t":"You come out in the Gullet , a chamber of flesh with a Throat in its floor that takes you back up. \"It's warm down here. It's always been warm down here.\" The Deep is a dimension of its own: huge warm caverns under everything, with seas of blood at the bottom. The Warm Dark is the Hive's flesh grown over the rock. In the Root Hollows the Bloom's roots hang down through the roofs. The Old Halls are the pale worked stone of whoever was down there first. You can't sleep there (\"You can't sleep down here. Something is always listening.\"). If you're carrying a fragment, it whispers: \"home. we are home. come and find us. we are deeper.\" Two places to look for: Low Marrow , a hamlet the ground opened under one night, pulled down whole into a cavern of its own, its cottages tipped over and half sunk in a lake that isn't water any more and its church upended in the middle (the reeve and the priest both wrote down why); and the Old Halls, at the end of a road of way-stones (squat columns with a spiral cut in them like an ear and an ember cap burning on top) that starts at the Gullet."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The older ones","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-older-ones","t":"Something was down there first, and it hates the Chorus as much as it hates you. The Listeners can't see you. They hear you: every step, every block broken or set, every door, every mouthful. A Listener goes to the sound fast and rakes whatever's there. Sneak and it can't hear you walk; throw something and it goes to where it lands. They nest in the root hollows and hunt the Chorus's forms too. Stitch two of their ears over leather boots (with string) for Hushed Boots and walk as quietly as sneaking ( Not a Sound ). The Deaf King is the oldest thing in the Deep, the one that carved the Old Halls. Long ago it drove a plug of stone into each ear so it wouldn't hear the Chorus singing. It can't hear or see you; it feels you through the floor. Stand still and you aren't there. It sits on its dais at the end of the Old Halls. Kill it ( Stand Still ) and its crown cracks off and leaves the King's Ear-Stones . Carry them into the last fight."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"The Warm Heart","u":"story/chapter-5.html#the-warm-heart","t":"Follow the fragment to where the Chorus went to ground (\"here. we are right here. we are finished growing.\"): a great round chamber, its floor of flesh running down to a lake of blood under a vault of chitin ribs, with four nerve nodes on their stalks round the shore. Come down into it and the Chorus, whole rises out of the blood, made again from everything it took, with a second pair of arms and the Bloom's roots run all through it. \"Up out of the blood it comes - whole again, and every voice in it singing.\" It fights in three parts. First as it did in its pit, harder, with its nodes and its hands round the shore. At two thirds the walls crack and the older ones break in : the Listeners come through for it, its things and you, and its song gets worse (carry the King's Ear-Stones and the song can't get into you at all). With a third left it tears itself up out of its lake , ripping out its cords as it goes: no nodes any more, everything it has, as fast as it can. Then it dies. Really, this time: every voice in it goes quiet one after another and it sinks into the blood. \"Far below, the singing stops. It doesn't start again.\" Everything of its in the chamber falls apart and the world above stops feeling it. See the Chorus for the whole fight. Out of it comes the Last Voice , the one voice it couldn't swallow, still trying to tell you something ( The Last Voice ). A while later, someone else has something to say to whoever was there: it's quiet down there now. i can hear you breathing. you've got something of it. one voice it couldn't swallow. keep it. there's a door at the end of the world with a seal on it. i made that seal. i can't open it. that voice can. when you're ready, take it to the end. ??? after the Chorus, whole, is dead Hold the Last Voice up and it talks too: \"...there's a door. at the end. he sealed it...\", \"...take me to the end of the world. i'll open it for you...\", \"...the one in the black coat knows. ask him what he locked up...\". Its lines are collected on Tapes and broadcasts ."},{"p":"Chapter five: The Static","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-5.html#what-comes-next","t":"The story's music changes to Quiet Now , the Lullaby's tune in a major key. But the Watcher has just told you he sealed something, and the Last Voice wants to be carried to it. Take it into the End: that's Chapter Six: The Door at the End of the World ."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"","u":"story/chapter-6.html","t":"He shut the End after the Carrier died. Now you know why he'd want to. Out past the obsidian there's a door he made, and a seal he put on it with his own hands, and the one voice the Chorus couldn't swallow knows how to open it. Chapter Six came in three parts, 1.56.0 to 1.58.0. The mod's title cards call them The Door at the End of the World - Part One: The Audience , Part Two: The Watcher's Vault and Part Three: What He Kept Out . It starts once the Chorus, whole, is dead and you're holding the Last Voice ."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The seal","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-seal","t":"Carry the Last Voice into the End. The Watcher can't keep you out of it any more. The voice talks first (\"...here. it's here. can you feel it? something on the other side is listening...\" and then \"...hold me up. here. he made this seal with his own hands. i can open it...\"), and something cracks all the way across the End's sky and stays cracked: \"Something cracks, all the way across the End's sky - and stays cracked. The seal he put on it is broken.\" He says one word. ...don't. ??? as the seal breaks That's The Door at the End of the World . From then on the End is open to everyone, as it was. Since 1.61.1 the dragon waiting there is always the Infested Ender Dragon , so come ready for it. Since 1.60.2, the first time anyone's in the End the island's ground over the obsidian platform gives way into a shaft up to the sky, so you don't arrive shut in end stone. Out past the obsidian, a causeway of seal-stone (black, his glyphs cut into it, a few still faintly lit) runs east over the void to an island. On the island is the Door : a frame of seal-stone taller than a house with nothing in it but humming static. The voice tells you where: \"...there. out past the obsidian. a door. go through it. i'll be quiet now...\""},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Part one: the Audience","u":"story/chapter-6.html#part-one-the-audience","t":"Walk into the static. It takes you to the Stalls : an old picture house's seats out in the open in the dark, row after row of them in long curves, every one facing the Great Screen. The screen is two hundred feet wide, its curtains drawn back, and between the static it plays the story so far, frame by frame. Behind the seats are the lot, wrecked cars, speaker posts and the projection booth on its tower. \"Rows and rows of seats in the dark, every one of them facing a screen. Some of them are taken.\" You can't sleep there (\"Not here. Not with them watching.\"), and the way home is the Door behind you. That's Take Your Seat . If you're still carrying the Last Voice, it has one more thing to say as you come in: \"...shh. don't wake them. they're watching...\""},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Keep quiet","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-audience","t":"The Audience. Forty of the seats are taken by grey people in grey clothes, faces turned up to the screen, a ticket in their laps. They don't look round, but they hear you: a step near them, a block broken, a door. Then they get up, slowly, a finger to their lips, and come and hold you where you are. Sneak and they can't hear you walk. Lose them and they go back and sit down. Some of them have a Ticket Stub . The Ushers. Four of them walk the aisles with lamps, tall, too thin, maroon uniforms, white gloves and no face. An Usher sees, it doesn't hear, so sneaking won't help. If its lamp finds you (\"The Usher's lamp is on you.\") it puts a finger to where its lips should be, the SHHH goes through the house, and everyone sitting near you gets up. Then it comes for you, bashing you with the lamp, and if it gets hold of your collar it walks you back up the aisle toward the Door. Show one a Ticket Stub (use it on the Usher) and it tears it in two and looks away: for a minute its lamp doesn't see you. Now and then one drops its lamp. The Usher's Lamp. Held, it lights the dark round you. Use it and it flashes: Audience and Ushers caught in the flash reel with their hands over their faces for a few seconds. It needs eight seconds to warm again."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The Crowd","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-crowd","t":"Step out onto the front aisle under the screen and \"The picture on the screen is you.\" Every one of the Audience gets up (the Last Voice, if you have it: \"...they're getting up. all of them...\") and comes down to the front, into one heap, and it stands up: the Crowd , three men high, two great arms made of people and a knot of faces on top, every one of them looking at you. It doesn't leave the front. It reaches across the front rows, slams both arms down (jump the ring), applauds (each clap a wall of air) and sheds people who get up and come for you. From two thirds down comes the Hush (\"Quiet, please.\"): for four seconds anyone who moves or strikes is grabbed by hands up out of the floor. Stand still ( Quiet, Please ), or flash an Usher's Lamp at it to break the Hush. In its last third it roars with every mouth at once. Dead, it comes apart into the people it was, they come apart into static, and the screen goes dark ( Standing Ovation ). \"Something's left in the middle of where it stood: a ticket. It's warm.\" That's the Last Ticket , one for everyone who was there."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Front Row","u":"story/chapter-6.html#front-row","t":"The screen is dark and the house is empty, but one seat in the front row is still taken. It's the Watcher. it was a good show. you weren't meant to see the end of it. you want to know what i locked up. come and see, then. ??? in the front row He gets up, goes to the screen, puts his hand on it and tears it open, and goes through. It closes behind him to a seam of light down the middle: \"There's a seam of light down the middle of the screen where he went through. It won't stay shut forever.\" That's Front Row , and the title card: Chapter Six , The Door at the End of the World - Part One: The Audience ."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Part two: the Watcher's Vault","u":"story/chapter-6.html#part-two-the-watchers-vault","t":"Hold the Last Ticket (\"ADMIT ONE - THE VAULT\") up to the seam. The ticket tears in two in your hand and the seam opens wide, from the top of the screen down to the stage, light pouring out, and stays open for everyone ( Admit One ). Walk into it. You come out of a tear in a great dark canvas into the Watcher's Vault , his archive behind the picture: the stacks, steel shelving going up into the dark with cans of film and boxes of tape on every shelf, labelled in his hand, and old television sets among them, some still on. Down the middle runs a long nave. You can't sleep there (\"Not here. Not with them standing out there in the stacks.\"), and the way back is the tear you came through ( Behind the Picture ). ...in here. all the way up. don't look at them. ??? as you come into the Vault"},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The Tuned","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-tuned","t":"Standing in the aisles are people from the neck down, an old television set where the head should be. Unlike most things, the Tuned only move while you're looking at them : watch one and it comes for you in jerks, your face on its screen; look away and it stops dead. Close and watched, it takes your head in its hands and tunes you. Flash an Usher's Lamp at one and it can't move for four seconds, watched or not. In the dark, or in the Projectionist's light, they move whether you look or not. Some drop a Vacuum Tube."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The Watch","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-watch","t":"At the far end of the nave is his desk, his chair, and a wall of sets thirty-seven across and sixteen high, all showing one picture. The first time anyone comes in: this is where i watch from. they watch the picture. i watch them. your world's a show to them. the worse it gets, the more of them come. they left you a ticket. it admits one. not you. something came in behind you. it's come for what i kept. the omni. the carrier. my first reel. get to them before it does. bring them here. ??? at the Watch"},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The keeps","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-keeps","t":"\"Three keeps off the nave, behind round steel doors: the Omni's heart, what's left of the Carrier, his first reel. Bring them to the Watch.\" Use a door or its wheel and the bolts draw back one after another. On a plinth in each is what he kept: The Omni's Heart : \"every colour at once, turning. It's lighter than it looks, and warm.\" What's Left of the Carrier : a knot of it, still beating. Take it and its static pours out, and every Tuned near you is loose for a few seconds (\"...quick. they can all move while it's loose like that.\"). His First Reel , in a glass case: \"On the lid, in his hand: THE OTHER SIDE. FIRST. DO NOT RUN.\" All three is What He Kept ."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The Projectionist","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-projectionist","t":"Bring all three to the Watch and every set on the wall goes to it (\"...it's here. it's in the wall.\"). Then it steps down out of them: the Projectionist , twice a man's height, a long coat made of film, and a cinema projector for a head with a lens you can't look into. It sweeps its beam across the Watch (while you're in it, the Tuned can move), projects reruns of old bosses' best moves onto the air, lashes film round you, splices itself behind you, and changes its reels at each third (hit it then). In the last third comes Intermission : every set and bulb goes out and there's only its lens (\"Please remain seated.\"). Dead, it burns through from the middle like film stuck in the gate and leaves the Projectionist's Lens ( The Final Reel )."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The First Reel","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-first-reel","t":"He runs it. The projector on his desk clatters into life: this is the first thing anyone ever saw on the other side. i kept it so i'd never forget what it looks like. that's what i kept out. it's all for that one. the whole show. and now it's seen you. it's coming through. ??? running his first reel On the wall: a dark so big it has a shape, sitting, with an eye in it, opening. The eye turns to look at you. Then the wall shows the Door at the End of the World. \"Every set on the Watch Wall shows the Door at the End of the World. The static in it has gone black.\" That's What He Kept Out , and the title card for Part Two. He keeps his three things now."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Part three: what he kept out","u":"story/chapter-6.html#part-three-what-he-kept-out","t":"The Door's static has gone black : the dark on the far side of it, looking out. It hums, and the air is drawn into it. Walk into it. The other side is a stage behind the screen your world is shown on: the back of the screen behind you, as big as a cliff, with your world playing across it the wrong way round; the wings either side; painted flats of places from your story; footlights along the front; and past the edge, nothing. \"The other side. A stage, behind the screen your world's on - and past its edge, nothing. Something's sat out there in it.\" You can't sleep there (\"Not here. Not with it out there.\"). Fall off the edge and the dark puts you back on the boards, which hurts. The way home is the seam in the back of the screen ( The Other Side )."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"Curtain Up","u":"story/chapter-6.html#curtain-up","t":"The first time anyone comes through, the Watcher is at a projector at the back of the stage. you came through. good. it hasn't looked this way. not yet. this is the other side. it's watched your world since the first picture. everything that ever happened to you - it watched. now it wants to see you up close. stay out of its eye. get behind the scenery. when it leans in - hit it. i'll run the projector. ??? Curtain Up"},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The Viewer","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-viewer","t":"Out in the dark, knees like hills, hands on the stage's edge with fingers like felled trees, and an eye opening: the Viewer , the last boss. It's so big you only ever fight its eye and its hands. Its gaze wanders the stage; stand in its light with the eye in sight of you and you're Seen , more and more, until it reaches for you. A flat between you and the eye hides you. When it leans in , its eye right at the stage's edge, hit it. With its eye shut nothing hurts it. Plywood stand-ins hop out of the wings and point at you to bring its eye straight to you; knock them over. His last projector does the rest. At two thirds he loads it with the Omni's Heart (\"...its eye's shut. now - the heart.\" then \"every colour at once. it's never seen that.\"), and it reels, blinded ( Every Colour at Once ). At one third he loads the Carrier (\"...the carrier. it carries whatever's put on it.\" then \"your world. all of it. out onto it.\"): the stand-ins burn and it gets up (\"it's getting up. keep its hands off the projector.\"). Standing, it comes faster, the footlights go out, and it reaches for the projector from both sides; beat its hands back ( It Gets Up ). Get through the first third without it ever seeing you right through for Out of Sight ."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"The last show","u":"story/chapter-6.html#the-last-show","t":"It can't be killed. At the last it's held (\"...now. give it the reel.\"), and he threads his first reel and runs it, for it. everyone's always watched it. nobody ever showed it to itself. there. something to watch. it'll watch that forever. it won't look at your world again. somebody has to run the projector. go home. ...thank you for watching. ??? the last show Its own eye goes up on it. It goes still and sits back into the dark, watching itself. He sits down by the projector. Then black, and the credits: STATIC HOLLOW made by Death with the Hollow Saint · the Gardener, Reborn · the Great Bloom · the Flesh · the Carrier · the Chorus, whole · the Deaf King · the Crowd · the Projectionist and the Watcher (he's still running the projector) and you (who watched) THANK YOU FOR WATCHING Everyone who was there gets Thank You for Watching and the record Thank You for Watching . The Omni's Heart, what's left of the Carrier and his first reel are his again, and the Door's static goes back from black to grey. The story's music becomes The Show Goes On , the music box warm and in a major key at last, a projector still running somewhere and slowing. Chapter Six is done."},{"p":"Chapter six: The Door at the End of the World","h":"...not yet","u":"story/chapter-6.html#not-yet","t":"Since 1.59.0 the credits don't end there. They stop on THANK YOU FOR WATCHING, and he speaks: ...not yet. ??? over the last line of the credits His hand comes up through the picture, filling it, and closes round you. That's Chapter Seven: The First Signal . A world whose last show was over before 1.59.0 gets the same moment, the \"encore\", the next time anyone's at home."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"","u":"story/chapter-7.html","t":"The credits roll to their last line, THANK YOU FOR WATCHING, and stop. \"...not yet.\" His hand comes up through the picture and closes round you, and you're somewhere he made. Chapter Seven arrived in 1.59.0, and the mod calls it CHAPTER SEVEN - THE FIRST SIGNAL , \"to be continued\". Since 1.62.0 it runs straight on into Chapter Eight : the jump at its end no longer brings you home. See the landing below."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"The Hub","u":"story/chapter-7.html#the-hub","t":"Everyone who saw the last show is brought to the Hub ( The Hub ): a floating plaza of pale Hub Stone with his marks lit in it, in a sky of drifting static, pieces of realm hanging out in it every way. Along its north side is a gallery of six replay portals , one for each chapter, each playing its chapter on an old set. On its south side is the edge , a walk out over nothing. You can't sleep there. The Hub His speech, at the gallery of replay portals."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"His speech","u":"story/chapter-7.html#his-speech","t":"He turns round to you, and for once he talks for a long time: this is the hub. i made it. a realm. it isn't mine - nothing is - but i made it. through these, you can go back. every chapter. play it again. or jump off the edge. it'll take you home, and you can carry on. this was only the beginning. thank you. ...i could wipe you from existence, you know. find another one of you. but you passed the first trials. all of them. every one made me stronger. whatever held me back - it's gone. i can make realms now. make things you wouldn't dare believe could exist. all thanks to you. i think we'll be fighting forever. until one day i'm strong enough to bring you up to my level. what do you- ??? in the Hub As he says he can make realms now, he lifts a hand, and out in the static a new piece of realm comes together."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"ENOUGH","u":"story/chapter-7.html#enough","t":"The picture breaks up. The sky over the gallery tears open, and a voice comes out of it, low, huge, more than one voice at once: ENOUGH. He goes at the rift with both hands, pushing it shut, and a hand comes out of it and stops him. It tears the rift wide and comes through. The First Signal is your shape and your size. Its skin is crawling static. It wears a long charcoal studio coat, old broadcast headphones round its neck and a little red ON AIR lamp on its chest, lit, and a plain white mask with an eye in the dark behind each eye-hole, always on you. It never hurries. When it moves fast it skips like a signal, frames of it missing and its colours coming apart. It comes for you both. He turns to run, and it shakes its head: no. He stops, turns back, and shoves it with everything he has. It's thrown five hundred blocks out over the static, tumbling. It catches itself with a hand dug into the static, tears a piece of his realm loose, stamps it to rubble, and comes back in jumps, landing on the pieces of his realm one after another as each crumbles behind it. jump. ??? at the edge You go off the edge together. Falling, he shuts the realm behind you: a wall of static , slammed down. It stops at the wall with its hand flat against it. That's ENOUGH . The First Signal \"the first signal. it was here before me. before the first picture.\""},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"The landing","u":"story/chapter-7.html#the-landing","t":"Where the fall takes you depends on when your world got here. Since 1.62.0 (any world that reaches the Hub from then on): falling, he tears a blue portal of signs open under you both, and you come down through it onto an oil rig in the Dead Water. What he says there, and the Remote breaking in your hand, are on Chapter Eight . You still get The First Signal and Channel Changer . In 1.59.0 to 1.61.1 the fall brought you home instead. He came down crouched beside you, wherever you landed: ...it's awake. the first signal. it was here before me. before the first picture. every bit of static you ever heard - that was it. asleep. i made a realm out of its static. and it noticed. i shut the realm behind us. it'll hold. for now. it'll come for me. then for you. ...we're going to need more than i've got. take this. if you need to go back - it's still there. ??? the landing (worlds that came down before 1.62.0) He looks up at a hairline tear across the sky, gives you the Remote and goes. The title card reads CHAPTER SEVEN , THE FIRST SIGNAL , to be continued , and the chat says: \"Somewhere past the static, the First Signal is awake - and it knows your name. Chapter Seven: The First Signal.\" Those worlds get Chapter Eight the next time someone takes the Remote to the Hub and jumps off its edge: he's there, falling beside you (\"not that way. not this time.\" \"hold on.\"), and tears the portal open under you."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"The Remote","u":"story/chapter-7.html#the-remote","t":"An old television's remote; its blank button is warm. Use it and you go into the Hub; use it in the Hub and you go home. The edge takes you home too, with no harm from the fall (but since 1.62.0, if you've never been down to the Dead Water, going off the edge takes you there instead: see Chapter Eight ). In the Hub the First Signal is still there, past the faint wall he shut, standing, watching you. Now and then you hear it. You can't sleep in the Hub (\"Not here. Not with it out there, past the wall.\"). Since 1.62.0 the Remote breaks in the Dead Water and has to be mended before it works again. Mended, crouch and press it to go back to the rig. See getting home ."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"Replays","u":"story/chapter-7.html#replays","t":"Walk into one of the gallery's portals and you're back at that chapter's place in your world. A moment later its last fight comes back for another go: Portal Where it takes you Who comes back The Hollow The Hollow Cathedral The Hollow Saint , rising out of the floor Act Two The Botanic Gardens' glasshouse The Gardener The Bloom The Great Bloom's arena The Gardener, Reborn The Flesh The Laboratory Specimen Zero The Static The Deep The Deaf King The Door The Stalls The Crowd , getting up out of the heap of them The story stays told: beating a replay sets nothing off (no new act, no lockdown, no tickets). Go far from it, leave, die or take too long, and the replay is over: \"The replay's over - it's gone back into the static.\" Your first one is Previously On... . When you've beaten it (\"beaten again\"), the Remote takes you back to the Hub."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"Rerun Reels","u":"story/chapter-7.html#rerun-reels","t":"Since 1.60.0 a replay beaten again leaves three or four Rerun Reels behind (\"AS SEEN BEFORE\"; Rerun ). Chapter Seven's gear, the On Air armour, the Antenna Glaive, the On Air Mace and the Hub-Stone tools, is made with them. See Gear for every chapter ."},{"p":"Chapter seven: The First Signal","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-7.html#what-comes-next","t":"The story's music for this chapter is The First Signal : glass over a bowed bass, static under it all, a skip now and then, and its four notes, low. \"...we're going to need more than i've got.\" In worlds since 1.62.0 the next thing that happens is the Dead Water: Chapter Eight ."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"","u":"story/chapter-8.html","t":"Off the edge of the Hub, with the First Signal behind a wall of static, the fall goes somewhere else. The Watcher tears a portal open under you both, and you come down onto an oil rig in a dead green sea that goes on forever. Chapter Eight arrived in 1.62.0, and 1.63.0 to 1.63.3 filled its sea. The title card reads CHAPTER EIGHT , DEAD WATER , the deep is listening . Its realm is the Dead Water , a dimension of its own."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"Getting there","u":"story/chapter-8.html#getting-there","t":"In a world that reaches the Hub in 1.62.0 or later, it follows straight on from ENOUGH : you jump, and falling, he tears a blue portal of signs open under you. A world that already had Chapter Seven's landing at home gets here the next time someone takes the Remote to the Hub and goes off its edge. He's there, falling beside you: not that way. not this time. hold on. ??? off the Hub's edge, in a world that landed before 1.62.0 Either way you come out over the rig's helipad and land, and he lands after you, crouched ( Dead Water ). ...we're out. it's awake now. the first signal. it'll come for me - then for you. but it can't hear us here. not through all this water. take this. it'll get you back - to the hub, and home. ...no. nothing of mine works right here. then you stay. there's food. beds. i built this place a long time ago - for when i needed somewhere to hide. fix it. the big ones down there sing on its frequency - cut out what they sing with. ??? on the rig's helipad He gives you the Remote , and it breaks in your hand, turning into the Broken Remote (press it and \"It sparks. The warm button's cold. Nothing.\"). Then he goes over the rail into the sea. The chat says what you need: \"Chapter Eight: Dead Water. The Remote's broken - mend it with a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ and a copper ingot. They live deep.\""},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The rig","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-rig","t":"An oil platform standing alone in the Dead Water, four great legs of rusted steel going down into the black. He built it a long time ago, he says, and it's been waiting with its lights on and its larders full: The cellar deck: the moon pool (a square of open water with a ladder down into it), the dive locker, the pumps, the pens (chickens, sheep, cows and a pig, let out when you arrive), the boat dock below it with two boats, and since 1.63.0 the sub bay off the dock, where the submarine Orpheus lies in its clamps. The main deck: the quarters (eight beds), the mess and its kitchen, the infirmary, the workshop, the stores and the greenhouse (crops under glass, water channels, a composter). The upper deck: the control room, the radio room, the armoury, and the helipad you came down on. The derrick in the middle with red lights at its crown, two cranes, the flare stack out over the sea that never goes out, and the lifeboats. You're stranded until the Remote is mended. The rig's beds set your spawn but you can't sleep in them (\"You can't sleep here. The sea won't let you.\"). Die out here and the sea brings you back to the quarters: \"The sea brings you back. Nothing leaves the Dead Water while the Remote's broken.\" You can't lose the Broken Remote either; it's always still in your pocket. The rig's chests (the armoury, the dive locker, the mess, the stores, the sub bay) have what you'll need for the sea: the Harpoon Gun (hold to pump, let go to fire, in water or out; it reels you to the catch or the catch to you) and Harpoon Bolts, Marine Flares (a minute of red light, even underwater), Rig Rations and Air Tanks (a dozen breaths). Thirst and the cold (also new in 1.62.0) follow you here, so keep a canteen filled too. All of it is on Every item and block ."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The Watcher's chart","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-watchers-chart","t":"A little after you come down, the Watcher presses a rolled chart into your hands: here. the sea, as far as i ever charted it. every water has its own colour. the black, hatched in red - that's the dead zone. the black below. nothing down there is small. don't take the little boat over it. ??? handing you his chart The Watcher's Chart covers four thousand blocks of sea round the rig, every water in its own colour and named, the floor's depths shaded and contoured, and the Black Below hatched in red as THE DEAD ZONE. Held, it's a map of the stretch you're in (a thousand blocks a square), with you as an arrow, the others down there with you, and the rig. Use it to unroll the whole chart: scroll to zoom, drag to look round, R to come back to you. Point at a water and you get his note on it. A Map, a Glow Ink Sac and a Prismarine Shard make another."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The twelve waters","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-twelve-waters","t":"Out past the rig the sea is split into twelve waters, each with its own colour and murk, its own floor, plants, life, sound, music and light. The notes are his, from the chart. Water What it's like His note The Grey Shelf The rig's own grey-green. \"Grey water over grey silt. The rig stands in it. Nothing here is in a hurry - mostly.\" The Haemal Reach Blood-red water, thick as soup. \"The water's thick with blood. Clotfish come in swarms; the Siphons wait for them to pass.\" The Wireweed Dark green, a forest of singing wire. \"Weed like wire, and it sings. The Choir Eels nest in it. Don't touch the bright ones.\" The Lantern Fields Black-blue and clear, lit by its plants. \"Lights in the dark as far as you can see. Most of them are bulbs. Some of them aren't.\" The Ossuary Flats Milky, a floor of bone sand. \"A plain of bone. Whatever died here, died big. The Stiltfins pick it clean.\" The Brine Sink Sick yellow-green, with lakes of brine that eat you. \"The brine pools eat what falls in. The water's sour, and the Puffbloats like it.\" The Molar Reef Teal and pink, a reef of teeth and gum. \"Teeth, grown into a reef. The Grinners live in it. They smile at you.\" The Drowned Mycelia Violet, spores in the water. \"Mushrooms the size of towers, drowned. Their spores burst if you brush them.\" The Rime Shelf Cold and clear under a roof of ice. \"Ice under the sea. Things are frozen in it. Some of them wake up.\" The Ember Vents Rust-orange, smoking vents. \"Vents roaring up from below. Warm. The Mantlecrabs crowd round them - mind your power.\" The Carrier Wave Blue-grey, static shimmering through it. \"The static's loudest here. The water hums. Your instruments won't like it.\" The Black Below The abyss: near black, two hundred blocks deeper, nothing alive in it but one thing. \"THE DEAD ZONE. The floor drops away and doesn't stop. The leviathans live down there. Don't.\" What lives in them runs from cute to eldritch: gentle things like the one-eyed Pipeye and the singing Hymnback whales, hunters like the Clotfish, the Hookjaw (which steals your metal) and the Mantlecrab (its pulse kills every light near it, the submarine's too), and the Mouth of the Floor , buried in the floors of the Grey Shelf, the Ossuary Flats and the Molar Reef with only a ring of rocks showing. Pass over it and its jaws open out of the sand and swallow you, submarine and all. Each water also has places of its "},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"Orpheus","u":"story/chapter-8.html#orpheus","t":"The submarine Orpheus waits in its own sub bay off the rig's dock (1.63.0; it's added to rigs that were already up). Since 1.63.2 it's a real submarine thirteen blocks long, with a cabin you walk about in, for up to four people. Climb in by its hatch and down the ladder (\"The helm is up in the bow, under the dome; the bunks, lockers, galley and battery are aft. Walk about her, and use whatever you're looking at.\"). At the bow, under the dome: the helm (take it and drive; crouch to step away), the floodlight switches and the sonar console. Down its length: the chart table (the Watcher's chart), two bunks (lie down to heal, once every two minutes), lockers (27 slots, kept with the sub), a workbench, the galley (its hot plate cooks what you hold), the battery bank (charged with copper ingots, redstone or a block of redstone), the repair board (iron ingots patch the hull and the dome's cracks) and the motor. Driving: W/S thrust, A/D turn, jump to rise, sprint to dive. Use switches the floodlights (they light the water ahead, and draw things that love light, and things that hunt it), attack works its claw, and swap-hands pings the sonar. A submarine's sonar shows where a Mouth of the Floor lies. Depth: it's rated to 183 m down. Past that the hull creaks and the glass cracks, and at nothing it implodes. Pressure Plating (iron blocks, Needle Teeth, Shroud Hide and obsidian, or found down there) lets it go as deep as the sea goes. Lost it? The bay's console builds another for 16 iron ingots and 8 glass. Orpheus Its instruments: depth, hull, power, lamps and sonar."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The Static Leviathan","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-static-leviathan","t":"What you need lives deep. The Signal Organ comes from the Static Leviathan , a boss with its own bar, forty-five blocks long since 1.63.2, with fangs, tusks and its ribs showing through its rotted hide. It charges, it swallows you whole, and it sings on the Remote's frequency. Go more than forty blocks under the surface, anywhere but the Black Below, and now and then one comes up out of the dark after you. (Back home they live in the Overworld's new deep oceans too, down in the Hadal Dark and the Trench.)"},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"The Black Below","u":"story/chapter-8.html#the-black-below","t":"Don't take the little boat over it. In the abyss there's only the sound of the ocean. Stay deep in it and something notices: a rumble from below, and the Undertow comes up out of the dark, a thing three thousand blocks long whose head is a flower of jaws. Since 1.63.3 it doesn't come straight at you. It stalks you, out where you aren't looking, keeping pace (\"Something vast is keeping pace with you, out in the dark.\"). You can't see thirty blocks down there, but you can see its eyes, a cluster of pale points that turn as you turn. It learns you, and tells you so: It has learned how you move. It saw you run for the surface. It will be waiting under you. It has learned your light. It keeps out of it. It knows you now. What it learns, it keeps. It eats when it's hungry (\"It is hungry.\"). Only when it's starving does it roar and come for you; before that, if a lost whale is near, it eats the whale instead (\"It has fed. For now.\"), so a whale nearby can save you. When it comes, it roars (a submarine's glass cracks and its power dies), lunges and swallows you whole. Run for the surface and it breaches after you, hundreds of blocks into the sky. It only goes back down when you leave the Black Below."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"Getting home","u":"story/chapter-8.html#getting-home","t":"Craft the Broken Remote, the Static Leviathan's Signal Organ and a copper ingot together ( Back On Air ): \"The Remote works again. Press it: the Hub (and in the Hub, home). Crouch and press it: back to the rig.\" The Dead Water stays yours to come back to. The rig and each of the twelve waters have music of their own."},{"p":"Chapter eight: The Dead Water","h":"What comes next","u":"story/chapter-8.html#what-comes-next","t":"The First Signal is still awake, past the wall in the Hub. \"it'll come for me - then for you.\""},{"p":"Story overview","h":"","u":"story/index.html","t":"Static Hollow tells one story across eight chapters. You don't need to read anything to follow it: the Watcher tells you where to go, the needles it hands you point there, and the papers left on lecterns fill in what happened before you arrived. This page is the whole path in order, for when you've lost the thread."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"How the story is told","u":"story/index.html#how-the-story-is-told","t":"The Watcher. A tall black figure with glowing eyes, named only \"???\" in the game. It never attacks. It turns up at each turning point, says a few words in chat, and points. Everything it says is collected on its own page. Title cards. The big moments put words across your screen, like THE FLESH WAKES / the flower made it and CHAPTER FIVE . Trackers and needles. When you need to collect parts, a tracker along the top of the screen counts them. When a new place wakes, the Watcher hands everyone a needle: a compass that only ever points there. Papers and tapes. Almost every place has a journal, a log or a notice on a lectern or in a chest. The Laboratory's tapes are voiced. All of them are on the lore pages . Cutscenes. The biggest moments take the camera: the Device's last flight, the Omni Ray, the Watcher taking the Omni back, the late show at the drive-in, signing off, the Chorus speaking ( It Speaks , The Mind , It Runs ), Front Row, the Watch, the First Reel, Curtain Up, the last show and its credits, the Hub and ENOUGH, and the rig. In the modpack they play since 1.47.1 (Entity Culling used to stop them). Music. Since 1.55.0 none of Minecraft's music plays. The world keeps track of how far its story has got, and its music follows: the further along, the more often it's the chapter's own piece. See the soundtrack ."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The whole path, in order","u":"story/index.html#the-whole-path","t":""},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Wake the Forsaken Altar","u":"story/index.html#wake-the-forsaken-altar","t":"Chapter one Every world has one, 500 to 1000 blocks from spawn. Follow the blue smoke, then right-click the altar with an empty hand. The nine creepypastas start hunting everyone in the world."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Take nine heads","u":"story/index.html#take-nine-heads","t":"Each creepypasta always drops its head the first time you kill one. After your ninth kill the Watcher tells you about a church that isn't on any map."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Raise the Hollow Saint","u":"story/index.html#raise-the-hollow-saint","t":"In the cathedral, put one head of each of the nine on the pedestals round the Hollow Reliquary and right-click it. Kill the Saint and the Watcher's beam drags it down to hell."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Go through the Breach","u":"story/index.html#go-through-the-breach","t":"Chapter two Where the Saint fell, a red wound tears open in the ground. It leads into the Void, to the Breach Altar on a floating island."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Wake the Breach Altar","u":"story/index.html#wake-the-breach-altar","t":"Every creepypasta is dragged back down. In their place come five killers and four things from the woods. The Watcher tells you where they live: the Murder Mansion."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Feed the Mending Altar","u":"story/index.html#feed-the-mending-altar","t":"One head from each of the new nine on the trophy pedestals. The Watcher sews them into the Mended . Kill it for the Rusted Garden Key."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Open the glasshouse","u":"story/index.html#open-the-glasshouse","t":"Chapter three The key opens the Botanic Gardens. Find the Gardener's clothes before you wake him, then kill the Gardener at his flower."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Go down the root","u":"story/index.html#go-down-the-root","t":"Three days later a green rift opens over the dead flower. Wear the Gardener's Weeds and go through into the Bloom . Break the Binding and run: ten seconds."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Great Bloom rises","u":"story/index.html#the-great-bloom-rises","t":"It comes up the root and through the glasshouse, and takes the gardens' place for good."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Flesh wakes","u":"story/index.html#the-flesh-wakes","t":"Chapter four Ten seconds later, what the flower was holding down punches up out of the ground east of the gardens, and starts to spread."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Collect the reactor's three parts","u":"story/index.html#collect-the-reactors-three-parts","t":"The Rear Assembly from a truck in Rosemont, the Core from the Laboratory's pool, the Front Assembly from Shelter No. 4, past its Warden ."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Build the Rosemont Device","u":"story/index.html#build-the-rosemont-device","t":"Wire the three parts in the Assembly Cradle, or bring them to a Forsaken Altar and let the Watcher build it. Carry it to the Bloom. The Flesh lets you pass."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Kill the Gardener twice more","u":"story/index.html#kill-the-gardener-twice-more","t":"The Bloom spits the Gardener, Reborn back up at you, and when he dies it grows him back again."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Launch the Device","u":"story/index.html#launch-the-device","t":"The Watcher tears the Bloom open. Set the Device on the launch mark, arm it, run. It goes off inside the Bloom, and the Bloom changes."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Build a gun that talks to the sky","u":"story/index.html#build-a-gun-that-talks-to-the-sky","t":"Three places wake. Bring back the power source parts, have the Watcher infuse the core, and build the Orbital Railgun. Three more places wake for the Ray Gun's parts."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Call down the Omni","u":"story/index.html#call-down-the-omni","t":"The Watcher turns the Ray Gun into the Omni . Fire it at the changed Bloom and SENTINEL comes down out of orbit. Then the Watcher takes the gun back and goes to rest."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Ten days later","u":"story/index.html#ten-days-later","t":"The Watcher finds you wherever you are, with a warning: the parasites came from somewhere else."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The static comes","u":"story/index.html#the-static-comes","t":"Chapter five Static Hound packs at night. One villager in every village hollowed out. Parasites that get into you and grow."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Take Relay 6 off the air","u":"story/index.html#take-relay-6-off-the-air","t":"Climb the mast, cut the tethers, and kill the Amalgam at its foot. It leaves the Relay Core."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Run the last reel","u":"story/index.html#run-the-last-reel","t":"At the Starlite Drive-In , kill Afterimages for four frames and hold them off the projector to the end."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Signing off","u":"story/index.html#signing-off","t":"Hold the reel over the tear and go down into the Null Static Zone . Cut the Carrier loose and kill it. The screen at the drive-in shows one line: SIGNING OFF."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The outbreak, and the End shut","u":"story/index.html#the-outbreak-and-the-end-shut","t":"The Carrier carried them all the way out. The Watcher comes to tell you the parasite's numbers are going off the charts, and shuts the End. From now on the outbreak is worse."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Hive","u":"story/index.html#the-hive","t":"It speaks through five of its pure forms, and the Watcher hands you a needle to the Hive . Tear open the four nerve nodes and bring the Chorus down to a quarter. It runs, deep, and leaves a fragment of itself."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Down into the Deep","u":"story/index.html#down-into-the-deep","t":"Follow the fragment's whispers to the Sinkhole , down the Burrow to the Throat, and into the Deep. Kill the Deaf King for his ear-stones."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Chorus, whole","u":"story/index.html#the-chorus-whole","t":"In the Warm Heart it rises out of the blood. Kill it for good. It leaves the Last Voice, and the Watcher tells you about a seal he made."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"Break the seal","u":"story/index.html#break-the-seal","t":"Chapter six Carry the Last Voice into the End. The seal breaks (\"...don't.\"), and out past the obsidian stands the Door at the End of the World."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Stalls","u":"story/index.html#the-stalls","t":"Sneak past the Audience and the Ushers' lamps in the Stalls , step onto the front aisle and bring down the Crowd . The Watcher was in the front row. He goes through the screen."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Watcher's Vault","u":"story/index.html#the-watchers-vault","t":"The Last Ticket opens the seam. In the Vault , take his three kept things to the Watch, kill the Projectionist , and see his first reel."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"What he kept out","u":"story/index.html#what-he-kept-out","t":"Through the black door to the other side . Stay out of the Viewer 's eye while he runs the projector, until it's held and shown itself. The credits roll."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Hub","u":"story/index.html#the-hub","t":"Chapter seven \"...not yet.\" His hand takes you to the Hub . His speech is cut short: ENOUGH. The First Signal breaks in. Jump."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The Dead Water","u":"story/index.html#the-dead-water","t":"Chapter eight Falling, he tears a portal open under you, onto a rig in the Dead Water . The Remote breaks in your hand. Mend it with a Static Leviathan's Signal Organ, and keep out of the Black Below, where the Undertow is."},{"p":"Story overview","h":"The chapters","u":"story/index.html#the-chapters","t":"1. The Nine The altar, the nine creepypastas, the cathedral and the Hollow Saint. 2. The Breach The Void, the killers and cryptids, the Murder Mansion and the Mended. 3. The Glasshouse The Gardener, the green rift and the Great Bloom. 4. The Flesh Rosemont, the Device, the changed Bloom and the Omni. 5. The Static Hounds, the relay, the drive-in, the Carrier, the outbreak, the Hive and the Deep. 6. The Door at the End of the World The seal, the Stalls, the Watcher's Vault, the other side and the last show. 7. The First Signal After the credits: the Hub, ENOUGH, the Remote and the replays. 8. The Dead Water The rig, the twelve waters, Orpheus and the Undertow."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"","u":"survival.html","t":"Since 1.62.0 staying alive takes more than outrunning what hunts you. You get cold, you get thirsty, the seasons turn, and the world itself moves: rain leaves puddles, rivers flood and running water eats at the land. None of it touches the story's own places. Most of this is built into the mod. The puddles, the erosion, the streams, the seasons and the workstation scenes come from other people's mods that the modpack brings in; they're credited on the credits page ."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Warmth","u":"survival.html#warmth","t":"A little dial sits over the middle of your hotbar, its needle swinging from frost-blue to red, with a chevron over it while you're warming up or cooling down. Your warmth eases toward what's round you: Where you are: the biome, the season, the sun and the night, rain and snow, how high up you are, and deep water. What's near you: fires, lava, campfires, furnaces, torches and lanterns warm you; ice and snow chill you. What you wear: leather keeps the cold out; any armour helps a little. The haunting: the air goes cold round the things that walk in the dark, and colder round the Watcher . The Flesh in you is a fever. What happens, getting worse Cold Your breath shows (a mist on your screen, and puffs that everyone else sees), you shiver and your teeth chatter, then you're slowed, then frost creeps in over your sight, and then it freezes you. Heat You sweat and pant, and you get thirsty faster. Then you weaken, a red haze wavers at the edges of your sight, and heatstroke strikes you down (\"collapsed in the heat\")."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Thirst","u":"survival.html#thirst","t":"A row of drops sits over your food bar. It drains a little all the time and more as you work (sprinting, fighting, digging), and faster in the heat. You go parched , then dehydrated , and then it kills you the way hunger does: on Easy it stops at five hearts, on Normal at half a heart."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Drinking","u":"survival.html#drinking","t":"Water bottles, milk, honey, stews, melon, berries and apples. Look straight up into the rain. Crouch at the water's edge with empty hands and hold use: you drink from your cupped hands."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Tainted water","u":"survival.html#tainted","t":"Water that isn't clean may leave you Tainted : you get thirsty faster and feel queasy (without the nausea effect's swimming screen), and your drops go murky."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"The Canteen","u":"survival.html#the-canteen","t":"Item How In game Canteen String on top, leather either side of an iron ingot, leather below. \"A dented tin flask in a stitched leather sleeve.\" Use it on water to fill it, or hold it out in the rain: rainwater's clean. Murky Canteen Filled from water. Five sips. It may leave you Tainted. \"Pond water. Things move in it if you hold it to the light.\" Clean Canteen Filled in the rain, or a murky one boiled in a furnace, a smoker or on a campfire. Five sips of good water: more thirst back, and it cools you. \"Good water's worth more than it used to be.\""},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"When it's off, and turning it off","u":"survival.html#turning-it-off","t":"Nothing about warmth or thirst changes in Creative, in Spectator, on Peaceful, during a cutscene, or in the story's own places ( the Hub , the Stalls , the Vault and the Other Side ). While a workstation scene plays, the gauges step aside with the rest of the screen. The settings are in config/statichollow-vitals.properties , made the first time a world starts: # Static Hollow - the cold and the thirst # thirst: true/false - the thirst bar, drinking, Tainted water thirst=true # temperature: true/false - warmth, cold and heat temperature=true # thirst_drain: how fast you get thirsty (1.0 as made; 0.5 half as fast) thirst_drain=1.0 # damage: how hard thirst, freezing and heatstroke hurt (1.0 as made; 0 never) damage=1.0 On a server it's the server's config folder that counts. The idea comes from Tough As Nails; none of its code is used."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"The seasons","u":"survival.html#the-seasons","t":"The modpack has Serene Seasons (unmodified, with Static Hollow's own settings in config/sereneseasons ), and the mod fits itself to it: Summer days are hot and winter is bitter; the tropics have their wet and dry seasons. The hound packs come more often through the winter dark, and the things in the woods walk more in autumn. The fog closes in and goes the colour of frost in winter, amber in autumn and a pale haze in summer. The Watcher notices each season turn."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Every sound, where it is","u":"survival.html#every-sound-where-it-is","t":"Since 1.61.1 every sound in the world sounds like the place you're in. A few times a second the mod feels out what's round you: how far away the walls are, how much is open to the sky, and what it's all made of. Stone, metal and glass throw sound back; wood less; earth and sand less again; snow, wool, leaves, moss and the Flesh hardly at all. A cave rings and booms for a second or two. A great cavern's tail runs on for seconds and sound comes back off its far walls as an echo. A stone cellar is short and hard, a wooden room warmer, a wool one dead, a forest a soft close wash, open ground almost nothing. Walk from one into another and it changes smoothly with you. The further off a sound is, the more of it reaches you as the place's echo. Through walls it's muffled, more so the more there is between you; far off, the air takes the top off it. Under water everything is heavy, dull and boomy, and a sound from under the water is muffled the same when you hear it from above. In the Dead Water the echo follows the water: longer and darker the deeper you go. Music and the menus' sounds are left alone. It works the same on Forge and Fabric, with or without shaders. Sound Physics Remastered is still in the modpack but switched off in its settings, since it would do it all a second time. To use it instead, set enabled=true in config/sound_physics_remastered/soundphysics.properties ; the mod's own then steps aside."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Puddles and floods","u":"survival.html#puddles-and-floods","t":"Puddles & Floods (PigCart's) leaves puddles in the rain, under drips and where water runs, and rivers flood their banks. Static Hollow's own water stays on top of it. It also has to be on a server, so the puddles that water, drips and potions leave work there too. Forge has no build of it for 26.3, so the Forge pack carries a port made for it."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Water that wears the world away","u":"survival.html#erosion","t":"Water Erosion (13rac1's, ported to 26.3 for this pack) lets running water dig creeks deeper, cut banks back and dig in under waterfalls. Earth crumbles down to gravel and sand, and stone by running water goes mossy. Only running water erodes, so still water and the deep oceans cost nothing. The pack's settings keep buildings standing and leave the story's places alone ( config/water-erosion.properties )."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Streams (Fabric)","u":"survival.html#streams","t":"The Fabric modpack has Streams: Reflowing (NiceJohn's, unmodified): streams that follow the land down to lakes, rivers and the sea, with whitewater and drifting leaves. It makes its own settings in the config folder the first time; if new chunks are slow to appear, pick a lower quality preset there."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Workstations as scenes","u":"survival.html#workstations-as-scenes","t":"Cinematic Interactions (Southware's, in a build made for this pack) turns crafting tables, furnaces, anvils, grindstones, stonecutters, looms, enchanting tables, brewing stands, lecterns, bookshelves, jukeboxes, campfires and beacons into first-person scenes: you lay the ingredients on the table, load the furnace by hand and hammer at the anvil. Its pages, chimes, hums, the beacon's tuning and the hammer sound like an old house and a dying radio, and its film bars come in with an edge of static."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Falling stars and Channel Zero","u":"survival.html#falling-stars","t":"At night shooting stars streak over the sky, and now and then a small one comes down somewhere near you. Mine the Fallen Star it leaves for Star Static : \"A splinter of the dead channel over the world. It's still warm. It crackles if you hold it to your ear.\" The first one earns Fallout . Channel Zero is a remote that calls things down out of the sky. It's Creative-only for now, with no recipe yet. Point it at the ground and press it; crouch and press it for the next channel: Channel What comes down CH 1 Falling Star : a crater lined with static stone, and a Fallen Star left glowing in it. CH 2 Starfall : nine small stars over four seconds. CH 3 Dead Satellite : it falls burning for five seconds and leaves a wreck, and a satellite core's chest. CH 4 Test Card : colour bars thrown over the ground, and each bar burns in turn. It makes craters only where the TNT game rule lets things blow up. If it isn't pointed at a block it says \"No signal. (Point it at the ground.)\", and too near your own feet, \"Too close - you'd be under it.\""},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Small things that share a space","u":"survival.html#small-things","t":"Seven sets of little things that fit one to four to a block space, each piece turned to face whoever put it down. Place one on another to add a piece; break it and one piece comes off. You'll find them out in the Hollow's own country , on the deep sea floors, on the rig, in the cathedral's crypts and at the altar's pilgrim stones. Set In game Grave Candles \"Tallow candles, a stub, a skull. Up to four in one space; light them.\" Light them and put them out. Bone Pile \"A skull, its jaw, bones. Up to four in one space.\" Rot Caps \"The Blightwood's fungi. They glow a little, and breathe out spores.\" Hanging Chains \"Hung from a ceiling: chains, a hook, a shackle, a weight.\" They creak. Rig Clutter \"What's left lying about on the rig: a tin, an oil can, a wrench, bolts.\" Cairn Stones \"Flat stones, stacked by pilgrims. The top one is carved.\" At night something whispers from the cairn. Ritual Offerings \"A bowl of ash, a straw doll, a red candle, dried herbs.\" The idea of small blocks sharing a space comes from Olaf's Relatively Placed Blocks; nothing of it is used."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"Wearing heads","u":"survival.html#wearing-heads","t":"Since 1.60.0 every creature head can go on your head. It goes on over your own (yours is hidden under it), the edges of the screen darken as you look out of it, and its own kind notice you from only half as far off."},{"p":"Cold, thirst and the world","h":"The rest of the world","u":"survival.html#the-rest-of-the-world","t":"The oceans go down to about 2,000 blocks below the waves, and the Hollow has five places of its own in the Overworld. New worlds only: see the Hollow's own country . The Ender Dragon is always the Infested Ender Dragon since 1.61.1: see the turned . The music is all the mod's own: see the soundtrack ."}];
